News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support The University Of Texas at El Paso Main Content About UTEP The University of Texas at El Paso is America\u2019s leading Hispanic-serving university. Located at the westernmost tip of Texas, where three states and two countries converge along the Rio Grande, 84% of our 26,000 students are Hispanic, and more than half are the first in their families to go to college. UTEP offers 171 bachelor\u2019s, master\u2019s and doctoral degree programs at the only open-access, top-tier research university in America. Our Mission Undergraduate Programs President\u2019s Welcome UTEP At a Glance Become a Miner 171 degree programs and world-class faculty means UTEP has a major for you! Students learn and engage in the classroom, outside UTEP, and around the world. Whatever your interest or passion, we can help you get where you want to go. Learn More Explore UTEP Take a closer look at our unique, Bhutanese-inspired facilities. The 420-acre campus is bustling with growth, including the construction of a new Advanced Manufacturing and Aerospace Center, a new classroom building, and the recently completed Interdisciplinary Research Building. Watch Video History and Traditions The Texas State School of Mines and Metallurgy, now The University of Texas at El Paso, opened its doors Sept. 23, 1914, with buildings located on present-day Fort Bliss. A fire destroyed the campus in 1916 and the University moved to its current location. Learn More By the Numbers 171 Degree Programs 26,297 Students 84% Percentage of Hispanic students $146 Million Annual research expenditures 1 Million + Hours of community service annually contributed by students $1.4 Billion UTEP\u2019s contribution to the El Paso County economy annually Mining Minds \u201cMining Minds\u201d is a steel sculpture installed in 2010 to enhance The University of Texas at El Paso campus and celebrate our mining heritage through the iconic pickaxe head. At night, lights illuminate the structure, while LEDs emanate from the perforated ones and zeroes at each end of the pick. On special occasions, including historic dates, major annual milestones and to celebrate special accomplishments, the pick is illuminated in blue and orange. Learn more <!--\n#theMinds .div-style {\n    background-color: #041e42;\n}\n#theMinds h2,\n#theMinds p {\n    color: #fff;    \n}\n\n@media (min-width: 1250px) {\n    .img-style { \n        float: left; \n        margin-left: 50px;\n    }\n    .div-style {\n        margin-left: -100px;\n        margin-top: 50px;\n        padding: 50px;\n    }\n}\n@media (max-width: 1249px) {\n    .div-style {\n        padding: 15px;\n    }\n}\n--> CONNECT WITH UTEP <!--\n.carousel-control {\n    display: none;\n}\n.fw-section {\n    padding-top: 40px!important;\n    padding-bottom: 40px!important;\n}\n\n.fw-section h1 {\n    text-transform: uppercase;\n    letter-spacing: 1px;\n    font-size: 72px;\n    text-align: center;\n}\n\n.fw-section h2 {\n    text-transform: uppercase;\n    letter-spacing: 3px;\n}\n\n.fw-section h3 {\n    font-size: 36px;\n    letter-spacing: 3px;\n}\n\n.fw-section p { \n    font-size: 16px;\n}\n\n.btn-primary, a.btn-primary {\n    color: white;\n    background-color: #041E42 !important;\n    padding: 10px 30px;\n    text-transform: uppercase;\n    font-weight: 700;\n}\n\n.btn-primary:hover, .btn-primary:focus, a.btn-primary:hover, a.btn-primary:focus {\n    color: #333;\n    background-color: #FF8200 !important;\n}\n\n.btn-primary-orange, a.btn-primary-orange {\n    color: #333;\n    background-color: #FF8200;\n    padding: 10px 30px;\n    text-transform: uppercase;\n    font-weight: 700;\n}\n\n.btn-primary-orange:hover, .btn-primary-orange:focus, a.btn-primary-orange:hover, a.btn-primary-orange:focus {\n    color: #333;\n    background-color: #ffffff;\n}\n\n#theBanner .theContent {\n    padding-top:5%;\n    padding-bottom:5%;\n}\n\n#theBanner .theConten