{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/chief-of-staff/", "title": "Executive Vice President and Chief of Staff", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search Departments Information Security Office Office of Auditing and Consulting Services Government Relations Office of Institutional Compliance Legal Affairs Planning University Police University Relations Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Executive Vice President and Chief of Staff Main Content Executive Vice President and Chief of Staff Welcome to the Division of the Executive Vice President and Chief of Staff Andrea Cortinas Executive Vice President and Chief of Staff acortinas@utep.edu (915) 747-5555 The Division of the Executive Vice President and Chief of Staff assists campus administrators in abiding by and carrying out the authority and responsibilities delegated to the University by The University of Texas System Board of Regents and the Texas Legislature. In addition, the division oversees key initiatives as directed by the administration. <!--\n.well{\n    position: relative;\n    padding-bottom: 30px;\n}\n.btn-primary{\n    position: absolute;\n    bottom: 15px;\n    left: 20px;\n    right: 20px;\n}\n--> Departments Information Security Office The mission of the Information Security Office (ISO) is to protect information acquired and found throughout the University by conducting risk assessments on all sensitive information, promoting security related training and awareness programs, monitoring university systems, and auditing and compliance in support of the University\u2019s missions and goals. Learn More Office of Auditing and Consulting Services The University of Texas at El Paso is a large, complex and growing teaching and research institution whose successful management requires firm control over all activities through a system of financial and operational procedures. The Office of Auditing and Consulting Services (OACS) is charged with the critical function of overseeing management's disposition of these procedures. Learn More Office of Government Relations The Office of Government Relations (OGR) strives to promote dialogue and engagement on a wide range of policy and budget issues. OGR works with elected officials, the UT System Administration and Board of Regents, and government agency officials to address concerns that affect higher education. Learn More Office of Institutional Compliance In support of UTEP's and UT System's visions, missions and goals, the Office of Institutional Compliance strives to provide an atmosphere of compliance awareness so that all UTEP employees may conduct themselves with high ethical standards in compliance with all applicable laws, rules and regulations by being professional, objective, resourceful, and customer oriented. Learn More Office of Legal Affairs The Office of Legal Affairs provides legal advice to The University of Texas at El Paso and the President, administrative officers, faculty, and staff when acting within the course and scope of their employment. Learn More Planning The primary purpose of the Center for Metrics-Based Planning is to study and improve how metrics and analytics are used within a planning framework to improve organizational outcomes at UTEP and other institutions. Learn More University Police The University of Texas at El Paso's Police Department is committed to fulfilling the University\u2019s vision to provide a top tier higher education by ensuring a safe and welcoming campus environment for students, staff, faculty and the public. Learn More University Relations & Events The Office of University Relations oversees the planning and management of University events and conferences. Additionally, the office directs promotional activities that enhance UTEP\u2019s image, assists departments in their goals and attracts more attendance at University-sponsored events. Learn More Human Resources The Office of Human Resources supports the mission of The University of Texas at El Paso by delivering strategic and comprehensive services across recruitment, employee relations, compensation, benefits, training, and organizational development. HR fosters a culture of engagement and excellence by promoting policies and practices that attract, retain, and support our workforce in alignment with UTEP\u2019s mission. Learn More <!--\n.fw-section a {\n    color: #337ab7;\n}\n.fw-section a.btn.btn-primary {\n    color: #fff;\n}\n#theBanner .theContent {\n    padding-top:6%;\n    padding-bottom:6%;\n    max-width:50%;\n}\n#theBanner p {\n    font-size:18px;\n}\n.background-blue #theBanner .btn-primary, .background-blue a.btn-primary {\n    background-color: white;\n    color: #041E42;\n    font-weight: 600;\n    text-transform: uppercase;\n    padding: 9px 15px;\n    font-size: 16px;\n    margin-top: 12px;\n    margin-right: 12px;\n}\n\n@media (max-width: 767px) {\n     #theBanner .theContent {\n         max-width:100%;\n     }\n}\n\n\n\n\n#intro a.btn.btn-primary {\n        font-size: 16px;\n        font-weight: 600;\n        padding: 9px 15px;\n        min-width: 240px;\n    }\n.contactUsBlock {\n    padding-top: 24px !important;\n    padding-bottom: 24px !important;\n}\n.contactUsBlock h3 {\n    text-transform: uppercase;\n    letter-spacing: 2px;\n    margin-top: 0px;\n}\n.contactUsBlock p {\n    line-height: 1.5;\n}\n.contactUsBlock .cubHeading {\n    font-size: 16px;\n    font-weight: 700;\n    margin-top