{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/research/", "title": "Research & Innovation", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About About Research & Innovation Our Units Business Center Research Administration Research Compliance and Regulatory Assurances Research Advancement For Researchers Events Expertise Connector Explore Our Services Find Funding Interdisciplinary Research (IDR) Office of Technology Commercialization Policies/Procedures Research News Research Protections Research & Sponsored Projects Council Submit an NOI - VPN University Research Institute (URI) For Prospective Faculty Research at UTEP For Industry/Partners Office of Technology Commercialization Research Relations and Strategy Research Centers Major Research Centers Events Events Resource Library Learning Opportunities Video Resources Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Research & Innovation Main Content An Open-Access, Top-Tier Research University $158M in annual research expenditures (FY24) RANKED #5 FOR FEDERAL R&D EXPENDITURES AMONG TEXAS 'PUBLIC GENERAL ACADEMIC INSTITUTIONS' (FY24) MESSAGE FROM THE VPRI FACULTY/PI INFO EVENTS EXPLORE OUR SERVICES SUBMIT AN NOI* GO TO Toggle Dropdown R&I Business Center Research Administration Office of Sponsored Projects Grant Management Accounting Research Compliance & Regulatory Assurances Human Subjects Research (IRB) Institutional Animal Care and Use Program (IACUP) Institutional Biosafety Committee (IBC) Dual Use Research Of Concern (DURC-PEPP) Laboratory Animal Resources Center (LARC) Post Approval Verification and Education (PAVE) Research Compliance Research Protections Research Advancement Interdisciplinary Research (IDR) Proposal Development Research Development Research Analytics, Intelligence, and Data Support (RAIDS) Research Relations and Strategy Research, Evaluation, and Assesment Services (REAS) Mike Loya Center for Innovation and Commerce Office of Technology Commercialization (OTC) Message from the Vice President for Research & Innovation Ahmad M. Itani Ph.D. Vice President for Research & Innovation University of Texas at El Paso The University of Texas at El Paso is home to experts who are leaders in their fields and creators of new research thrusts. From Computing to the Arts, our faculty, students, and staff are shaping the future, finding practical answers to complex problems. Supported by state-of-the-art research facilities, we have demonstrated a long-term commitment to preparing students to thrive in a time of fusion of the digital, physical, and biological worlds. Our researchers are creating technologies that will change the world. With more than $158 million in research activity, UTEP is ranked among the top public research universities nationwide. The Research & Innovation division supports this world-class research enterprise by advancing transformative research excellence across campus and nurturing an innovative, cross-disciplinary culture. In all our work, we maintain a constant focus on our public mission of increasing access to excellent higher education and advancing discovery that positively impacts the health, culture, education, and economy of our region, the State of Texas, the nation, and the world. We do so by enabling the research success of our faculty and students through supporting the university research mission by providing research development, stewardship, compliance and safety services, and securing strategic external partnerships. Faculty/PI Information Quickly access your area of interest! Find Funding Proposal Submission Submit a Notice of Intent (NOI) * F&A Rates Transmittal Approval * Grant Management Accounting Events Agreements (CLM) Proposal Development Services Intellectual Property Research Protection & Compliance Research Budget Tool URI Awards Research Data Portal * * Accessible through VPN or UTEP Network Only! F&A Rates Effective Period Rate (%) Location Applicable To 09/01/2022 - 08/31/2025 53.50 On Campus Organized Research 09/01/2020 - 08/31/2025 52 On Campus Instruction 09/01/2020 - 08/31/2025 35 On Campus Other Sponsored Activities 09/01/2020 - 08/31/2025 26 Off-campus All Programs 09/01/2025 - Until Amended Use same rates & conditions as those cited for fiscal year ending Aug 31, 2025 For more information regarding F&A Rates please go to Office of Sponsored Project's Post Award page! Close FEDERAL RESEARCH UPDATES 2025 <!--\n.rsrch-slide{\n    background: #fff;\n  /*  margin: 0 15px; */\n}\n.rsrch-slide .rsrch-img{\n    position:relative;\n    float: left;\n   width:50%; \n    height: auto;\n}\n.rsrch-slide .over-layer{\n    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6);\n    width: 100%;\n    height: 100%;\n    position: absolute;\n    opacity:0;\n    cursor: pointer;\n    transition: opacity 0.30s ease 0s;\n}\n.rsrch-slide .over-layer:after{\n    color: #fff;\n    content: \"+\";\n    font-size: 52px;\n    position: absolute;\n    top: 31%;\n    left:42%;\n}\n.rsrch-slide .rsrch-img:hover .over-layer{\n    opacity:1;\n}\n.rsrch-slide .rsrch-img img{\n    width:100%;\n    height: auto;\n}\n.rsrch-slide .rsrch-review{\n    float: left;\n    padding: 5px 5px;  /* 20px 20px; */\n    width: 95%;  /*  50 */\n   /* background-color: #041e4252; */\n}\n.rsrch-slide .rsrch-title{\n    margin:0 0 5px 0;\n    color: #0a1f40;\n}\n.rsrch-slide .rsrch-title a{\n    color: #0a1f40;\n  /*  \n    font-size: 20px;\n    font-weight: 700;\n    */\n    display: block;\n    text-transform: capitalize;\n    transition:color 0.30s ease;\n}\n.rsrch-title > a:hover{\n    text-decoration: none;\n    color:#0a1f40;\n}\n.rsrch-slide .rsrch-date{\n    display:block;\n    font-size:15px;\n    font-weight:700;\n    margin-bottom:17px;\n}\n.rsrch-description{\n    color: #0a1f40;\n    font-size: 15px;\n    font-weight:400;\n    text-align:left;\n    border-left: #bbc4c1 2px solid;\n  padding-left: 10px;\n  margin-top: 20px;\n\n}\n.owl-pagination{\n    margin-top: 15px;\n}\n.owl-theme .owl-controls .owl-page.active span, .owl-theme .owl-controls.clickable .owl-page:hover span{\n    background: #f28328;\n}\n@media only screen and (max-width: 990px){\n    .rsrch-slide .over-layer:after{\n        top:39%;\n        left: 45%;\n    }\n}\n@media only screen and (max-width: 640px){\n    .rsrch-slide .rsrch-img{\n        width:100%;\n    }\n    .rsrch-slide .rsrch-review{\n        width:100%;\n        padding:10px;\n    }\n}\n--> Research at UTEP Top-Ranked Faculty Twenty of UTEP\u2019s researchers have been ranked among the top 2% most cited researchers in the world! In addition, our faculty have earned distinctions such as the prestigious NSF Early Career award, CUSA Faculty of the Year award, Fulbright, and topping the Edu-Scholar Public Influence Rankings \u2013 and more. Their research has been shared in publications like Scientific American, The Guardian, The Independent, and The New York Times . State-of-the-Art Facilities and Centers UTEP is home to numerous high-quality research centers advancing discovery in aerospace, additive manufacturing, Hispanic health disparities, and more. UTEP\u2019s unique programs have supported research endeavors at the intersections of law and psychology, borderlands history, counseling through play, and a wide range of health, science, and engineering topics. Unique Location UTEP\u2019s unique location on the border of Cd. Ju\u00e1rez, Chihuahua, Mexico allows for highly targeted research, from migration and safety to inter-border trade, pharmaceutical disparities, and more. Plus, UTEP is close to major National Laboratories, such as Sandia National Labs and White Sands Missile Range, allowing for further collaboration. Our Global Impact UTEP\u2019s research impact goes beyond the borderland. From the snow and ice of Antarctica and Alaska to the jungles of Africa, you can find UTEP researchers \u2013 both faculty and students alike \u2013 on every continent. R1-Level Research Opportunities for All As the only open-access R1 institution in the nation and a Hispanic-Serving Institution, UTEP is paving the way to inclusive research opportunities. UTEP is also one of only a few universities that provides a wealth of research opportunities to undergraduate students, increasing our faculty\u2019s impact as educators. 2025 R&I Awardees <!--\n.post-slide{\n    background: #f8f8f8;\n    margin: 0 15px;\n    padding: 4px 4px;\n    border: 1px solid #dedde1;\n}\n.post-slide .post-header{\n   /* margin-bottom: 10px; */  /* if heading text on top */\n    margin-top: 10px;\n}\n.post-slide .subtitle{\n    color:#2f6fa7;  \n    font-size:14px;\n    display: inline-block;\n    margin-bottom:5px;\n    text-transform: uppercase;\n    transition: all 0.4s ease 0s;\n}\n.post-slide .subtitle:hover{\n    color:#333;\n    text-decoration: none;\n}\n.post-slide .post-title{\n    margin: 0;\n    padding: 5px;\n}\n.post-slide .post-title a{\n   /*\n   color:#333;\n    font-size:18px;\n    font-weight: bold;\n    */\n    text-transform:capitalize;\n    transition: all 0.4s ease 0s;\n}\n.post-slide .post-title a:hover{\n    color:#2f6fa7;\n    text-decoration: none;\n}\n.post-slide .pic{\n    overflow: hidden;\n    position: relative;\n}\n.post-slide .pic img{\n    width: 100%;\n    height: auto;\n    transform: rotate(0deg) scale(1,1);\n    transition: all 0.9s ease 0s;\n}\n.post-slide:hover img{\n    transform: rotate(-2deg) scale(1.1,1.1);\n}\n.post-slide .pic:after{\n    content: \"\";\n    position: absolute;\n    top:0;\n    left:0;\n    width: 100%;\n    height: 100%;\n    background: rgba(255,255,255,0);\n    transition: all 0.9s ease 0s;\n \n}\n.post-slide:hover .pic:after{\n    background: rgba(255,255,255,0.2);\n}\n.post-slide .post-bar{\n    list-style: none;\n    padding:12px 5px;\n    margin: 0;\n}\n.post-slide .post-bar li{\n    display: inline-block;\n    margin-right:3px;\n    color:#aaa;\n}\n.post-slide .post-bar li:last-child{\n    margin-right: 0;\n}\n.post-slide .post-bar li a{\n    color:#aaa;\n    transition:0.3s ease;\n}\n.post-slide .post-bar li a:hover{\n    text-decoration: none;\n    color:#2f6fa7;\n}\n.post-slide .post-description{\n    font-size: 14px;\n    line-height: 24px;\n    margin-bottom:15px;\n    color:#767676;\n    padding: 5px;\n}\n.post-slide .read-more{\n    color:#2f6fa7;\n    font-size: 14px;\n    font-style: italic;\n    text-transform: capitalize;\n}\n.post-slide .read-more:hover{\n    color:#333;\n    text-decoration:none;\n}\n@media only screen and (max-width: 479px) {\n    .post-slide{\n        padding: 15px;\n    }\n    .post-slide .post-bar li{\n        margin-bottom: 5px;\n    }\n    .post-slide .post-bar li:last-child{\n        margin-bottom: 0;\n    }\n}\n--> Research News Fly Like a Bird: UTEP Engineers Seek to Translate the Mysteries of Bird Flight into Aircraft Sept. 4, 2025 Have you ever wondered how birds can soar gracefully through the air for long periods without flapping their wings? The answer lies in temperature, wind patterns and the way air moves up and down in the atmosphere. A coalition that includes researchers from The University of Texas at El Paso are using these insights from bird flight to develop uncrewed aircraft systems (UAS), or drone technology, that can save energy and fly more efficiently. Read More UTEP Names James P. Carney Executive Director of W.M. Keck Center for 3D Innovation Aug. 28, 2025 James P. Carney, Ph.D., is the new executive director of The University of Texas at El Paso\u2019s W.M. Keck Center for 3D Innovation, one of the nation's premier university-based additive manufacturing (AM) research facilities. His appointment begins Sept. 1. Carney brings extensive leadership experience in advanced manufacturing from his recent role as manager of the Center for Advanced Manufacturing and Innovation (CAMINO) at Sandia National Laboratories. Read More EUTEP PRESIDENT: RESEARCH AT UTEP REMAINS STRONG Aug. 22, 2025 In her state of the University address during UTEP\u2019s 2025 Convocation, President Heather Wilson congratulated University researchers for the continued strength of their work, touting a number of recent and successful University research initiatives. Read More UTEP Study: Drinking Coffee at Night Increases Impulsive Behavior Aug. 5, 2025 Do you find yourself reaching for a cup of coffee at night to stay alert? A new study from The University of Texas at El Paso suggests you might want to reconsider. A team of UTEP biologists have discovered that nighttime caffeine consumption can increase impulsive behavior, potentially leading to reckless actions. Read More UTEP Researchers Boost Microalgae Biofuel Yields with Nanotechnology Jul. 24, 2025 As global energy use continues to rise, the demand for renewable energy sources such as biofuels is also growing \u2013 especially in the transportation sector. Now, researchers at The University of Texas at El Paso have demonstrated how nanotechnology can significantly improve biofuel production from microalgae, offering a sustainable path forward. Read More Education Professor Earns U.S. Fulbright Scholar Award Jul. 21, 2025 Maria Teresa de la Piedra, Ph.D., a professor in the Department of Teacher Education, says that she always dreamed of conducting research in her home country of Peru and teaching at her alma mater, Pontifica Universidad Cat\u00f3lica del Peru. Starting in Fall 2025, de la Piedra will make that dream a reality as the recipient of a U.S. Fulbright Scholar Award. Read More Ciudad Ju\u00e1rez Sees Higher Wages, Pivots to More Computer and Medical Manufacturing, UTEP Research Finds Jul. 9, 2025 The Hunt Institute for Global Competitiveness at The University of Texas at El Paso has released a new white paper that provides an in-depth look at the evolving labor landscape in one of North America\u2019s most critical manufacturing hubs. Read More UTEP Researchers Reveal Alcohol Impacts Decision-Making in Males More Than Females Jul. 2, 2025 Alcohol consumption is widely known to affect decision-making, but a recent study led by researchers from The University of Texas at El Paso found that the extent of that impact may have something to do with the drinker\u2019s gender. Read More Being an Adult Moth is No Picnic, UTEP Research Finds Jul. 1, 2025 Age is just a number, or is it? A new study by UTEP researchers shows that adult moths are more vulnerable to attack than when they are young. Read More More Research News Contact Us Administration Building (Rm. 209) 500 W University Ave. El Paso, TX 79968 Main: 915-747-5680 Fax (Main): 915-747-6474 <!--\n#myBtn {\n  display: none;\n  position: fixed;\n  bottom: 20px;\n  right: 30px;\n  z-index: 99;\n  font-size: 18px;\n  border: none;\n  outline: none;\n  background-color: #041e42;\n  color: white;\n  cursor: pointer;\n  padding: 15px;\n  border-radius: 4px;\n}\n\n#myBtn:hover {\n  background-color: #ff8200;\n}\n--> // <![CDATA[\n//Get the button\nvar mybutton = document.getElementById(\"myBtn\");\n\n// When the user scrolls down 20px from the top of the document, show the button\nwindow.onscroll = function() {scrollFunction()};\n\nfunction scrollFunction() {\n  if (document.body.scrollTop > 20 || document.documentElement.scrollTop > 20) {\n    mybutton.style.display = \"block\";\n  } else {\n    mybutton.style.display = \"none\";\n  }\n}\n\n// When the user clicks on the button, scroll to the top of the document\nfunction topFunction() {\n  document.body.scrollTop = 0;\n  document.documentElem