 unpaid ticket charges are paid in full. Financial and academic holds can be viewed on Goldmine. Tickets are billed first to the permit holder and then to the vehicle's registered owner if no permit is displayed. Permit holders are responsible for all tickets issued to their permit, regardless of vehicle ownership. Pay Citations Online Use this tool to view and pay the citations associated to your account. View and/or Pay Citations Appeal a Citation Use this tool to submit an appeal if applicable to your citation. Appeal a Citation Parking and Traffic Offenses Review all violations and their amount of fine. List of Parking and Traffic Offenses Parking Portal Citations Guest Parking Schedule Appointment Miner Shuttle Tracker Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso Parking and Transportation Services 3737 N. Mesa Ave Suite A El Paso, Texas 79902 E: parking@utep.edu P: (915)747-5724 THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Texas Veterans Portal Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 | SITE FEEDBACK Modal X"}
{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/parking-and-transportation/parking/service-awards-certificate-of-redemption.html", "title": "Service Awards", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search Parking at a Glance Campus Gate Access Forms and Guides FAQs Parking at UTEP Visitors, Vendors, and Special Guests ADA/DV Parking Motorcycle Parking Policy Cross-Parking Guidelines Overview Prices and Fees Student Permits Faculty and Staff Permits Faculty and Staff Wait List Inner Campus (IC) Orange Departmental Permit Policy Student Carpool Parking Payroll Deduction Service Awards Enforcement and Appeals Citations Parking Offenses Miner Metro Shuttles Miner Metro Resources Announcements Donations for Citations Vision and Mission Prices and Fees Contact PTS Staff Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Parking and Transportation Main Content UTEP Parking and Transportation parking UTEP Parking and Transportation parking Service Awards Please visit the Employee Service Award Guidelines page to see if you are eligible. Contact UTEP Human Resources for any inquiries on eligibility. Service Award Redemption for 2025-2026 has closed as of August 15, 2025. We will look forward to serving the campus community again in May 2026. *** Starting May 1, 2026, the Redeem Now link will go live for an e-form to redeem your incentive. You can complete this entire process electronically with us. There is no need to visit the office unless you want to see our smiling faces. Service Awards may be redeemed for a permit credit . Redemption of service award does not guarantee a permit. You will need to purchase an employee permit before being eligible for a service award redemption credit. Service awards are non-transferable and may not be rolled over to another year. How do service awards work? You purchased your permit and redeemed your service award for parking. What happens next? Parking will apply your service award to your permit purchase. If your permit credit is higher than the price of the permit, your permit is paid for in full. No money is or further credit is issued to you. If your permit credit is lower than the price of the permit, you are responsible for the outstanding amount Example Your permit credit is valued at up to the remote permit price for that year, for illustration purposes $300, but you purchased a perimeter permit priced at $400. Parking will apply the $300 credit, and you will only be responsible of paying the remaining $100 of your permit. If the amount outstanding on your permit after your service award is applied is $100 or LESS - this will be collected via a ONE-TIME deduction If the amount outstanding on your permit after your service award is applied is $100 or MORE -collections will be subject to the preferences submitted at the time you purchased your permit Remember that Service Awards are awarded the Spring of the current fiscal year, but are applicable to the upcoming fiscal year, not the current one. Parking Portal Citations Guest Parking Schedule Appointment Miner Shuttle Tracker Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso Parking and Transportation Services 3737 N. Mesa Ave Suite A El Paso, Texas 79902 E: parking@utep.edu P: (915)747-5724 THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Texas Veterans