{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/parking-and-transportation/parking/faculty-staff-wait-list.html", "title": "Faculty and Staff Wait List", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search Parking at a Glance Campus Gate Access Forms and Guides FAQs Parking at UTEP Visitors, Vendors, and Special Guests ADA/DV Parking Motorcycle Parking Policy Cross-Parking Guidelines Overview Prices and Fees Student Permits Faculty and Staff Permits Faculty and Staff Wait List Inner Campus (IC) Orange Departmental Permit Policy Student Carpool Parking Payroll Deduction Service Awards Enforcement and Appeals Citations Parking Offenses Miner Metro Shuttles Miner Metro Resources Announcements Donations for Citations Vision and Mission Prices and Fees Contact PTS Staff Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Parking and Transportation Main Content UTEP Parking and Transportation parking UTEP Parking and Transportation parking Faculty and Staff Wait List How does the wait list work? For parking permit type based on locations or zone choices that are not immediately available, faculty and staff may submit an application to be placed on the wait list of their desired permit type. Only full-time faculty and staff may apply to the wait list Customers can be on a wait list for 1 permit type (i.e. Inner Campus Orange, Schuster 4, Sun Bowl Garage). Being on the wait list does not guarantee a permit in your preferred location or zone will be available to you Being on the wait list is not a substitute for parking, nor does it guarantee a space If you need to park on campus you need to purchase a permit or utilize the paid visitor parking options. Purchasing a permit will not interfere with your wait list application When can I apply to be on the wait list? Applications open from first business day in September of the current year and close on March 31 of the following year. You may not submit an early application. If you submit an application prior to the opening date it will not be considered. Wait list applications do not automatically renew for next year. If you were not contacted during the year that you applied for, this means a permit in your desired location or zone did not become available. If you want to be considered for the same location for next year, you must submit a new application once the next cycle opens. When will I be notified regarding my wait list application? Waiting list information is confidential and not available to anyone. If a permit in your preferred location or zone becomes available and you are next on the wait list, we will contact you directly. There is no specific timeframe when you will be contacted. It is contingent upon what locations or zones become available and what you selected in your wait list application. Positions on the wait list are determined on a first come, first served basis for those that submit the application correctly, complete, and during the timeframe they are open. I was contacted because a permit in my desired location or zone became available, what do I do next? When a permit in your wait list location or zone becomes available, we will send you an email directly with instructions on what is next. This notification is time sensitive and you have three (3) business days to respond with the requested information. Failure to respond constitutes the cancellation of your waitlist application and we will move on to the next person on the wait list. If you want to be re-considered for that same location and you missed the deadline to respond, you will be required to submit a new application. I have a permit, but I was contacted to exchange because a permit opened up in my preferred location or zone, how does this impact my payroll collections? If you are paying for your current permit via monthly payroll deduction, collections for your current permit stop and new collections are started for your new permit at a pro-rated amount subject to the date of purchase. If the exchange of permits occurs between the\u00a01 st and\u00a0the 15 th day of the month, deductions for your new permit will start on your\u00a0current month\u00a0paycheck. If the exchange of permits occurs\u00a0between\u00a0the 16 th and\u00a0the end of the month, a final deduction is done on your current permit, on your current month paycheck. Deductions for your new permit will start on the following month paycheck. Faculty & Staff Wait List For 2025-2025 Permits will be available on September 2, 2025 on MyParking Account portal. Log into your Parking Account using your UTEP credentials Click on the Add Waitlist button and follow the prompts. You may only select one parking permit/parking lot to be added on the waiting list. Parking Portal Citations Guest Parking Schedule Appointment Miner Shuttle Tracker Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso Parking and Transportation Services 3737 N. Mesa Ave Suite A El Paso, Texas 79902 E: parking@utep.edu P: (915)747-5724 THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Texas Veterans Portal Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 | SITE FEEDBACK Modal X"}
{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/parking-and-transportation/parking/faculty-staff-permits.html", "title": "Faculty and Staff Permits", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search Parking at a Glance Campus Gate Access Forms and Guides FAQs Parking at UTEP Visitors, Vendors, and Special Guests ADA/DV Parking Motorcycle Parking Policy Cross-Parking Guidelines Overview Prices and Fees Student Permits Faculty and Staff Permits Faculty and Staff Wait List Inner Campus (IC) Orange Departmental Permit Policy Student Carpool Parking Payroll Deduction Service Awards Enforcement and Appeals Citations Parking Offenses Miner Metro Shuttles Miner Metro Resources Announcements Donations for Citations Vision and Mission Prices and Fees Contact PTS Staff Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Parking and Transportation Main Content UTEP Parking and Transportation parking UTEP Parking and Transportation parking Faculty and Staff Permits PURCHASING AN employee permit Full-time Employees - Getting Started Full-time faculty and staff may purchase a multi-year employee permit through the My Parking Account by logging in using their UTEP credentials. Available permits can be found by clicking the button called \"Get Permits.\" P ermits are sold year-round on the portal as available. Things to consider: A ll full-time employee permits are paid through payroll deduction with a monthly deduction (9 months or the remaining number of months in the 9-month cycle at purchase time) or a one-time deduction option . Permit prices are prorated monthly (on the fift eenth of each month) . Permits are sold\u202fyear-round,\u202fand the allocated inventory is constantly changing, contingent on several factors, such as, parking facility utilization , permit returns, and construction. Employees may place themselves on the employee waiting list for one permit type ( i.e. Inner Campus Orange, Schuster 4, Sun Bowl Garage). New Employees Don't have your credentials yet? Please send an email with your employment letter to parking@utep.edu . Our staff will assist you with next steps. You do not need to wait until you r first day of employment to contact us. We recommend you reach out to purchase your permit as soon as you receive an offer letter so that we have time to process your permit prior to your first day of work. Part-time Employees Part-time employees are non-student employees who are employed for 20 hours or less for UTEP.\u00a0 P lease contact our office ( parking@utep.edu) with your employment offer letter to assist you with part-time employee (faculty/staff) permit option s. Note: Part-time employees are not eligible for payroll deduction as payment for their parking permit. Additionally, there are no refunds for annual part-time employee permits. employee PARKING LOT OPTIONS: UTEP Sun Bowl Parking Garage Permit (SBG) Permit allows parking in designated lot all day. After 3pm, permit allows you to crosspark into any Silver or Blue perimeter lot. After 4pm, permit allows you to park in the Sun Bowl Garage and the Schuster Garage. After 5pm, permit allows you to park inside of campus (with the exception of numbered reserved spaces). $575.00 per year* See Map Questions? Please email us at parking@utep.edu . Sign on to your Parking Account for additional details or availability. UTEP Schuster Parking Garage (SCG) Permit allows parking in designated lot all day. After 3pm, permit allows you to crosspark into any Silver or Blue perimeter lot. After 4pm, permit allows you to park in the Sun Bowl Garage and the Schuster Garage. After 5pm, permit allows you to park inside of campus (with the exception of numbered reserved spaces). $575.00 per year* See Map Questions? Please email us at parking@utep.edu . Sign on to your Parking Account for additional details or availability. UTEP Health Sciences - College of Nursing Parking Garage (HNG) Permit allows parking in designated lot all day. After 3pm, permit allows you to crosspark into any Silver or Blue perimeter lot. After 4pm, permit allows you to park in the Sun Bowl Garage and the Schuster Garage. After 5pm, permit allows you to park inside of campus (with the exception of numbered reserved spaces). Access into the garage requires obtaining a permit and being granted access via your Miner Gold Card. $575.00 per year* See Map Questions? Please email us at parking@utep.edu . Sign on to your Parking Account for additional details or availability. Red (Reserved Inner-Campus) Allows parking in the designated location on the front of the permit (example: Red UN3 permits may park in Lot UN3) and all orange, blue, and green zones. After 3pm, permit allows you to crosspark into any Silver perimeter lot. After 4pm, permit allows you to park in the Sun Bowl Garage and the Schuster Garage. After 5pm, permit allows you to park anywhere inside of campus (with the exception of numbered reserved spaces). $930.00 per year* Prices for Reserved spaces IC-R $600.00 per year* Prices for red zone UN2, UN3, KE1, WI4, HG1, SB1, SB2 Red, SB9 See Map Questions? Please email us at parking@utep.edu . Sign on to your Parking Account for additional details or availability. Orange (Inner-Campus) Allows parking in all orange, blue, and green zones. After 3pm, permit allows you to crosspark into any Silver perimeter lot. After 4pm, permit allows you to park in the Sun Bowl Garage and the Schuster Garage. After 5pm, permit allows you to park anywhere inside of campus (with the exception of numbered reserved spaces). $525.00 per year* See Map Questions? Please email us at parking@utep.edu . Sign on to your Parking Account for additional details or availability. Blue Perimeter (DA1, SB5, SB6, SC1 through SC5, GR1, GR2, GR3, GR5, OR2) Permit allows parking in designated lot all day. After 3pm, permit allows you to crosspark into any Silver or Blue perimeter lot. After 4pm, permit allows you to park in the Sun Bowl Garage and the Schuster Garage. After 5pm, permit allows you to park inside of campus (with the exception of numbered reserved spaces). $400.00 per year* See Map Questions? Please email us at parking@utep.edu . Sign on to your Parking Account for additional details or availability. Brown (GR4 Reserved) Permit allows parking in designated lot all day. After 3pm, permit allows you to crosspark into any Silver or Blue perimeter lot. After 4pm, permit allows you to park in the Sun Bowl Garage and the Schuster Garage. After 5pm, permit allows you to park inside of campus (with the exception of numbered reserved spaces). $500.00 per year* See Map Questions? Please email us at parking@utep.edu . Sign on to your Parking Account for additional details or availability. Green Remote (SB7-SB8, SB10-SB11, ME1, NE2 and NE3) Permit allows parking in green remote zones. After 3pm, permit allows you to crosspark into any Silver or Blue perimeter lot. After 4pm, permit allows you to park in the Sun Bowl Garage and the Schuster Garage. After 5pm, permit allows you to park inside of campus (with the exception of numbered reserved spaces). $300.00 per year* See Map Questions? Please email us at parking@utep.edu . Sign on to your Parking Account for additional details or availability. *Academic year from 8/16 of current year to 8/15 of next year. <!--\n.permitSection h3 { \tmargin: 0; } .permitSection .col-md-6.garagePics { \tpadding-left: 0; \tmargin-bottom: 12px; }\n--> SEPARATING EMPLOYMENT FROM THE UNIVERSITY? If you are leaving, return your permit! Full-time employees leaving the university should return their permit online using the e-form available on their parking account . Employees who paid one-time may be entitled to a refund on their payroll depending on time of year. Employees who selected monthly deductions will have additional payroll deductions stopped. More information on payroll deductions and refunds for employees can be found on the Payroll Deductions webpage . Cross Parking Is allowed in Silver Premium Perimeter and Blue Perimeter lots AFTER 3:00 pm. From 3pm to 8pm, any current and valid UTEP parking permit on display is allowed to park on these areas Is allowed in the UTEP Sun Bowl and Schuster Parking Garage AFTER 4:00 pm. From 4pm to 8pm, any current and valid UTEP parking permit on display is allowed to park on these areas Is allowed in Green Remote lots with any current and valid UTEP parking permit from 7am to 8pm. Is allowed in Red/Orange Inner-Campus lots AFTER 5:00 pm (Except for Red Zone WI1,or Reserved parking, that is designated and enforced 24 hours, 7 days a week) Parking Portal Citations Guest Parking Schedule Appointment Miner Shuttle Tracker Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso Parking and Transportation Services 3737 N. Mesa Ave Suite A El Paso, Texas 79902 E: parking@utep.edu P: (915)747-5724 THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Texas Veterans Portal Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 | SITE FEEDBACK Modal X"}
