 services effectively. We will make every effort to utilize creativity in finding solutions to the parking challenges faced by the University and its customers. We strive to provide excellent customer service through timely and customer-focused communication. We uphold accountability and integrity through fair and unbiased enforcement of the University\u2019s Parking Rules and Regulations. We embrace adaptability in addressing the rapidly changing parking and transportation needs of the University community. We exhibit the highest standards of professionalism and respect in all interactions with customers and University guests. We pursue excellence through teamwork . Parking Portal Citations Guest Parking Schedule Appointment Miner Shuttle Tracker Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso Parking and Transportation Services 3737 N. Mesa Ave Suite A El Paso, Texas 79902 E: parking@utep.edu P: (915)747-5724 THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Texas Veterans Portal Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 | SITE FEEDBACK Modal X"}
{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/parking-and-transportation/announcements1/donationsforcitations.html", "title": "Donations for Citations", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search Parking at a Glance Campus Gate Access Forms and Guides FAQs Parking at UTEP Visitors, Vendors, and Special Guests ADA/DV Parking Motorcycle Parking Policy Cross-Parking Guidelines Overview Prices and Fees Student Permits Faculty and Staff Permits Faculty and Staff Wait List Inner Campus (IC) Orange Departmental Permit Policy Student Carpool Parking Payroll Deduction Service Awards Enforcement and Appeals Citations Parking Offenses Miner Metro Shuttles Miner Metro Resources Announcements Donations for Citations Vision and Mission Prices and Fees Contact PTS Staff Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Parking and Transportation Main Content UTEP Parking and Transportation Announcements UTEP Parking and Transportation Announcements Donations for Citations Resolve one eligible parking citation by donating items to the UTEP Food Pantry. This limited-time program partners the UTEP Student Government Association, Parking & Transportation Services, Center for Community Engagement, and the UTEP Food Pantry to meet student basic needs while offering a community-focused path to resolve one qualifying citation. \ud83d\udcdd Start Your Donation Dismissal Request \ud83d\udcc5 Program Window Event dates: November 17\u201321 Eligible citations issued: Aug\u00a01, 2024 \u2013 Nov\u00a016, 2025 One dismissal per person during the event. Base fine must be $50 or less . Late fees will be adjusted as part of the program. \u2705 Who\u2019s Eligible? You have one unpaid citation with a base fine \u2264 $50 , issued within the eligible dates. The citation is not under appeal (or you agree to withdraw the appeal). \ud83d\udeab Not Eligible ADA violations, fire lane, fraudulent permit use, tow/boot fees, illegal entry/exit, property damage, or any violation with a base fine over $50. \ud83d\udee0\ufe0f How It Works Complete the online request form. Bring your donations and form confirmation to a collection site during the event window. We verify eligibility and count your items on the spot. If everything checks out, your qualifying citation is dismissed immediately . You\u2019ll receive a confirmation number for your records. Exchange rate: 10 full-sized accepted items = 1 eligible citation (\u2264 $50) dismissed. \ud83c\udf81 What to Donate All items must be full-sized, new, sealed, unexpired, and in original packaging . Size limits help the Food Pantry store and distribute donations efficiently. \ud83d\udce6 Size Limits Canned items: up to 15 oz Shelf-stable milk: up to 32 oz Juice: up to 20 oz Dry rice/beans: up to 2 lbs Pasta sauce: up to 24 oz ; tomato sauce up to 12 oz \u2705 Most-Needed Items Peanut butter; canned meats; vegetables/beans Chef Boyardee, soups, chili; rice/pasta; cereal & oatmeal Mac & cheese cups, ramen, granola bars, Pop-Tarts Applesauce & fruit cups; 100% juice boxes Toilet paper; shampoo/conditioner; soap; lotion Menstrual pads (unopened); toothpaste & toothbrushes Electrolyte drinks; protein snacks (nuts, trail mix, Slim Jims) Opened, damaged, or expired items do not count toward the total. \ud83d\udccd Where to Donate Drop off donations at the Parking Office (3737 N. Mesa St., Suite A) or any staffed tabling site during the event. Look for signs and volunteers with collection bins. \ud83d\udcdd Program Terms (Summary) One citation dismissal per person during the event. Citation must be unpaid, with base fine \u2264 $50, issued within the eligible window. Appeals must be withdrawn before we can process dismissal. No refunds or credits for citations already paid. PTS reserves the right to decline ineligible submissions. \ud83d\udceb Questions? We\u2019re happy to help you check eligibility or item requirements. \ud83d\udce7 parking@utep.edu Start Your Donation Dismissal Request <!--\nul { list-style-position: outside; margin-bottom: 1rem; }\n  .alert { border-left: 5px solid #ff8200; }\n  .btn-warning:hover { background-color:#e67600; color:#fff; }\n--> Parking Portal Citations Guest Parking Schedule Appointment Miner Shuttle Tracker Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso Parking and Transportation Services 3737 N. Mesa Ave Suite A El Paso, Texas 79902 E: parking@utep.edu P: (915)747-5724 THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Texas Veterans Portal Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 | SITE FEEDBACK Modal X"}
{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/ehs/emergency%20managment/message-from-emc.html", "title": "Message from EMC", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About About Meet the Team Organization Chart Programs Environmental Protection Occupational Safety Wild Animals on Campus Workers Compensation Lab Safety Biological Safety Radiation Safety SciShield Waste Fire Prevention Fire Prevention Fire Safety Fire Extinguishers Student Housing Safety Training Laboratory Training CPR/Fire Trainings Emergency Management Emergency Management AEDs Regulations Dichloromethane Forms Manuals Standard Operating Procedure Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Environmental Health & Safety Main Content UTEP Environmental Health & Safety Emergency Managment UTEP Environmental Health & Safety Emergency Managment Message from EMC Ricardo Gonzalez\u00a0EFO, MPA, CEM Assistant Director of EH&S Emergency Management Coordinator / Fire Marshal The safety of The University of Texas at El Paso (UTEP) community during an emergency is predicated on advance planning, as well as situational awareness among the campus response teams, faculty and staff about how the emergency plans will be implemented and their roles in an emergency. Students, faculty, staff and visitors are better prepared in an emergency when they understand how the University has planned respond, where they can find important information regarding plans, and what they each should do to protect themselves and others around them. The Office of Emergency Management is part of the Environmental Health and Safety Department at UTEP. The Emergency Management Office is an essential resource for evaluating emergency plans, offering constructive input to planning efforts, and exercising plans to assure readiness. The staff is responsible to coordinate emergency exercises, fire drills, and training the UTEP Campus Responders to a high degree of readiness. Emergency Management Message from EMC Emergency Action Guide AEDs Evacuation Chairs Fire Prevention SDS Database Emergency Management Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso Environmental Health and Safety Department El Paso Natural Gas Building, Room 10 500 W University Avenue El Paso, Texas 79968 E: eh&s@utep.edu P: (915) 747-7124 F: (915) 747-8126 THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Texas Veterans Portal Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 | SITE FEEDBACK Modal X"}
{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/ehs/manuals.html", "title": "Manuals", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About About Meet the Team Organization Chart Programs Environmental Protection Occupational Safety Wild Animals on Campus Workers Compensation Lab Safety Biological Safety Radiation Safety SciShield Waste Fire Prevention Fire Prevention Fire Safety Fire Extinguishers Student Housing Safety Training Laboratory Training CPR/Fire Trainings Emergency Management Emergency Management AEDs Regulations Dichloromethane Forms Manuals Standard Operating Procedure Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Environmental Health & Safety Main Content UTEP Environmental Health & Safety UTEP Environmental Health & Safety Manuals A - E H - M O - Z Animals on Campus Policy Learn More Automated External Defibrillator Guidelines Learn More Biological Safety Manual Learn More Chemical Hygiene Plan Learn More Confined Space Guidelines Learn More Emergency Action Guide (HTML) Learn More Emergency Action Guide (PDF) Learn More Emergency Management Plan Learn More Environmental Health and Safety Manual Learn More Exposure Control Plan Learn More Hazardous Materials Handling and Disposal Policy Learn More Hearing Conservation Program Manual Learn More Lab Animal Allergy Information Learn More Laboratory Safety Manual Learn More Laser Safety Manual Learn More Minors in Hazardous Work Areas Learn More Occupational Health Medicine Program Guidelines Learn More Radiation Safety Manual Learn More Respiratory Protection Program Learn More Return To Work Policy Learn More Safe Handling of Peroxide Forming Chemicals Learn More Texas Hazard Communication and Right to Know Learn More \u00d7 Animals on Campus Policy Information and procedures to follow for animals brought to campus. Download Close \u00d7 Automated External Defibrillator Guidelines Information on the Automated External Defibrillator (AED) Program. Where they are located and available training in Cardio Pulmonary Resuscitation (CPR), AED use, and basic first aid to campus personnel. Download Close \u00d7 Biological Safety Manual The Biological Safety Manual presents biosafety practices as recommended by the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) and National Institutes of Health (NIH). The Biological Safety Manual is supplemental to the University\u2019s Laboratory Safety Manual which addresses safe working practices in the laboratory. Download Close \u00d7 Chemical Hygiene Plan A Chemical Hygiene Plan (CHP) is a \u201cwritten program developed and implemented by the employer which sets forth procedures, equipment, personal protective equipment and work practices that are capable of protecting employees from the health hazards presented by 5 hazardous chemicals used in a particular workplace\"(Code of Federal Regulations, 29 CFR 1910.1450b, Definitions). Download Close Confined Space Guidelines The Confined Space Entry Program establishes procedures for personnel who need to enter spaces with limited or restricted means for entry or exit and which are not designed for continuous occupancy. Download Close \u00d7 Emergency Action Guide (HTML) Actionable steps and information for university personnel on how to manage campus emergencies. Download Close \u00d7 Emergency Action Guide (PDF) Actionable steps and information for university personnel on how to manage campus emergencies. Download Close \u00d7 Emergency Management Plan The Emergency Management Plan (EMP) establishes policies, procedures, and organizational structure for response to emergencies at The University of Texas at El Paso. Download Close \u00d7 Environmental Health and Safety Manual The Environmental Health and Safety (EH&S) Manual establishes procedures for safe operation of campus spaces including offices, laboratories, workshops, studios, grounds. It is essential that students, staff and faculty follow the EH&S manual and actively work to mitigate hazards associated with campus activities under their control. Download Close \u00d7 Exposure Control Plan The Exposure Control Plan outlines policies and procedures to prevent or minimize the exposure of UTEP employees to bloodborne pathogens or other potentially infectious material. Download Close undefinedundefinedundefinedundefined \u00d7 Hazardous Materials Handling and Disposal Policy The Hazardous Materials Handling and Disposal policy outlines procedures to follow to manage and properly dispose of regulated waste generated by campus personnel. Download Close \u00d7 Hearing Conservation Program Manual The Hearing Conservation Program manual provides information for the protection of UTEP employees from hearing loss associated with high noise levels in the workplace. Download Close \u00d7 Lab Animal Allergy Information Information for UTEP researchers who handle laboratory animals and who are at risk of potential exposure to animal allergens found in dander, urine, saliva. Lab animal-related allergies are one of the most significant health hazards faced by laboratory animal researchers. Download Close \u00d7 Laboratory Safety Manual The Laboratory Safety Manual establishes general rules and procedures, and promotes safe practices while working in UTEP laboratories. Download Close \u00d7 Laser Safety Manual The Laser Safety Manual provides information, safety procedures and controls relevant research and educational activities involving Lasers. Download Close \u00d7 Minors in Hazardous Work Areas This document establishes operating procedures to assist UTEP personnel and departments in addressing the requirements for allowing minors to participate in internships, volunteer work or sponsored programs specific to activities in potentially hazardous laboratories on the UTEP campus. Download Close \u00d7 Occupational Health Medicine Program Guidelines Information on the Occupational Health Program for UTEP researchers. The purpose and guidelines for participation in the medical surveillance program. Download Close \u00d7 Radiation Safety Manual The Radiation Safety Manual is a supplement to federal, state, and local regulations for the control of radiation. It provides policy and procedures to follow for the safe handling of radioactive materials. Download Close \u00d7 Respiratory Protection Program The Respiratory Protection Program manual outlines procedures to ensure the protection of UTEP employees from respiratory hazards through the proper fit and use of approved respirators. Download Close \u00d7 Return To Work Policy The policy document provides information to employees who due to a work-related injury are temporarily restricted from performing their regularly assigned duties. Supervisors and injured employees can use the program to place the employee in a temporary position (also known as modified duty) that addresses the injured employee\u2019s work restrictions. Download Close \u00d7 Safe Handling of Peroxide Forming Chemicals Chemicals that react with oxygen to make peroxides create hazards and the chemical can explode with impact, heat, or friction. The guidance document provides information for the safe handling of peroxide forming chemicals. Download Close \u00d7 Texas Hazard Communication and Right to Know This policy manual informs UTEP employees and the general public about chemical hazards at UTEP. It provides employees with information and procedures to follow to protect themselves from hazardous chemicals to which they may be exposed in their work area(s). Download Close Forms Forms Manuals SDS Database Emergency Management Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso Environmental Health and Safety Department El Paso Natural Gas Building, Room 10 500 W University Avenue El Paso, Texas 79968 E: eh&s@utep.edu P: (915) 747-7124 F: (915) 747-8126 THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Texas Veterans Portal Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 | SITE FEEDBACK Modal X"}
