epared in any event. Learn More Fire Extinguishers Information on the type fires and classes of fire extinguishers here on campus. Learn More Student Housing Safety Helpful information about fire prevention and awareness for residents living in stuednt housing. Learn More <!--\n.highligtsWrapper {\n\t    display: flex;\n\t    display: -webkit-flex;\n\t    flex-wrap: wrap;\n\t}\n.highligtsWrapper .col-md-4 {\n           margin-bottom: 30px;\n    }\n.highligtsWrapper .well {\n\t    box-shadow: 0px 2px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);\n\t    -webkit-box-shadow: 0px 2px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);\n\t    height: 100%;\n\t    padding: 0;\n\t     text-align:center;\n    }\n.highligtsBody {\n    \tpadding: 0 24px 0 24px;\n\t}\n.highligtsBody p:nth-last-of-type(1) {\n    \tmargin-bottom: 45px;\n\t}\n.highligtsBody .btn-primary {\n        display: block;\n    margin-top: 15px !important;\n}\n--> Smoking On Campus The use of tobacco products (including but not limited to, cigarettes, cigars, pipes, water pipes (hookah), bidis, kreteks, electronic cigarettes, smokeless tobacco, snuff, chewing tobacco or \u00a0all other \u00a0tobacco products) as well \u00a0as \u00a0smoking or use of any smoking device, by students, faculty, staff, and visitors is prohibited at all times on University Property. Learn more. FAQs Who should I call in the event of a fire? If there is a fire, evacuate immediately and call UTEP Campus Police at\u00a0915-747-5611 or 9-1-1. What should I do if I notice a fire safety violation? If you notice a fire safety violation on campus, contact EH&S. Please let us know your concerns. Do not call us if your concern involves a life-threatening emergency or fire, however. In the event of an emergency or fire, please call 9-1-1 or Campus Police at 915-747-5611. <!--\n    .accWrapper > div {\n    padding-left:24px;\n    }\n    .collapseToggleControl.collapsed span.glyphicon:before {\n        content: \"\\002b\";\n    }\n    .collapseToggleControl span.glyphicon:before {\n       