y. If you or an employee you supervise has an on-the-job injury, medical care is available through the IMO Network of medical care providers. For emergency care an urgent care clinic or emergency room visit may also be used. Additionally the supervisor of the injured person is required to complete the Supervisor\u2019s First Report of Injury or Illness, and to forward the completed form to the Workers Compensation Advisor within EH&S. Reporting work related injuries and illnesses insures proper accident investigation and possible development of mitigation strategies to reduce accident rates. Injury Incident Report What to Do if Injured Employees These are the steps an employee should follow when injured on the job. M\u00e1s Informaci\u00f3n Learn More Supervisors Supervisor should follow these steps if there is an injured employee on the job. M\u00e1s Informaci\u00f3n Learn More Everyone Anyone who is injured on campus, can report through the Incident Report form. M\u00e1s Informaci\u00f3n Learn More <!--\n.highligtsWrapper {\n\t    display: flex;\n\t    display: -webkit-flex;\n\t    flex-wrap: wrap;\n\t}\n.highligtsWrapper .col-md-4 {\n           margin-bottom: 30px;\n    }\n.highligtsWrapper .well {\n\t    box-shadow: 0px 2px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);\n\t    -webkit-box-shadow: 0px 2px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);\n\t    height: 100%;\n\t    padding: 0;\n\t     text-align:center;\n    }\n.highligtsBody {\n    \tpadding: 0 24px 0 24px;\n\t}\n.highligtsBody p:nth-last-of-type(1) {\n    \tmargin-bottom: 45px;\n\t}\n.highligtsBody .btn-primary {\n        display: block;\n    margin-top: 15px !important;\n}\n--> Injury Reporting: Incident Report Injured individuals on campus, including faculty, staff, and student employees, can report incidents via the Incident Report form. Incident Report IMO Network Acknowledgement Forms This form confirms receipt of information (Notice of Network Requirements & Employee Handbook Material) necessary to access healthcare under Workers\u2019 Compensation Insurance WCI Treating Doctors UTEP employees with job-related injuries have access to medical care through the IMO Network. Scan QR codes or visit urgent care clinics or emergency rooms. Network Ack. Form WCI Treating Doctors WCI First Fill Prescription Card For work-related medication needs, follow instructions on the poster to obtain your First Fill Prescription Card. WCI First Fill Prescription Card Programs Environmental Protection Occupational Safety Wild Animals on Campus Workers Compensation SDS Database Emergency Management Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso Environmental Health and Safety Department El Paso Natural Gas Building, Room 10 500 W University Avenue El Paso, Texas 79968 E: eh&s@utep.edu P: (915) 747-7124 F: (915) 747-8126 THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Texas Veterans Portal Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 | SITE FEEDBACK Modal X"}
