{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/ehs/laboratory%20safety/radiation-safety-program.html", "title": "Radiation Safety", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About About Meet the Team Organization Chart Programs Environmental Protection Occupational Safety Wild Animals on Campus Workers Compensation Lab Safety Biological Safety Radiation Safety SciShield Waste Fire Prevention Fire Prevention Fire Safety Fire Extinguishers Student Housing Safety Training Laboratory Training CPR/Fire Trainings Emergency Management Emergency Management AEDs Regulations Dichloromethane Forms Manuals Standard Operating Procedure Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Environmental Health & Safety Main Content UTEP Environmental Health & Safety Laboratory Safety UTEP Environmental Health & Safety Laboratory Safety Radiation Safety Program Radiation Safety Program The Radiation Safety Program provides institutional support and oversight for the receipt, use, and disposal of radioactive materials, lasers, and X-ray producing equipment, as well as compliance with applicable state and federal regulations. Radiation Safety Manual _____________________________________ Laser Safety EH&S also monitors operations of Class 3B and 4 lasers on campus to ensure compliance with national and state regulations, and institutional procedures and policies. Fundamental properties of lasers, laser classification and hazards, biological effects, safety practices, common accidents and emergency procedures, orientation to University safety policies. Laser Safety Manual Laser Institute of America _____________________________________ Radiation Registration Radiation Safety is responsible for the proper licensing and registration of regulated sources of radiation and liaison activities with pertinent regulatory agencies.\u00a0Procedures such as time, distance and shielding that must be followed while working with radiation at UTEP in order to minimize personnel exposure. Request to Order Radioactive Material Application for Authorization to use radioactive materials Laboratory Safety Biological Safety Radiation Safety SciShield Waste SDS Database Emergency Management Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso Environmental Health and Safety Department El Paso Natural Gas Building, Room 10 500 W University Avenue El Paso, Texas 79968 E: eh&s@utep.edu P: (915) 747-7124 F: (915) 747-8126 THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Texas Veterans Portal Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 | SITE FEEDBACK Modal X"}
{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/parking-and-transportation/resources/prices-fees.html", "title": "Prices and Fees", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search Parking at a Glance Campus Gate Access Forms and Guides FAQs Parking at UTEP Visitors, Vendors, and Special Guests ADA/DV Parking Motorcycle Parking Policy Cross-Parking Guidelines Overview Prices and Fees Student Permits Faculty and Staff Permits Faculty and Staff Wait List Inner Campus (IC) Orange Departmental Permit Policy Student Carpool Parking Payroll Deduction Service Awards Enforcement and Appeals Citations Parking Offenses Miner Metro Shuttles Miner Metro Resources Announcements Donations for Citations Vision and Mission Prices and Fees Contact PTS Staff Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Parking and Transportation Main Content UTEP Parking and Transportation Resources UTEP Parking and Transportation Resources Permit Pricing and Fees \ud83d\udcd1 Table of Contents \ud83d\uddd3\ufe0f Multi-Year Employee Permits \ud83d\udcbc Employee Permit Prices \ud83c\udf93 Student Permits \ud83d\udcd8 Student Permit Prices \ud83d\udcb2 Fees \ud83d\uddd3\ufe0f Multi-Year Employee Permits Eligibility Notice: These permit types and prices are available to full-time UTEP employees only . Employees must be benefits-eligible and have an active payroll record to qualify. Part-time employees, contractors, and affiliates should contact Parking & Transportation for alternative permit options. Multi-year permits are prorated monthly on the 16th of each month from September through May . The prices listed reflect the cost of a full year . These permits renew automatically each year . If you're on payroll deduction, your payments will continue into the new permit year unless you make a change. When enrolling in payroll deduction, you select: One-time or monthly payments Pre-tax or post-tax deductions These preferences will carry over automatically when your permit renews. \ud83d\udcbc Standard Yearly Permit Prices Permit Type Yearly Price IC Reserved Spaces $930.00 IC Red $600.00 IC Orange $525.00 Sun Bowl Parking Garage (SBG) $575.00 Schuster Parking Garage (SCG) $575.00 Health Science Parking Garage (HNG) $575.00 Perimeter (Blue) $400.00 Motorcycle $228.00 Remote (GRN) $300.00 Brown (GR4) $500.00 Motorcycle Permit (secondary) $30.00 \ud83c\udf93 Student Permits Student permits are required for any student parking on campus between 7:00 AM and 8:00 PM . Permit types include garage, perimeter, remote, housing, and motorcycle options. Housing permits are available only to students living in Miner Village, Miner Canyon, or Miner Heights. These permits are enforced 24/7 and valid only in assigned housing lots. Permits are valid for one full academic year. If you need to cancel a permit, you may be eligible for a prorated refund through May 31 . Contact parking@utep.edu for questions. For after-hours access rules, visit our Cross-Parking Guidelines page. \ud83d\udcd8 Student Permit Prices Permit Type Yearly Price Sun Bowl Parking Garages (SBG) $400.00 Schuster Parking Garage (SCG) $400.00 Perimeter (Silver) $300.00 Perimeter (Blue) $225.00 Evening (4PM to 8PM) $150.00 Remote (GRN) $165.00 Miner Housing (Purple) $225.00 Motorcycle $150.00 Motorcycle (Secondary) $30.00 \ud83d\udcb2 Fees Permit Replacement Fee: If your hangtag or physical permit is lost or stolen, a replacement may be issued for a $30.00 fee . Contact parking@utep.edu or visit the Parking Office to submit a replacement request. Fees are subject to change and are non-refundable unless otherwise stated in UTEP\u2019s Parking Rules & Regulations. Parking Portal Citations Guest Parking Schedule Appointment Miner Shuttle Tracker Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso Parking and Transportation Services 3737 N. Mesa Ave Suite A El Paso, Texas 79902 E: parking@utep.edu P: (915)747-5724 THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Texas Veterans Portal Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 | SITE FEEDBACK Modal X"}
{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/ehs/laboratory%20safety/bio-chem-safety.html", "title": "Biological Safety", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About About Meet the Team Organization Chart Programs Environmental Protection Occupational Safety Wild Animals on Campus Workers Compensation Lab Safety Biological Safety Radiation Safety SciShield Waste Fire Prevention Fire Prevention Fire Safety Fire Extinguishers Student Housing Safety Training Laboratory Training CPR/Fire Trainings Emergency Management Emergency Management AEDs Regulations Dichloromethane Forms Manuals Standard Operating Procedure Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Environmental Health & Safety Main Content UTEP Environmental Health & Safety Laboratory Safety UTEP Environmental Health & Safety Laboratory Safety Biological Safety Program The Biological Safety Program mission is to support the research goals of the University while promoting a safe laboratory working environment by ensuring regulatory compliance of laboratory equipment, hazardous chemicals and infectious biological agents. The staff provides support to UTEP students, faculty, and staff by identifying, evaluating, and controlling chemical, biological, and physical hazards. The primary goal is to provide the safest work environment for the UTEP community, as well as minimizing risk to the environment and property. Biological and Chemical Safety staff is responsible for laboratory surveys and audits in order to ensure safety and compliance in dealing with hazardous materials. The staff also participates in the UTEP Institutional Biosafety Committee (IBC) and the Institutional Animal Care and Use Committee (IACUC) and is available to consult with the campus community on research that incorporates the use of hazardous chemicals or infectious agents. Stay Informed Laboratory Safety Manual Learn More Laboratory Safety Manual \u00d7 This Laboratory Safety Manual has been provided by the University Environmental Health and Safety (EH&S) Office to establish basic procedures and to promote safety practices in UTEP\u2019s laboratories. This manual is not intended to cover every procedure and only touches on certain generic subjects As part of your introduction to the laboratory, before starting experiments in any lab, become familiar with the procedures, chemicals, and safety equipment in each area that you will be using. Learn more: Laboratory Safety Manual Biological Safety Manual Learn More Biological Safety Manual \u00d7 This Biological Safety Manual presents general information and biosafety practices as recommended by the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) and National Institutes of Health (NIH). This Biological Safety Manual is supplemental to the University\u2019s Laboratory Safety Manual which addresses safe working practices in the lab and Industrial Hygiene aspects of the laboratory work up to and including medical prophylaxis and monitoring for laboratory worker protection Learn more: Biological Safety Manual Occupational Health Guidelines Learn More Occupational Health\u00a0Program Guidelines \u00d7 This document also establishes operating procedures to assist departments and individuals in addressing the requirements for participation in the Occupational Health Program at UTEP. This program is designed to: 1. Prevent and detect disease and illness resulting from exposure to possible health hazards in the research environment; 2. Offer prompt and appropriate treatment for exposures; and 3. Establish baseline health data for future comparison Learn more: Occupational Health Program Guidelines Occupational Health Medicine Questionnaire NIH Guidelines for Working with recombinant and synthetic DNA Learn More NIH Guidelines for Working with recombinant and synthetic DNA \u00d7 The purpose of the NIH Guidelines is to specify the biosafety practices and containment principles for constructing and handling: (i) recombinant nucleic acid molecules, (ii) synthetic nucleic acid molecules, including those that are chemically or otherwise modified but can base pair with naturally occurring nucleic acid molecules, and (iii) cells, organisms, and viruses containing such molecules. Learn more: NiH Guidelines Biosafety in Microbiological and Biomedical Laboratories Learn More Biosafety in Microbiological and Biomedical Laboratories \u00d7 Biosafety in Microbiological and Biomedical Laboratories (BMBL) has become the overarching guidance document for the practice of biosafety in the U.S.\u2014 the mechanism for addressing the safe handling and containment of infectious microorganisms and hazardous biological materials Learn more: Biosafety in Microbiological and Biomedical Laboratories, 6th Edition UTEP Office Of Research and Sponsored Projects Learn More Office of Reasearch and Sponsored Projects \u00d7 The vision of the Office of Research and Sponsored Projects (ORSP) is to accelerate the\u00a0research and sponsored program enterprise while adhering to university policies and federal regulations. The purpose of the Institutional Animal Care and Use Committee (IACUC) is to assure that UTEP researchers care for and use animals in ways judged to be scientifically, technically, and humanely appropriate. The mission of the Institutional Biosafety Committee (IBC) at The University of Texas at El Paso(UTEP) is to ensure that research involving recombinant DNA (rDNA), synthetic nucleotides, infectious agents (pathogens), biological toxins, nanotechnology, or select agents is classified at the appropriate biosafety level and done in accordance with all appropriate guidelines, regulations and good safety practices. Learn more: Office of Reasearch and Sponsored Projects Institutional Animal Care and Use Program (IACUP) Institutional Biosafety Committee (IBC) <!--\n    .accWrapper > div {\n    padding-left:24px;\n    }\n    .collapseToggleControl.collapsed span.glyphicon:before {\n        content: \"\\002b\";\n    }\n    .collapseToggleControl span.glyphicon:before {\n        content: \"\\2212\";\n    }\n    .optionalblock {\n        margin-top: 30px;\n        margin-bottom: 30px;\n    }\n /*flex*/\n.highligtsWrapper {\n    display: flex;\n    display: -webkit-flex;\n    flex-wrap: wrap;\n    margin-left: -14px;\n}\n.highligtsWrapper .col-md-4:nth-last-child(1) {\n    margin-bottom: 30px;\n}\n.highligtsWrapper .well {\n\tbox-shadow:0px 2px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);-webkit-box-shadow:0px 2px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);;\n\theight: 100%;\n\tpadding: 0;\n}\n.highligtsBody {\n\tpadding: 0 24px 0 24px;\n}\n.highligtsBody .btn-primary {\n    \tdisplay:block;\n    \tmargin-top: 30px;\n}\n\n.highligtsWrapper .col-md-4 {\n   margin-bottom: 30px;\n}\n\n.lightWhiteBg {\n\tbackground: rgba(255,255,255,.85);\n    padding: 4px 24px 24px 24px;\n    margin-bottom: 20px;\n}\n--> <!--\ndiv.facebook .pp_top .pp_left{background:#fff;}div.facebook .pp_top .pp_middle{background:#fff;}div.facebook .pp_top .pp_right{background:#fff;}div.facebook .pp_content_container .pp_left{background:#fff;}div.facebook .pp_content_container .pp_right{background:#fff;}div.facebook .pp_expand{background:url(//www.utep.edu/university-communications/_UC-Global-Files/lightbox/theme/sprite.png) -31px -26px no-repeat;cursor:pointer}div.facebook .pp_expand:hover{background:url(//www.utep.edu/university-communications/_UC-Global-Files/lightbox/theme/sprite.png) -31px -47px no-repeat;cursor:pointer}div.face