 a Storm Water Management Program. Storm Water Management Program The department of Environmental Health and Safety has submitted an annual report for the period beginning 01/01/2024 and ending 12/31/2024 . 2024 MS4 Annual Report Download Visual Aid body h2:target {\n        padding-top: 135px;\n        margin-top: -135px;\n    } Environmental Quality The Environmental Protection Program (EPP) comprehensively evaluates, monitors, and controls environmental releases in the form of air, water, hazardous waste, and assets, and ensures releases to the environment are safe, compliant, and cost effective. The program utilizes a systematic approach to manage hazardous materials and environmental affairs and strives to raise awareness of environmental impacts throughout the UTEP community. Texas Commision on Environmental Quality Environmental Protection The program also reviews planning and design documents involved with construction, renovation, and demolition. This is a service that is provided to ensure compliance with the various air, water, and waste regulations, safety regulations, such as asbestos, PCBs, lead based paint, mercury, and petroleum products. Environmental Protection Agency Programs Environmental Protection Occupational Safety Wild Animals on Campus Workers Compensation SDS Database Emergency Management Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso Environmental Health and Safety Department El Paso Natural Gas Building, Room 10 500 W University Avenue El Paso, Texas 79968 E: eh&s@utep.edu P: (915) 747-7124 F: (915) 747-8126 THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Texas Veterans Portal Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 | SITE FEEDBACK Modal X"}
