{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/parking-and-transportation/resources/faq.html", "title": "FAQs", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search Parking at a Glance Campus Gate Access Forms and Guides FAQs Parking at UTEP Visitors, Vendors, and Special Guests ADA/DV Parking Motorcycle Parking Policy Cross-Parking Guidelines Overview Prices and Fees Student Permits Faculty and Staff Permits Faculty and Staff Wait List Inner Campus (IC) Orange Departmental Permit Policy Student Carpool Parking Payroll Deduction Service Awards Enforcement and Appeals Citations Parking Offenses Miner Metro Shuttles Miner Metro Resources Announcements Donations for Citations Vision and Mission Prices and Fees Contact PTS Staff Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Parking and Transportation Main Content UTEP Parking and Transportation Resources UTEP Parking and Transportation Resources How Can We Help? Need help with permits, citations, visitor parking, or the shuttle? We've organized our most common questions below. Still stuck? Email us , check out our Forms & Guides , or review the full Rules and Regulations. \ud83c\udd7f\ufe0f Permits Do I need a permit? Yes. All vehicles on campus must have a valid permit or pay for hourly parking. Enforcement is 24/7. When can I buy my permit? Permit sale dates are posted online and emailed out. Fall permits usually go on sale in August. Once permits go one sale for the new academic year, they are sold\u00a0year-round,\u00a0and the\u00a0allocated\u00a0inventory is constantly changing, contingent on several factors, such\u00a0as,\u00a0parking facility\u00a0utilization, permit returns, and construction. What if I forgot my permit? Visit the East or West entrance gates for a one-day pass or email parking@utep.edu. Can I register more than one vehicle? Yes, but only one vehicle may be on campus at a time under the same permit. Permit holders receive only one permit which can be moved between vehicles. Stickers are made with repositionable adhesive, allowing you to move them from one vehicle to another. I haven't received my permit yet! Permits for the Fall 2025/Spring 2026 school year began mailing out on 8/15/2025. Permits take 7-10 business days to arrive. Keep an eye out for an envelope like this: \ud83d\udd01 Permit Returns Can I return my permit? Yes! Permits can be returned if you no longer need them. Students may be eligible for a prorated refund based on the quarter, and employees on payroll deduction may stop future deductions by returning their permit. If I just purchased my permit, can I submit a return request? You must have your current permit in hand to submit a return request. If you have just purchased it, you must wait until you receive the permit to request a return. Any valid request submitted prior to 8/31 will be eligible for a full refund. How do I request a permit return? Fill out the Permit Return Request form online. What if I lost my permit? Report it immediately. Replacement fees may apply. If it was stolen, provide a police report for the fee to be waived. \ud83c\udf93 Student Permits Can employees buy student permits? No. Employees must purchase employee permits. I live on campus \u2014 what permit do I need? A Purple (Housing) permit. It\u2019s valid only for your assigned housing lot. Can I park anywhere with a student permit? No. Each permit is only valid in specific zones. Check your purchase confirmation or permit map. For specific student permit details, click here . \ud83d\udcdd Student Parking Permit Sales Guide 2025\u20132026 Where can I find everything about student permits? Visit our comprehensive Student Permit Sales Guide for full details on sale dates, permit types, housing restrictions, ADA eligibility, and more. Does the guide include garage, remote, and housing info? Yes! It breaks down all permit zones and who qualifies for each one, including parking times and cross-parking rules. Is there a direct link to buy a permit? Yes. The guide includes a direct link to the UTEP Parking Portal . \u26a0\ufe0f Citations How do I pay a citation? Students and current employees with UTEP credentials must pay through Pete's Payments. For information on how to pay for a citation as a visitor, visit our guides . Can I appeal a citation? Current students, faculty, and staff can appeal eligible citations through their parking accounts at parking.utep.edu. Your appeal will be reviewed and you will get a final decision in 12\u201314 business days. Citations are only eligible for appeal within 18 calendar days of the date of issuance. Not all violations are eligible for appeal , including ILLEGAL ENTRY/EXIT OF FACILITY and EXPIRED METER. What are invalid reasons for appeal? The following reasons are examples of potentially invalid appeals. (These are not all inclusive.) Parked for only a few minutes Not agreeing with the rules/regulations Inclement weather Late for class/meeting Lot full Only drives occasionally and does not want to purchase a permit A friend/coworker told me it was okay to park here Other vehicles were also parked improperly/illegally No one told me my permit expired No one told me where or how to park on campus \u267f ADA / DV Parking Do I still need a UTEP permit with my ADA placard? Yes. You must have both a valid UTEP permit and your state-issued ADA placard or plates. Can I park anywhere with ADA credentials? A valid UTEP permit allows you to park in the designated lot, and your ADA credentials allow you to park in any ADA space within that lot. Fire lanes, reserved spots, and loading zones are still restricted. What are the requirements for DV parking? DV permit holders must display both a state-issued plate (with the ISA symbol or a matching placard) and a complimentary UTEP parking permit. The plate or placard must be registered to the UTEP-affiliated driver or occupant. What if my DV plate doesn\u2019t have the ISA symbol? You may still receive a complimentary permit, but only for specific areas (such as Perimeter, Remote, or Garage zones). You cannot park in ADA spaces without the ISA symbol or a placard. \ud83d\udc65 Visitors How do visitors park on campus? They can use pay-by-phone lots or request a guest permit through a department host. Click here to learn more about visitor parking . Can UTEP students or employees use guest permits? No. Guest permits are only for official visitors who are not affiliated with UTEP. \ud83d\ude8c Shuttles & Mobility Is the Miner Metro free? Yes! Shuttle service is free to all UTEP students, employees, and visitors. Where can I find shuttle routes? Visit utep.passiogo.com to track real-time locations and see routes. Parking Portal Citations Guest Parking Schedule Appointment Miner Shuttle Tracker Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso Parking and Transportation Services 3737 N. Mesa Ave Suite A El Paso, Texas 79902 E: parking@utep.edu P: (915)747-5724 THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Texas Veterans Portal Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 | SITE FEEDBACK Modal X"}
