sa Ave. Use the GR5 or OR2 lots near the Don Haskins Center and Glory Road Terminal, then take the Miner Metro Shuttle to campus. \ud83d\udfe0 West-Side Access Points SB2 (Sun Bowl 2) \u2014 across from Kelly Hall and the Health Sciences Building (elevator access to pedestrian bridge) Perfect for west-side arrivals near the Bookstore and Sun Bowl area. \u26a0\ufe0f Note: No drop-offs at Sun Bowl 3 or the Mining Minds Pick Roundabout for safety reasons. \ud83d\udd35 Central Campus Access DA1 (Dawson 1) \u2014 beside Sun Bowl Stadium and Sun Bowl Garage Convenient for access to Fox Fine Arts, Psychology, Centennial Plaza, Education, and Liberal Arts buildings. \ud83d\udfe3 South-Side Access SC1 (Schuster 1) \u2014 across from Schuster Garage near the College of Business and Mike Loya Academic Services Building Ideal for drop-offs serving the Business, Engineering, and Library areas. \ud83d\udeab Reminder: Avoid curbside drop-offs near campus entrances. Please use designated drop-off zones for safety and smoother traffic flow. \ud83d\udea7 Campus Gate Access Overview UTEP uses automated gate controls to manage traffic flow within the Inner Campus. During peak hours, only vehicles with valid Orange or Red Inner-Campus permits are allowed through the gates. \u23f0 Restricted hours: Monday\u2013Friday, 7:00 a.m. \u2013 5:00 p.m. \ud83d\ude97 Open access: After 5:00 p.m. (permit still required until 8:00 p.m.) Visitors attending events or arriving with temporary, VIP, or media passes should enter through the lanes marked for visitors at the University Avenue entrances. Community Service Guards stationed at the east and west gates will assist anyone who needs directions to the nearest visitor parking area. \ud83c\udd7f\ufe0f Campus Gate Access Locations 1\ufe0f\u20e3 East Gate Entrance University Ave / Oregon St (next to Hilton Garden Inn) \ud83d\udccd GPS: 111 W University Ave, El Paso, TX 79902 Access via gate guard, Miner Gold card, or RFID tag with valid Inner Campus permit\u00a0(7:00 a.m. \u2013 5:00 p.m., Monday\u2013Friday) UTEP permit required until 8:00 p.m. 2\ufe0f\u20e3 West Gate Entrance University Ave / Sun Bowl Dr (next to University Bookstore) \ud83d\udccd GPS: 2201 Sun Bowl Dr, El Paso, TX 79902 Access via gate guard, Miner Gold card, or RFID tag with valid Inner Campus permit\u00a0(7:00 a.m. \u2013 5:00 p.m., Monday\u2013Friday) UTEP permit required until 8:00 p.m. 3\ufe0f\u20e3 Hawthorne Entrance Hawthorne St / Rim Rd (next to Chemistry & Computer Science Building) \ud83d\udea7 Closed for construction until further notice \ud83d\udea7 4\ufe0f\u20e3 Rim Road Entrance Rim Rd / Hawthorne (next to Academic Services Building) \ud83d\udccd GPS: 601 W Schuster Ave, El Paso, TX 79968 Access via gate guard, Miner Gold card, or RFID tag with valid Inner Campus permit\u00a0(7:00 a.m. \u2013 5:00 p.m., Monday\u2013Friday) UTEP permit required until 8:00 p.m. 5\ufe0f\u20e3 Randolph Road Entrance Randolph Rd / Robinson St (next to Kidd Field) Access by Miner Gold card only \u2014 24 hours a day Miner Gold card must be scanned TWICE to open gate <!--\n  ul { list-style-position: outside; margin-bottom: 1rem; }\n  .card ul li { margin-bottom: .25rem; }\n  .btn-warning:hover { background-color:#e67600; color:#fff; }\n--> Parking Portal Citations Guest Parking Schedule Appointment Miner Shuttle Tracker Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso Parking and Transportation Services 3737 N. Mesa Ave Suite A El Paso, Texas 79902 E: parking@utep.edu P: (915)747-5724 THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Texas Veterans Portal Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 | SITE FEEDBACK Modal X"}
