{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/research/office-of-sponsored-projects/", "title": "Office of Sponsored Projects", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search Home Office of Sponsored Projects Grant Management Accounting ---------------- Business Center Research Administration Research Compliance and Regulatory Assurances Research Advancement About Meet the Team Find your RA Sponsored Project Lifecyle Services Pre-Award Post-Award Contracts and Agreements Subcontracts Support PI resources Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ) Policies/Procedures Policies/Procedures One Pagers One Pagers Quick Info Quick Info Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Office of Sponsored Projects Research & Innovation Main Content Office of Sponsored Projects DIRECTOR'S MESSAGE FACULTY/PI INFO FIND YOUR RA *INITIATE NOI * NOI is an internal form accessible in the UTEP network or VPN <!--\n.carousel-caption {\n    display: block !important;\n}\n--> Welcome to the Office of Sponsored Projects, better known as OSP! Under the leadership of the Vice President for Research & Innovation, OSP is the central administrative office for seeking and accepting external funding at UTEP. As Director of OSP, it is a privilege to steward the University\u2019s research efforts through integrity, professional execution, and careful management of UTEP\u2019s sponsored research activities together with regulatory compliance to the University's policies and procedures. Our team of Research Administrators and Contract Specialists purpose is to absorb the administrative burden of proposal submission and management of awarded grants, allowing faculty more time to focus on mentoring students in addition to fostering and performing their own research endeavors. To achieve continued success in the production of this core function, our team encourages good project management practices from PI\u2019s while providing pre- and post-award grant management support. OSP believes in collaborative relationships between administrators and investigators working jointly towards the common goal of winning outside funding for projects of benefit to the UTEP community. We also warrant compliance with state and federal regulations, sponsor requirements, and grant-specific terms and conditions. We look forward to working with you! Cory Brown Director - Office of Sponsored Projects Faculty/PI Information As a Principal Investigator (PI) at UTEP, you hold ultimate responsibility for all facets of your research, including compliance with university and federal regulations. OSP is dedicated to supporting you in this important role. The PI resources below have been developed to guide you through the research administration process. Sponsored Projects Lifecycle Find Funding Notice of Intent (NOI) Proposal Submission F&A Rates Research Budget Tool Transmittal Approval Grant Management Accounting Events & Training Agreements Quick Info One Pagers Faculty F&A Rates Effective Period Rate (%) Location Applicable To 09/01/2022 - 08/31/2025 53.50 On Campus Organized Research 09/01/2020 - 08/31/2025 52 On Campus Instruction 09/01/2020 - 08/31/2025 35 On Campus Other Sponsored Activities 09/01/2020 - 08/31/2025 26 Off-campus All Programs 09/01/2025 - Until Amended Use same rates & conditions as those cited for fiscal year ending Aug 31, 2025 For more information regarding F&A Rates please go to Office of Sponsored Project's Post Award page! Close Who We Are The Office of Sponsored Projects (OSP) is the centralized unit charged with providing comprehensive support to members of The University of Texas at El Paso (UTEP) research community engaged in the preparation and submission of proposals and the management of funded projects. OSP strives to maintain a supportive environment for research and scholarly endeavors and encourages faculty and staff to seek external funding to support the mission of the University and to explore alternatives to advance their professional interest. Please visit the OSP Team page to connect with us: Meet the Team <!--\n#title::after {\n  content: \"\";\n  display: block;\n  width:32px;\n  padding-top: 3px;\n  border-bottom: 2px solid #041E42;\n}\n--> What we do Before we share what we do at OSP, it is important to determine whether your opportunity is a sponsored project. A sponsored project is an activity in which there is a specified statement of work for the University to execute with a related, mutual transfer of something of value (whether tangible or intangible) for a public purpose or as a direct benefit to the sponsor. In short, sponsored projects are funded research, instruction, testing, training, service, or other scholarly activities in which a formal written agreement or contract is entered into between UTEP and the sponsor. OSP is responsible for ensuring that all research proposals and projects adhere to UTEP\u2019s academic and research policies and meet obligations to external sponsors. Through teamwork and partnership, OSP provides support and builds relationships with PI\u2019s to successfully apply for research funding. Our office oversees the following: Proposals and Grants: budget development and administrative review Contracts and Awards: contract review, negotiation, and award set-up Subaward Management and Monitoring: shared responsibility between PI and OSP Oversight of compensation confirmation process: allocating compensation charges to sponsored projects and timely reporting Contact Us OSP is located in Kelly Hall, 6th floor, East Wing 500 W University Ave El Paso, TX 79968 Main: 915-747-5680 osp@utep.edu Fax: 747-8977 Research Administration <!--\n#myBtn {\n  display: none;\n  position: fixed;\n  bottom: 20px;\n  right: 30px;\n  z-index: 99;\n  font-size: 18px;\n  border: none;\n  outline: none;\n  background-color: #041e42;\n  color: white;\n  cursor: pointer;\n  padding: 15px;\n  border-radius: 4px;\n}\n\n#myBtn:hover {\n  background-color: #ff8200;\n}\n--> // <![CDATA[\n//Get the button\nvar mybutton = document.getElementById(\"myBtn\");\n\n// When the user scrolls down 20px from the top of the document, show the button\nwindow.onscroll = function() {scrollFunction()};\n\nfunction scrollFunction() {\n  if (document.body.scrollTop > 20 || document.documentElement.scrollTop > 20) {\n    mybutton.style.display = \"block\";\n  } else {\n    mybutton.style.display = \"none\";\n  }\n}\n\n// When the user clicks on the button, scroll to the top of the document\nfunction topFunction() {\n  document.body.scrollTop = 0;\n  document.documentElement.scrollTop = 0;\n}\n// ]]> <!--\nh1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6   {text-align: left;}\n\n\n.card {\n    height: 140px;\n    width: 100%; \n   /* width: 115px; */\n  /*  background: #e6843e;  */\n  /*  box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px lightgrey; */\n    padding: 2px;\n    border:  1px solid #0a1f4042;\n  /*  border-radius: 4px; */\n    margin: 5px;\n    text-align:center;\n   /* font-family: \"arial narrow\"; */\n    font-weight:bold;\n    font-size: 13px;\n    letter-spacing: -0.5px;\n}\n\n.card:hover {\n    border: #f28328 1px solid;\n    \n}\n--> // <![CDATA[\n$(document).ready(function() { \n            \n                $(\"h2\").css(\"text-align\", \"left\"); \n                \n                $(\"a#bluelink\").css(\"color\", \"#337ab7\"); \n                \n             $('#ShowOSPMSG').click(function() {\n          \n           var classList =$(this).find('i').attr(\"class\");\n           co