{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/research/research-protections/research%20compliance%20training/training-faq.html", "title": "Training FAQs", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search Home Research Protections Human Subjects Research (IRB) Institutional Animal Care and Use Program (IACUP) Laboratory Animal Resources Center (LARC) Institutional Biosafety Committee (IBC) Dual Use Research of Concern - PEPP Post Approval Verification and Education (PAVE) Research Compliance ---------------- Business Center Research Administration Research Compliance and Regulatory Assurances Research Advancement Export Control Export Control EC Forms and Links International Travel Policies TCP Export Control Memo Thesis-Dissertation Foreign Visitors UTEP Export Control Manual Final.pdf International Transactions Controlled Items Safeguarding CUI Federal Clauses Disclosure Management Disclosure Management Disclosure Help Videos Disclosure Management One Pager.pdf FAQs Outside Activity Portal Policies schedule meeting Research Security Research Security Restricted Research Cybersecurity Insider Risk Program CITI Program Research Security Training Instructions.pdf CUI Controlled Unclassified Information CUI Processes and Procedures CUI Training CUI Regulations Quick Reference Quick Facts safeguarding_cui.pdf Docusign_VP_CUI_Memorandum_and_Visual.pdf RIO Research Integrity Office UTEP Research Integrity Policy Process Agency Reporting Requirements.pdf Flowchart Compliance Training Research Compliance Training Training Page CITI Program Research Security Training Instructions.pdf CITI Program Instructions - Add RCR Course.pdf CITI Program Instructions - Export Control.pdf Training FAQs Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Research Protections Research & Innovation Main Content Research Compliance Training Training FAQs Contact Us Mario E. Caire, Ph.D. Research Security Officer Kelly Hall, 4th floor, North Wing 500 W University Ave El Paso, TX 79968 Office: 915-747-8470 rso@utep.edu mcaire@utep.edu <!--\n.carousel-caption {\n    display: block !important;\n}\n--> What is the responsible conduct of research program? The RCR training program promotes a campus wide environment of responsible conduct for research, complying with requirements from the University of Texas (UT) System, and various funding agencies, particularly NIH and NSF. How do you register for the CITI Training? Go to the CITI Support Website and follow the instructions given. First you will need to register a new account. Use your UTEP email address as your log-in and institutional email address. When creating a CITI Program account choose Selecting your Organization Affiliation , and choose \u201cUniversity of Texas at El Paso\u201d. Which Participating Institution should I select as a New User? Make sure to affiliate yourself to The \u201cUniversity of Texas at El Paso\u201d from the \u201cParticipating Institutions\u201d drop down menu. Hint : In the search box enter \u201cEl Paso\u201d and select University of Texas at El Paso from the list. Why am I required to take RCR Training if I do not have an active grant? If you do not have an active grant, but you are teaching or conducting research, or otherwise have involvement with research projects, you should take the Responsible Conduct in Research Training for \u201cAdministrators\u201d. How do I know what learner group to choose? There are several ways to select a learner group.\u00a0 Best option is to select the group closest to the research you are conducting.\u00a0 For subjects such as Biomedical Engineering, you could pick either Biomedical RCR or RCR for Engineers, although it is preferred to default to your home college/department. Learner groups by discipline include: Biomedical Social & Behavioral Research Physical Sciences Humanities Engineers Administrators Can I complete the training in several sessions? Yes. You can leave and return to the CITI Program website to finish any uncompleted modules. How often do I need to take the RCR course to keep my training current? UTEP has elected to keep each RCR training certificate current for three (3) years. What do I do if I have forgotten my CITI Program Username and Password? CITI Program has an automated username and password retrieval system available at \u201c I can\u2019t log in to my account \u201d.\u00a0 You may also contact CITI support at 888.529.5929 or via e-mail at support@citiprogram.org . What if I have already completed the training prior to being employed at UTEP? A trainee must affiliate with The \u201cUniversity of Texas at El Paso\u201d and enroll in and select a course that is the same or similar as to the one from the prior institution. Refer to \u201c How to add/change your affiliated institution or transfer completions \u201d. How can I obtain a copy of my completion certificate? To retrieve your completion certificate, refer to \u201c How do I access my Completion Report/Certificate \u201d. Where do I go to access more help and support with the CITI web application? Refer to the CITI Program Support page. What if my username does not allow me to register? Someone else may already have the same user name, so create a new one by adding 1, 2, or other characters to your user name to avoid duplication. You\u00a0may also use your UTEP email as a unique user name. Please contact us at utepresearchtraining@utep.edu for any questions or concerns regarding the UTEP-CITI compliance training requirements. <!--\n#myBtn {\n  display: none;\n  position: fixed;\n  bottom: 20px;\n  right: 30px;\n  z-index: 99;\n  font-size: 18px;\n  border: none;\n  outline: none;\n  background-color: #041e42;\n  color: white;\n  cursor: pointer;\n  padding: 15px;\n  border-radius: 4px;\n}\n\n#myBtn:hover {\n  background-color: #ff8200;\n}\n--> // <![CDATA[\n//Get the button\nvar mybutton = document.getElementById(\"myBtn\");\n\n// When the user scrolls down 20px from the top of the document, show the button\nwindow.onscroll = function() {scrollFunction()};\n\nfunction scrollFunction() {\n  if (document.body.scrollTop > 20 || document.documentElement.scrollTop > 20) {\n    mybutton.style.display = \"block\";\n  } else {\n    mybutton.style.display = \"none\";\n  }\n}\n\n// When the user clicks on the button, scroll to the top of the document\nfunction topFunction() {\n  document.body.scrollTop = 0;\n  document.documentElement.scrollTop = 0;\n}\n// ]]> <!--\nh1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6   {text-align: left;}\n\n\n.card {\n    height: 140px;\n    width: 100%; \n   /* width: 115px; */\n  /*  background: #e6843e;  */\n  /*  box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px lightgrey; */\n    padding: 2px;\n    border:  1px solid #0a1f4042;\n  /*  border-radius: 4px; */\n    margin: 5px;\n    text-align:center;\n   /* font-family: \"arial narrow\"; */\n    font-weight:bold;\n    font-size: 13px;\n    letter-spacing: -0.5px;\n}\n\n.card:hover {\n    border: #f28328 1px solid;\n    \n}\n--> // <![CDATA[\n$(document).ready(function() { \n            \n                $(\"h2\").css(\"text-align\", \"left\"); \n                \n                $(\"a#bluelink\").css(\"color\", \"#337ab7\"); \n                \n             $('#ShowFEATUREMSG').click(function() {\n          \n          //  Just in case\n          \n        });\n        \n\n        \n        });\n// ]]> <!--\nbody {\n    position: relative;\n}\n\n/*header bg fix*/\n@media (min-width:1250px ) and (max-width: 1364px){\n\t.head