dio Mountains Graduate Research Grant Research is not a transaction. It\u2019s a pursuit. The University Research Initiative (URI) invests in faculty whose ideas have the power to redefine what is possible. Each award fuels projects that push boundaries, connect disciplines, and expand the reach of UTEP\u2019s research enterprise. This is not generic seed funding. It\u2019s the ignition of a strategic investment in the next breakthrough, led by the faculty shaping tomorrow\u2019s knowledge landscape. Purpose Progress begins with those who are willing to imagine differently. URI helps faculty move from concept to proof, from early insight to evidence, from idea to impact . Every award recognizes the courage to innovate and the discipline to deliver. Faculty selected through URI demonstrate UTEP\u2019s commitment to research that not only advances discovery but also defines excellence. Vision Transform strong ideas into competitive research trajectories. Empower early- and mid-career faculty to lead innovation in their fields. Strengthen cross-college collaboration through shared purpose. Position UTEP for national recognition in scholarly and creative leadership. Designed for Momentum Award Amount: Up to $5,000 Application Deadline: Fall Funding Period: One year Eligibility: Full-time, research-active faculty Apply via: InfoReady Selection Priorities The Faculty Research Committee selects projects that demonstrate: Scholarly Significance. Strength of the idea and its potential to advance the applicant\u2019s discipline. Strategic Fit. Alignment with UTEP\u2019s research priorities, emerging focus areas, or national research agendas. Outcomes and Deliverables. Specific products expected within the one-year award period, such as manuscripts, performances, exhibitions, or data collection leading to a proposal. Pathway to External Funding. A realistic plan for leveraging URI outcomes into external applications or collaborative funding. Leadership Development. Evidence that the project will strengthen the PI\u2019s visibility, influence, or network within their field or across disciplines. Annual Cycle The URI Program opens in late summer. Applications are due mid-fall. Awards are announced, and funding is released in early spring. Each project runs for one year and concludes with a report that documents outcomes, data generated, partnerships formed, publications submitted, and planned external proposals. These reports become part of UTEP\u2019s collective story of discovery and competitiveness. The Work That Defines Us (Coming soon: profiles of URI-funded projects that shaped new fields, built new collaborations, and redefined possibilities.) Back to Internal Funding Opportunities <!--\n#myBtn {\n  display: none;\n  position: fixed;\n  bottom: 20px;\n  right: 30px;\n  z-index: 99;\n  font-size: 18px;\n  border: none;\n  outline: none;\n  background-color: #041e42;\n  color: white;\n  cursor: pointer;\n  padding: 15px;\n  border-radius: 4px;\n}\n\n#myBtn:hover {\n  background-color: #ff8200;\n}\n--> // <![CDATA[\n//Get the button\nvar mybutton = document.getElementById(\"myBtn\");\n\n// When the user scrolls down 20px from the top of the document, show the button\nwindow.onscroll = function() {scrollFunction()};\n\nfunction scrollFunction() {\n  if (document.body.scrollTop > 20 || document.documentElement.scrollTop > 20) {\n    mybutton.style.display = \"block\";\n  } else {\n    mybutton.style.display = \"none\";\n  }\n}\n\n// When the user clicks on the button, scroll to the top of the document\nfunction topFunction() {\n  document.body.scrollTop = 0;\n  document.documentElement.scrollTop = 0;\n}\n// ]]> <!--\nh1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6   {text-align: left;}\n\n\n.card {\n    height: 140px;\n    width: 100%; \n   /* width: 115px; */\n  /*  background: #e6843e;  */\n  /*  box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px lightgrey; */\n    padding: 2px;\n    border:  1px solid #0a1f4042;\n  /*  border-radius: 4px; */\n    margin: 5px;\n    text-align:center;\n   /* 