{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/research/proposal-development/proposal-development-process-and-timeline/", "title": "Proposal Development Process and Timeline", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search Home Proposal Development Research Development Research, Evaluation, and Assessment Services Interdisciplinary Research (IDR) Interdisciplinary Research Building (IDRB) ---------------- Business Center Research Administration Research Compliance and Regulatory Assurances Research Advancement Our Team Our Team Research Development Honorific Awards 2025 R&I Awards 2024 R&I Awards Early Career Awardees Pioneering Researcher Reception Proposal Development Proposal Development Process and Timeline Preparing for Your Submission External Review Meet a Program Officer Letters of Support and Commitment Limited Submissions Limited Submissions Find Funding Find Funding Early Career Faculty Support Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Proposal Development Research & Innovation Main Content Proposal Development Process and Timeline Contact Us Research Development is located in Kelly Hall, 7th floor, West Wing 2101 Sun Bowl Drive 500 W University Ave (general address) El Paso, TX 79968 research dev@utep.edu (General Inbox) <!--\n.carousel-caption {\n    display: block !important;\n}\n--> Services with suggested timelines Through a strategic proposal development process, our team works to make your proposals as competitive as possible. Our office provides a wide range of services to help you every step of the way. The earlier you solicit our services, the more support we can give you. To get started, submit a Notice of Intent. Once we receive your NOI, we can: Analyze Funding Opportunities (by appointment)\u2013 We can go through funding opportunities and conduct funding searches to help you find grants, determine your eligibility, and help you prep to write your proposal. Schedule a Discovery Meeting \u2013 We like to kick off the proposal development process with a discovery meeting to learn more about your proposal and research, answer your questions, and create a game plan. Perform Internal Review (two weeks) \u2013 Our Proposal Development team is comprised of writers and editors who can help you edit your proposal to ensure it is clear, effective, grammatically sound, and competitive. Draft Additional Documentation (four weeks) \u2013 Our team can also help review supporting documents, such as CVs, Bio sketches, letters of support and assist in drafting letters of support requiring signature from the VPR. Send for External Review (four weeks) \u2013 If submitted early enough, we can submit your proposal for external review, receiving feedback from subject matter leaders in the field to make your proposal more competitive. This is free of charge for all UTEP faculty. Submission \u2013 The UTEP Research Administration team submits proposals on your behalf and assists you with compliance and budgeting. Proposal Development Office Hours We invite you to stop by during our weekly office hours! Join us between 9 am and 10 am on Tuesdays and 1 pm and 2 pm on Wednesdays. Our office is on the 7th floor of Kelly Hall. Additional University Resources Compliance Budget Support Intellectual Property Graduate School Office of Student Fellowships and Awards Marketing & Communications University Career Center <!--\nh1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6   {text-align: left;}\n--> // <![CDATA[\n$(document