{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/research/research-relations/partnerships/", "title": "Partnerships", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search Home Research Relations and Strategy Research Development Interdisciplinary Research (IDR) Interdisciplinary Research Building (IDRB) ---------------- Business Center Research Administration Research Advancement Research Compliance and Regulatory Assurances Our Team Our Team Partnerships Partnerships Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Research Relations and Strategy Research & Innovation Main Content Partnerships: Driving Innovation and Excellence Contact Us Kelly Hall, 7th floor, West Wing 500 W University Ave El Paso, TX 79968 researchrelations@utep.edu <!--\n.carousel-caption {\n    display: block !important;\n}\n--> Our office is proud to collaborate with a diverse network of federal agencies, national laboratories, academic institutions, and industry leaders to drive transformative research and innovation. These strategic alliances allow us to address critical challenges in space technologies, AI-driven solutions, cybersecurity, advanced materials science, sustainable energy, and beyond. Together, we bridge academic excellence with real-world applications, delivering groundbreaking solutions while creating opportunities for students, researchers, and partners. Our partnerships exemplify our commitment to: Innovation: Developing transformative technologies that address critical societal and national challenges. Education and Workforce Development: Creating opportunities for students and researchers from diverse backgrounds. Global Collaboration: Strengthening partnerships that impact both national and international communities. Together, these partnerships underscore our shared commitment to leveraging expertise, resources, and vision to shape the future of research, discovery, and societal progress. By collaborating across federal agencies, national laboratories, and academic institutions, we are building a foundation for impactful innovation and leadership that transcends boundaries. Federal Partnerships Department of Defense (DoD) and National Security Agency (NSA): Contributing to initiatives that enhance the nation's leadership in semiconductor technology and cybersecurity. U.S. Space Force: Advancing research and workforce development in aerospace and defense sectors through the University Partnership Program. NASA Johnson Space Center: Establishing a presence at the Johnson Space Center to drive cutting-edge aerospace research and workforce training. Air Force Research Laboratory (AFRL): Developing materials and technologies critical to hypersonic applications to enhance national defense capabilities. National Laboratory Partnerships Los Alamos National Laboratory (LANL): Advancing research, education, and workforce development in critical areas, including nuclear material science and electronics for extreme environments. Sandia National Laboratories: Collaborating on initiatives such as climate change mitigation, electronics for extreme environments, and STEM workforce development. Pacific Northwest National Laboratory (PNNL): Expanding STEM opportunities for students and fostering collaborative innovation in national security and advanced technologies. Oak Ridge National Laboratory (ORNL): Engaging in joint research initiatives to advance scientific discovery and technological innovation in areas such as energy production, materials science, and high-performance computing. University and Research Collaborations ASPIRE Engineering Research Center: Partnering with institutions like Utah State University, Purdue University, and the University of Colorado - Boulder to promote global sustainability through electrified transportation and infrastructure. Cross-Border Collaborations: Engaging with universities in Chihuahua, Mexico, to address shared challenges in environmental sustainability, public health, and manufacturing technology. Note: This list highlights a selection of our key partnerships and collaborations, showcasing the breadth and diversity of our engagements; it is not an all-\u2002encompassing inventory. These partnerships continuously evolve as we explore new opportunities and initiatives to drive innovation, expand research, and address critical challenges. <!--\n#myBtn {\n  display: none;\n  position: fixed;\n  bottom: 20px;\n  right: 30px;\n  z-index: 99;\n  font-size: 18px;\n  border: none;\n  outline: none;\n  background-color: #041e42;\n  color: white;\n  cursor: pointer;\n  padding: 15px;\n  border-radius: 4px;\n}\n\n#myBtn:hover {\n  background-color: #ff8200;\n}\n--> <!--\nh1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6   {text-align: left;}\n\n.card {\n    height: 140px;\n    width: 100%; \n   /* width: 115px; */\n  /*  background: #e6843e;  */\n  /*  box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px lightgrey; */\n    padding: 2px;\n    border:  1px solid #0a1f4042;\n  /*  border-radius: 4px; */\n    margin: 5px;\n    text-align:center;\n   /* font-family: \"arial narrow\"; */\n    font-weight:bold;\n    font-size: 13px;\n    letter-spacing: -0.5px;\n}\n\n.card:hover {\n    border: #f28328 1px solid;\n    \n}\n--> // <![CDATA[\n//Get the button\nvar mybutton = document.getElementById(\"myBtn\");\n\n// When the user scrolls down 20px from the top of the document, show the button\nwindow.onscroll = function() {scrollFunction()};\n\nfunction scrollFunction() {\n  if (document.body.scrollTop > 20 || doc