{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/research/research-development/prop-dev/before-you-submit.html", "title": "Preparing for Your Submission", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search Home Research Development Research Relations and Strategy Interdisciplinary Research (IDR) Interdisciplinary Research Building (IDRB) Research, Evaluation, and Assessment Services ---------------- Business Center Research Administration Research Compliance and Regulatory Assurances Research Advancement Research Advancement Strategic Research Advancement Faculty Travel Incentive Program Limited Submissions Find Funding Notice of Intent Form Research, Evaluation, and Assessment Services Interdisciplinary Research (IDR) Indio Mountains Research Station Graduate Research Grant Proposal Development Proposal Development About Proposal Development Preparing for Your Submission Process and Timeline External Review Meet a Program Officer Letters of Support and Commitment Professional Development Professional Development Star @ UTEP Learning Opportunities Video Resources Events Resource Library Honorifics Honorific Awards Internal Funding Internal Funding Opportunities Funding Opportunities Limited Submissions Early Career Faculty Support Pilot Grant Program COB Seed Funding for Grant Submissions Program Liberal Arts Career Enhancement Award Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Research Development Research & Innovation Main Content Preparing for Your Submission Proposal Development <!--\n.carousel-caption {\n    display: block !important;\n}\n--> Identifying Opportunities There are various ways to assist you in identifying\u00a0funding opportunities: Weekly ResearchCalls bulletin - features funding opportunities from national agencies, foundations, and other organizations. Pivot We encourage you to navigate through our funding sources for a list of funding agencies. Lastly, we invite you to set up a consultation with us to discuss and search for opportunities that match your research goals. Meeting With Program Officers Many major funding agencies offer opportunities to meet with program officers who oversee specific awards. This is a great way to learn more about the funding opportunity and to get tips for your proposal. Some good questions to ask include: Does my proposal align with the agency\u2019s current priorities? What are common concerns/reasons for rejection you often see in proposals? Are there any new areas of interest within the agency? Events and Learning Opportunities R&I advertises numerous events and learning opportunities to help you with writing your proposal. Be on the lookout for our Events & Learning Opportunities bulletin and regular update s on our events page to stay up to date on helpful opportunities offered by us and some of the major funding agencies, including NSF, NIH, and more. Work With a Research Administrator Our team of research administrators can help you kick off your proposals by supporting you. Upon a Notice of Intent submission, one will be assigned to you. Connect with them and they can assist with: Creating checklists Developing appropriate budgets Obtaining and completing necessary forms To get started, contact our team at propdev@utep.edu . <!--\nh1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6   {text-align: left;}\n--> // <![CDATA[\n$(document).ready(function() { \n            \n                $(\"h2\").css(\"text-align\", \"left\"); \n                \n                $(\"