{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/research/research-development/professional-dev/faculty-travel-incentive-program.html", "title": "Faculty Travel Incentive Program", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search Home Research Development Research Relations and Strategy Interdisciplinary Research (IDR) Interdisciplinary Research Building (IDRB) Research, Evaluation, and Assessment Services ---------------- Business Center Research Administration Research Compliance and Regulatory Assurances Research Advancement Research Advancement Strategic Research Advancement Faculty Travel Incentive Program Limited Submissions Find Funding Notice of Intent Form Research, Evaluation, and Assessment Services Interdisciplinary Research (IDR) Indio Mountains Research Station Graduate Research Grant Proposal Development Proposal Development About Proposal Development Preparing for Your Submission Process and Timeline External Review Meet a Program Officer Letters of Support and Commitment Professional Development Professional Development Star @ UTEP Learning Opportunities Video Resources Events Resource Library Honorifics Honorific Awards Internal Funding Internal Funding Opportunities Funding Opportunities Limited Submissions Early Career Faculty Support Pilot Grant Program Business Seed Funding Program Liberal Arts Career Enhancement Award Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Research Development Research & Innovation Main Content FACULTY TRAVEL INCENTIVE PROGRAM Where opportunity meets preparation. Go to Infoready Explore the Portfolio Contact Us Research Development is located in Kelly Hall, 7th floor, West Wing 2101 Sun Bowl Drive 500 W University Ave (general address) El Paso, TX 79968 researchdev@utep.edu (General Inbox) Explore the Portfolio Quickly access your area of interest! Pilot Grant Program (PGP) University Research Institute (URI) Liberal Arts Career Enhancement Award Business Seed Program Faculty Travel Incentive Program Indio Mountains Graduate Research Grant <!--\n.carousel-caption {\n    display: block !important;\n}\n--> Connection drives discovery. The Faculty Travel Incentive Program (FTIP) helps UTEP researchers expand their reach, funding travel that leads to new ideas, collaborations, and proposals. Every trip represents a conversation that could change a career, a partnership that could redefine a field, or a presentation that could open the next door. FTIP isn\u2019t just travel support. It\u2019s strategic mobility, an investment in visibility, credibility, and future funding. Purpose FTIP supports faculty who take UTEP\u2019s story beyond the campus, those who meet program officers face-to-face, present new work to peers, and build networks that strengthen future grant submissions. The goal is simple: to help researchers connect with where ideas are shared, shaped, and funded. Vision Empower faculty to engage directly with funding agencies. Increase visibility of UTEP\u2019s research and creative excellence. Support travel that leads to new proposals and partnerships. Reward proactive research leadership. Designed for Impact Cycles: Spring, Summer, Fall Award Amount: Travel support for professional meetings, agency visits, or proposal development Eligibility: Full-time faculty (tenured, tenure-track, and research and clinical faculty) Apply via: InfoReady Selection Priorities Reviewers look for: Strategic Intent. The connection between the travel activity and an upcoming funding opportunity, collaboration, or proposal development. Institutional Benefit. Potential of travel opportunity to strengthen UTEP\u2019s visibility, research competitiveness, or participation in national networks. Preparation and Planning. Documentation of confirmed meetings, invitations, or presentation acceptances demonstrating purpose and readiness. Outcomes and Follow-Up. Defined post-travel goals such as proposal submission, partnership agreement, or manuscript development. Award Cycles Cycle Apply By Notification Travel Period Spring October Early December Jan\u2013Apr Summer February Early April May\u2013Aug Fall May Early July Sep\u2013Dec Annual Cycle The Faculty Travel Incentive Program (FTIP) has three (3) cycles. Refer to the Award Cycles table above for information on releases and notifications. Each project runs for one year and concludes with a report that documents outcomes, data generated, partnerships formed, publications submitted, and planned external proposals. These reports become part of UTEP\u2019s collective story of discovery and competitiveness. Conversations That Changed the Trajectory (Coming soon: highlights of faculty whose FTIP travel led to new grants, collaborations, and ideas that reached national audiences.) Back to Internal Funding Opportunities <!--\n#myBtn {\n  display: none;\n  position: fixed;\n  bottom: 20px;\n  right: 30px;\n  z-index: 99;\n  font-size: 18px;\n  border: none;\n  outline: none;\n  background-color: #041e42;\n  color: white;\n  cursor: pointer;\n  padding: 15px;\n  border-radius: 4px;\n}\n\n#myBtn:hover {\n  background-color: #ff8200;\n}\n--> <!--\nh1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6   {text-align: left;}\n\n.card {\n    height: 140px;\n    width: 100%; \n   /* width: 115px; */\n  /*  background: #e6843e;  */\n  /*  box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px lightgrey; */\n    padding: 2px;\n    border:  1px solid #0a1f4042;\n  /*  border-radius: 4px; */\n    margin: 5px;\n    text-align:center;\n   /* font-family: \"ari