    padding: 0;\n    }\n\n    .upcoming-event {\n        position: relative;\n        overflow: hidden;\n    }\n\n    .story {\n        margin: 0;\n        border: none;\n        box-shadow: none;\n        background: #fff;\n    }\n\n    .story img {\n        width: 100%;\n        height: auto;\n        max-height: 600px;\n        object-fit: cover;\n    }\n--> <!--\n.miners-competition {\n        font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\n        background-color: #F4F4F4;\n        color: #041E42;\n        margin: 0;\n        padding: 20px;\n        text-align: center;\n    }\n\n    .miners-competition h1 {\n        color: #FF8200;\n        font-size: 2.5em;\n        margin-bottom: 10px;\n    }\n\n    .miners-competition p {\n        font-size: 1.2em;\n        margin: 10px 0 20px;\n        line-height: 1.5;\n    }\n\n    .miners-competition .event-details {\n        font-size: 1.2em;\n        font-weight: bold;\n        margin-bottom: 20px;\n    }\n\n    .miners-competition .cta {\n        margin-top: 20px;\n    }\n\n    .miners-competition .cta a {\n        display: inline-block;\n        padding: 15px 30px;\n        color: #fff;\n        background-color: #FF8200; /* Orange button */\n        border-radius: 5px;\n        text-decoration: none;\n        font-weight: bold;\n        font-size: 1.2em;\n        margin: 10px;\n        transition: transform 0.3s, background-color 0.3s; /* Smooth hover animation */\n    }\n\n    .miners-competition .cta a:hover {\n        background-color: #e76f00; /* Slightly darker orange on hover */\n        transform: scale(1.05); /* Slight zoom on hover */\n    }\n--> Miner Entrepreneurship Talks Learn from Local Visionaries, Lead with Impact Miner Entrepreneurship Talks is a hands-on workshop series where successful local founders and leaders share practical lessons from their own journeys. This Fall 2025, you\u2019ll learn how creativity, culture, leadership, and community impact can shape your entrepreneurial mindset across four interactive sessions. <!--\nbody {\n            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\n            margin: 0;\n            padding: 0;\n            background: #f0f0f5;\n            color: #333;\n        }\n        .container {\n            width: 90%;\n            max-width: 1200px;\n            margin: 0 auto;\n            padding: 20px;\n        }\n        header {\n            background: #ff8200;\n            color: #fff;\n            padding: 20px;\n            border-radius: 8px;\n            text-align: center;\n        }\n        header h1 {\n            margin: 0;\n        }\n        .intro {\n            background: #ffffff;\n            border-radius: 8px;\n            padding: 20px;\n            box-shadow: 0 4px 10px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);\n            margin: 20px 0;\n            text-align: center;\n        }\n        .intro p {\n            line-height: 1.6;\n            margin: 0;\n        }\n        .section {\n            margin: 20px 0;\n            background: #ffffff;\n            border-radius: 8px;\n            padding: 20px;\n            box-shadow: 0 4px 10px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);\n            display: flex;\n            align-items: center;\n            gap: 20px;\n            flex-wrap: wrap;\n        }\n        .section img {\n            flex: 1;\n            border-radius: 8px;\n            max-width: 50%;\n            height: auto;\n        }\n        .section-content {\n            flex: 2;\n        }\n        .section h2 {\n            border-bottom: 4px solid #ff8200;\n            padding-bottom: 10px;\n            margin-bottom: 15px;\n        }\n        .section p {\n            line-height: 1.6;\n        }\n        .cta {\n            text-align: center;\n            margin: 30px 0;\n        }\n        .cta a {\n            display: inline-block;\n            padding: 15px 25px;\n            color: #ffffff;\n            background-color: #ff8200;\n            border-radius: 5px;\n            text-decoration: none;\n            font-weight: bold;\n            transition: background-color 0.3s;\n        }\n        .cta a:hover {\n            background-color: #e76f00;\n        }\n--> 1: Sandra Arlette Morales - LOB Club September 17, 2:00-3:00 PM Union East - Andesite 102B Join us for the first session of Miner Entrepreneurship Talks \u2014 a fireside chat series where local entrepreneurs share their real-world experiences to inspire and empower students. Our first guest is Sandra Arlette Morales, a creative entrepreneur with over 25 years of experience leading purpose-driven projects around the world. She\u2019s the Founder of The League of Business, Editor-in-Chief of Real Entrepreneurs Magazine & Podcast, and a former Cultural Attach\u00e9 with a strong background in international business and diplomacy. \ud83d\udd39 What to Expect: Hear how Sandra built a global career rooted in creativity, purpose, and leadership Learn actionable advice on networking, personal branding, and launching ideas Ask your own questions in an open, student-centered conversation Don\u2019t miss the opportunity to connect and grow! 2: Patrick Gabaldon - Gabaldon Art September 30, 2:00-3:00 PM Union East - Cactus Flower 102C Meet Patrick Gabaldon artist, attorney, and creative entrepreneur! - POSTPONED - We'll be announcing the new date soon. Stay tuned! 3: Chelsie Evaldi - Chuco Relic October 15, 2:00-3:00 PM Union East - Cactus Flower 102C Join us for the third session of Entrepreneurship Talks \u2014 a fireside chat series where local entrepreneurs share their real-world experiences to inspire and empower students. Our next guest is Chelsie Evaldi, founder of Chuco Relic, a bold and colorful love letter to border culture. Growing up crossing the bridge between Mexico and the U.S., Chelsie was inspired to create a space that celebrates the orgullo, flavor, and identity of life on the frontera. Through Chuco Relic, she has built a Latina-owned, community-powered brand that supports over 20 local artists and prints most of its vibrant tees, totes, stickers, and prints right here in El Paso. \ud83d\udd39 What to Expect: Learn how Chelsie turned cultural pride into a successful retail brand and creative platform Gain insights on starting a business rooted in identity, collaboration, and local impact Join a candid conversation about entrepreneurship, representation, and staying true to your roots Celebrate borderland culture and hear how passion for community can grow into a thriving business! 4: Ricardo Mora - ELP Chamber October 28, 2:00-3:00 PM Union East - Cactus Flower 102C Join us for the final session of Entrepreneurship Talks \u2014 a fireside chat series where local entrepreneurs share their real-world experiences to inspire and empower students. We\u2019re honored to close our series with Ricardo Mora, a visionary leader and the current CEO of the El Paso Chamber. With a career spanning real estate, telecommunications, venture capital, and hospitality, Ricardo now dedicates his work to driving innovation, cross-border collaboration, and economic growth throughout the Borderplex region. His deep understanding of the unique dynamics between El Paso, Las Cruces, and Ciudad Ju\u00e1rez guides his efforts to build a more connected, competitive, and forward-thinking community. \ud83d\udd39 What to Expect: Hear how Ricardo has navigated diverse industries and now leads regional efforts for economic and social impact Learn about cross-sector leadership, community development, and staying purpose-driven in every venture Take part in a meaningful conversation about growth, collaboration, and building a stronger future for the region We\u2019re grateful to end the series with a leader who truly embodies the spirit of entrepreneurship, service, and regional pride. Join us! <!--\n.btn-primary {\n\t\t\tbackground-color: #ff8200; \n\t\t\tcolor: white;\n\t\t\tborder: none;\n\t\t\tborder-radius: 5px;\n\t\t\tpadding: 10px 20px;\n\t\t\tfont-size: 14px;\n\t\t\tfont-weight: bold;\n\t\t\ttext-align: center;\n