 Training FAQs Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Research Protections Research & Innovation Main Content Controlled Unclassified Information CUI Training Contact Us Mario E. Caire, Ph.D. Research Security Officer Kelly Hall, 4th floor, North Wing 500 W University Ave El Paso, TX 79968 Office: 915-747-8470 rso@utep.edu mcaire@utep.edu <!--\n.carousel-caption {\n    display: block !important;\n}\n--> Controlled Unclassified Information Training All personnel interacting with or otherwise handling Controlled Unclassified Information (CUI) for official University business, whether appointed, funded, or not, including PI\u2019s, CoPI\u2019s, senior personnel, student researchers, research administrators, etc., must take the below training before working with CUI. ( Note: this policy also applies to non-research staff, personnel, students with a lawful government purpose to access CUI. ) It is the responsibility of the Principal Investigator of an award to ensure all relevant personnel on a project meet training requirements and submit training certificates to the Information Security Office (ISO). Each training module takes about 1 hour to complete, and must be renewed annually for as long as access to CUI is required. Training Modules DoD Mandatory Controlled Unclassified Information (CUI) Training Insider Threat Awareness Phishing & Social Engineering Training: Virtual Communication Awareness Before handling CUI in any form, follow these steps to take the training modules and submit certificates: Click each link to be redirected to the training web page. Follow the steps on the training page to launch the training module. Upon completion of the training module , enter your first and last name on the certificate generation page. Print the certificate and save it to a secure location on your system. Best practice is to keep all training certificates in a compliance folder. After saving the certificate, email a copy to security@utep.edu . You will then receive an acknowledgement email from ISO\u00a0certifying completion of the modules. After completing the training, consult with the Office for Research Protections (ORP) and ISO to ensure the environment in which you plan to work is fully compliant with CUI law, regulation, and policy. For more information or assistance on specific training requirements, contact either of the following: security@utep.edu rso@utep.edu <!--\n#myBtn {\n  display: none;\n  position: fixed;\n  bottom: 20px;\n  right: 30px;\n  z-index: 99;\n  font-size: 18px;\n  border: none;\n  outline: none;\n  background-color: #041e42;\n  color: white;\n  cursor: pointer;\n  padding: 15px;\n  border-radius: 4px;\n}\n\n#myBtn:hover {\n  background-color: #ff8200;\n}\n--> // <![CDATA[\n//Get the button\nvar mybutton = document.getElementById(\"myBtn\");\n\n// When the user scrolls down 20px from the top of the document, show the button\nwindow.onscroll = function() {scrollFunction()};\n\nfunction scrollFunction() {\n  if (document.body.scrollTop > 20 || document.documentElement.scrollTop > 20) {\n    mybutton.style.display = \"block\";\n  } else {\n    mybutton.style.display = \"none\";\n  }\n}\n\n// When the user clicks on the button, scroll to the top of the document\nfunction topFunction() {\n  document.body.scrollTop = 0;\n  document.documentElement.scrollTop = 0;\n}\n// ]]> <!--\nh1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6   {text-align: left;}\n\n\n.card {\n    height: 140px;\n    width: 100%; \n   /* width: 115px; */\n  /*  background: #e6843e;  */\n  /*  box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px lightgrey; */\n    padding: 2px;\n    border:  1px solid #0a1f4042;\n  /*  border-radius: 4px; */\n    margin: 5px;\n    text-align:center;\n   /* font-family: \"arial narrow\"; */\n    font-weight:bold;\n    font-size: 13px;\n    lette