{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/keck/driveam/courses.html", "title": "DRIVE AM Trainings", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About Contact Us Faculty Global Test Artifact Global Test Artifact Drive AM DRIVE AM DRIVE AM Trainings Research Research Highlights Publications Patents Journal Economic Development Design Entrepreneurial Ventures Engineering Entrepreneurship Services Services Facilities America Makes Laboratory Binder Jetting Cell Culture (Tissue Engineering) Chemistry and Metallography CNC Machining and Soft Tooling Mechanical Testing Metals Metrology and Characterization Polymer Extrusion Polymers Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support W.M. KECK CENTER FOR 3D INNOVATION Main Content UTEP W.M. KECK CENTER FOR 3D INNOVATION DRIVE AM UTEP W.M. KECK CENTER FOR 3D INNOVATION DRIVE AM DRIVE AM Trainings Available Trainings Forums Smart Courses Tools Past Courses Testimonials <!--\nbody {\n      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\n      line-height: 1.6;\n      margin: 0;\n      padding: 0;\n    }\n\n    .section {\n      display: flex;\n      justify-content: space-between;\n      align-items: center;\n      padding: 20px;\n      border-bottom: 1px solid #ccc;\n    }\n\n    .section:nth-child(even) {\n      flex-direction: row-reverse; /* optional: alternates picture left/right */\n    }\n\n    .text {\n      flex: 2;\n      padding: 10px;\n    }\n\n    .image {\n      flex: 1;\n      padding: 10px;\n    }\n\n    .image img {\n      max-width: 100%;\n      border-radius: 10px;\n    }\n\n    .final-text {\n      padding: 30px;\n      text-align: center;\n      font-size: 1.2em;\n    }\n--> Introduction to Industrial AM: MEX and LPBF 3-Day Virtual Training 50 spots This course will: Identify the seven process categories of Additive Manufacturing (AM) Understand the AM workflow (design, fabrication, post processing, etc.) Learn the benefits and limitations of AM Understand reverse engineering and 3D scanning basics Identify the major components of a Stratasys Fortus 900 mc and have a general understanding of the working principles of the machine Identify the major components of an EOS M290 industrial printer and have a general understanding of the working principle of the machine Introduction to AM Workflow 3-Day In-Person Training 20 spots This course will: Identify the seven process categories of Additive Manufacturing (AM) Understand the AM workflow (design, fabrication, etc.) Recognize the limitations of AM Design parts using Computer Aided Design (CAD) Prepare parts for printing using slicing software Apply concepts to a final project for evaluation Engineering Drawing Interpretation 3-Day Virtual Training 50 spots This course will: Review fundamental concepts of engineering drawings and Technical Data Packages (TDPs) Interpret distribution statements, configuration management principles, and common elements in 2D/3D drawings Apply standards for surface texture, symbology, dimensioning, and tolerancing Recognize and interpret fasteners, welding symbols, and related features Understand engineering involvement in technical data acquisition Material Extrusion Foundation 3-Day In-Person Training 20 spots This course will: Design a part for fabrication using material extrusion List the material extrusion processing parameters that have an impact on fabrication and part outputsIdentify the major components of a material extrusion AM machine Explain the working principle of material extrusion AM Identify post processing techniques for a particular application Recognize opportunities for machine maintenance and fabrication troubleshooting LAser Powder Bed Fusion Foundation 3-Day In-Person Training 10 spots This course will: Identify the differences between PBF, LPBF vs EBPBF and the ability to explain working principle of LPBF Demonstrate the capability to design for AM (DfAM) LPBF Metals Ability to identify and employ software packages used for pre-processing (STL healing, orientation, part duplication, labeling, support generation) Understand the commonalities for performing machine setups on different LPBF OEM/vendors Ability to perform setup and maintain LPBF equipment using best industry practices Show understanding of powder-laser (material-energy source) interaction; physical phenomena and effects on the LPBF process (print-wise, metallurgically, material properties) Understand effects of process variables such as laser power, velocity, scanning strategy, shielding gas flow, etc. To schedule a training session, please contact: Maria Estrada \u2013 mfestrada3@utep.edu Our team will guide you through course selection, participant registration, and logistics. Trainings can also be customized to meet specific organizational needs for an additional fee. DRIVE AM Forums The DRIVE AM Forum hosted by Discord is a dedicated platform for sharing and disseminating information related to additive manufacturing. This space was created to foster collaboration, knowledge sharing, and community engagement within the realm of 3D printing. Here, you can not only resolve your doubts but also find valuable and updated information about laser powder bed fusion, material extrusion, and the seven process categories. Join us to enjoy all the content. Join the forum now! https://discord.gg/9wGcaN8xfx What can you expect? General forum view Main forum features Smart Courses Tools Hello! Thanks for registering to the DRIVE AM Smart Courses. In this page, you'll find how to register to Confluence, how to access the Smart Course you registered for and any additional information you might need in order to make this course easy to navigate. Creating a confluence account 1. After registering on the specific Smart Course QuestionPro, you'll receive the following message: \"After completing registration, anticipate receiving the link to access the training within 2-3 business days. This link will provide with direct entry to the training session. Please be patient as we process your registration.\" QuestionPro registration 2. On the secondary email you provided you'll receive an invitation to join Confluence, where you'll accept the invite and create an account using the personal email you provided. Confluence invite Accessing the Smart Course Option 1 After registering and signing in on Confluence, you will receive an email that you have been assigned to a course. Click on the Visit the course link and it should take you to the course. Accessing through email invite Option 2 You can also access it by logging in directly at https://driveam.atlassian.net/wiki/home . Once logged in, go to the top bar, click on \"Apps,\" and then select the \"Courses\" tab. Accessing through DRIVE AM Confluence site Frequently asked Questions Where do I sign in? Visit https://driveam.atlassian.net/wiki/home , and in the top left corner, you'll see an icon where you can sign in. Once signed in, you'll know you're logged in if you see an icon with your initials and a tag that says \"Guest.\" Where to sign in on Confluence How do I know if im on the correct space? To verify you're in the correct space, the screen should display the course name and a play icon to access the content. Smart Courses home page Is my progress getting marked as I take the course? Yes, t o confirm that your progress is being tracked, the tab of the module you've completed will turn grey compared to the other modules. Display of course How many days do 