ustry but also to national and international clientele. Visualization of your final product has never been easier. We can create a help create a CAD model for your design along with various manufacturing techniques and testing to make your ideas become a reality. Design Design from Scratch We can create a 3D CAD model using 2D drawings or provide one-on-one guidance with our engineers to help you get started in the manufacturing process. Reverse Engineering / 3D Scan / CT Data Extraction These methods are ideal when only a physical version of your part is available. Industrial grade 8-axis Scanner by FARO 3D CAD or STL file delivery Inspection (Physical part vs CAD model) STL file creation using CT scan data Manufacturing Additive Manufacturing Allows for the creation of complex, customized, and intricate structures with a wide range of materials. Injection Molding Method utilied when a working prototype is needed with materials that will mimic the final product. Post-Processing Various processes are available to give your part a final touch, enhancing visual appeal and/or mechanical properties Machining, painting, sealing, electroplating, and dyeing Ultrasonic metal powder removal Testing Environmental Testing Method that utilizes testing chambers for exposure to UV light, humidity, chemicals, and temperature fluctuations. Mechanical Testing Testing that utilizes top-of-the-line equipment for various strength and tension realted insight Tests tensile, compression, impact, flexural, and cyclical (Axial+Torsional) Material property characterization including viscosity and hardness Characterization Microscopy Optical and scanning electroin microscopy (SEM) available Performed by state-of-the-art equipment for characterizing polymers, ceramics, and metal materials. Metrology 3D measurement technology with optical and touch probe sensors to validate printed parts. Education and Training Qualified personnel with approximately 15 years of experience in 3D printing (or Additive Manufacturing) are at your service. We provide industrial-grade equipment and a vast variety of materials for all your application needs. Vat Photopolymerization (Resin) Provides outstanding translucent parts and great resolution for small features. Max build capacity: 20 x 20 x 24in. Materials: WaterShed XC 11122 Somos NeXt Accura SL5530 Origin Materials Somos Perform Somos NanoForm 15120 Somos 9120 Prototherm 12120 ProtoCast AF 19120 FormLabs Resins Material Extrusion (Plastic) Excellent for tough applications which may require high temperature and impact resistant materials. Max build capacity: 36 x 24 x 36 in. Materials: ABS PC ULTEM 9085 Antero ABSi PC-ABS PC-ISO TPU ABS-ESD7 Nylon ULTEM 1010 Custom Powder Bed Fusion (Metal) Ideal for applications requiring high-strength and corrosion resistant materials like aerospace, biomedical, or automotive. Max build capacity: (EOS) 7.7 x 7.7 x 13in. (Renishaw) 5 x 5 x 3in (Aconity) 9.8 x 9.8 x 12in Materials: Ti6Al4V Inconel 625 Tool Steel Alsi12Mg Ti6Al4V ELI Inconel 718 Stainless Steel 316L Alsi7Mg Cobalt-Chromium Maraging Steel ALsi10Mg AlSi9Cu3 Binder Jetting (Metal) Capable of producing sand casting molds, high strength metal or ceramic parts. Max build capacity: 15.7 x 9.8 x 9.8 in. (Zcorp) 8 x 10 x 8in. Materials: Stainless Steel Iron Sand Inconel 625 Inconel 718 Cobalt-Chromium Tungsten Material Jetting Can provide prints with embedded colors, elastic materials, or textures. Max build capacity: (Stratasys) 5.5 x 7.8 x 7.4in. Materials: VeroUltra Elastico Digital ABS 1. Compile Information Gather information such as Drawing files (If applicable) CAD model (If applicable) Quantity Process and Material selection Special instructions or any of your related questions. 2. Send in Your Information Email us at wmkeckcenter@utep.edu with your information. 3. Payment A quote will be provided to you within 24 hours via email. Credit cards or purchase orders are welcome. Phone: (915) 747 - 6631 <!--\n    .accWrapper > 