{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/research/idrb/resources/idrb-visualization-lab.html", "title": "IDRB Visualization Lab", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search Home Interdisciplinary Research Building (IDRB) Interdisciplinary Research (IDR) Proposal Development Research Development Research, Evaluation, and Assessment Services ---------------- Business Center Research Administration Research Advancement Research Compliance and Regulatory Assurances About Vision, Mission, and Guiding Principles People Teams at IDRB IDRB Management Resources Space Reservations Space Reservations (Restricted Areas) Visualization Lab Interactive Collaboration Lab R&I Home Research & Innovation Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Interdisciplinary Research Building (IDRB) Research & Innovation Main Content Interdisciplinary Research Building (IDRB) Visualization Lab <!--\n.carousel-caption {\n    display: block !important;\n}\n--> Spaces Available for Reservation Visualization Wall The Visualization Lab is available for researchers, faculty and professional staff that require an ultra-high resolution display surface geared for Scientific Exploratory Research and Collaboration. Purpose: Allow Researchers to visualize and explore large complex data sets. Provides collaborating research teams to share and display results. Facilitate decision making collaborations for High-Profile UTEP Administrative Presentations that require sharing and analysis of data with local and external organizations/decision-makers. Specs: Planar 4x3 100 million Pixel Ultra-High Resolution Visualization Tile System. Meeting Canvas 3.0 is a software windowing platform that enables multidisciplinary collaboration, research and data-driven decision making. Allows wired, wireless and networked connected sources One Single-Click Wireless Presentation and Collaboration System allowing up to eight sources to be displayed Rack-Mounted Silverdraft Demon Workstation, One Intel Xeon Gold 6246R CPU, 92GB RAM, Four Nvidia RTX 8000 GPUs, Nvidia SYNC II, 10GB NIC 1080P PTZ Camera Audio/Video Conferencing System for External Collaborative Meetings Ceiling Beamforming Microphones and Speakers TGX High Performance Remote Desktop Software TGX\u2019s low latency, like-local performance, even at 4K resolution, makes it the ideal remote desktop for high-end graphics workstations and video applications. Allows for Distributed Visualizations across campus/world. Image Quality: TGX delivers sharp, non-distorted images that do not lose pixels or even tear. High Resolution: Work remotely in resolutions at 4K or higher. Real-Time Response: Experience consistent, real-time keyboard and mouse response. Render Node The High-Performance Render Node is available for Researchers that require specific visualization-intensive software to be able to display high-resolution scientific data models on the Visualization Wall. Purpose: Allow Installation of resource intensive visualization software tools for the study and exploration of scientific datasets. Specs: Rack-Mounted Silverdraft Demon Workstation, Two Intel Xeon Gold 6246R Processor, 16 Cores, 32 Threads, 3.4 - 4.1 Ghz, 192GB RAM Two 512 SSDs for Dual-Boot OS (Windows 10, Redhat Linux) 2TB SSD for Application Storage Four NVIDIA Quadro RTX 8000 48GB GDDR6 10GB Network Interface Card Control Desk Microsoft Surface Tablet Control Station. Purpose: Control and display of content and sources on Meeting Canvas. Reservations Capacity: 30 Location: IDRB 2.215 No food or drinks allowed. The IDRB Visualization Lab is available to research related encounters where users are actually in need of the power/technology of the machines in this space. If you want to reserve this space, please click on the button below to make the request. CALENDAR/RESERVATIONS More Pictures <!--\nh1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6   {text-align: left;}\n--> // <![CDATA[\n$(document).ready(function() { \n               /* Moves H2 headers to the left  */\n                $(\"h2\").css(\"text-align\", \"left\"); \n                /* Colors links with blue  */\n                $(\"a#bluelink\").css(\"color\", \"#337ab7\"); \n        \n        });\n// ]]> <!--\nbody {\n    position: relative;\n}\n\n/*header bg fix*/\n@media (min-width:1250px ) and (max-width: 1364px){\n\t.headerContainer {\n\t    width: 100%;\n\t}\n}\n/*Carousel FW*/\n#container + .container {\n\tmax-width: none !important;\n\twidth: auto!important;\n}\n.slide-transfer {\n    display:none!important;\n}\n.video-wrapper {\n\tmax-height: none !important;\n}\n.carousel-caption {\n\tdisplay: none;\n}\n.slide-transfer {\n\tdisplay: none;\n}\n/*FullWidthSection*/\n.fw-section {\n\tpadding-top: 40px;\n\tpadding-bottom: 60px;\n}\n.sectionAnchor {\n    padding-top:135px;\n    margin-top:-135px;\n}\n.fw-section h2 {\n\ttext-align: center;\n}\n.fw-section:after {\n\tclear: both;\n}\n.container-narrow {\n\tmax-width: 800px;\n}\n.row {\n\tmargin-left: 0;\n\tmargin-right: 0;\n}\n@media (max-width: 991px){\n    .col-md-4 {\n        width:100%;\n    }\n}\n/*Gray Bg Section*/\n.background-gray {\n\tbackground-color: #f2f2f2;\n}\n/*Blue Bg Section*/\n.background-blue {\n\tbackground-color: #041E42;\n\tcolor: #fff;\n}\n.background-blue h2 {\n\tcolor: #fff;\n}\n.background-blue .btn-primary, .background-blue a.btn-primary {\n    background-color: #FF8200;\n}\n.background-blue .btn-primary:hover, .background-blue .btn-primary:focus, .background-blue a.bt