l on Tuesdays and Wednesdays, where a member of the Proposal Development Team will be available to provide you with the necessary support. F&A Rates Effective Period Rate (%) Location Applicable To 09/01/2022 - 08/31/2025 53.50 On Campus Organized Research 09/01/2020 - 08/31/2025 52 On Campus Instruction 09/01/2020 - 08/31/2025 35 On Campus Other Sponsored Activities 09/01/2020 - 08/31/2025 26 Off-campus All Programs 09/01/2025 - Until Amended Use same rates & conditions as those cited for fiscal year ending Aug 31, 2025 For more information regarding F&A Rates please go to Office of Sponsored Project's Post Award page! Close Research Development is dedicated to equipping faculty with the essential skills for successful proposal development. An expanding collection of resources offers comprehensive insights and practical guidance on every aspect of the proposal process. Explore the video content below for valuable insights, guidance on navigating our services and understanding various funding mechanisms. Exploring Proposal Development Services Learn more about the services offered to faculty members by Research & Innovations Research Development. Explore processes, policies, tools, and resources available to faculty who are seeking grant funding. (Search for the video in the player below) Navigating Pivot-RP to Find Funding Opportunities Master the use of PIVOT to uncover funding opportunities that align with your research interests. Learn to utilize advanced search features, track relevant calls, and set alerts so you never miss a potential funding opportunity. (Search for the video in the player below) NSF Career Award A short, high-level, overview of the National Science Foundation\u2019s Faculty Early Career Development Program, including, purpose of the award, award amount, covered directorates, eligibility, and significant items. (Search for the video in the player below) Deconstructing a Funding Announcement Learn about the various ways funding agencies refer