{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/research/pave/about/about-pave-program.html", "title": "Introducing the PAVE Program", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search Home Post Approval Verification and Education (PAVE) ---------------- Business Center Research Advancement Research Compliance and Regulatory Assurances Research Advancement About PAVE Introducing the PAVE Program Staff and Contact Information Meet the Team Support Offices Human Subjects Research (IRB) Institutional Animal Care and Use Program (IACUP) Institutional Biosafety Committee (IBC) Dual Use Research of Concern - PEPP Laboratory Animal Resources Center (LARC) Post Approval Verification and Education (PAVE) Research Compliance Research Protections Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Post Approval Verification and Education (PAVE) Research & Innovation Main Content Introducing the PAVE Program Contact Us Administration Building 2101 Sun Bowl Drive 500 W University Ave (general address) El Paso, TX 79968 pave@utep.edu <!--\n.carousel-caption {\n    display: block !important;\n}\n--> Introducing the Post Approval Verification and Education (PAVE) office within Research & Innovation (R&I)! PAVE\u2019s primary goal is to foster partnership \u2013 between UTEP and its researchers, funding and regulatory agencies, and the public by assisting researchers to stay in compliance with approved protocols, policies, regulations, and by working to promote best research practices. Currently, the PAVE office supports research involving human subjects, animals, and recombinant DNA research by verifying through observation and documentation comparison, an accurate and consistent protocol performance conducted in accordance with the University of Texas at El Paso\u2019s (UTEP) Institutional Review Board (IRB), Biosafety (IBC), Animal Use and Care Committees (IACUC) - approved protocol and federal regulations. If observed research activities are deemed non-compliant, the PAVE office will work alongside the PI and research team to resolve the deficiency and get back into compliance in a quick and efficient manner to ensure that research is not delayed or compromised. Benefits of PAVE Prospectively identify potential issues of non-compliance Compliance Assistance, to include training and continuing Review, inspections, and support for internal or external audits Protocol and procedural guidance PAVE reviews may be initiated for the following reasons: Higher than minimal risk studies Random selection The PI or PI\u2019s department may wish to have research studies reviewed proactively Other reasons, such as risk and safety. PI request to initiate, please visit: : https://pave-scheduling.questionpro.com the PAVE monitoring process: If a PAVE review is initiated, the PI will receive notification of a PAVE visit via email to the Principal Investigator (PI) and Faculty Sponsor (if the PI is a student). The PAVE office will work with the PI to establish a PAVE review time within thirty (30) days of initial contact. Remember : The goal of post-approval verification and education is not to \u201ccatch\u201d you doing something you aren\u2019t supposed to be doing. The goal is to verify that research is being conducted in a manner\u202fthat meets\u202ffederal regulations and university policy by assisting researchers\u202fin identifying and correcting\u202fany deficiencies. We work together to keep you in compliance! Your feedback about PAVE is important and we invite you to share your experiences, opinions, and concerns, by visiting : https://pave-scheduling.questionpro.com . <!--\nh1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6   {text-align: left;}\n--> // <![CDATA[\n$(document).ready(function() { \n            \n                $(\"h2\").css(\"text-align\", \"left\"); \n                \n                $(\"a#bluelink\").css(\"color\", \"#337ab7\"); \n        \n        });\n// ]]> <!--\nbody {\n    position: relative;\n}\n\n/*header bg fix*/\n@media (min-width:1250px ) and (max-width: 1364px){\n\t.headerContainer {\n\t    width: 100%;\n\t}\n}\n/*Carousel FW*/\n#container + .container {\n\tmax-width: none !important;\n\twidth: auto!important;\n}\n.slide-transfer {\n    display:none!important;\n}\n.video-wrapper {\n\tmax-height: none !important;\n}\n.carousel-caption {\n\tdisplay: none;\n}\n.slide-transfer {\n\tdisplay: none;\n}\n/*FullWidthSection*/\n.fw-section {\n\tpadding-top: 40px;\n\tpadding-bottom: 60px;\n}\n.sectionAnchor {\n    padding-top:135px;\n    margin-top:-135px;\n}\n.fw-section h2 {\n\ttext-align: center;\n}\n.fw-section:after {\n\tclear: both;\n}\n.container-narrow {\n\tmax-width: 800px;\n}\n.row {\n\tmargin-left: 0;\n\tmargin-right: 0;\n}\n@media (max-width: 991px){\n    .col-md-4 {\n        width:100%;\n    }\n}\n/*Gray Bg Section*/\n.background-gray {\n\tbackground-color: #f2f2f2;\n}\n/*Blue Bg Section*/\n.background-blue {\n\tbackground-color: #041E42;\n\tcolor: #fff;\n}\n.background-blue h2 {\n\tcolor: #fff;\n}\n.background-blue .btn-primary, .background-blue a.btn-primary {\n    background-color: #FF8200;\n}\n.background-blue .btn-primary:hover, .background-blue .btn-primary:focus, .background-blue a.btn-primary:hover, .background-blue a.btn-primary:focus {\n    color: #041b3c;\n    background-color: #ddd;\n}\n/*flex*/\n.highligtsWrapper {\n    display: flex;\n    display: -webkit-flex;\n    flex-wrap: wrap;\n}\n.highligtsWrapper .well {\n\tbox-shadow:0px 2px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);-webk