{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/research/research-at-utep/", "title": "Research at UTEP", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About About Research & Innovation Our Units Business Center Research Administration Research Compliance and Regulatory Assurances Research Advancement For Researchers Events Expertise Connector Explore Our Services Find Funding Interdisciplinary Research (IDR) Office of Technology Commercialization Policies Research News Research Protections Research & Sponsored Projects Council Submit an NOI - VPN University Research Institute (URI) For Prospective Faculty Research at UTEP For Industry/Partners Economic Development Office Office of Technology Commercialization Research Relations and Strategy Research Centers Major Research Centers Events Events Resource Library Learning Opportunities Video Resources Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Research & Innovation Main Content Research at UTEP UTEP is home to a diverse and accomplished array of researchers who, through our high-quality facilities and research, engage in a wide range of projects that support our community, our campus, and the world beyond. With nine colleges and schools, UTEP faculty and students conduct research in areas like engineering, science, business, education, humanities, arts, fine arts, and social sciences. As the only open-access R1 research university in the United States, you can thrive as a researcher when you pick UTEP <!--\n.carousel-caption {\n    display: block !important;\n}\n--> Woody L. Hunt College of Business Faculty members within the Hunt College of Business make an everyday impact with their research in economics, marketing, finance, and real estate. Utilizing UTEP\u2019s unique location along the U.S.-Mexico border, you have the opportunity to engage in hands-on trade research and make impact on everyday imports, exports, and the efficiency of each. The Hunt College of Business is also home to the 6th most cited real estate researcher in the world. You\u2019ll be joining a dedicated and vibrant community of passionate faculty, students, and staff. College of Business College of Education Researchers within UTEP\u2019s College of Education conduct research impacting students at every grade level, from Pre-K to doctoral level. With an eye for diversity and supporting Spanish-speaking students, your work can have a direct impact on the community UTEP serves. Specializations within the college also include higher education, educational policy, administration, and mental health counseling. College of Education College of Engineering From biomedical engineering and additive manufacturing to advancing the field of aerospace and defense engineering, faculty at UTEP\u2019s College of Engineering make waves globally with their research. With advanced facilities and partnerships with some of the biggest names in the industry, like Sundt Corporation, NASA, and Blue Origin, you\u2019ll find many ways to engineer advancements in discovery. College of Engineering College of Health Sciences The College of Health Sciences brings together interdisciplinary researchers working to advance discovery across the broad spectrum of health, including physical therapy, social work, occupational therapy, speech-language pathology, and more. Research within this college has encompassed everything from student well-being to supporting the health of immigrants, veterans, and addressing disparities in Hispanic communities. The College of Health Sciences is home to more than 20 labs and centers advancing research in communication, physiology, experimental food, health disparities, and more. College of Health Science College of Liberal Arts The largest college at UTEP, the College of Liberal Arts houses UTEP\u2019s communications, English, fine arts, social and behavioral sciences, and art programs and researchers. Housed within the College of Liberal Arts are research centers dedicated to studying border security, the intersections of law and psychology, borderlands history, minority alcohol consumption, and beyond. College of Liberal Arts College of Nursing Researchers within UTEP\u2019s College of Nursing combine their clinical and research expertise to execute research projects advancing nursing and healthcare in the region and beyond. Partnering with researchers from other colleges and centers, including the Border Biomedical Research Center, faculty in this college make a direct impact on the community they serve. College of Nursing College of Science The College of Science offers a wide array of research areas to UTEP faculty, from math, teaching, and data science to biomedical research. Home to the Border Biomedical Research Center, UTEP researchers often work with hypotheses and projects that analyze the health disparities of the region. College of Science School of Pharmacy Researchers at UTEP\u2019s School of Pharmacy make inroads in pharmaceutical and health research, including dementia, pancreatic cancer, and more. UTEP\u2019s School of Pharmacy is the only accredited pharmacy school on the border and places an emphasis on supporting Hispanic health disparities. School of Pharmacy UTEP Health In 2024, UTEP received a matching grant of $4.5 million from the Paso del Norte Health Foundation \u2013 the region\u2019s premier nonprofit organization dedicated to supporting the health needs of El Paso; Cd. Juarez, Mexico; and Southern New Mexico \u2013 to enhance UTEP Health, a collaborative effort bringing together UTEP\u2019s Colleges of Health Sciences and Nursing, School of Pharmacy, Mental Health Counseling program within the College of Education, and Psychology Department within the College of Liberal Arts to support health professionals and researchers from the region who are dedicated to serving the region. UTEP Health Center for Community Engagement UTEP\u2019s Center for Community Engagement connects UTEP students with community and civic engagement opportunities in El Paso and beyond, and they also provide opportunities for research collaborations to faculty at UTEP. Faculty members may also elect to make their classes \u201ccommunity engagement courses,\u201d which come with service hours and a special designation on your students\u2019 transcripts. UTEP has also received distinction in community engagement from the Carnegie Foundation, which is given for strides in scholarly partnerships with local and national organizations. Center for Community Engagement Collaboration with Mexico Located on the border, UTEP possesses strong ties with researchers in Mexico, opening the door for collaboration between UTEP faculty and researchers from across Mexico. Recently, UTEP awarded fellowships to six researchers to boost collaboration between researchers from both countries at the benefit of the Paso del Norte region. Collaboration with Mexico <!--\n#myBtn {\n  display: none;\n  position: fixed;\n  bottom: 20px;\n  right: 30px;\n  z-index: 99;\n  font-size: 18px;\n  border: none;\n  outline: none;\n  background-color: #041e42;\n  color: white;\n  cursor: pointer;\n  padding: 15px;\n  border-radius: 4px;\n}\n\n#myBtn:hover {\n  background-color: #ff8200;\n}\n--> // <![CDATA[\n//Get the button\nvar mybutton = document.getElementById(\"myBtn\");\n\n// When the user scrolls down 20px from the top of the document, show the button\nwindow.onscroll = function() {scrollFunction()};\n\nfunction s