{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/research/research-and-sponsored-projects-council/", "title": "Research & Sponsored Projects Council", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About About Research & Innovation Our Units Business Center Research Administration Research Compliance and Regulatory Assurances Research Advancement Commercialization, Entrepreneurship, and Economic Development\u200b For Researchers Events Expertise Connector Explore Our Services Find Funding Interdisciplinary Research (IDR) Office of Technology Commercialization Policies Research News Research Protections Research & Sponsored Projects Council Submit an NOI - VPN University Research Institute (URI) For Prospective Faculty Research at UTEP For Industry/Partners Economic Development Office Office of Technology Commercialization Research Relations and Strategy Research Centers Major Research Centers Events Events Resource Library Learning Opportunities Video Resources Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Research and Sponsored Projects Council Research & Innovation Main Content Research & Sponsored Projects Council Next Meeting:\u00a0 TBA Contact Us Main: 915-747-5680 <!--\n.carousel-caption {\n    display: block !important;\n}\n--> What we do The Research & Sponsored Projects Council provides a forum for discussing strategic development and expansion of research and sponsored project activities. The Council is intended to create a communication channel among Research & Innovation (R&I), colleges, and other units, including the faculty, staff, and administration. The Council aims to create an institutional research climate that realizes the potential of its faculty and research staff in research and scholarly activity and to enhance the University\u2019s research capacity. Meetings are to be held on a monthly basis at a minimum; the membership will be composed of the Vice President for Research & Innovation (R&I), Associate Vice President of R&I, and each college\u2019s dean, associate dean, or representative. Research Council Charge The proposed Research & Sponsored Projects Council charge is to: Recommend strategic actions/opportunities that can advance the University\u2019s research capacity. Disseminate information in a timely manner regarding agency solicitations, proposal development, and training opportunities, as well opportunities related to entrepreneurial activities Announce submissions and awards Review and formulate recommendations for policies and procedures on proposal development, submission processes, and post-award management that improve the research infrastructure. Advise on incentives for research and scholarly activity, including the URI mechanism and process Be actively involved in efforts focused on: Identifying faculty, staff, and administrators who can who can respond to an RFP individually or as part of a team Mentoring faculty, staff, and doctoral students in grantsmanship and research development within your college Recognizing those who excel in research and sponsored projects Ensuring recommendations and proposal submissions are made in a timely manner, e.g., limited submissions Associate Deans for Research Erik Devos, Ph.D. Associate Dean for Research - College of Business Administration Business Administration, Room 247 (915) 747-7770 hdevos@utep.edu Johannes M. Strobel, Ph.D. Associate Dean of Research and Graduate Studies Education Building, Room 414 Z