submit the disclosure form for review. * Please Note : If you generated your disclosure, you MUST do the following: Review all sections of the form, ensure you are disclosing for 2024, update the Start and End Dates to reflect the 2024 year, and SUBMIT the disclosure. Generate Disclosure Submit a Disclosure If you participated in an outside activity but did not submit a request for approval during the 2024 calendar year, click on Activity Form to begin a disclosure form. Click here for a quick instructional video or here for easy instructions on how to begin a disclosure form. Submit a Disclosure Report No Activity If you did not participate in any outside activity during the 2024 calendar year, you are required to report no activity.\u00a0Click here for a quick instructional video or here for easy instructions on how to report no activity. Report No Activity .highligtsWrapper {\n\t    display: flex;\n\t    display: -webkit-flex;\n\t    flex-wrap: wrap;\n\t}\n.highligtsWrapper .col-md-4 {\n           margin-bottom: 30px;\n    }\n.highligtsWrapper .well {\n\t    box-shadow: 0px 2px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);\n\t    -webkit-box-shadow: 0px 2px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);\n\t    height: 100%;\n\t    padding: 0;\n\t     text-align:center;\n    }\n.highligtsBody {\n    \tpadding: 0 24px 0 24px;\n\t}\n.highligtsBody p:nth-last-of-type(1) {\n    \tmargin-bottom: 45px;\n\t}\n.highligtsBody .btn-primary {\n    \tdisplay:block;\n    \ttext-align:center;\n        position: absolute;\n        bottom: 15px;\n        left:30px;\n        right:30px;\n\t} A Disclosure is for an activity that has occurred (in the past) or is occurring. \u00a0It is also more comprehensive, covering outside activities and interests such as substantial interest in a business entity or gifts over $250 , which may be a conflict of interest. a disclosure also covers family members any substantial interest in a business entity should be disclosed no later than 30 days after acquiring the interest. Disclosure requirements apply to: Executive Officers who are defined as all individuals who report directly to the President (other than administrative support positions), and any employee who exercises broad and significant discretion over key institution functions. Employees involved in procurement activities - an employee who makes decisions or recommendations regarding: contract terms or conditions on a contract who is to be awarded a contract preparation of a solicitation for a contract evaluation of a bid or proposal minimum threshold for purchases and contracts over $15,000 Executive Officers, employees involved in procurement activities, and employees involved in contract management with nothing to disclose must affirmatively indicate that fact in the Outside Activities Portal . When in doubt in determining whether an activity or interest should be disclosed, the individual should resolve the doubt in favor of disclosure. Below are brief training videos available to assist with completing the required disclosures: How to Report No Activity How to Generate a Disclosure from a Final Approved Activity Request How to Create a New Disclosure Form To read the full policy, please go to the Handbook of Operating Procedures, Section V, Chapter 29 . For assistance or if you have any questions, please email conflictsofinterest@utep.edu . Please note: Research Conflicts of Interests subject to UT System UTS175 and HOP Section IV , Chapter 2 are managed by the Office of Research and Innovation. \u00a0For more information, please visit the Research Compliance and Regulatory Assurances web site . Conflicts of Interest Conflicts of Interest Submit a Disclosure Request for Approvals of Outside Activities Conflict of Interest, Commitment, and Outside Activities Information Policy Definitions Training Resources Online Training Compliance Helpline Risk Management Conflicts of Interest Handbook of Operating Procedures Title IX Outside Activity Portal // \n$(\".dropdown-menu a[href^='https://