ition to a new electronic form beginning December 1, 2025. Read More IMPORTANT TRAVEL UPDATE: EU ENTRY/EXIT SYSTEM LAUNCHES OCTOBER 12 September 30, 2025 Starting October 12, 2025 , the European Union (EU) will begin implementing the Entry/Exit System (EES), a new digital border control system for non-EU nationals entering the Schengen Area for short stays. Read More SOUTHWEST A-LIST PREFERRED TIER EXPERIENCE September 15, 2025 Earn promotional A-List Preferred status on Southwest Airlines. Read More ACCEPTABLE DIGITAL SIGNATURES June 23, 2025 Effective September 1, 2025, only certificate-based digital signatures will be accepted on Disbursement and Travel Services PDF documents. Read More DISBURSEMENT AND TRAVEL SERVICES BUSINESS PROCESS GUIDELINE UPDATES April 23, 2025 The UTEP Disbursement and Travel Services office has posted two new business process guidelines: Authorized Delivery Locations for Reimbursement and Non-PO Vouchers Restricted Vendors for Reimbursement and Non-PO Vouchers The full Business Process Guidelines can be located on the webpages below: Business Affairs Business Process Guidelines Travel Office Business Process Guidelines SOUTHWEST AIRLINE BAGGAGE CHANGES April 14, 2025 For reservations booked and ticketed or changed on or after May 28, 2025, checked baggage fees will apply. Southwest Airlines has announced that any customer with a valid Group Ticket ticketed on ore before January 5, 2026, will be able to check two (2) pieces of baggage free of charge.\u00a0 Please note, each piece will need to meet the size and weight limits outlined in Southwest Airlines Contract of Carriage.\u00a0 Groups of ten or more travelers qualify for Group Tickets.\u00a0 Please make every effort to book group tickets, if applicable, through the rest of the year to minimize travel costs. Read More REAL ID REQUIREMENTS AND PREPARATION December 19, 2024 Beginning May 7, 2025, U.S. travelers will be required to have a REAL ID-compliant license or another acceptable fo