s, helping researchers secure funding that advances UTEP\u2019s research enterprise. About Proposal Development Proposal Process and Timeline Preparing for Your Submission External Review Letters of Support & Commitment Submit an NOI Honorifics Honorifics celebrates research excellence by recognizing UTEP faculty through prestigious awards, fellowships, and memberships in national honor societies and academies. Internal awards from Research & Innovation further honor impactful contributions within UTEP\u2019s research community, highlighting early-career and seasoned scholars who drive academic and research achievements. About Honorific Awards Pioneering Researcher Reception 2025 R&I Awards 2025 President's Honors Past Awards Faculty Recognitions Collection Form Resources Discover a curated collection of tools and materials designed to support your success. From ready-to-use templates and expert training videos to quick tips and answers to common questions, we offer support to enhance your skills, navigate opportunities, and achieve your goals. Explore learning opportunities, recorded sessions, and more. Learning Opportunities Upcoming Events Training Video Library Resource Libray Contacting a Program Officer Internal Funding Opportunities Research & Innovation offers various internal funding opportunities to support faculty research and scholarly activities. These programs provide resources to advance research ideas, foster innovation and collaboration, and build the foundation for external funding success. University Research Institute (URI) Pilot Grant Program (PGP) Faculty Travel Incentive Program College of Business Seed Funding Liberal Arts Career Enhancement Award IMRS Graduate Research Grant About Us Research Advancement at UTEP integrates Research Development, Federal Relations & Strategic Partnerships, and Research Evaluation and Assessment Services (REAS)\u00a0to support a vibrant and collaborative research ecosystem. Our Research Development\u00a0team enhances interdisciplinary research by fostering strategic thinking and meticulous planning, helping researchers build impactful teams and secure funding. Federal Relations & Strategic Partnerships\u00a0connects researchers with national opportunities, aligning UTEP\u2019s research with federal priorities and expanding our collaborative network. REAS\u00a0provides rigorous evaluation tools and assessments that strengthen proposals and project outcomes, ensuring impactful research. With services tailored to every stage, Research Advancement empowers researchers to transform innovative ideas into meaningful results, driving progress in key areas of inquiry and discovery. Leadership Team Research Advancement Marc Cox, M.S.P.H., Ph.D. Associate Vice President for Research mbcox@utep.edu (915) 747-0595 Kelly Hall, Rm. 717 Lorraine Limon McCullough Administrative Associate To Associate Vice President For Research & Innovation llmccullough@utep.edu (915) 747-0763 Kelly Hall, Rm. 715 Research Advancement is committed to supporting UTEP\u2019s research efforts by providing strategic services to enhance the university\u2019s competitiveness in today\u2019s research landscape. Our team, comprised of research developers, evaluation experts, and writers, guides faculty through every step, from identifying funding opportunities to research development to garnering collaborative approaches and formative and summative evaluation. We work across all colleges, departments, and units, offering comprehensive services to advance research, innovation, and impact. View IDRB Contact IDRB Interdisciplinary Research & Team Science Thenral Mangadu, M.D., M.P.H., Ph.D. Associate Vice President tdmangadu@utep.edu (915) 747-5093 Kelly Hall, Rm. 723A Research Development David Hern\u00e1ndez Director dahernandez49@utep.edu (915) 747-7693 Kelly Hall, Rm. 716A Nora Hernandez Assistant Director norag@utep.edu (915) 747-5072 Kelly Hall, Rm. 719A Research Development is dedicated to fostering a vibrant and collaborative research environment at UTEP by enhancing researchers' success across all disciplines. Innovative research thrives on addressing complex challenges that demand diverse expertise, and our team is here to support those efforts with strategic guidance and comprehensive planning. Our services are designed to empower researchers at every stage of their journey. From identifying and promoting funding opportunities, supporting research development, building interdisciplinary teams, and pursuing prestigious honorific awards, we provide the tools and expertise to turn ideas into impactful research outcomes. Let us partner with you to advance your research and amplify its success. View Research Dev Contact Research Development Scientific Computing and Artificial Intelligence Salamah Salamah, Ph.D. Associate Vice President isalamah@utep.edu (915) 747-6671 Kelly Hall, Rm. 726 View RAIDS Contact RAIDS Research Relations & Strategy Adrianna Leyva Manager amleyva@utep.edu (915) 747-7230 Kelly Hall, 7th floor Research Relations and Strategy advances UTEP\u2019s research by fostering strategic partnerships with federal agencies, aligning initiatives with national priorities, and promoting interdisciplinary collaboration. We facilitate impactful collaborations, coordinate strategic initiatives, and connect UTEP with opportunities that advance research excellence, address critical challenges, and drive innovation with societal impact. View Research Relations & Strategy Contact Research Relations & Strategy Research, Evaluation, and Assessment Services (REAS) Sandra Oviedo Ramirez, Ph.D. Director sloviedoramirez@utep.edu (915) 747-7935 Kelly Hall, Rm. 705 The Research, Evaluation, and Assessment Services (REAS) center offers comprehensive evaluation planning support to members of the University of Texas at El Paso (UTEP) community engaged in the preparation of proposals. The REAS center offers evaluation and technical assistance services on a fee-for-service basis. View REAS Contact REAS Office of Technology Commercialization (OTC) Jacob Croft Director jrcroft@utep.edu (915) 747-7820 Kelly Hall, Rm. 213A UTEP\u2019s Office of Technology Commercialization (OTC) manages UTEP\u2019s intellectual property and facilitates the marketing and licensing of technologies to industry and start-ups. OTC\u2019s webpage contains information on all UTEP developed technologies available to your business, as well as resources and instructions on how to license our technologies. Our technologies can be transformed into commercial products that can assist your business in reaching its goals. View OTC Contact OTC Mike Loya Center for Innovation and Commerce (MLCIC) Nicole Aguilar, MBA Director inaguilar2@utep.edu (915) 747-5971 Prospect Hall, Rm. 316 The MLCIC serves as your comprehensive resource hub for entrepreneurship activities, programs, and education. Our center is dedicated to three primary avenues: Fostering Innovation and entrepreneurial mindset, supporting UTEP faculty and students in entrepreneurship education and the creation of ventures, and contributing to the entrepreneurial ecosystem. We offer a range of services aimed at empowering individuals in their entrepreneurial pursuits. These include providing entrepreneurship education, organizing entrepreneurship competitions, and offering guidance and mentorship to UTEP students, faculty, and staff. View MLCIC Contact MLCIC <!--\n#myBtn {\n  display: none;\n  position: fixed;\n  bottom: 20px;\n  right: 30px;\n  z-index: 99;\n  font-size: 18px;\n  border: none;\n  outline: none;\n  background-color: #041e42;\n  color: white;\n  cursor: pointer;\n  padding: 15px;\n  border-radius: 4px;\n}\n\n#myBtn:hover {\n  background-color: #ff8200;\n}\n--> <!--\nh1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6   {text-align: left;}\n\n.card {\n    height: 140px;\n    width: 100%; \n   /* width: 115px; */\n  /*  background: #e6843e;  */\n  /*  box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px lightgrey; */\n    padding: 2px;\n    border:  1px solid #0a1f4042;