{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/research/office-of-sponsored-projects/policies/indirect-cost-recovery-waiver-policy.html", "title": "Indirect Cost Recovery and Waivers Policy", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search Home Office of Sponsored Projects Grant Management Accounting ---------------- Business Center Research Administration Research Compliance and Regulatory Assurances Research Advancement About Meet the Team Find your RA Sponsored Project Lifecyle Services Pre-Award Post-Award Contracts and Agreements Subcontracts Support PI resources Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ) Policies/Procedures Policies/Procedures One Pagers One Pagers Quick Info Quick Info Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Office of Sponsored Projects Research & Innovation Main Content Indirect (Facilities & Administrative) Cost Recovery and Waivers Policy <!--\n.carousel-caption {\n    display: block !important;\n}\n--> Purpose This policy outlines the University\u2019s approach to recovering indirect costs, also known as Facilities and Administrative (F&A) costs, from sponsored projects and defines the circumstances under which exceptions or waivers may be granted. Indirect costs are real and necessary expenses incurred by the University to support research, instruction, and other sponsored activities. These costs include, but are not limited to: Utilities, Facility maintenance and Research administration services Because these expenses are incurred for common or shared objectives, they cannot always be directly attributed to a specific project. The University negotiates its indirect cost rate every four years with the U.S. Department of Health and Human Services (DHHS) Cost Allocation Services. Indirect costs are calculated by applying the negotiated indirect cost rate to the Modified Total Direct Costs (MTDC) of each sponsored project. In accordance with federal regulations, these negotiated rates are legally binding. Recovering indirect costs is essential to maintaining the University\u2019s research infrastructure. Funds generated through indirect cost recovery are reinvested in areas such as: Research core facilities, Renovation and maintenance of research space, Faculty start-up packages, and Research administrative staff support All sponsored projects must charge the full, applicable DHHS-negotiated indirect cost rate, regardless of the sponsor type. This requirement applies to proposals submitted to: Federal and state government agencies Private companies and industry groups Foundations and non-profit organizations Any other external sponsor Exceptions 1.\u00a0 Non-Profit and Governmental Sponsors The University may grant an exception when a non-profit sponsor or governmental agency has an explicit, published policy or statute that limits indirect cost recovery. Requirements: A copy of the sponsor\u2019s published policy or statute must be included in the proposal materials submitted to the Office of Sponsored Projects (OSP). The reduced indirect cost rate will be applied to total direct costs, unless the sponsor specifies otherwise. Important Note: Any limitation on indirect cost recovery must be applied consistently by the sponsor to all recipients. Behind-the-scenes negotiations by university employees with sponsoring agencies regarding indirect costs are strictly prohibited and not binding on the University. 2.\u00a0 For-Profit Sponsors (including clinical trial projects) For-profit sponsors are always charged the full, applicable indirect rate for the project activity. Subsidizing a for-profit project with university resources constitutes an improper use of public funds for private benefit and is strictly prohibited. Indirect Cost Waiver An indirect cost waiver allows the University to charge less than the full applicable indirect cost rate. Waivers are granted only under exceptional circumstances, where the programmatic benefit to the University is compelling and outweighs the institutional benefit of full cost recovery. Waivers will not be approved for the following reasons: To increase the perceived competitiveness of a proposal. Because the sponsor has capped the total award amount. Waiver Request process All waiver requests must be approved by the Director of the Office of Sponsored Projects (OSP) before the proposal is submitted. Waiver requests must comply with the University\u2019s five-day proposal submission policy. Waivers will not be considered after an award has been accepted by the University. Contact Us OSP is located in Kelly Hall, 6th floor, East Wing 500 W University Ave El Paso, TX 79968 Main: 915-747-5680 osp@utep.edu Fax: 747-8977 Research Administration <!--\nh1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6   {text-align: left;}\n--> // <![CDATA[\n$(document).ready(function() { \n            \n                $(\"h2\").css(\"text-align\", \"left\"); \n                \n                $(\"a#bluelink\").css(\"color\", \"#337ab7\"); \n        \n        });\n// ]]> <!--\nbody {\n    position: relative;\n}\n\n/*header bg fix*/\n@media (min-width:1250px ) and (max-width: 1364px){\n\t.headerContainer {\n\t    width: 100%;\n\t}\n}\n/*Carousel FW*/\n#container + .container {\n\tmax-width: none !important;\n\twidth: auto!important;\n}\n.slide-transfer {\n    display:none!important;\n}\n.video-wrapper {\n\tmax-height: none !important;\n}\n.carousel-caption {\n\tdisplay: none;\n}\n.slide-transfer {\n\tdisplay: none;\n}\n/*FullWidthSection*/\n.fw-se