{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/hoop/section-7/ch-7.html", "title": "Chapter 7: Financial Aid and Scholarships Code of Conduct", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search Policies I - Introduction and University Administration II - Student Affairs III - Academic Affairs IV - Research and Innovation V - Human Resources VI - Equal Opportunity VII - Financial Services VIII - Facilities Services IX - Environmental Health & Safety X - Information Resources XI - Institutional Advancement Regents' Rules and Regulations Regents' Rules and Regulations UTS Policies Library UTS Policies Library Policy Approval Process Policy Approval Process Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Handbook of Operating Procedures Main Content UTEP Handbook of Operating Procedures Section 7 UTEP Handbook of Operating Procedures Section 7 Chapter 7: Financial Aid and Scholarships Code of Conduct 7.1 Policy and Purpose It\u00a0is the policy of The University of Texas at El Paso to commit to and adopt a Financial Aid and Scholarships Code of Conduct and standards concerning student financial aid services and lending practices in connection with such student financial aid services. The purpose of this policy is to exhibit educational leadership and demonstrate a commitment to student financial aid programs that best serve the needs of students and parents and enable future generations to achieve the numerous benefits afforded by higher education. This policy is adopted pursuant to the requirements in the federal Higher Education Act of 1965, as amended (P.L. 89-329), as further amended by the Higher Education Opportunity Act (P.L. 110-315). This also implements Texas Education Code, Sec. 51.9645, relating to prohibiting certain activities by financial aid employees. 7.2 Adoption of Code of Conduct The University of Texas at El Paso hereby accepts, adopts and implements, the Code of Conduct and Statement of Ethical Principles maintained by the National Association of Student Financial Aid Administrators (NASFAA).\u00a0 A complete copy of the Financial Aid and Scholarships Code of Conduct and Ethical Principles is located at: https://www.utep.edu/financial-aid/more-information/code-of-conduct.html . 7.3 Training On an annual basis, every employee within the Office of Financial Aid and Scholarships at The University of Texas at El Paso, and other identified officers and employees as determined by the President, shall receive training concerning the Financial Aid and Scholarships Code of Conduct.\u00a0 The annual training module will be administered by the Office of Institutional Compliance. 7.4 References Financial Aid and Scholarships Code of Conduct and Ethical Principles 7.5 Dates Approved or Updated September 16, 2025 August 27, 2021 7.6 Contact Information Financial Aid and Scholarships (915) 747-5204 studentfinancialaid@utep.edu utep.edu/financial-aid/ Section 7: Financial Services Chapter 1: Audit and Consulting Services Chapter 2: Fraudulent or Dishonest Activities Chapter 3: University-Owned Property and Equipment Chapter 4: Transfer of Capital and Controlled Equipment Chapter 5: Cost Center/Project Review Policy Chapter 6: Travel Policy Chapter 7: Financial Aid and Scholarships Code of Conduct Chapter 8: Identity Theft Prevention, Detection and Mitigation Policy (Red Flags Rule) Chapter 9: Employer-Provided Vehicles Including Courtesy Donor Cars Chapter 10: Records and Information Manag