{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/newsfeed/2024/august/utep-welcomes-new-faculty-members.html", "title": "UTEP Welcomes New Faculty Members for 2024-25 Academic Year", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Newsfeed Main Content UTEP Welcomes New Faculty Members for 2024-25 Academic Year The University of Texas at El Paso welcomed a new cohort of tenured, tenure-track, and instructional faculty members to begin the 2024-25 academic year. The new faculty members come to UTEP with a breadth of expertise that ranges from science, health sciences, pharmacy, and the performing arts to humanities, education, engineering, social sciences, and business. The University of Texas at El Paso has hired dozens of new faculty members in anticipation of the 2023-24 school year, including Pedro Cortes, Ph.D., a new professor in the College of Engineering. Along with their expertise and wealth of knowledge, the newest members of the UTEP faculty bring an unbridled excitement as they join the University and form part of its mission. \u201cI am excited and honored to be part of the UTEP family,\u201d said Pedro Cortes, Ph.D., a professor of metallurgical, materials and biomedical engineering in the college of engineering. \u201cI am joining UTEP because of its excellence in education and scholarship. I look forward to supporting the advanced manufacturing initiatives to further grow UTEP's leadership in this field.\u201d The cohort includes two new department chairs: Hind Al-Abadleh, Ph.D., professor and chair of the Department of Biological Sciences; and Kendal Hirschi, Ph.D., professor and chair of the Department of Earth, Environmental and Resource Sciences. Al-Abadleh comes to UTEP from Wilfrid Laurier University in Waterloo, Ontario, Canada where she was a professor in the chemistry and biochemistry department. Hirschi comes to UTEP from the Baylor College of Medicine where he was a professor in the Department of Pediatrics and focused on the nutritional improvement of agriculturally important crops. \u201cIt has been great to welcome a new cohort of exceptional faculty who embody UTEP\u2019s mission of providing access to an excellent education and producing research that improves people\u2019s lives,\u201d said John Wiebe, Ph.D., provost and vice president for academic affairs. \u201cAt the heart of our university is a strong faculty dedicated to providing students with a transformative education; we look forward to seeing how this new cohort impacts the lives of their students.\u201d Read more about the faculty members\u2019 expertise at https://www.utep.edu/provost/faculty/new-faculty-profiles-2024-2025.html . The new tenured, tenure-track, and instructional faculty members include: Hind A. Al-Abadleh, Ph.D., chair and professor, Department of Earth, Environmental and Resource Sciences Brianna Anderson, Ph.D., assistant professor, Department of English Christiana Antwi-Obimpeh, Ph.D., assistant professor, Department of Accounting and Information Systems Tessa Arsenault, Ph.D., assistant professor, Department of Counseling and Special Education Elisabeth Baker Martinez, Ph.D., assistant professor, Department of Latin-US and Linguistics Mart\u00edn Balmaceda, MFA, assistant professor, Department of Theatre and Dance William Campillo Terrazas, PharmD, clinical assistant professor, Department of Pharmacy Practice and Clinical Sciences 