{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/business/undergraduateprograms/academic-programs/realestate.html", "title": "Real Estate (CRE) Minor", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About About Hunt College Accreditation Contact Us Our Mission and Vision Hunt Insights Hunt Connect Academic Programs Undergraduate Programs Master of Accountancy Master of Business Administration (MBA) Master of Science in Economics with Data Analytics Ph.D. in Business Administration Certificate of Accountancy Certificate in Innovation and Entrepreneurship Corporate Academies at Hunt College Departments Accounting and Information Systems Department Economics and Finance Marketing, Management and Supply Chain People Current Doctoral Students Dean's Office Faculty UTEP Campus Directory Research Center for Free Enterprise Border Region Modeling Project Center for Multicultural Management and Ethics Hunt Institute The Mike Loya Center for Innovation and Commerce Seminars Alumni and Partners Alumni Hunt Business Leadership Council Giving to UTEP Distinguished Alumni Gold Nuggets Resources Student Resources Faculty and Staff Resources BUSN Space Reservation Data Request Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Bachelor of Business Administration Woody L. Hunt College of Business Main Content OPEN TO ALL BUSINESS MAJORS AND NON-BUSINESS MAJORS The minor in Real Estate (CRE) was designed with substantial input from real estate industry professionals and practitioners. It is intended to fill a stated need in the industry for professionals who have knowledge of the real estate industry upon completion of coursework and entering the real estate profession. The minor focuses heavily on providing students with skills that are necessary to establish a successful career in real estate. The real estate minor consists of four (4) required courses for business majors at the Woody L. Hunt College of Business, or six (6) required courses for non-business majors at other colleges in UTEP. The Real Estate Courses can be taken as business electives, upon the department\u2019s approval. Real Estate Faculty Real Estate Courses are taught by nationally and internationally recognized UTEP faculty specializing in real estate and finance. Faculty members are globally ranked top producers of real estate research. Additionally, the teaching mission is enhanced by senior real estate professionals from the Greater El Paso Region and beyond. Erik Devos, Ph.D. Associate Dean for Faculty, Research, and Graduate Programs hedevos@utep.edu Zifeng Feng, Ph.D. Assistant Professor of Finance zfeng@utep.edu Steven R. Gragg, MAI, CCIM\u2019 Assistant Professor of Practice srgragg@utep.edu Carleen R. Barth, CCIM Adjunct Lecturer crbarth@utep.edu Scott Winton, AICP Adjunct Faculty gswinton@utep.edu Industry Connections Design by Hunt Creative UTEP Ranked as One of the Top Producers of Real Estate Research UTEP has been ranked one of the top institutions for real estate research productivity in the world, according to the Real Estate Academic Leadership (REAL) Rankings for 2019-2023. More Information UTEP Real Estate & CCIM Unlock your future with the CCIM University Fast Track Undergraduate Membership, which grants graduates of approved real estate or finance programs automatic credit for the first designation course and streamlines your path to earning the prestigious CCIM Designation in under six years . Join today to access elite education, cutting\u2011edge tools, and a powerful commercial real estate network, all while accelerating your career before graduation. More Information CCIM Scholarships The Greater El Paso CCIM Chapter supports the new Minor in Real Estate at the Woody L. Hunt College of Business by offering student Scholarships. The local real estate nonprofit provides networking, education, and tech opportunities for those in the real estate industry. These Scholarships are aimed at Hunt College students pursuing the Minor in Real Estate who demonstrate excellence and have an interest in entering the real estate industry. Student Membership and active participation in the Greater El Paso CCIM Chapter's annual activities is encouraged. Annual deadline to apply is May 1 st . . More Information Real Estate Courses Real Estate Courses for Business Majors CRE 3301: Intro to Real Estate CRE 4301: Real Estate Finance Select two of the following courses: CRE 4302: Real Estate Investments CRE 4341: Real Estate Development CRE 4342: Property Management CRE 4325: International Real Estate Real Estate Courses for Non-Business Majors CRE 3301: Intro to Real Estate CRE 4301: Real Estate Finance Select four of the following courses: FIN 3350: Personal Financial Planning (no prereq) BLAW 3301: Legal Environment of Business (no prereq) CRE 4302: Real Estate Investments CRE 4341: Real Estate Development CRE 4342: Property Management CRE 4325: International Real Estate Real Estate initiatives Real Estate Field Trips spring 2024 field trip Spring 2024 - Montecillo fall 2024 field trip Fall 2024 - Downtown El Paso spring 2025 field trip Spring 2025 - River Oaks Properties fall 2025 field trip Fall 2025 - Industrial, Manufacturing & Distribution Properties Site Tour Real Estate Career Fair fall 2023 fair Fall 2023 Fair spring 2024 fair Spring 2024 Fair fall 2024 fair Fall 2024 Fair spring 2025 fair Spring 2025 Fair fall 2025 fair Fall 2025 Fair <!--\n.video-container {\n            position: relat