{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/engineering/rimes/", "title": "Research Institute for Manufacturing and Engineering Systems (RIMES)", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About About Us Research Research People People Publications Publications Contracts and Grants Contracts and Grants Resources Resources Patents and Products Patents and Products News News Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Research Institute for Manufacturing and Engineering Systems (RIMES) College of Engineering Main Content UTEP College of Engineering Research Institute for Manufacturing and Engineering Systems (RIMES) UTEP Professor Awarded Fellowship to Travel to Israel LEARN MORE UTEP, Drexel University Plan Online Collaboration to Increase Minority, Women Graduates in Green STEM Fields LEARN MORE Previous Next UTEP College of Engineering Research Institute for Manufacturing and Engineering Systems (RIMES) Research Institute for Manufacturing and Engineering Systems (RIMES) RIMES was created in 1995 as the Institute for Manufacturing and Materials Management (IM3). We have recently renamed the Institute while maintaining its focus on Manufacturing and Materials Management. The institute has also evolved and taken the lead in focusing on the research of new knowledge of systems and its applications to Manufacturing and Engineering Systems. As part of The University of Texas at El Paso, the Institute is committed to education. Members of the staff teach classes, sponsor research at the University, and are encouraged to participate in seminars, conferences and lectures. The institute has a long history of collaboration with private industry. We are committed to continue and expand this synergy. If you are an engineer who wants to help solve today's business problems and meet your future career goals, our Graduate Certificate Program is perfect for you. The program employs an interdisciplinary approach based on an \"entire view\" of missions and operational environments. It combines the capabilities of platforms, systems, operators, and support to fashion solutions that meet customer needs. - Dr. Bill Tseng, Director - Dr. Md Fashiar Rahman, Associate Director FEATURED NEWS KTEP Launches Campaign to Raise Funds to Pay for NPR Content EL PASO, Texas (Aug. 13, 2025) \u2013 KTEP Public Media, a service of The University of Texas at El Paso, announced that it will hold a fundraising drive August 15 and 16 to raise funds to pay for its popular National Public Radio programming for the next fiscal year. STAY CONNECTED Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso RIMES Engineering Bldg., Room A-130 500 W University El Paso, Texas 79968 E: rimes@utep.edu P: (915) 747-5336 F: (915) 747-5437 THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Texas Veterans Portal Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 | SITE FEEDBACK Modal X"}
{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/vpba/peoplesoft/training/classes.html", "title": "Trainings", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About PeopleSoft Browser Support News News Training Training Resources Trainings Training Calendar Resources PeopleSoft Chartfield Conversion Tool Additional Resources Forms Forms Payroll Calendar Calendar FAQs General FAQs Interim Approval Process FAQs Asset Management FAQs eForm FAQs Electronic Leave Request FAQs Electronic Timesheet FAQs Finance FAQs Time Reporting FAQs HR FAQs Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Peoplesoft Business Affairs Main Content UTEP Business Affairs Peoplesoft Training UTEP Business Affairs Peoplesoft Training Online Self-Paced Training How to Register: Choose your Course: Browse the available courses and select the one you would like to register for. Click on the course link to view detailed instructions on how to fill out the Front Office Access Request Form. Submit the Access Request Form: Complete the form with the required information. Once submitted, it will be automatically routed to your supervisor for approval. Wait for Supervisor Approval: Your supervisor will review and approve your request. PeopleSoft Team Review: After your supervisor approves the request, the PeopleSoft team will review and will provide a link to the designated training. Check Your Email for Confirmation: You will receive an email with instructions on how to access and begin the training. \ud83d\udd14 Reminder: You can track the status of your access request form using the confirmation email you received after submitting the form. It is recommended that you check your email regularly for instructions regarding training access to ensure a smooth start! Not sure which roles to select or how to find the form? Detailed guidance is available in the links below. Online Training Course Approximate Duration Instructions Accounts Payable: Vendors & Vouchers 40 minutes Click here Budget Management & Queries 60 minutes Click here SAHARA Part 1 80 minutes Click here SAHARA Part 2 40 minutes Click here Time Reporting 30 minutes Click here Travel I 60 minutes Click here Travel II 60 minutes Click here Advanced Travel 60 minutes Click here NOTE: Have questions after completing a PeopleSoft training? Join the Finance's team monthly PeopleSoft Workshop for assistance with any financial-related questions. These sessions offer additional support and assistance. To see the Training Calendar use the link below: View Training Calendar Training Content Travel 1: Travel and Expense Policies For all department supporting staff who process travel documents as well as expense reimbursements. This class will cover travel authorization and reimbursement policies and procedures (Pre & Post-travel). Travel I, Travel II, Advanced Travel training are required for the Travel & Expense Creator role which grants the user access to enter travel authorizations and process employee expense reports. Travel 2: Travel and Expense Reimbursements For personnel who process travel reimbursements as well as expense reimbursements. The training covers information on how to navigate and process these documents in PeopleSoft. Travel I, T ravel II, and Advanced Travel training are required for the Travel & Expense Creator role which grants the user access to enter travel authorizations and process employee expense reports. SAHARA I For personnel who reconcile accounts, the training covers a quick overview of the tool and the policies and procedures regarding SAHARA. Account Reconciliation Training is now required for access to the reconciler role. Access will be granted as per approval of the account owner and/or CAO. SAHARA II For personnel who reconcile accounts, this course provides a step by step process on how to reconcile your accounts using SAHARA and should be taken after SAHARA I training. Account Reconciliation Training is now required for access to the reconciler role. Access will be granted as per approval of the account owner and/or CAO. Accounts Payable: Vendors & Vouchers For personnel who perform payment activities and enter receipt information, non-contract payments, and returning goods. Accounts Payable: Vendors & Vouchers training is required for the Voucher Creator role, this role grants the user access to process Non-Po Vouchers. Advanced Travel/ Reimbursement For personnel who process travel reimbursements as well as reimbursement requests for other purchases. This training follows the Travel I and Travel II training, and covers additional tips and tricks for creating travel authorizations and expense reimbursements. Creators will also learn about the available expense types, other functions, and queries. Budget Management & Queries For any personnel with budgetary or contract/grant authority and their support staff. This session covers how to access your financial information as well as how to pull queries. Budget Management & Queries training is required for the Budget Reviewer role. This role grants the user access to view budget overview information which shows budget balance, encumbrances, available balance, expenses and other transactions that affect budget. Time Reporting For personnel who assist with timekeeping, the training covers information on how to process timesheets for all employee types and further details on how to support your department in timekeeping activities. Time Reporting training is required for the Time Reporting role, which grants the user access to enter, adjust, or delete time for employees in their department. HR Processes & eForms For all personnel who initiate new hire paperwork, DBTs, and other requests for changes to employee records. The training covers the hiring process, more information regarding each employee type, how to process DBTs and payroll information. The training also includes an overview on how to process End Employee Assignment, Retirement, and Position Funding Change eForms in PeopleSoft. HR Processes & eForms training is required for the HR Reviewer and eForms Processor roles which grant access to view job and position data required when initiating position request/modifications, funding changes, recruitment, hiring, and other HR transactions. Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions // \n$(\".dropdown-menu a[href^='https://']\").attr(\"target\",\"_blank\");\n$(\".leftSidebar .nav a[href^='https://']\").attr(\"target\",\"_blank\");\n$('.dropdown-menu a[href*=\".pdf\"]').attr(\"target\",\"_blank\");\n$('.leftSidebar .nav a[href*=\".pdf\"]').attr(\"target\",\"_blank\");\n// Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso PeopleSoft - 500 W University El Paso, Texas 79968 E: helpdesk@utep.edu P: - THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Texas Veterans Portal Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 | SITE FEEDBACK Modal X"}
