{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/health/", "title": "UTEP Health", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support UTEP Health Main Content Educating Excellent Healthcare Professionals Read the announcement Support UTEP Health .logo-image {\n    width: 390px;\n    height: auto;\n}\n@media screen and (max-width: 991px){\n    .logo-image {\n        width: 430px;\n        height: auto;\n    }\n}\n@media screen and (max-width: 767px){\n    .logo-image {\n        max-width: 360px;\n        height: auto;\n        text-align: left;\n        margin-bottom: 0;\n    }\n}\n.s-col img {\n    width: 25px;\n    height: 25px;\n}\n.cel-arrow img {\n    width: 25px;\n    height: 25px;\n    margin-top: -1px;\n}\n.dw-arrow img {\n    width: 20px;\n    height: 20px;\n    margin-top: -1px;\n}\n.fw-section .btn-primary-1, .fw-section a.btn-primary-1 {\n    background-color: #edf2f9;\n    color: #fa9b49 !important;\n    font-weight: bold;\n    text-transform: uppercase;\n    text-align: center;\n    border: none;\n    letter-spacing: 1px;\n    padding: 15px;\n    font-size: 16px;\n    margin: 12px auto 0;\n    border-radius: 6px !important;\n}\n.fw-section .btn-primary-1:hover, .fw-section a.btn-primary-1:hover {\n    background-color: #ff8200;\n    color: #041e42 !important;\n} UTEP Health is a comprehensive initiative of The University of Texas at El Paso aimed at elevating the standard of health care in the Paso del Norte region. The initiative will increase the number of healthcare professionals with a high-quality education. The Paso del Norte Foundation is generously supporting this effort with a $4.5 million matching grant. Show your support for UTEP Health by making a gift to help double the impact to $9 million. UTEP Health Advances Healthcare in El Paso Healthcare Professionals Dedicated to the Paso del Norte Region A Top Tier Education That is Changing the Face of Healthcare Research that Helps People Live Longer and Healthier Lives Healthcare Professionals Dedicated to the Paso del Norte Region UTEP Health encompasses more than 4,400 students in the College of Health Sciences, the College of Nursing, the School of Pharmacy and other health professions, programs and research \u2013 more than 70 percent of whom will stay in the community to practice upon graduation. \"For every five doctors, there are 95 health care professionals to take care of you and your family. UTEP Health will focus on meeting the need in our region for that 95 percent of healthcare professionals to a very high standard.\" - UTEP President Heather Wilson A Top Tier Education that Meets the Needs of Healthcare in the Region UTEP Health's academic programs educate excellent healthcare professionals across 7 bachelor's, 8 master's and 4 doctoral programs. As Texas faces a critical shortage of healthcare professionals that is particularly acute in El Paso and the surrounding region, UTEP Health will expand the enrollment of degree programs, upgrade labs and facilities and expand research into Hispanic health disparities. \"UTEP Health is an effort to take what we are already doing in healthcare and dial it up. With more highly skilled healthcare workers and greatly expanded research into the factors that impact Hispanic health, I am confident that this initiative will result in longer, healthier lives for the people in this community.\" -John Wiebe, Ph.D., UTEP Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs Explore UTEP Health degree programs Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Research that Helps People Live Longer and Healthier Lives $4.5M Grant to UTEP Health Increases Nurses, Health Professionals UTEP Researchers to Design Movement-Based Training to Support Local Health Providers UTEP Clinical Trial to Encourage Healthy Walking Habits UTEP Researchers Discover Compound that Fights Leukemia, Lymphoma UTEP Team to Help Improve Employment Opportunities for People with Disabilities Coffee Grounds May Hold Key to Preventing Neurodegenerative Diseases <!--\nbody {\n    position: relative;\n}\n\n/*header bg fix*/\n@media (min-width:1250px ) and (max-width: 1364px){\n\t.headerContainer {\n\t    width: 100%;\n\t}\n}\n/*Carousel FW*/\n#container + .container {\n\tmax-width: none !important;\n\twidth: auto!important;\n}\n.slide-transfer {\n    display:none!important;\n}\n.video-wrapper {\n\tmax-height: none !important;\n}\n.carousel-caption {\n\tdisplay: none;\n}\n.slide-transfer {\n\tdisplay: none;\n}\n/*FullWidthSection*/\n.fw-section {\n\tpadding-top: 40px;\n\tpadding-bottom: 60px;\n}\n.sectionAnchor {\n    padding-top:135px;\n    margin-top:-135px;\n}\n.fw-section h2 {\n\ttext-align: center;\n}\n.fw-section:after {\n\tclear: both;\n}\n.container-narrow {\n\tmax-width: 800px;\n}\n.row {\n\tmargin-left: 0;\n\tmargin-right: 0;\n}\n@media (max-width: 991px){\n    .col-md-4 {\n        width:100%;\n    }\n}\n/*Gray Bg Section*/\n.background-gray {\n\tbackground-color: #f2f2f2;\n}\n/*Blue Bg Section*/\n.background-blue {\n\tbackground-color: #041E42;\n\tcolor: #fff;\n}\n.background-blue h2 {\n\tcolor: #fff;\n}\n.background-blue .btn-primary, .background-blue a.btn-primary {\n    background-color: #FF8200;\n}\n.background-blue .btn-primary:hover, .background-blue .btn-primary:focus, .background-blue a.btn-primary:hover, .background-blue a.btn-primary:focus {\n    color: #041b3c;\n    background-color: #ddd;\n}\n/*flex*/\n.highligtsWrapper