5s ease;\n        color: white;\n        text-align: center;\n        padding: 10px;\n        margin-bottom: 16px;\n        font-size: 18px;\n        -webkit-appearance: button;\n        -moz-appearance: button;\n        appearance: button;\n        border: none;\n        outline:none;\n        text-decoration: none;\n        color: #102244 !important;\n    }\n--> The College of Science CORE offers academic advising and guidance to empower students to realize their full potential. The relationship between you and your advisors is one of the most important that you will have while at UTEP. We highly suggest that you use this site to complement this partnership. Within these pages you will find tools to strategically navigate your degree, material to fully comprehend college and university policies, mechanisms for exploring careers in math and science, support for transitioning to your next career goal, and information (like important deadlines) to ensure successful progress. We are here to help you attain your dreams. Let us know if you need anything. Dr. Kristine M. Garza Associate Dean for Student Success College of Science Hours of Operation <!--\n.blue {\n        background-color: #102244;\n        color: white;\n        padding-left: 10px;\n        padding-bottom: 10px;\n        padding-top: 4px;\n        \n    }\n    \n    .white { \n        color: #102244;\n    }\n    \n    .button-link {\n        background-color: #f7821a;\n        transition: 0.5s ease;\n        color: white;\n        text-align: center;\n        padding: 10px;\n        margin-bottom: 16px;\n        font-size: 18px;\n        -webkit-appearance: button;\n        -moz-appearance: button;\n        appearance: button;\n        border: none;\n        outline:none;\n        text-decoration: none;\n        color: #102244 !important;\n    }\n--> Hours of Operation Monday through Friday 8:00 AM - 5:00 PM Saturday & Sunday CLOSED Closed during all UTEP-recognized holidays. Our schedule is subject to change; the office is closed during advisor trainings that occur approximately every two weeks on Fridays. Carl Hertzog Building Room 101 (915) 747 - 8027 core@utep.edu Other Important Sites <!--\n.table-square {\n        background-color:  #102244;\n        color: white;\n        text-align: center;\n        padding: 6px;\n    }\n    .table-square:hover {\n        background-color:#f7821a;\n    }\n    .blue {\n        background-color: #102244;\n        color: white;\n        padding-left: 10px;\n        padding-bottom: 10px;\n        padding-top: 4px;\n        \n    }\n    .link{\n        color: white;\n        text-decoration: none;\n    }\n--> Table with links to course schedule, course catalog, academic calendar, and registration information UTEP Course Catalog UTEP Academic Calendar Course Schedule Registration Schedule FEATURED NEWS UTEP Awarded $500,000 Grant to Protect Nuclear Plants with AI-Driven Cybersecurity EL PASO, Texas (Oct. 16, 2025) \u2013 The University of Texas at El Paso has received a grant from the U.S. Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) to support pioneering work to harness artificial intelligence and strengthen cybersecurity for nuclear power plants. City of El Paso, UTEP Strengthen Partnership to Drive Advanced Manufacturing and Aerospace Innovation, Expanding High-Quality Jobs EL PASO, Texas (Oct. 14, 2025) \u2015 The El Paso City Council approved a resolution authorizing the Mayor to sign an Interlocal Agreement with The University of Texas at El Paso to jointly advance the region\u2019s aerospace and defense manufacturing capabilities as part of the U.S. Economic Development Administration\u2019s Build Back Better Regional Challenge (BBBRC). STAY CONNECTED Welcome Central Office for Readiness and Engagement (CORE) Book An Appointment Mission and Goals CORE Directory CORE Announcements Advising Graduation College of Science UTEP Edge Careers in Health Professions Teaching Math and Science FAQs Resources Academic Planning Tools College of