our success, please share your compliments/feedback . This information can be made anonymously if you like. For more serious concerns, please see the Student Life Policies and Procedures . It gives detail on the different types of concerns and explains how to ensure it is heard by the proper office. The information at that link will ensure you know the University rules. To help you file your concern, the following is a brief summary of the information you will find. There are four different types of concerns, each with its own filing process: Equal Educational Opportunity Complaints : (for example exclusion from participation on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex, age, genetic information, veteran status, disability, sexual orientation, or gender identity) Address the concern to the University's Equal Opportunity Office, Kelly Hall, 3rd Floor, at (915) 747-5662 or eoaa@utep.edu Grade Review : Follow the instructions on the Office of Student Life Web page under the heading \"Grade Grievance\" before submitting the Grievance Form . Other Academic Complaints : Submit your concern not covered by #1 or #2. This type of concern requires a person from the Dean\u2019s office to contact you so it cannot be done anonymously . The Dean and Associate Dean for Academic Affairs are the only two people who can access this information. Non-Academic Complaints : (example the interpretation of student policies) There is not a specific link for this, but the Student Life Policies and Procedures explains how to file your concern. Title IX: The University of Texas at El Paso is committed to maintaining a learning and working environment that is free from discrimination based on sex in accordance with Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 (Title IX), which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex in any federally funded educational programs or activities. The University\u2019s webpage about Title IX provides information about Title IX and how to report an incident. Resources Advising Dean's List College of Engineering Honors Program Pre-Professional Experiences Student Feedback Student Life Student Opportunities Technology Support Tutoring Women in Engineering E-Newsletter Undergraduate Admission Undergraduate Catalog Graduate Admissions Graduate Catalog Helpful Links Business Center Engineering IT Resources Event Calendar Questions or Concerns Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso College of Engineering Engineering Edge Center Engineering Building, Room E-201B 500 W University El Paso, Texas 79968 E: engredge@utep.edu P: (915) 747-5460 F: (915) 747-5616 THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Texas Veterans Portal Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 | SITE FEEDBACK Modal X"}
