{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/engineering/ctis/news/2025/ctis-phd-students-attend-2025-trb-annual-meeting.html", "title": "CTIS PhD Student's attend 2025 TRB Annual Meeting", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About Dean's Welcome Mission And Vision History College Leadership and Administration College Directory Advisory Board Alumni Spotlights News Academic Programs Undergraduate Programs Master's Programs Doctoral Programs Online Programs Certification Programs Departments Educational Leadership and Foundations Counseling and Special Education Teacher Education Research Office of Research Support Paso del Norte Partnership for Education Research Research Centers Recent Grants Resources Student Resources Dean's List Schedule Teacher Prep and ACP Appointment Business Center Faculty and Staff Resources Technical Support Become an Educator Become a Teacher...Inspire Change M.Ed. in Education Administration with Certification Become a Superintendent Giving Giving Events Past Events Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Center for Transportation Infrastructure Systems College of Engineering Main Content UTEP College of Engineering Center for Transportation Infrastructure Systems News 2025 UTEP College of Engineering Center for Transportation Infrastructure Systems News 2025 2025 TRB Annual Meeting CTIS PhD Student's attend 2025 TRB Annual Meeting Proudly showcasing the impactful research presented by CTIS PhD students at the 2025 TRB Annual Meeting! The 2025 Transportation Research Board (TRB) Annual Meeting featured valuable research contributions from CTIS PhD students Reza Kamalizadeh , Pedram Balooch Sirgani , Parastoo Bahri Iraei , Suhail Rashid Vaid, Farzad Khallaghi , Dasina Francis, Isaac Zu\u00f1iga and Hector Cruz, who presented their work through informative lectern and poster sessions. Their research covered important areas in transportation engineering, from continuous structural pavement evaluation to the integration of wireless power transfer systems in pavements. The presentations also addressed studies on asphalt mixture performance, including the effects of laboratory-molded density design, field sand content, binder grade, and hydrated lime on stripping potential, as well as sustainable practices through full-depth reclamation with engineered emulsions. These researchers contributed to advancing our understanding of sustainable transportation infrastructure through their dedicated work and research findings. Last updated on December 12, 2024, at 11:00 AM | Originally published on January 22, 2025. By\u202fCTIS\u202fStaff, UTEP Center for Transportation and Infrastructure Systems (CTIS) Technical Support Technical Support Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions EDUCATIONAL PSYCHOLOGY AND SPECIAL SERVICES DEPARTMENT College of Education External Link Test COE_Front.jpg EXPLORE OUR PROGRAMS College of Education Rodolfo Rincones Faculty and Course Information Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso College of Education Education Building, Room 414 500 W University El Paso, Texas 79902 E: education@utep.edu P: (915) 747-5572 THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Texas Veterans Portal Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 | SITE FEEDBACK Modal X"}
{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/engineering/ctis/news/2025/epcc-ctis-student-workers.html", "title": "Empowering Future Engineers: UTEP and EPCC\u2019s Collaborative Research in Transportation Infrastructure", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About Director's Message TLC UTC ASA Research Current Research Past Research Facilities Asphalt Binder Testing Laboratory Hot Mix Asphalt Laboratory Computer Lab Concrete Testing Laboratory Large Scale and Material Testing Laboratory Nondestructive Field Testing Soils and Aggregate Testing Laboratory Transportation Lab Publications Publications Products Products Events Events Directory Faculty Staff Research Assistants Volunteers Alumni News News Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Center for Transportation Infrastructure Systems College of Engineering Main Content UTEP College of Engineering Center for Transportation Infrastructure Systems News 2025 UTEP College of Engineering Center for Transportation Infrastructure Systems News 2025 CTIS | March 26, 2025 Empowering Future Engineers: UTEP and EPCC\u2019s Collaborative Research in Transportation Infrastructure Advancing Transportation research together EPCC students, Angel Salinas (left) and Paul Alvidrez (right), preparing sample asphalt mixes for laboratory testing at CTIS asphalt lab. The Center for Transportation Infrastructure Systems (CTIS) at the University of Texas at El Paso (UTEP) is proud to continue its collaboration with El Paso Community College (EPCC), fostering research advancements to meet the growing demand for engineers in transportation-related fields. This partnership reflects CTIS\u2019s commitment to developing the next generation of engineers through hands-on experience and high-level collaboration in research and education. The collaboration includes the TRIP (Transportation Research Immersive Program) five-day transportation research symposium to expose EPCC and early college high school students to the various aspects of transportation which includes planning, materials, construction, and the future of transportation with electric vehicles. Currently, eight EPCC students are actively engaged in this collaborative effort: Armando Gutierrez, Jesus Rosales, Elein Rodela, Tatiana Tellez Rodriquez, Luis Chavarria, Angel Salinas, Paul Alvidrez, and Elyan Flores. These students are participating as part of the Southern Plains Transportation Center, a U.S. Department of Transportation Region 6 Regional University Transportation Center (UTC), a national initiative designed to promote safe, efficient, and environmentally sustainable transportation systems. EPCC students participating in this program gain practical research experience, engineering skills and knowledge in transportation engineering by working alongside UTEP faculty and students. This initiative is a multi-state consortium involving institutions from Oklahoma, Louisiana, Texas, Arkansas, and New Mexico. Through this collaborative network, students, faculty, and transportation experts from across the country unite to address pressing transportation challenges and innovate in infrastructure development. CTIS Lab Pictures As part of the UTC program, these EPCC students are working alongside UTEP researchers and faculty, gaining invaluable insights into the complexities of transportation engineering. This initiative is a multi-state consortium involving institutions from Oklahoma, Louisiana, Texas, Arkansas, and New Mexico. Through this collaborative network, students, faculty, and transportation experts from across the country unite to address pressing transportation challenges and innovate in infrastructure development. The UTC program brings together two- and four-year institutions to create centers of excellence in specialized transportation research topics. EPCC students participating in the program have expressed their enthusiasm for the opportunities provided. They highlight the chance to engage with some of the most skilled and experienced civil engineers in their fields, as well as the benefits of collaborating with UTEP students. This exchange of ideas broadens their perspectives on research methodologies, problem-solving approaches, and practical applications in civil engineering transportation. The partnership continues to foster academic and professional growth for students while contributing to advancements in transportation research. Through this collaboration, both institutions remain dedicated to equipping future engineers with the skills and knowledge needed to address the evolving challenges of transportation infrastructure. <!--\n    .accWrapper > div {\n    padding-left:24px;\n    }\n    .collapseToggleControl.collapsed span.glyphicon:before {\n        content: \"\\002b\";\n    }\n    .collapseToggleControl span.glyphicon:before {\n        content: \"\\2212\";\n    }\n    .optionalblock {\n        margin-top: 30px;\n        margin-bottom: 30px;\n    }\n /*flex*/\n.highligtsWrapper {\n    display: flex;\n    display: -webkit-flex;\n    flex-wrap: wrap;\n    margin-left: -14px;\n}\n.highligtsWrapper .col-md-4:nth-last-child(1) {\n    margin-bottom: 30px;\n}\n.highligtsWrapper .well {\n\tbox-shadow:0px 2px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);-webkit-box-shadow:0px 2px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);;\n\theight: 100%;\n\tpadding: 0;\n}\n.highligtsBody {\n\tpadding: 0 24px 0 24px;\n}\n.highligtsBody .btn-primary {\n    \tdisplay:block;\n    \tmar