omplished alumni, including Nancy Beltran, Director of Concrete Pavements at the Cement Council of Texas; Luiza Barros, Director of Quality Advancement at Texas Materials; Gisel Carrasco, TxDOT Austin District Engineer; Ruben Carrasco, TxDOT Austin District Pavement Analysis and Design Branch Manager; and Aldo Madrid, TxDOT El Paso District Director of Construction. These industry leaders shared their career journeys and insights, inspiring attendees to envision new possibilities in transportation innovation. The day concluded with a vibrant research poster session, where CTIS students showcased their latest projects. This session fostered meaningful connections between students and alumni, creating an enriching platform for mentorship, collaboration, and knowledge exchange. Events such as CTIS Research Connect play a vital role in fostering connections among professionals, students, and faculty within the transportation engineering community, honoring its rich legacy while advancing its future. Last updated on December 12, 2024, at 11:00 AM | Originally published on December 12, 2024. By\u202fCTIS\u202fStaff, UTEP Center for Transportation and Infrastructure Systems (CTIS) <!--\n    .accWrapper > div {\n    padding-left:24px;\n    }\n    .collapseToggleControl.collapsed span.glyphicon:before {\n        content: \"\\002b\";\n    }\n    .collapseToggleControl span.glyphicon:before {\n        content: \"\\2212\";\n    }\n    .optionalblock {\n        margin-top: 30px;\n        margin-bottom: 30px;\n    }\n /*flex*/\n.highligtsWrapper {\n    display: flex;\n    display: -webkit-flex;\n    flex-wrap: wrap;\n    margin-left: -14px;\n}\n.highligtsWrapper .col-md-4:nth-last-child(1) {\n    margin-bottom: 30px;\n}\n.highligtsWrapper .well {\n\tbox-shadow:0px 2px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);-webkit-box-shadow:0px 2px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);;\n\theight: 100%;\n\tpadding: 0;\n}\n.highligtsBody {\n\tpadding: 0 24px 0 24px;\n}\n.highligtsBody .btn-primary {\n    \tdisplay:block;\n 