{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/engineering/ctis/news/2025/aspire-annual-meeting-2025.html", "title": "ASPIRE 2025 Annual Meeting", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About Director's Message TLC UTC ASA Research Current Research Past Research Facilities Asphalt Binder Testing Laboratory Hot Mix Asphalt Laboratory Computer Lab Concrete Testing Laboratory Large Scale and Material Testing Laboratory Nondestructive Field Testing Soils and Aggregate Testing Laboratory Transportation Lab Publications Publications Products Products Events Events Directory Faculty Staff Research Assistants Volunteers Alumni News News Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Center for Transportation Infrastructure Systems College of Engineering Main Content UTEP College of Engineering Center for Transportation Infrastructure Systems News 2025 UTEP College of Engineering Center for Transportation Infrastructure Systems News 2025 CTIS |November, 2025 <!--\n.carousel-inner > .item > img {\n            width: 100%;\n            height: 500px;         \n            object-fit: cover;     \n            }\n            .carousel-caption {\n                left: 0;\n                right: 0;\n                bottom: 0;\n                background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6);\n                padding: 20px;\n            }\n--> UTEP/EPCC CTIS Research Students and Faculty Present at ASPIRE 2025 Annual Meeting CTIS Staff and Students Missel Sanchez serving as Master of Ceremony Pedram Balooch presenting research project UTEP Research Team testing fiber optic sensors EV Truck used for electrified roadway testing Isaac Zu\u00f1iga and Pedro Chavez at the Innovation Challenge Previous Next On November 2nd \u2013 5th, the UTEP and CTIS research students and staff participated in the ASPIRE Annual Meeting 2025. The ASPIRE Annual Meeting 2025 in Logan, Utah, was a week-long event of collaboration and innovation, bringing together researchers, students, industry partners, and leaders from core and affiliated universities to advance the future of electrified transportation infrastructure. This year's meeting highlighted the innovative research, exciting technology, and meaningful connections that are the foundation of the ASPIRE community. From the first-ever Innovation Challenge to insightful discussions on the future of electrified transportation, the meeting showcased the momentum driving the research forward with poster presentations from students working at the CTIS with projects associated with ASPIRE. Among the students who presented where Pedram Balooch with his project of \u201cSimulation of Thermal-Structural Performance of Electrified Asphalt Pavements Using Accelerated Testing.\u201d Elyan Flores and Tatiana Tellez-Rodriguez (both affiliated students from EPCC) also presented the \u201cEvaluating Flexural and Shear Strengths in Pavements with Embedded Dynamic Wireless Power Transfer (DWPT) Module\u201d and the \u201cUse of Distributed Strain Sensing (DSS) Fiber Optic System for Structural Monitoring of Pavements with Embedded DWPT,\u201d respectively. In this annual event, Isaac Zu\u00f1iga and Pedro Chavez, CTIS research graduate students, were participants of the Innovation Challenge while also being members of the Council of Presidency in the ASPIRE Student Association. CTIS Alumni Missel Sanchez served as Master of Ceremony for the Industry and Innovation Day, facilitating conversations on barriers and potential solutions for ASPIRE's next major milestone. The UTEP research team- Pedram Balooch, Elyan Flores, Dr. Hector Cruz, and Dr. Cesar Tirado- visited the Electric Vehicle Roadway (EVR) to conduct follow-up testing on fiber optic sensors that were installed in September 2024. The purpose of this visit was to evaluate the functionality of the distributed fiber optic strain sensors embedded at the EVR track and to assess the quality and reliability of the data they provide, along with strain measurements obtained when trafficked by Class 6 and Class 8 EV trucks. For the testing, both trucks were driven over the instrumented section. The collected measurements provide real-time information on pavement responses, helping evaluate the structural response that can support the calibration of pavement response models. <!--\n    .accWrapper > div {\n    padding-left:24px;\n    }\n    .collapseToggleControl.collapsed span.glyphicon:before {\n        content: \"\\002b\";\n    }\n    .collapseToggleControl span.glyphicon:before {\n        content: \"\\2212\";\n    }\n    .optionalblock {\n        margin-top: 30px;\n        margin-bottom: 30px;\n    }\n /*flex*/\n.highligtsWrapper {\n    display: flex;\n    display: -webkit-flex;\n    flex-wrap: wrap;\n    margin-left: -14px;\n}\n.highligtsWrapper .col-md-4:nth-last-child(1) {\n    margin-bottom: 30px;\n}\n.highligtsWrapper .well {\n\tbox-shadow:0px 2px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);-webkit-box-shadow:0px 2px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);;\n\theight: 100%;\n\tpadding: 0;\n}\n.highligtsBody {\n\tpadding: 0 24px 0 24px;\n}\n.highligtsBody .btn-primary {\n    \tdisplay:block;\n    \tmargin-top: 30px;\n}\n\n.highligtsWrapper .col-md-4 {\n   margin-bottom: 30px;\n}\n\n.lightWhiteBg {\n\tbackground: rgba(255,255,255,.85);\n    padding: 4px 24px 24px 24px;\n    margin-bottom: 20px;\n}\n--> <!--\ndiv.facebook .pp_top .pp_left{background:#fff;}div.facebook .pp_top .pp_middle{background:#fff;}div.facebook .pp_top .pp_right{backgrou