tudents participated in the first ASPIRE Student Innovation Challenge at the 2025 Annual Meeting, collaborating in a 24-hour, industry-mentored competition to develop innovative solutions to real-world transportation challenges. Read More EPCC and Early College High School Students Get a Behind-the-Scenes Look at TXDOT with CTIS As part of the 2025 Transportation Research Immersive Program (TRIP), sponsored by the Southern Plains Transportation Center (SPTC), students from El Paso Community College (EPCC) and local Early College High Schools recently teamed up with the Center for Transportation Infrastructure Systems (CTIS) for an exclusive visit to the Texas Department of Transportation (TXDOT) El Paso Regional Headquarters. Read more. EPCC Students Explore Engineering at the 2025 Transportation Research Immersive Program (TRIP) El Paso Community College (EPCC) and Early College High School (ECHS) students participated in the 2025 Transportation Research Immersive Program (TRIP) , sponsored by the Southern Plains Transportation Center (SPTC), a USDOT Regional University Transportation Center. Read more. UTEP CTIS Graduate Students Shine at 2025 IAI Summit El Paso, TX \u2013 May 25, 2025 \u2014 Graduate student researchers from UTEP\u2019s Center for Transportation Infrastructure Systems (CTIS) made a strong impression at the 2025 Infrastructure Advancement Institute (IAI) Summit. Read More. CTIS Welcomes NREL Representatives to Foster Research Alignment This visit marks an important step toward fostering impactful partnerships that advance innovation and expand the reach of both institutions' research missions. Read More. UTEP Students Shine at 2025 Asphalt Road-eo, Irish Miners Take 3rd Place A huge congratulations to our UTEP undergraduate civil engineering students who are part of and represent the Center for Transportation Infrastructure Systems (CTIS) for their outstanding performance at the 2025 Asphalt Road-eo! Read More. Community Outreach CTIS Lab Tours Read More. Advancing Transportation research together The Center for Transportation Infrastructure Systems (CTIS) at the University of Texas at El Paso (UTEP) is proud to continue its collaboration with El Paso Community College (EPCC). Read more. CTIS Graduate Students attend 2025 TRB Annual Meeting Proudly showcasing the impactful research presented by CTIS PhD students at the 2025 TRB Annual Meeting! Read more. TRB 2025 Highlights Excellence of DDETP Fellows and TRB Minority Fellows! Read more. Congratulations to Zahra Mohajeri for Being Selected as an IRF Fellow for the Class of 2025! CTIS is proud to announce one of our students for getting selected for the IRF Fellowship Program! We want to extend our congratulations to Zahra Mohajeri! Read more. Exploring the Future of Concrete: Key Insights from the Concrete Innovations and Challenges Workshop On November 20, 2024, the Cement Council of Texas (CCT), in collaboration with the Center for Transportation Infrastructure Systems (CTIS), hosted a groundbreaking workshop focused on advancements in concrete technology. Held at the University of Texas at El Paso, the event brought together industry leaders, engineers, and researchers to discuss innovative solutions and tackle pressing challenges in the field of concrete construction. Read more. Bridging the Past and Future: CTIS Research Connect On November 21, 2024, the Center for Transportation Infrastructure Systems (CTIS) hosted CTIS Research Connect: Bridging the Past and Future at the University of Texas at El Paso.\u00a0This forum served as a bridge between the groundbreaking contributions of CTIS alumni and the promising future of transportation engineering. Read more. CTIS students selected for the 2024-2025 Dwight D. Eisenhower Student Fellowship Program CTIS is proud to announce that five of our students got selected for the Dwight D. Eisenhower Transportation Fellowship Program. We want to extend our congratulations to Sebastian Morales, Jesus Macias, Flavio Chavarria, Hector Cruz, and Emilio Torres. Read more CTIS Present at 2024 Infrastructure Advancement Institute (IAI) Summit Conference CTIS researchers and graduate students took part in the 2024 Infrastructure Advancement Institute (IAI) Summit, that took place in Denton, TX. Read more CTIS PhD student Farzad Khallaghi passes PhD qualifiers exam CTIS is pleased to announce that Farzad Khallaghi, a PhD student in Civil Engineering, has successfully passed his qualification exam. Read more CTIS Graduate Student Researchers Advance to PhD Candidacy READ MORE CTIS welcomes new research students READ MORE CTIS welcomes Hector Cruz as a research associate READ MORE Dr. Abdallah Attends 2024 Transportation Industry and Workforce Symposium READ MORE CTIS research presented at the 97th Transportation Short Course in College Station, Texas READ MORE How can current asphalt mix design guidelines be adjusted to create better performing recycled mixtures? READ MORE UTEP Teams Participated at the 2023 Asphalt ROAD-EO in Buda, Texas READ MORE Stanton and Ysleta Bridges Microsimulation Models: Update READ MORE <!--\n    .accWrapper > div {\n    padding-left:24px;\n    }\n    .collapseToggleControl.collapsed span.glyphicon:before {\n        content: \"\\002b\";\n    }\n    .collapseToggleControl span.glyphicon:before {\n        content: \"\\2212\";\n    }\n    .optionalblock {\n        margin-top: 30px;\n        margin-bottom: 30px;\n    }\n /*flex*/\n.highligtsWrapper {\n    display: flex;\n    display: -webkit-flex;\n    flex-wrap: wrap;\n    margin-left: -14px;\n}\n.highligtsWrapper .col-md-4:nth-last-child(1) {\n    margin-bottom: 30px;\n}\n.highligtsWrapper .well {\n\tbox-shadow:0px 2px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);-webkit-box-shadow:0px 2px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);;\n\theight: 100%;\n\tpadding: 0;\n}\n.highligtsBody {\n\tpadding: 0 24px 0 24px;\n}\n.highligtsBody .btn-primary {\n    \tdisplay:block;\n    \tmargin-top: 30px;\n}\n\n.highligtsWrapper .col-md-4 {\n   margin-bottom: 3