ant, multicultural Paso del Norte border region, we are dedicated to offering boundary-breaking education. Our programs are designed to inspire innovative thinkers, engaged citizens, and leaders who shape the future of education. We specialize in areas critical to today\u2019s world: teacher and bilingual education, leadership, early childhood, STEM and computer science education, counseling, literacy, social and cultural foundations, special education, and mental health services. Our commitment to community engagement is reflected in our partnerships with local schools, districts, and community organizations, creating a dynamic ecosystem that benefits all. Through close collaboration with El Paso\u2019s school districts and the broader community, our faculty design innovative programs and exceptional educational experiences. Whether you\u2019re pursuing a bachelor\u2019s, master\u2019s, or doctoral degree, our team is dedicated to your success, bridging the gap between classroom learning and real-world application. At the UTEP College of Education, we\u2019re not just preparing professionals \u2013 we\u2019re building leaders who make lasting contributions as educators, scholars, and public servants. Our focus is clear: to foster excellence in teaching, learning, and leadership, all while creating a positive impact on the students, children, and families we serve. We believe education transforms lives. Join us at UTEP College of Education, where you\u2019ll find programs designed to help you achieve your professional goals while contributing to a bold legacy of shaping a brighter future for education. Sincerely, Clifton Tanabe, Ph.D., J.D. Dean About Dean's Welcome Mission And Vision College Leadership and Administration History Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Graduate Inquiry Form Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso College of Education Education Building, Room 414 500 W University El Paso, Texas 79902 E: education@utep.edu P: (915) 747