{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/engineering/homecoming/", "title": "Homecoming", "text": "Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search Home Homecoming Distinguished Alumni Past Distinguished Alumni Gold Nugget Past Gold Nuggets Photo Gallery Photo Gallery RSVP APO Breakfast CE and CEM Homecoming Alumni Luncheon Gold Nugget and Alumni Breakfast Giving Give Now Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Homecoming College of Engineering Main Content UTEP College of Engineering Homecoming Save the Date: Sept. 21-27, 2025 LEARN MORE Previous Next UTEP College of Engineering Homecoming Welcome Home, Miner Engineers and Computer Scientists! The UTEP College of Engineering invites all engineering and computer science alumni, friends, and supporters to join us in celebrating Homecoming Week: September 21\u201327, 2025! Each year, the Gold Nugget Award honors exceptional alumni who have excelled professionally and remain deeply connected to UTEP. In 2025, we are especially proud to celebrate two outstanding leaders from the College of Engineering: Ruben Chavez (B.S. in Civil Engineering, 1995), founder and president of CEA Engineering Group, whose work has transformed infrastructure across the region; and Bernardino Olague (B.S. in Civil Engineering, 1991; M.S. in Civil Engineering, 2001), president and CEO of LOI Engineers, recognized for his leadership in geotechnical engineering and his commitment to supporting future engineers through mentorship and service. Their achievements reflect the impact and excellence of Miner Engineers. Read the announcement . Whether you graduated five years ago or fifty, this is your chance to reconnect and see how Miner Engineers continue to make an impact. On this page, you\u2019ll find 