) Program at The University of Texas at El Paso, serves as an overarching entity to coordinate activities and groups that synergistically encourage, enlighten, and empower (E3) women in engineering. Specifically, the WIN E3 Program develops initiatives designed to increase and support the number of women in engineering majors and careers. WIN was envisioned to have three major groups the drive entwined activities. The groups are students within the College of Engineering and K-12 students, faculty in the College of Engineering who foster a culture that promotes equity and professional practicing engineers interested in sharing their experiences, skills, and knowledge to assist and encourage girls and young women to pursue an engineering career. Activities Women in Engineering Brunch organized by ASCE El Paso Branch YMG September 14, 2024 UTEP Campus RSVP by September 6 E-Week @ UTEP: Introduce a Girl to Engineering Luncheon February 20, 2025 Activities, 9:30 ~ 11:00am Lunch, 11:30am - 1:30pm UTEP Campus NCWIT Aspirations in Computing Reception & Ceremony April 2025 Time & Location TBA Women in STEM Conference tentatively April 2025 Time & Location TBA Photo Gallery Partners/Sponsors ASCE Texas Section \u2013 El Paso Branch YMG El Paso Electric Cummins National Center for Women & Information Technology She Creates Shell Oil Company Texas Department of Transportation Women in engineering and computing student organizations at UTEP Young Women\u2019s STEAM Research & Preparatory Academy Resources Advising Dean's List College of Engineering Honors Program Pre-Professional Experiences Student Feedback Student Life Student Opportunities Technology Support Tutoring Women in Engineering - Photo Gallery E-Newsletter Undergraduate Admission Undergraduate Catalog Graduate Admissions Graduate Catalog Helpful Links Business Center Engineering IT Resources Event Calendar Questions or Concerns Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso College of Engineering Engineering Bu