{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/engineering/graduateceremony/", "title": "Graduate Hooding Ceremony", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About Administration Fact Sheet Accreditation Alumni Academic Programs Degrees & Programs Undergraduate Programs Undergraduate Catalog Graduate Programs Graduate Catalog Departments Aerospace and Mechanical Engineering Civil, Environmental and Construction Engineering Computer Science Electrical and Computer Engineering Engineering Education and Leadership Industrial, Manufacturing and Systems Engineering Metallurgical, Materials and Biomedical Engineering Engineering Edge Center Research Research Centers and Facilities Awards and Recognition Research and Support Services Student Opportunities Research Newsfeed Resources Advising Dean's List College of Engineering Honors Program Pre-Professional Experiences Student Feedback Student Life Student Opportunities Technology Support Tutoring Women in Engineering E-Newsletter K-12 K-12 Outreach Aspirations in Computing Discover-E E-Week @ UTEP ExciTES Robotics Events E-Week Homecoming Graduate Hooding Ceremony The Order of the Engineer TCM Day Giving Give Now Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Graduate Hooding Ceremony College of Engineering Main Content Hooding Ceremony LEARN MORE Previous Next <!--\na {\n\t color: #337ab7;\n\t text-decoration: none;\n}\n a:hover, a:focus {\n\t color: #23527c;\n\t text-decoration: underline;\n}\n--> The Graduate Hooding Ceremony Join us in honoring our engineering graduates at the College of Engineering Pre-Commencement Ceremony. This special event celebrates our graduates with both the Order of the Engineer Ceremony and the Graduate Hooding Ceremony . Bachelor of Science candidates will recite the Obligation of an Engineer and receive their rings, while master\u2019s and PhD graduates will be hooded by their advisors, recognizing their academic achievements. Thursday, December 11, 2025 7:30 pm Don Haskins Center, UTEP Campus regalia required for all graduates Group Photos: 6:30 pm \u2013 Department of Aerospace & Mechanical Engineering 6:40 pm \u2013 Department of Civil, Environmental & Construction Engineering 6:45 pm \u2013 Department of Computer Science 6:50 pm \u2013 Department of Electrical & Computer Engineering 6:55 pm \u2013 Department of Engineering Education & Leadership 7:00 pm \u2013 Department of Industrial, Manufacturing & Systems Engineering 7:05 pm \u2013 Department of Metallurgical, Materials and Biomedical Engineering Questions regarding group photos before the ceremony and individual photos taken on stage during the ceremony can be directed to engineer@utep.edu Students Family & Guests Faculty Volunteers Students Tickets for Family & Guests: Guest tickets are not required to enter the Don Haskins Center. All seats are on a first-come, first-served basis. Reserving seats is prohibited. The doors will open one hour prior to the ceremony. Regalia: All students must wear regalia which includes cap & gown. Refer to the UTEP Commencement FAQ webpage on how to purchase regalia. Check-in & Group Photos: Arrive at 6:00pm at the Don Haskins South Entrance concourse to receive your name card. If you do not receive your card before your Department\u2019s Group Photos, you will receive it while in line up to 20 minutes before the ceremony starts. Professional photos will be taken of all graduates crossing the stage receiving their ring; inquiries should be directed to the Customer Service Department at (800) 261-2576, online at www.gradimages.com , or email ecc.giservice@gradimages.net . The Order of the Engineer Ring: Graduate students who did not participate in the Order of the Engineer as undergraduates are eligible to receive their ring by taking the Obligation of the Engineer oath. Please note that while they will be formally inducted and receive their ring, they will not participate in the on-stage crossing portion of the ceremony. Please visit the QuestionPro link to get your ring size and submit a request for a ring. If you have already participated in the ceremony and have lost your ring, you can request a replacement by visiting the Order of the Engineer website . Questions & Concerns: Email engineer@utep.edu . FAMILY & GUESTS Tickets: Guest tickets are not required to enter the Don Haskins Center. Seats: All seats are on a first-come, first-served basis. Reserving seats is prohibited. Please review the University\u2019s Clear Bag Policy - Pol\u00edtica de Bolsa Transparente and Prohibited Items - Articulos Prohibidos and leave strollers and carriages in your car. Parking: Family and friends are encouraged to park at the Glory Road Garage . Please visit the following webpage for further instructions: https://www.utep.edu/commencement/guest-information/directions-and-parking.html Photos: A professional photographer will be on-site taking department group photos with faculty and students, photos of individual students crossing the stage and headshot photos will be taken during the event. Faculty Tickets: Faculty do not need tickets for this ceremony. Regalia: Regalia should be worn for the group photo and ceremony. Group Photos & Check In: Faculty are encouraged to park in lots GR5 or GR3 and check in at the Gordon Family Courtside Club of the Don Haskins Center. Please arrive 10 minutes prior to your Department\u2019s group photo time. Please visit the following webpage for further instructions: https://www.utep.edu/commencement/guest-information/directions-and-parking.html Faculty Speakers: Speakers should report at the South Entrance for the Don Haskins Center 20 minutes prior to the start of the ceremony to lead the procession. Volunteers Individuals interested in volunteering should contact Paulina Alvarado at palvarado4@utep.edu . View past recognitions and previous College ceremonies click here <!--\nbody {\n    position: relative;\n}\n\n/*header bg fix*/\n@media (min-width:1250px ) and (max-width: 1364px){\n\t.headerContainer {\n\t    width: 100%;\n\t}\n}\n/*Carousel FW*/\n#container + .container {\n\tmax-width: none !important;\n\twidth: auto!important;\n}\n.slide-transfer {\n    display:none!important;\n}\n.video-wrapper {\n\tmax-height: none !important;\n}\n.carousel-caption {\n\tdisplay: none;\n}\n.slide-transfer {\n\tdisplay: none;\n}\n/*FullWidthSection*/\n.fw-section {\n\tpadding-top: 40px;\n\tpadding-bottom: 60px;\n}\n.sectionAnchor {\n    padding-top:135px;\n    margin-top:-135px;\n}\n.fw-section h2 {\n\ttext-align: center;\n}\n.fw-section:after {\n\tclear: both;\n}\n.container-narrow {\n\tmax-width: 800px;\n}\n.row {\n\tmargin-left: 0;\n\tmargin-right: 0;\n}\n@media (max-width: 991px){\n    .col-md-4 {\n        width:100%;\n    }\n}\n/*Gray Bg Section*/\n.background-gray {\n\tbackground-color: #f2f2f2;\n}\n/*Blue Bg Section*/\n.background-blue {\n\tbackground-color: #041E42;\n\tcolor: #fff;\n}\n.background-blue h2 {\n\tcolor: #fff;\n}\n.background-blue .btn-primary, .background-blue a.btn-primary {\n    background-color: #FF8200;\n}\n.background-blue .btn-primary:hover, .background-blue .btn-primary:focus, .background-blue a.btn-primary:hover, .background-blue a.btn-primary:focus {\n    color: #041b3c;\n    background-color: #ddd;\n}\n/*flex*/\n.highligtsWrapper {\n    display: flex;\n    display: -webkit-flex;\n    flex-wrap: wrap;\n}\n.highligtsWrapper .well {\n\tbox-shadow:0px 2px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);-webkit-box-shadow: