{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/engineering/k12/excites/", "title": "ExciTES", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search Home K-12 Aspirations in Computing Aspirations in Computing Discover-E Discover-E E-Week @ UTEP E-Week @ UTEP ExciTES ExciTES Robotics Robotics Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support K-12 Outreach College of Engineering Main Content UTEP College of Engineering K-12 Outreach excites UTEP College of Engineering K-12 Outreach excites ExciTES Summer Institute ExciTES encourages rising 3rd graders through 11th graders from the El Paso/Ciudad Juarez region to use their knowledge, imagination, and creativity to 1) become aware of the diverse fields and careers of engineering and computing, and 2) be encouraged to attend college, specifically, UTEP's College of Engineering. During any sessions in the ExciTES Summer Institute, students will meet other students of similar age while engaged in inquiry-based and team-oriented projects and activities developed by faculty and facilitated by undergraduate students. The exploration of the various engineering fields and careers will connect to the Bachelor of Science degrees offered through the UTEP College of Engineering. Application Process Students, along with their parents, can apply online to the ExciTES Summer Institute starting April 1. An exact timeline of the application process is shown on our online application page . Upon acceptance to ExciTES, fees will be collected on the first day of the session. Do not send payment prior to being accepted. 2026 ExciTES Sessions & Fees Rising 3 rd thru 5 th graders \u2013 Elementary Sessions \u2013 $150/student/week Robotics Session: dates in June/July TBA Rising 6 th thru 9 th graders \u2013 ExciTES Sessions \u2013 $200/student/week ExciTES Session: dates in June/July TBA Rising 9 th thru 11 th graders \u2013 Challenge Sessions \u2013 $200/student/week Mining Engineering Camp Session 1: Jun 22-26, all-day/residential experience; cost TBA Mining Engineering Camp Session 2: Jul 13-17, all-day/residential experience; cost TBA Rising 6 th thru 12 th graders - Cyber and Artificial Intelligence (AI) Camps \u2013 FREE! Cyber Camp I (2 weeks): June 9-13 and 16-20, 10am-2pm AI Camp I: June 23-27, 10am-2pm Cyber Camp II (2 weeks): July 7-11 and 14-18, 10am-2pm AI Camp II: July 21-25, 10am-2pm/li> Learn More Students with disabilities ages 14 thru 21 \u2013 ExploreSTEAM \u2013 FREE! Internet of Things: June 23-27, 9am-2pm Computational Engineering: July 7-11, 9am-2pm Artificial Intelligence: July 14-18, 9am-2pm Augmented Reality/Virtual Reality: July 21-25, 9am-2pm Learn More Dual Credit/AP Course Takers and EPCC Students Transportation Research Immersive Program (TRIP) \u2013 June 23-27 Learn More Teachers ASM Materials Camp: Jun 8-12 Learn More ExciTES Team Partners/Sponsors Consortium for Education and Research in Electronics for Extreme Environments (E3C) NSF Advancing Sustainability through Powered Infrastructure for Roadway Electrification (ASPIRE) FIRST Inspires UTEP Civil Engineering Department UTEP Computer Science Department UTEP Electrical and Computer Engineering Department UTEP Metallurgical, Material and Biomedical Engineering Department UTEP Upward Bound Young Women\u2019s STEAM Research & Preparatory Academy K-12 Outreach K-12 Homepage Aspirations in Computing Discover-E E-Week @ UTEP ExciTES - FAQs - Online Application Robotics Undergraduate Admission U