 Distinction: Complete the College of Engineering requirements Complete a minimum of 4 full terms with UHP Maintain a cumulative GPA of 3.5 and above Attend 4 UHP Group Events Submit necessary practice forms and completion forms On the last semester before graduation, student must submit the Senior Clearance From by deadline High Impact Experiences for Honors Credit Capstone Experience: allowed once and cannot be part of degree plan Community Engagement: allowed once and must participate in 40 hours of service and register using The CUE Creative Activities: multiple engagements are allowed and must have a significant contribution to the student competition Internships: multiple engagements in respective field are allowed and register for College of Engineering course or register using Job Mine/Handshake Professional Preparation: multiple engagements are allowed and shadow professional in respective field for 40 hours Research and Scholarly Activity: multiple engagements are allowed; must register for RSRC 4033 and obtain a grade of S Student Leadership: allowed once and just be involved in a UTEP registered student organization as an officer for 1 year Study Abroad/Away: allowed twice and abroad experience or faculty-led international study activity while a UTEP student with at least a 3.5 GPA Student Employment: only Research Assistant or Teaching Assistant are allowed Contact Info University Honors Program Office, uhpnetwork@utep.edu For specific questions regarding College of Engineering High Impact activities: Contact: Gabby G\u00e1ndara , University Honors Faculty Council Representative, gabby@utep.edu Edge Experiences Community Engagement Internships Research Opportunities Student Employment Student Leadership Study Abroad-Study Away College of Engineering Honors Program Undergraduate Admission Undergraduate Catalog Graduate Admissions Graduate Catalog Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso College of Engineering Engineering Edge Center Engineering