ration: underline;\n}\n--> Join CS The Computer Science (CS) Department is\u00a0committed to providing our students with an innovative educational program that contributes to their effective learning and prepares our graduates to become leaders and innovators in computer science. Learn More Help Improve CS The Computer Science Student Council (CSSC) represents and advocates the interests of Computer Science students. This Council serves to facilitate communication and collaboration between the students, CS organizations, faculty, and staff. Learn More Reconnect with CS UTEP CS is working hard to educate students and participants in our regional and national community about the importance of using computer science to foster innovative thinking and to solve real world problems. Learn More <!--\n.highligtsWrapper {\n\t    display: flex;\n\t    display: -webkit-flex;\n\t    flex-wrap: wrap;\n\t}\n.highligtsWrapper .col-md-4 {\n           margin-bottom: 30px;\n    }\n.highligtsWrapper .well {\n\t    box-shadow: 0px 2px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);\n\t    -webkit-box-shadow: 0px 2px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);\n\t    height: 100%;\n\t    padding: 0;\n\t     text-align:center;\n    }\n.highligtsBody {\n    \tpadding: 0 24px 0 24px;\n\t}\n.highligtsBody p:nth-last-of-type(1) {\n    \tmargin-bottom: 45px;\n\t}\n.highligtsBody .btn-primary {\n        display: block;\n    margin-top: 15px !important;\n}\n--> CS Facebook Feed <!--\n@media(max-width:1400px){\n        .picture{\n            display:none;\n        }\n    }\n--> Contribute to CS We thank our contributors for working with our department to engage CS students and support the growth of the department! Contributions\u00a0have impact in numerous ways: supporting faculty and students involved in research, assisting the department in enhancing students' educational paths, serving as role models and mentors, supporting departmental efforts focused on the advancement of underrepresented groups in computing, contributing to the eco