{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/newsfeed/2023/utep-kicks-off-spring-2023-with-miner-welcome.html", "title": "UTEP Kicks Off Spring 2023 with Miner Welcome", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Newsfeed Main Content UTEP Kicks Off Spring 2023 with Miner Welcome UTEP is welcoming students to campus for the spring semester with a two-week event series called Miner Welcome. Students are invited to learn more about opportunities and resources on campus and connect with their fellow students. Miner Welcome events take place during the first two weeks of the spring semester and provide fun opportunities for students to get engaged and learn about campus resources. Photo: J.R. Hernandez / UTEP Marketing and Communications The series kicks off with a Martin Luther King Jr. Day celebration at 11:30 a.m. Tuesday, Jan. 17 at Centennial Plaza. Hosted by the Student Engagement and Leadership Center, the Multicultural Greek Council and the Black Student Union, the event will feature performers and speakers who will honor King and other civil rights leaders. Speakers and performers include Carleton Brown, Ph.D., associate professor in the College of Education, and student Abeni Merriweather, who will perform \u201cLift Every Voice and Sing,\u201d known as the Black national anthem. Free food will also be available. With more than 25 Miner Welcome events scheduled, students will have no shortage of things to do their first two weeks back on campus, including learning more about the Student Recreation Center, sororities and fraternities, and other ways to get involved. \u201cThe goal behind Miner Welcome is to help our students either as first-time students or returning students to engage on campus with our campus community and to learn about resources and opportunities for them,\u201d said Charlin Jones-Chavez, Ph.D., assistant dean of students at UTEP. Chalk the Plaza is a new event for the spring semester and takes place Monday, Jan. 23. Students are invited to show off their artistic prowess through chalk illustrations at the Union Plaza. First held in Fall 2021 and continued again in Fall 2022, this is the first time this event will be held in the spring. \u201cWe have some amazingly talented students on our campus,\u201d Jones-Chavez said. \u201cThis is an awesome opportunity for them to create some artwork that gets to live at the Union Plaza for about 24 to 48 hours.\u201d Students can also look forward to the Get Involved and Well-being Fair on Wednesday, Jan. 18 and Thursday, Jan. 19 at the Union. \u201cIt\u2019s a chance to interact with our student organizations and learn about departmental resources available to students,\u201d Jones-Chavez said. Other Miner Welcome events include: 7 p.m. Saturday, Jan. 21: Men\u2019s Basketball vs. Florida Atlantic University Show your Miner pride and watch the UTEP men\u2019s basketball team take on Florida Atlantic University at the Don Haskins Center. Free student tickets are available at www.utepminers.com/tickets . Click on \u201cClaim Student Tickets.\u201d 3-5 p.m. Monday, Jan. 23: Leadership Kick-Off Spring 2023 Kick off your leadership development with activities and hot cocoa. Students are invited to join the UTEP Student Engagement and Leadership Center in Union Building East, Bhutan Lounge. 6 p.m. Monday, Jan. 23: Get Rec\u2019d Students will experience sports activities, outdoor adventure clinics, fitness classes and swimming at the Student Rec Center, as well as learn about job opportunities, intramural sports, outdoor adventure trips and more. 10 a.m. Wednesday, Jan. 25: Meet the Greeks Students are invited to visit Centennial Plaza to learn more about the sororities and fraternities available on campus. Check out utep.edu/MinerWelcome for a full roster of events. Last Updated on January 13, 2023 at 12:00 AM | Originally published January 13, 2023 By Julia Hettiger UTEP Marketing and Communications var title = document.getElementById (\"newsTitle\").innerHTML;\n    var loc = document.location.href;\n    document.getElementById(\"newsMailAnchor\").href = \"mailto:?subject=\" + encodeURI (title) + \"&body=\" + encodeURI(loc); 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Texas Veterans Portal Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 | SITE FEEDBACK"}
