nt Campus Community Engagement 2026 Carnegie Community Engagement Classification: UTEP Application Highlights The University of Texas at El Paso (UTEP) submitted its application for the 2026 Carnegie Community Engagement Classification in April 2025. The application was led by the Center for Community Engagement (CCE) in collaboration with UTEP faculty, staff, students, and community partners. This national classification recognizes institutions that demonstrate a sustained commitment to reciprocal, impactful community engagement across teaching, research, and partnerships. UTEP has held this designation since 2010 and was reclassified in 2020 . The 2026 application reflects our university\u2019s continued leadership in building strong, collaborative relationships with our community to advance educational equity, promote health and well-being, foster economic development, and strengthen civic life across the Paso del Norte region. We will be notified of our classification status in January 2026 . About the Carnegie Community Engagement Classification The Carnegie Community Engagement Classification is an elective designation awarded by the Carnegie Foundation for the Advancement of Teaching to higher education institutions that demonstrate institutionalized practices of community engagement. The classification recognizes campuses that are aligned with their communities through teaching and learning, research and scholarship, and reciprocal partnerships that contribute to the public good. Learn more: View Carnegie Classifications <!--\n.academic-year-container {\n  max-width: 1000px;\n  margin: auto;\n  border-radius: 20px !important;\n  overflow: hidden !important;\n  box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1) !important;\n}\n\n.academic-year-header {\n  background: #041E42;\n  color: white;\n  font-family: 'Tungsten';\n  font-size: 40px;\n  font-weight: bold;\n  padding: 15px 20px;\n}\n\n.academic-year-grid {\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);\n  gap: 10px; /* space between tiles */\n  background: white;\n  padding: 15px;\n}\n\n.academic-year-card {\n  background: #f8dfc2 !important;\n  border: 1px solid #ddd !important;\n  border-radius: 30px !important;\n  padding: 10px 15px !important;\n  transition: background-color 0.3s ease, color 0.3s ease !important;\n}\n\n.academic-year-card:nth-child(even) {\n  background: #9fa6c0 !important; /* subtle striping */\n}\n\n.academic-year-card:hover {\n  background: #FF8200 !important;\n  color: #fff !important;\n}\n.academic-year-card:nth-child(even):hover {\n  background: #041E42 !important; /* alternate hover background */\n  color: #fff !important;\n}\n\n.academic-year-card:hover .academic-year-stat,\n.academic-year-card:hover .academic-year-title {\n  color: #fff !important;\n}\n.academic-year-card:nth-child(even):hover .academic-year-stat,\n.academic-year-card:nth-child(even):hover .academic-year-title {\n  color: #fff !important;\n}\n\n.academic-year-stat {\n  font-weight: bold !important;\n  font-family: 'Tungsten';\n  font-size: 60px !important;\n  text-align: center;\n  color: #FF8200 !important;\n}\n\n.academic-year-title {\n  color: #FF8200 !important;\n  font-family: 'Tungsten';\n  font-size: 30px !important;\n  text-align: center;\n}\n.academic-year-card:nth-child(even) .academic-year-title,\n.academic-year-card:nth-child(even) .academic-year-stat{\n  color: #041E42 !important;\n}\n--> ACADEMIC YEAR 2022-2023 DATA 6,894 Students in Service Learning 740,000 Community Engaged Hours 235 Community Engaged Faculty 7,365 Students Contributing to Community Service $22M Economic Impact (Independent Sector) 335 Community Engaged Classes To view specific data per each UTEP college/unit click here . Highlights from UTEP\u2019s 2026 Carnegie Application UTEP\u2019s 2026 application demonstrated the depth and breadth of the university\u2019s community engagement, including: 197 active community partnerships across the Paso del Norte region. More than 85 faculty members engaged in community-based teaching and research. The Community Engagement & Leadership (CEL) course designation expanded across colleges to promote community-based learning. The Community-University Engagement (CUE) platform tracks more than 100,000 student community engagement hours annually. UTEP\u2019s 2030 Strategic Plan includes Community Impact and Public Service as a core institutional priority. UTEP\u2019s research agenda addresses community priorities such as public health, education equity, workforce development, environmental sustainability, and border issues. The Center for Community Engagement (CCE) continues to serve as UTEP\u2019s institutional hub for advancing community engagement across teaching, research, and service. Application Writing Team The preparation of UTEP\u2019s 2026 Carnegie Community Engagement Classification application was a collaborative effort . We extend our sincere thanks to the writing team, led by the Center for Community Engagement, with significant contributions from: Faculty and staff across UTEP\u2019s colleges, schools, and departments Members of the Provost\u2019s Community Engagement Council Community partners who provided valuable input and feedback Institutional leaders and staff from: Academic Affairs Student Affairs Center for Institutional Evaluation, Research, and Planning (CIERP) Office of Research and Innovation This collective effort reflects UTEP\u2019s deep institutional commitment to advancing community engagement as a public-serving research university. View the Writing Team Members Next Steps UTEP will be notified of its 2026 Carnegie Community Engagement Classification status in January 2026 . In the meantime, the university continues to strengthen its community-based teaching, research, and partnerships in alignment with its mission and strategic priorities. \u201cCommunity engagement is core to who we are at UTEP, and I intend to continue making it a priority.\u201d \u2014 Heather Wilson , President of The University of Texas at El Paso (Excerpt from UTEP\u2019s 2026 Carnegie Community Engagement Classification application) <!--\n    .accWrapper > div {\n    padding-left:24px;\n    }\n    .collapseToggleControl.collapsed span.glyphicon:before {\n        content: \"\\002b\";\n    }\n    .collapseToggleControl span.glyphicon:before {\n        content: \"\\2212\";\n    }\n    .optionalblock {\n        margin-top: 30px;\n        margin-bottom: 30px;\n    }\n /*flex*/\n.highligtsWrapper {\n    display: flex;\n    display: -webkit-flex;\n    flex-wrap: wrap;\n    margin-left: -14px;\n}\n.highligtsWrapper .col-md-4:nth-last-child(1) {\n    margin-bottom: 30px;\n}\n.highligtsWrapper .well {\n\tbox-shadow:0px 2px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);-webkit-box-shadow:0px 2px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);;\n\theight: 100%;\n\tpadding: 0;\n}\n.highligtsBody {\n\tpadding: 0 24px 0 24px;\n}\n.highligtsBody .btn-primary {\n    \tdisplay:block;\n    \tmargin-top: 30px;\n}\n\n.highligtsWrapper .col-md-4 {\n   margin-bottom: 30px;\n}\n\n.lightWhiteBg {\n\tbackground: rgba(255,255,255,.85);\n    padding: 4px 24px 24px 24px;\n    margin-bottom: 20px;\n}\n--> <!--\ndiv.facebook .pp_top .pp_left{background:#fff;}div.facebook .pp_top .pp_middle{background:#fff;}div.facebook .pp_top .pp_right{background:#fff;}div.facebook .pp_content_container .pp_left{background:#fff;}div.facebook .pp_content_container .pp_right{background:#fff;}div.facebook .pp_expand{background:url(//www.utep.edu/university-communications/_UC-Global-Files/lightbox/theme/sprite.png) -31px -26px no-repeat;cursor:pointer}div.facebook .pp_expand:hover{background:url(//www.utep.edu/university-communications/_UC-Global-Files/lightbox/theme/sprite.png) -31px -47px no-repeat;cursor:pointer}div.facebook .pp_contract{background:url(//www.utep.edu/university-communications/_UC-Global-Files/lightbox/theme/sprite.png) 0 -26px no-repeat;cursor:pointer}div.facebook .pp_contract:hover{background:url(//www.utep.edu/university-communications/_