{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/aerospace/", "title": "Aerospace Center", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About About Aerospace Center Student Success Research Stations Mission Crew Aerospace Leadership Frontiers STAR Frontier Space Frontier Aeronautics and Defense Frontier Energy and Sustainability Frontier Astro Fab Astro Fab Explore Prosperity Explore Prosperity Digital Engineering Digital Engineering Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Aerospace Center Main Content MESSAGE FROM EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR REQUEST A TOUR EXPLORE OUR RESEARCH STATIONS OPEN AN INTERSTELLAR COMMUNICATION <!--\n@media (max-width: 991px) {\n    .fw-section{\n            background-attachment: unset !important;\n        }\n    }\n--> Welcome to the Aerospace Center at The University of Texas at El Paso (UTEP) \u2014 we serve as a nexus for innovation, forging strategic partnerships across a dynamic ecosystem (a New Frontier Ecosystem !) of government agencies, industry leaders, small businesses, venture studios, venture capital firms, other research centers, and national laboratories. By translating and integrating cutting-edge research with real-world applications, our partnerships accelerate breakthroughs, cultivate entrepreneurial ventures, and drive the future of aerospace technology. We are dedicated to advancing aerospace technologies through pioneering research in space systems, hypersonic vehicles, AI-driven materials science, and more. By providing students hands-on experiences and access to cutting-edge research, we are preparing the next generation of engineers, scientists, technicians, and leaders to shape the future of aerospace. Create opportunities through careers in aerospace \u2013 Drive research expertise and talent development to foster job creation and business development \u2013 Inspire , engage, and excite the Paseo del Norte region to pursue careers in aerospace, creating a pipeline of talent for the future. Our commitment to research preeminence is matched by our focus on student development programs, offering valuable pathways to success in high-demand aerospace fields, while fostering partnerships within a New Frontier Ecosystem. Together, these efforts drive economic development in the Paseo del Norte region, attract investment, and strengthen national security through innovation and technological advancement well into the future! <!--\n.rsrch-slide{\n    background: #fff;\n  /*  margin: 0 15px; */\n}\n.rsrch-slide .rsrch-img{\n    position:relative;\n    float: left;\n   /* width:50%; */\n    height: auto;\n}\n.rsrch-slide .over-layer{\n    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6);\n    width: 100%;\n    height: 100%;\n    position: absolute;\n    opacity:0;\n    cursor: pointer;\n    transition: opacity 0.30s ease 0s;\n}\n.rsrch-slide .over-layer:after{\n    color: #fff;\n    content: \"+\";\n    font-size: 52px;\n    position: absolute;\n    top: 31%;\n    left:42%;\n}\n.rsrch-slide .rsrch-img:hover .over-layer{\n    opacity:1;\n}\n.rsrch-slide .rsrch-img img{\n    width:100%;\n    height: auto;\n}\n.rsrch-slide .rsrch-review{\n    float: left;\n    padding: 5px 5px;  /* 20px 20px; */\n    width: 95%;  /*  50 */\n   /* background-color: #041e4252; */\n}\n.rsrch-slide .rsrch-title{\n    margin:0 0 5px 0;\n    color: #0a1f40;\n}\n.rsrch-slide .rsrch-title a{\n    color: #0a1f40;\n  /*  \n    font-size: 20px;\n    font-weight: 700;\n    */\n    display: block;\n    text-transform: capitalize;\n    transition:color 0.30s ease;\n}\n.rsrch-title > a:hover{\n    text-decoration: none;\n    color:#0a1f40;\n}\n.rsrch-slide .rsrch-date{\n    display:block;\n    font-size:15px;\n    font-weight:700;\n    margin-bottom:17px;\n}\n.rsrch-description{\n    color: #0a1f40;\n    font-size: 15px;\n    font-weight:400;\n    text-align:left;\n    border-left: #bbc4c1 2px solid;\n  padding-left: 10px;\n  margin-top: 20px;\n\n}\n.owl-pagination{\n    margin-top: 15px;\n}\n.owl-theme .owl-controls .owl-page.active span, .owl-theme .owl-controls.clickable .owl-page:hover span{\n    background: #f28328;\n}\n@media only screen and (max-width: 990px){\n    .rsrch-slide .over-layer:after{\n        top:39%;\n        left: 45%;\n    }\n}\n@media only screen and (max-width: 640px){\n    .rsrch-slide .rsrch-img{\n        width:100%;\n    }\n    .rsrch-slide .rsrch-review{\n        width:100%;\n        padding:10px;\n    }\n}\n--> AEROSPACE CENTER FRONTIERS STAR frontier Space Technologies and AI-Driven Research (STAR) in Advanced Materials Science Frontier. The Aerospace Center\u2019s newest frontier will lead AI-driven advanced materials research to accelerate scientific breakthroughs for space, defense, and industry. By leveraging AI and machine learning, we aim to streamline material discovery, testing, and development, creating lightweight, durable, high-performance materials for extreme space conditions. More Info Space Frontier The Space Frontier advances strategic research in lunar resource utilization, propulsion, robotic landers, surface habitation, microgravity manufacturing, and small spacecraft technologies in support of NASA\u2019s Artemis program and Moon to Mars vision. Led by Md Mahamudur Rahman, Ph.D., a UTEP Mechanical Engineering associate professor, the division fosters innovation through hands-on, real-world research, equipping scientists with critical investigative and technical skills. More Info aeronautics & Defense frontier The Aeronautics and Defense Frontier supports the research and development of hypersonic, missile, and uncrewed aerial systems technologies. This frontier supports the U.S. Space Force\u2019s Space Superiority domain through innovation in Space Domain Awareness and Space Access & Sustainment. More Info energy & sustainability frontier The Energy and Sustainability Frontier provides capabilities from sub-pilot to commercial-scale fossil, nuclear, and renewable energy technology development; prototype-to-commercial-product demonstrations, and testing and evaluation. More Info <!--\n.post-slide{\n    background: #f8f8f8;\n    margin: 0 15px;\n    padding: 4px 4px;\n    border: 1px solid #dedde1;\n}\n.post-slide .post-header{\n   /* margin-bottom: 10px; */  /* if heading text on top */\n    margin-top: 10px;\n}\n.post-slide .subtitle{\n    color:#0b99bc;\n    font-size:14px;\n    display: inline-block;\n    margin-bottom:5px;\n    text-transform: uppercase;\n    transition: all 0.4s ease 0s;\n}\n.post-slide .subtitle:hover{\n    color:#333;\n    text-decoration: none;\n}\n.post-slide .post-title{\n    margin: 0;\n    padding: 5px;\n}\n.post-slide .post-title a{\n   /*\n   color:#333;\n    font-size:18px;\n    font-weight: bold;\n    */\n    text-transform:capitalize;\n    transition: all 0.4s ease 0s;\n}\n.post-slide .post-title a:hover{\n    color:#0b99bc;\n    text-decoration: none;\n}\n.post-slide .pic{\n    overflow: hidden;\n    position: relative;\n}\n.post-slide .pic img{\n    width: 100%;\n    height: auto;\n    transform: rotate(0deg) scale(1,1);\n    transition: all 0.9s ease 0s;\n}\n.post-slide:hover img{\n    transform: rotate(-2deg) scale(1.1,1.1);\n}\n.post-slide .pic:after{\n    content: \"\";\n    position: absolute;\n    top:0;\n    left:0;\n    width: 100%;\n    height: 100%;\n    background: rgba(255,255,255,0);\n    transition: all 0.9s ease 0s;\n \n}\n.post-slide:hover .pic:after{\n    background: rgba(255,255,255,0.2);\n}\n.post-slide .post-bar{\n    list-style: none;\n    padding:12px 5px;\n    margin: 0;\n}\n.post-slide .post-bar li{\n    display: inline-block;\n    margin-right:3px;\n    color:#aaa;\n}\n.post-slide .post-bar li:last-child{\n    margin-right: 0;\n}\n.post-slide .post-bar li a{\n    color:#aaa;\n    transition:0.3s ease;\n}\n.post-slide .post-bar li a:hover{\n    text-decoration: none;\n    color:#0b99bc;\n}\n.post-slide .post-description{\n    font-size: 14px;\n    line-height: 24px;\n    margin-bottom:15px;\n    color:#767676;\n    padding: 5px;\n}\n.post-slide .read-more{\n    color:#0b99bc;\n    font-size: 14px;\n    font-style: italic;\n    text-transform: capitalize;\n}\n.post-slide .read-more:hover{\n    color:#333;\n    text-decoration:none;\n}\n@media only screen and (max-width: 479px) {\n    .post-slide{\n        padding: 15px;\n    }\n    .post-slide .post-bar li{\n        margin-bottom: 5px;\n    }\n    .post-slide .post-bar li:last-child{\n        margin-bottom: 0;\n    }\n}\n--> AEROSPACE CENTER News UTEP, City of El Paso Collaborate to Drive Growth in Aerospace and Manufacturing Oct. 14, 2025 The City of El Paso and The University of Texas at El Paso are strengthening their partnership to advance aerospace and advanced manufacturing in the region. Supported by a $10 million federal award, this collaboration will expand high-quality job opportunities, boost innovation, and position the Paso del Norte region as a hub for next-generation technology and workforce development. Read More UTEP Cleared for Takeoff: BVLOS Approved! Jul. 24, 2025 Our UAS research program just received FAA approval for Beyond Visual Line of Sight operations\u2014granting 87 square miles of authorized range. This leap forward puts UTEP at the forefront of drone and advanced air mobility research. Read More UTEP Partners with CPFD Software to Advance Blue Hydrogen Research Using Barracuda Virtual Reactor Apr. 18, 2025 The University of Texas at El Paso (UTEP), in collaboration with CPFD Software, is leading advanced research in sustainable energy with a focus on co-gasification of sustainable feedstocks. Researchers from UTEP's Aerospace Center are using Barracuda Virtual Reactor, a powerful computational fluid dynamics (CFD) software, to model and optimize fluidized bed systems that convert municipal solid waste (MSW) and biomass into blue hydrogen fuel. Read More AMAC: Where Your Next Innovation Awaits Liftoff Apr. 11, 2025 The future is launching at UTEP! On 04.11, we celebrated the grand opening of the Advanced Manufacturing and Aerospace Center \u2014 home to the Aerospace Center and W.M. Keck Center. This cutting-edge facility will fuel aerospace and defense innovation. Watch the highlights UTEP Celebrates Opening of Advanced Manufacturing and Aerospace Center Apr. 11, 2025 UTEP's new Advanced Manufacturing and Aerospace Center (AMAC) brings together the Aerospace Center and W.M. Keck Center to drive groundbreaking research in defense, space technology, and advanced manufacturing. This cutting-edge facility empowers researchers and students to develop next-generation innovations, from rocket engines to hypersonic systems, strengthening UTEP's role as a leader in national aerospace advancement. Read More Launching Her Future: UTEP\u2019s Montserrat Hernandez Named 2025 Brooke Owens Fellow Feb.10, 2025 What does it take to launch a career in aerospace? For Montserrat Hernandez, a mechanical engineering senior and fast-track master\u2019s student at UTEP, it\u2019s a mix of passion, perseverance, and hands-on experience. Recently named a 2025 Brooke Owens Fellow, Hernandez has secured a prestigious internship with Blue Origin, where she will contribute to cutting-edge projects at Launch Site 1. Read More UTEP Graduate Wins ASC Student Paper Award at 2025 AIAA SciTech Jan. 16, 2025 UTEP Engineering graduate Emmanuel Vielma has won the 2025 ASC Student Paper Award for his research on aerospace composites, recognized at the AIAA SciTech Forum. His work, conducted at UTEP\u2019s Aerospace Center with AFRL support, showcases the university\u2019s commitment to student excellence and innovation in aerospace engineering. Read More UTEP Names Shery Welsh Executive Director of Aerospace Center Jun. 20, 2024 Dr. Shery Welsh is the Executive Director of UTEP\u2019s Aerospace Center. With extensive aerospace leadership experience, she will drive pioneering research, DoD and industry partnerships, and innovation. Her vision focuses on expanding the center\u2019s impact, fostering economic growth, and creating opportunities for students and faculty in advanced aerospace research and development. Read More Leadership in Action: Recent Visits 2024-2025 Dr. Shery Welsh, Executive Director, recently visited key aerospace and research institutions, including NewSpace Nexus, Oak Ridge National Lab, Spaceport America, and the American Astronautical Society. These visits focused on fostering innovation, strengthening industry partnerships, and advancing aerospace research, reinforcing the organization's commitment to cutting-edge technological development and collaboration. Read More CONNECT WITH US Advanced Manufacturing and Aerospace Center Building 1800 Hawthorne St. El Paso, TX 79968 Main: 915.747.8252 Fax: 915.747. 5549 Contact Us UTEPAerospaceCenter/ utep_aerospace_center <!--\n#myBtn {\n  display: none;\n  position: fixed;\n  bottom: 20px;\n  right: 30px;\n  z-index: 99;\n  font-size: 18px;\n  border: none;\n  outline: none;\n  background-color: #041e42;\n  color: white;\n  cursor: pointer;\n  padding: 15px;\n  border-radius: 4px;\n}\n\n#myBtn:hover {\n  background-color: #ff8200;\n}\n--> // <![CDATA[\n//Get the button\nvar mybutton = document.getElementById(\"myBtn\");\n\n// When the user scrolls down 20px from the top of the document, show the button\nwindow.onscroll = function() {scrollFunction()};\n\nfunction scrollFunction() {\n  if (document.body.scrollTop > 20 || document.documentElement.scrollTop > 20) {\n    mybutton.style.displa