{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/engineering/rimes/about/", "title": "About Us", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About About Research Research People People Publications Publications Contracts and Grants Contracts and Grants Resources Resources Patents and Products Patents and Products News News Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Research Institute for Manufacturing and Engineering Systems (RIMES) College of Engineering Main Content UTEP College of Engineering Research Institute for Manufacturing and Engineering Systems (RIMES) About UTEP College of Engineering Research Institute for Manufacturing and Engineering Systems (RIMES) About About Us The Research Institute for Manufacturing and Engineering Systems (RIMES) is a multidisciplinary center under the Department of Industrial, Manufacturing, and Systems Engineering (IMSE) at The University of Texas at El Paso (UTEP). RIMES is dedicated to advancing research, innovation, and education in manufacturing and engineering systems, with a focus on solving complex industrial challenges through cutting-edge technologies, data-driven decision-making, and collaborative partnerships. By integrating expertise in areas such as smart manufacturing, digital twins, automation, industrial data analytics, and sustainable engineering practices, RIMES fosters impactful solutions that enhance productivity, efficiency, and competitiveness. The institute serves as a hub for faculty, students, industry, and government agencies to collaborate on research projects, workforce development initiatives, and technology transfer, contributing to regional and global advancements in manufacturing and engineering systems. Our Objectives Advance Cutting-Edge Research \u2013 Conduct innovative, interdisciplinary research in manufacturing and engineering systems to address current and emerging industry challenges. Promote Industry\u2013Academia Collaboration \u2013 Foster strong partnerships with industry, government agencies, and academic institutions to accelerate technology transfer and practical applications. Integrate Emerging Technologies \u2013 Explore and apply advanced tools such as Artificial Intelligence, Digital Twins, Industry 4.0 technologies, automation, computer simulation, virtual/augmented reality, and industrial data analytics to optimize manufacturing systems. Support Workforce Development \u2013 Provide hands-on training, workshops, and educational programs to prepare students and professionals for leadership roles in modern manufacturing and engineering. Enhance Sustainability and Resilience \u2013 Develop innovative approaches that promote sustainable manufacturing practices and resilient engineering systems. Facilitate Interdisciplinary Collaboration \u2013 Bring together faculty, students, and researchers from diverse disciplines to address complex engineering and manufacturing problems. Serve as a Regional Innovation Hub \u2013 Act as a catalyst for economic growth and technological advancement in the El Paso region and beyond through applied research and innovation. Vision To be a nationally and internationally recognized leader in advancing innovative manufacturing and engineering systems, driving technological excellence, sustainability, and economic growth through cutting-edge research, education, and industry collaboration. Mission The Research Institute for Manufacturing and Engineering Systems (RIMES) at UTEP\u2019s Department of Industrial, Manufacturing, and Systems Engineering is dedicated to transforming the future of manufacturing through interdisciplinary research, technology integration, and workforce development. We strive to bridge the gap between academia and industry by fostering innovation in areas such as smart manufacturing, digital twins, automation, and sustainable engineering practices. Through impactful partnerships, hands-on training, and knowledge dissemination, RIMES empowers students, professionals, and organizations to achieve greater productivity, efficiency, and global competitiveness. About About Us Vision and Mission Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso RIMES Engineering Bldg., Room A-130 500 W University El Paso, Texas 79968 E: rimes@utep.edu P: (915) 747-5336 F: (915) 747-5437 THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Texas Veterans Portal Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 | SITE FEEDBACK Modal X"}
{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/engineering/cassmar/", "title": "CASSMAR", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About CASSMAR People Leadership Staff Interns Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support CASSMAR College of Engineering Main Content CASSMAR <!--\na {\n\t color: #337ab7;\n\t text-decoration: none;\n}\n a:hover, a:focus {\n\t color: #23527c;\n\t text-decoration: underline;\n}\n--> CENTER FOR THE ADVANCEMENT OF SPACE SAFETY AND MISSION ASSURANCE RESEARCH The CASSMAR mission is to enable human spaceflight through interdisciplinary research to identify, characterize, and mitigate the leading risks to safety and mission assurance. By forging partnerships with government and commercial spaceflight organizations, CASSMAR serves as an example for interdisciplinary, cross-functional and sustainable research at UTEP with a focus on the enhancement of the safety and reliability for human spaceflight. CASSMAR directly contributes to the education of UTEP\u2019s 21st century demographic into the next generation of competent, diverse, and enthusiastic space engineers and scientists specializing in risk assessment and mitigation. RESEARCH FOCUS AREAS Micrometeoroid and Orbital Debris (MMOD): Detection and Tracking; Measurement and Characterization; Modeling, Prediction and Mitigation Performance in compositional modeling, and analysis of extreme spaceflight environments: Atmospheric re-entry; High pressure gaseous media; Hazardous, energetic fluid systems and propellants Forensic characterization of spacecraft material degradation mechanisms: Space Shuttle Columbia artifact analysis Systems Engineering, reliability, risk analysis and forensics engineering INDUSTRY PARTNERSHIPS Jacobs Engineering NASA Johnsons Space Center- Orbital Debris Program Office NASA Kennedy Space Center- Columbia Research and Preservation Office NASA White Sands Test Facility (WSTF) International Association for the Advancement of Space Safety Boeing Lockheed Martin Air Force Research Lab (AFRL) Johns Hopkins University- Applied Physics Laboratory Contact Us CASSMAR Engineering Building, Room M-201C 500 W University El Paso, Texas 79968 E: CASSMAR@utep.edu P: (915) 747-6904 <!--\n/* General styles */\n\n #container + .fw-section {\n\t background-position: center -70px !important;\n\t background-attachment: unset !important;\n}\n @media screen and (max-width: 1365px){\n\t #container + .fw-section {\n\t\t background-position: center 0 !important;\n\t\t background-attachment: unset !important;\n\t}\n}\n @media screen and (max-width: 991px){\n\t #container + .fw-section {\n\t\t background-position: 160px 70px !important;\n\t\t background-attachment: unset !important;\n\t}\n}\n @media only screen and (max-width: 767px) {\n\t .container + .fw-section {\n\t\t background-image:none !important;\n\t}\n}\n\n\n/* Banner Section */\n #mcBanner {\n\t height: 500px;\n\t display: flex;\n\t justify-content: flex-end;\n\t align-items: center;\n}\n #mcBanner .theContent-mobile {\n\t display:none;\n}\n #mcBanner h1 {\n\t font-size: 60px;\n\t color: #fff;\n\t letter-spacing: 2px;\n\t text-transform:uppercase;\n\t margin-top: 0;\n\t margin-bottom: 2px;\n\t line-height:0.9;\n\t text-align: left;\n}\n #mcBanner p {\n\t font-size:17px;\n\t line-height: 1.7;\n\t margin-bottom: 0;\n\t text-align: left;\n\t color: #fff;\n\t letter-spacing: 1px;\n}\n #mcBanner p.mc-buttons {\n\t margin-top:15px;\n\t margin-bottom:15p