{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/aerospace/news/", "title": "Leadership in Action: Recent Visits", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About About Aerospace Center Student Success Research Stations Mission Crew Aerospace Leadership Frontiers STAR Frontier Space Frontier Aeronautics and Defense Frontier Energy and Sustainability Frontier Astro Fab Astro Fab Explore Prosperity Explore Prosperity Digital Engineering Digital Engineering Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Aerospace Center Main Content Leadership in Action: Recent Visits <!--\n.carousel-caption {\n    display: block !important;\n}\n--> <!--\n@media (max-width: 991px) {\n    .fw-section{\n            background-attachment: unset !important;\n        }\n    }\n--> NewSpace Nexus\u00a0and\u00a0COSMIAC Exploring the New Frontier: Advancing Space Innovation Through Collaboration The recent visit to NewSpace Nexus\u00a0and\u00a0COSMIAC\u00a0was an out-of-this-world experience, filled with energy, innovation, and a shared passion for advancing space technologies. A special thanks goes to\u00a0Casey Anglada DeRaad, Arial DeHerrera (NewSpace Nexus), and Craig Kief (COSMIAC)\u00a0for their collaboration and commitment to shaping the future. At\u00a0UTEP, the\u00a0College of Engineering, College of Science, and Aerospace Center\u00a0continue to lead groundbreaking research, fostering economic growth in\u00a0Paso del Norte\u00a0and supporting national defense. By uniting science, technology, and collaboration,\u00a0The New Frontier Ecosystem\u00a0is pushing the boundaries of space innovation. NewSpace Nexus Visit Oakridge National Lab Collaborating for a Greater Tomorrow A recent visit to Oak Ridge National Laboratory (ORNL) and University of Tennessee, Knoxville (UTK) , hosted by Dr. \"Suresh\" Sudarsanam Babu , provided an incredible opportunity to explore world-class research facilities. Stops included the Manufacturing Science Division, TNMade, and UT\u2019s Advanced Materials & Manufacturing HQs , where strategic discussions focused on accelerating innovation. Collaboration is key in aerospace research, unlocking greater potential in R&D. Special thanks to the teams at ORNL, UTK, and TNMade for their hospitality, and to Tony Schmitz, Jonathan Phipps, Ph.D., and Suresh for an inspiring dinner that sparked new project collaborations. Oakridge National Lab Visit Spaceport America Reaching for the Stars with Spaceport America A cosmic shout-out to Spaceport America\u00a0in New Mexico, especially\u00a0Director Scott McLaughlin, for an unforgettable visit! Scott and his team rolled out the interstellar red carpet, leading mission-critical discussions on attracting more space-faring energy to the\u00a0NM/TX region. A special highlight was the\u00a0Virgin Galactic\u00a0tour, led by the legendary\u00a0Michael Moses. UTEP Aerospace Center, UTEP College of Engineering, and Ken Meissner\u00a0joined fellow explorers from\u00a0NMSU, NM Tech, City of Las Cruces, and Commissioner Iliana Holguin, including\u00a0NMSU President Dr. Valerio Ferme. Together, they continue pushing boundaries and reaching for the stars! Spaceport America Visit American Astronomical Society Dr. Shery Welsh Joins Prestigious von Braun Space Exploration Symposium The American Astronautical Society invited Dr. Shery Welsh, Ph.D., SES (ret) to serve as a panelist at the 2024 von Braun Space Exploration Symposium . Dr. Welsh joined NASA Chief Technologist Dr. A.C. Charania and U.S. Space Force Chief Science Officer Dr. Stacie Williams in a roundtable discussion led by Dr. Andy Kwas (UNM/Northrop Grumman) . The panel explored advancements in space technology, DoD-academic partnerships, and future challenges. Events like these strengthen Dr. Welsh\u2019s role in the space ecosystem, fostering collaborations that drive innovation and national impact. American Astronomical Society Visit <!--\n#myBtn {\n  display: none;\n  position: fixed;\n  bottom: 20px;\n  right: 30px;\n  z-index: 99;\n  font-size: 18px;\n  border: none;\n  outline: none;\n  background-color: #041e42;\n  color: white;\n  cursor: pointer;\n  padding: 15px;\n  border-radius: 4px;\n}\n\n#myBtn:hover {\n  background-color: #ff8200;\n}\n--> // <![CDATA[\n//Get the button\nvar mybutton = document.getElementById(\"myBtn\");\n\n// When the user scrolls down 20px from the top of the document, show the button\nwindow.onscroll = function() {scrollFunction()};\n\nfunction scrollFunction() {\n  if (document.body.scrollTop > 20 || document.documentElement.scrollTop > 20) {\n    mybutton.style.display = \"block\";\n  } else {\n    mybutton.style.display = \"none\";\n  }\n}\n\n// When the user clicks on the button, scroll to the top of the document\nfunction topFunction() {\n  document.body.scrollTop = 0;\n  document.documentElement.scrollTop = 0;\n}\n// ]]> <!--\nh1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6   {text-align: left;}\n\n\n.card {\n    height: 140px;\n    width: 100%; \n   /* width: 115px; */\n  /*  background: #e6843e;  */\n  /*  box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px lightgrey; */\n    padding: 2px;\n    border:  1px solid #0a1f4042;\n  /*  border-radius: 4px; */\n    margin: 5px;\n    text-align:center;\n   /* font-family: \"arial narrow\"; */\n    font-weight:bold;\n    font-size: 13px;\n    letter-spacing: -0.5px;\n}\n\n.card:hover {\n    border: #f28328 1px solid;\n    \n}\n--> // <![CDATA[\n$(document).ready(function() { \n            \n                $(\"h2\").css(\"text-ali