{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/science/bbrc/people/new-advisory-committees.html", "title": "Advisory Committees", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About Mission Cores Administrative Core (AC) Community Engagement Core (CEC) Investigator Development Core Recruitment Core Research Infrastructure Core People Faculty Staff Advisory Committees Research Basic Project Clinical project Resources Health Survey Factsheet.pdf Food and Housing Security Student Data.pdf Links BBRC Seminar Calendar Biographical Sketches Biographical Sketches PPP Patents, Presentations and Publications Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Border Biomedical Research Center College of Science Main Content UTEP College of Science Border Biomedical Research Center People UTEP College of Science Border Biomedical Research Center People Advisory Committee Internal Advisory Committee (IAC) The IAC\u2019s promotes the success of the RCMI program at UTEP. They meet quarterly to perform the following which includes: 1) Maintain and develop standard operating procedures, 2) Set priorities for efficient core functioning, 3) Identify and secure resources to drive the research enterprise, 4) Monitor operations and management of programs and 5) Generate a competitive research environment that will enhance grant success. The IAC consists of individuals with the significant knowledge of the RCMI program and its daily activities such as the Vice President for Research, RCMI Program Director and the Core Leads, among others. IAC Membership Robert Kirken, Dean College of Science, RCMI Principal Investigator; IAC Chair Renato Aguilera, Research Deputy Director Dr. Michael Kenney , Cores Deputy Director Elizabeth Walsh, Toxicology expertise Igor Almeida, Director of Biomolecule Analysis, Omics unit and Genomic Analysis Amy Wagler, Director of Statistical Consulting Ming-Ying Leung, Director of the Bioinformatics Laboratory Bibiana Mancera, Director of the Community Engagement Core External Advisory Committee (EAC) The primary function of the EAC is to review the progress of the RCMI program at UTEP on an annual basis and provide direction and areas for development. It constructively evaluates progress made with respect to funding, publications, scientific and faculty development, and areas for growth. They reinforce activities that will result in a \u201cmeasurable emphasis\u201d on making discoveries of clinical and translational significance. The current Chair of the EAC is Dr. Susan Opava, Professor Emeritus California Poly University. Her analysis, and that of the committee, continues to provide strong impetus for us to streamline our operations of biomedical research and assists with innovative ideas and strategies to maximize the BBRC activities The EAC also includes external advisors for each of the Cores and research projects. They operate following best practices, provide high-quality services, operate at comparable levels to other similar facilities and make relevant progress toward sustainability. BBRC EXTERNAL ADVISORY COMMITTEE MEMBERS Susan T. Weintraub, Ph.D. Chair, Department of Biochemistry Director, Mass Spectrometry Laboratory, External Advisory Comittee The University of Texas Health Science Center at San Antonio 7703 Floyd Curl Drive MC 7760 San Antonio, Texas\u00a0 78229-3900 Phone: (210) 567-4043 Cell: (210)-823-6985 Fax: (210) 567-5524 E-mail: weintraub@uthscsa.edu Abraham Arag