ember 2021 Professor Josiah Heyman chosen as winner of Distinguished Achievement Award The College of Liberal Arts and the Department of Sociology & Anthropology are proud to announce that Professor Josiah Heyman has been chosen as the winner of the 2021 Distinguished Achievement Award in the Critical Study of North America from the Society for the Anthropology of North America (SANA). SANA is a part of the Anthropological Association of America (AAA). Inaugurated in 1994, the SANA Prize for Distinguished Achievement in the Critical Study of North America recognizes scholars with a notable long-term program of research and publication, and also takes into account contributions in other areas, such as teaching and training, SANA/AAA service, and community, activist, or policy involvements outside academia. SANA says of Joe, \"You have excelled in all of these areas, and we cannot think of a more deserving person for this prestigious award!\" For more information, please visit: https://www.utep.edu/newsfeed/campus/anthropologists-honor-uteps-heyman-for-body-of-work.html <!--\n    .accWrapper > div {\n    padding-left:24px;\n    }\n    .collapseToggleControl.collapsed span.glyphicon:before {\n        content: \"\\002b\";\n    }\n    .collapseToggleControl span.glyphicon:before {\n        content: \"\\2212\";\n    }\n    .optionalblock {\n        margin-top: 30px;\n        margin-bottom: 30px;\n    }\n /*flex*/\n.highligtsWrapper {\n    display: flex;\n    display: -webkit-flex;\n    flex-wrap: wrap;\n    margin-left: -14px;\n}\n.highligtsWrapper .col-md-4:nth-last-child(1) {\n    margin-bottom: 30px;\n}\n.highligtsWrapper .well {\n\tbox-shadow:0px 2px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);-webkit-box-shadow:0px 2px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);;\n\theight: 100%;\n\tpadding: 0;\n}\n.highligtsBody {\n\tpadding: 0 24px 0 24px;\n}\n.highligtsBody .btn-primary {\n    \tdisplay:block;\n    \tmargin-top: 30px;\n}\n\n.highligtsWrapper .col-md-4 {\n   margin-bottom: 30px;\n}\n\n.lightWhiteBg {\n\