{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/liberalarts/cibs/about/", "title": "Director's Welcome", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About Director's Welcome Vision & Mission Business Center Forms Academic Programs Academic Program Information Undergraduate Program Master's Program People Staff Affiliated Faculty News & Events Recent News Upcoming Events Research CIBS Research CIBS Border Studies Working Papers CIBS Faculty Research Profiles Building Scholars Immigration and Border Communities REU Socio-Environmental and Geospatial Analysis Lab Resources CIBS Resources Documents produced at CIBS Resources at UTEP Resources on the web UTEP Student Success Resource Hub Outreach Documents For The Community Borderzine Give Now! Give now! Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Center for Inter-American and Border Studies College of Liberal Arts Main Content UTEP College of Liberal Arts Center for Inter-American and Border Studies About UTEP College of Liberal Arts Center for Inter-American and Border Studies About Welcome to the Center for Inter-American and Border Studies (CIBS) Welcome to the Center for Inter-American and Border Studies (CIBS). The Center provides UTEP\u2019s focal point for activities concerning Latin America, Mexico, the U.S.-Mexico Border, and borders more generally. While an emphasis on our local region is interwoven through most UTEP activities, CIBS creates a central point of leadership and support for other units in academic programs, research, and outreach activities. Our website contains informati on about our academic programs (an undergraduate major and minor, a new interdisciplinary MA), our research programs, our outreach activities, opportunities for students and faculty, and resources\u00a0on the U.S.-Mexico Border and Latin America at UTEP and elsewhere. The University of Texas at El Paso is located in the world\u2019s largest urban center on a land border.\u00a0 The binational metroplex of over 2 million inhabitants presents opportunities for academic study and practical experience unmatched anywhere.\u00a0\u00a0They include the entire range of academic endeavor:\u00a0the arts, the sciences, commerce and economics, political studies at both the local and international levels, environmental studies, technology, health, th e social sciences, and the humanities.\u00a0The Center for Inter-American and Border Studies invites visitors to this page to begin exploring the multifaceted realities of the Border and related areas in these pages, and through programs and activities we organize and sponsor. -Josiah Heyman,\u00a0CIBS Director The Rio Grand e winds its way down northwest El Paso ( El flujo del R\u00edo Bravo por el \u00e1rea noroeste de El Paso) Bienvenidos al Centro de Estudios Interamericanos y de la Frontera (CIBS) CIBS se convierte en el centro de atenci\u00f3n de UTEP para actividades relacionadas con la Frontera M\u00e9xico-Estados Unidos, Am\u00e9rica Latina y las fronteras de manera m\u00e1s general. Mientras que el \u00e9nfasis en nuestra regi\u00f3n local se entrelaza con casi todas las actividades de UTEP, CIBS crea un punto central de liderazgo y apoyo para otras unidades en programas acad\u00e9micos, investigaci\u00f3n y actividades de difusi\u00f3n y contacto. Nuestro sitio web contiene informaci\u00f3n sobre nuestros programas acad\u00e9micos (una licenciatura con un \u00e1rea de especializaci\u00f3n mayor y otra menor, y una maestr\u00eda interdisciplinaria nueva), programas de investigaci\u00f3n, actividades d e difusi\u00f3n y contacto, oportunidades para los estudiantes y profesorado, y recursos sobre la Frontera M\u00e9xico-Estados Unidos y Am\u00e9rica Latina, tanto en UTEP como en otras partes. La Universidad de Texas en El Paso est\u00e1 localizada en el centro urbano m\u00e1s grande del mundo en un \u00e1rea fronteriza. El \u00e1rea metropolitana binacional de m\u00e1s de 2 millones de personas presenta oportunidades para estudios acad\u00e9micos y experiencia pr\u00e1ctica incomparable. Las mismas incluyen una amplia gama de \u00e1reas de enfoque: las artes, ciencias, comercio y econom\u00eda, estudios de pol\u00edtica tanto a nivel local como internacional, estudios medioambientales, tecnolog\u00eda, salud, ciencias sociales y humanidades. El Centro de Estudios Interamericanos y de la Frontera invita a los visitantes de esta p\u00e1gina electr\u00f3nica a que empiecen a explorar las realidades multifac\u00e9ticas de la frontera y \u00e1reas relacionadas en estas p\u00e1ginas, as\u00ed como por medio de los programas y actividades que organiz amos y apoyamos. -Josiah Heyman,\u00a0Director de CIBS Borderzine About Director's Welcome Vision & Mission Business Center Forms Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso Center for Inter-American and Border Studies Physical location: : Old Main Building 102 Mailing Address: 500 West University Avenue El Paso, Texas 79968 E: cibs@utep.edu P: (915) 747-5196 THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Texas Veterans Portal Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 | SITE FEEDBACK Modal X"}
{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/science/bbrc/core/investigator-development-core.html", "title": "Investigator Development Core", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About Mission Cores Administrative Core (AC) Community Engagement Core (CEC) Investigator Development Core Recruitment Core Research Infrastructure Core People Faculty Staff Advisory Committees Research Basic Project Clinical project Resources Health Survey Factsheet.pdf Food and Housing Security Student Data.pdf Links BBRC Seminar Calendar Biographical Sketches Biographical Sketches PPP Patents, Presentations and Publications Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Border Biomedical Research Center College of Science Main Content UTEP College of Science Border Biomedical Research Center Core UTEP College of Science Border Biomedical Research Center Core Investigator Development Core Our long-term vision is that the BBRC will enhance the capacity of UTEP to conduct exceptional basic biomedical, behavioral, and clinical research . We also envision that the center will be a critical focal point at UTEP where a culture develops for nurturing, sustaining and retaining world-class talent . The goals of the IDC will be to 1) enhance our research capacity to conduct world-class basic biomedical, behavioral, and/or clinical research; 2) improve the success rates of all investigators, especially early-stage investigators (ESI), seeking extramural support; and 3) foster an environment that is conducive to enhancing career development for ESI. The overarching goal of the IDC will be to foster excellence in the BBRC investigator ranks by enabling them to secure competitive extramural funding in research and become adept at establishing robust research programs aligned with the center\u2019s mission. Leadership The IDC Leader, Dr. Marc Cox is a Professor and experienced BBRC RCMI investigator and as well Director of UTEP\u2019s Center for Faculty Leadership and Development. The Goals of the IDRC are to: 1) enhance our research capacity to conduct world-class basic biomedical, behavioral, and/or clinical research; 2) improve the success rates of all investigators, especially early-stage investigators (ESI), seeking extramural support for externally funded research projects; and 3) foster an environment that is conducive to enhancing career development for ESI. Awarded Cohort 2 Projects 2021 Jong Wha Chang, PhD \u2013 BEHAVIORAL - Prevalence, and Factors Associated with Potentially Inappropriate Medication Use in Older Patients with Non-small Cell Lung Cancer (NSCLC) Jorge Cervantes, MD, PhD \u2013 CLINICAL - Investigation of the Microbiota of Colon Cancer Precursors in the Border Region Kisuk Min, PhD \u2013 BASIC - Exploring the Role of Calpain in Doxorubicin-Induced Skeletal Muscle Myopathy MD Nurunnabi, PhD \u2013 BASIC - Development of a Noninvasive Imaging-Based Detection Technology and a Sustainable Treatment Approach for Gastric Cancer Michael Pokojovy, PhD \u2013 BASIC - Utilizing Machine Learning for Prostate Cancer Diagnosis Awarded Cohort 1 Projects 2020 Sylvia Chavez-Baray, Ph.D. \u2013 BEHAVIORAL - Cancer Knowledge, Attitudes and Practices (C-KAP) Pilot Study Alexander Philipovskiy, M.D., Ph.D. \u2013 CLINICAL - Evaluation of Mutation and Gene Expression Profiles in Breast Cancers Anita Quintana, Ph.D. \u2013 BASIC - Role of HCFC1 in Cancer Cell Proliferation Georgialina Rodriguez, Ph.D. \u2013