tudents Director's Message Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso Center for Environmental Resource Management 211 Kelly Hall 500 W University El Paso, Texas 79902 E: cerm@utep.edu P: (915) 747-6069 THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Texas Veterans Portal Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 | SITE FEEDBACK Modal X"}
{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/onewater/events/world-water-day-26.html", "title": "World Water Week 26", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search Who We Are Directors' Message People Research Lines of Research Our Region Geography Events World Water Week 26 Connect With Us Connect With Us Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support One Water Cluster Main Content UTEP One Water Cluster Events UTEP One Water Cluster Events UTEP's One Water Cluster and UACJ faculty and staff Present: March\u00a0 23 - 28,\u00a0\u00a02026 World Water Day, observed annually on March 2nd since 1993, celebrates water and raises awareness of the 2.2 billion people living without access to safe water . The UTEP One Water Cluster, faculty and staff at UACJ are inviting you to our annual celebration of World Water Day in March 2026. As we have for the past four years, we will celebrate with a week of interdisciplinary events. These events are designed to engage faculty, students, and community partners who are working on the issue of water from various perspectives. This creates a public platform to increase visibility of water scholarship and activism. It also provides an opportunity to develop new connections and working relationships on the topic. We expect to have a mixture of online and in-person events. This year\u2019s theme is: \u201cWater, Health and Gender\u201d . Water Week 2026\u00a0highlights the interconnections between water access, public health, and gender equality. Around the world, limited access to clean water and sanitation affects women and men differently, often placing a disproportionate burden on women and girls who manage household water collection and care responsibilities. Ensuring fair and sustainable access to water supports health, education, and opportunity for all, strengthening the foundations of equity and community well-being. SAVE THE DATE! WWW 2026 RESERVA LA FECHA! WWW 2026 Submit your proposal to participate: World Water Week 2026 An Interdisciplinary Conference and Celebration Water, Health, and Gender March 23-28, 2026 Call for Community, Artistic, and Scholarly Contributions World Water Day, celebrated each March 22 since 1993, raises awareness of the global challenges surrounding water and inspires action toward universal access to safe and sustainable water and sanitation. The UTEP One Water Cluster, together with faculty and staff at UACJ, invites you to our 2026 World Water Week celebration\u2014a week of interdisciplinary events exploring the theme \u201cWater, Health, and Gender.\u201d As we have for the past five years, we will celebrate with a week of interdisciplinary events that are designed to engage faculty, students, and community partners who work on water-related issues from various perspectives. This celebration creates a public platform to increase the visibility of water scholarship and activism, while also providing an opportunity to develop new connections and working relationships on this important topic. We expect a mix of online and in-person events. This year\u2019s theme is: \u201cWater, Health, and Gender\u201d This year\u2019s theme highlights the interconnections between water access, public health, and gender equality. Around the world, limited access to clean water and sanitation affects women and men differently, often placing a disproportionate burden on women and girls who manage household water collection and care responsibilities. Ensuring fair and sustainable access to water supports health, education, and opportunity for all, strengthening the foundations of equity and community well-being. We invite community members, artists, students, scholars, groups, and organizations to submit proposals to share their work through interdisciplinary sessions scheduled for Monday, March 23, through Saturday, March 28, 2026. This is not a traditional academic conference\u2014we welcome creative, participatory, and experimental formats that promote dialogue, collaboration, and new perspectives on the relationship between water, health, and gender. Possible Formats include : Artistic or literary performances by one or more individuals engaging with the conference's annual theme; Roundtables/public conversations uniting experts, practitioners, and community voices; Interactive workshops demonstrating scientific, educational, or creative approaches to water-related topics within the context of \u201cWater, Health, and Gender.\u201d Panels or discussions combining academic, activist, and community perspectives on water-related issues; Practical workshops focused on water conservation, health, and equitable access, particularly in border and underserved regions . Sessions are planned to be a maximum of one hour and twenty minutes. You are welcome to contact this year\u2019s conference coordinators, Julian Hernandez ( jhernandez88@utep.edu ), Ana C. Maass ( acmaass@utep.edu ), and Judith R\u00edos ( jrios@uacj.mx )\u00a0 for any questions about alternative formats, ideas, or comments about World Water Week 2026 at UTEP and UACJ. Fill out the online Google form (link below) by no later than Monday, January 13, 2026. We will respond to proposals by\u00a0January 23, 2026, and follow up with the final schedule no later than January 31, 2026. Google form (English version): https://forms.gle/sudf7Jy3gZxwummv5 Google form (Spanish version): https://forms.gle/sdfU22abZ148RCz37 Deadline to Submit Proposals: 1/13/26 Notice of Acceptance: 1/23/26 Final Event Schedule with time slot confirmation : 1/31/26 For more information, visit: World Water Week 26 Thank you from all of us from the UTEP and UACJ Organizing Committee, the UTEP One Water\u00a0Cluster, the Center for Environmental Resource Management, the Universidad Aut\u00f3noma de Ciudad Ju\u00e1rez, the Rubin Center for the Visual Arts, and the Centennial Museum at UTEP. Te invitamos a participar en nuestro evento: Mundial del Agua en UTEP 2026 Conferencia y Celebraci\u00f3n Interdisciplinaria Agua, Salud y G\u00e9nero 23-28 de Marzo, 2026 Convocatoria para Contribuciones Art\u00edsticas, y Escolares de la Comunidad El D\u00eda Mundial del Agua, celebrado cada 22 de marzo desde 1993, busca crear conciencia sobre los desaf\u00edos globales relacionados con el agua e inspirar acciones que promuevan el acceso universal al agua y al saneamiento de forma segura y sostenible. El Cl\u00faster One Water de UTEP y el cuerpo docente y personal de la UACJ te invitan a participar en la Semana Mundial del Agua 2026, una semana de eventos interdisciplinarios que explorar\u00e1n el tema \u201cAgua, Salud y G\u00e9nero\u201d . Como lo hemos hecho durante los \u00faltimos cinco a\u00f1os, celebraremos la ocasi\u00f3n con una semana de eventos interdisciplinarios. Estos eventos est\u00e1n dise\u00f1ados para involucrar a profesores, estudiantes y miembros de la comunidad que trabajan desde diversas perspectivas en el tema del agua. Esto crea una plataforma p\u00fablica para aumentar la visibilidad de la investigaci\u00f3n y el activismo sobre el agua, adem\u00e1s de brindar la oportunidad de desarrollar nuevas conexiones y relaciones de trabajo sobre el tema. Esperamos tener una mezcla de eventos en l\u00ednea y presenciales. El tema de este a\u00f1o es: \u201cAgua, Salud y G\u00e9nero\u201d El tema de este a\u00f1o resalta la relaci\u00f3n entre el acceso al agua, la salud p\u00fablica y la equidad de g\u00e9nero. En muchas partes del mundo, la falta de acceso al agua y al saneamiento afecta de manera desigual a mujeres y hombres, siendo las mujeres y ni\u00f1as quienes suelen asumir mayores responsabilidades en la recolecci\u00f3n y el cuidado del agua. Garantizar un acceso justo y sostenible al agua fortalece la salud, la educaci\u00f3n y las oportunidades, promoviendo la equidad y el bienestar de las comunidades. En este contexto, se invita a miembros de la comunidad, artistas, estudiantes, acad\u00e9micos, grupos y organizaciones a enviar propuestas para participar en sesiones interdisciplinarias programadas entre el lunes 23 de marzo y el s\u00e1bado 28 de marzo de 2026. Esta no es una conferencia acad\u00e9mica tradicional:\u00a0se alientan formatos creativos, participativos y experimentales que fomenten el di\u00e1logo, la colaboraci\u00f3n y nuevas perspectivas sobre la relaci\u00f3n entre agua, salud y g\u00e9nero. Tipos de formatos: Presentaciones art\u00edsticas o literarias de una o m\u00e1s personas que abordan el tema anual de la conferencia; Mesas redondas o conversatorios que re\u00fanan a expertos, profesionales y voces de la comunidad; as\u00ed como talleres interactivos que presenten enfoques cient\u00edficos, educativos o innovadores sobre temas relacionados con el agua en el contexto de \u201cagua, salud y g\u00e9nero\u201d; Paneles integrados por acad\u00e9micos, activistas y/o miembros de la comunidad que trabajen en problem\u00e1ticas del agua desde distintas perspectivas. Talleres enfocados en la conservaci\u00f3n, la salud y el acceso equitativo al agua, especialmente en zonas fronterizas o de atenci\u00f3n prioritaria. Las sesiones est\u00e1n planeadas para desarrollarse durante una hora y veinte minutos, como m\u00e1ximo. Si\u00e9ntase con la libertad de contactar a los coordinadores de la conferencia de este a\u00f1o, Juli\u00e1n Hern\u00e1ndez ( jhernandez88@utep.edu ), Ana C. Maass ( acmaass@utep.edu ) y Judith R\u00edos ( jrios@uacj.mx ) para preguntar sobre formatos alternativos, ideas o comentarios sobre la Semana Mundial del Agua 2026 en UTEP y UACJ. Para enviar su propuesta, complete el formulario de Google en l\u00ednea (enlace al final del p\u00e1rrafo) antes del lunes 13 de enero de 2026. La respuesta a las propuestas se dar\u00e1 a conocer el 23 de enero, seguida de la calendarizaci\u00f3n final del evento a m\u00e1s tardar el 31 de enero de 2026. Formulario de Google (Ingl\u00e9s): https://forms.gle/sudf7Jy3gZxwummv5 Formulario de Google (Espa\u00f1ol): https://forms.gle/sdfU22abZ148RCz37 Fecha l\u00edmite para mandar propuestas: 13 de enero, 2026 Notificaciones de aceptaci\u00f3n: 23 de enero, 2026 Calendario final de eventos : 31 de enero, 2026 Para m\u00e1s informaci\u00f3n visita: World Water Week 26 Gracias de parte del Comit\u00e9 Organizador de UTEP y UACJ, el Cluster de \u201cOne Water\u201d, el Centro de Manejo de Recursos Ambientales, la Universidad Aut\u00f3noma de Ciudad Ju\u00e1rez, el Centro Rubin para las Artes Visuales y el Museo Centennial en UTEP. <!--\n    .accWrapper > div {\n    padding-left:24px;\n    }\n    .collapseToggleControl.collapsed span.glyphicon:before {\n        content: \"\\002b\";\n    }\n    .collapseToggleControl span.glyphicon:before {\n        content: \"\\2212\";\n    }\n    .optionalblock {\n        margin-top: 30px;\n        margin-bottom: 30px;\n    }\n /*flex*/\n.highligtsWrapper {\n    display: flex;\n    display: -webkit-flex;\n    flex-wrap: wrap;\n    margin-left: -14px;\n}\n.highligtsWrapper .col-md-4:nth-last-child(1) {\n    margin-bottom: 30px;\n}\n.highligtsWrapper .well {\n\tbox-shadow:0px 2px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);-webkit-box-shadow:0px 2px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);;\n\theight: 100%;\n\tpadding: 0;\n}\n.highligtsBody {\n\tpadding: 0 24px 0 24px;\n}\n.highligtsBody .btn-primary {\n    \tdisplay:block;\n    \tmargin-top: 30px;\n}\n\n.highligtsWrapper .col-md-4 {\n   margin-bottom: 30px;\n}\n\n.lightWhiteBg {\n\tbackground: rgba(255,255,255,.85);\n    paddin