{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/engineering/cassmar/people/", "title": "Leadership", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About CASSMAR People Leadership Staff Interns Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support CASSMAR College of Engineering Main Content UTEP College of Engineering CASSMAR People UTEP College of Engineering CASSMAR People Leadership Shalayna Smith, Ph.D., P.E. Director Dr. Smith serves as Director of CASSMAR and Professor of Practice in the Department of Metallurgical, Materials, and Biomedical Engineering at UTEP. In her academic role, she focuses on delivering practical, applied engineering experiences that connect classroom learning to real problems and real industry needs. She leads capstone projects and supports research efforts in the expanding space engineering/research landscape. Dr. Smith is also actively involved in workforce development and outreach initiatives aimed at strengthening student pathways into aerospace and materials science careers, including ongoing collaboration efforts with LANL, NASA & Amentum. In addition to her academic work, Dr. Smith is a licensed Professional Engineer in Texas and a Principal Engineer at Herrera, Stafford & Associates in El Paso, where she conducts failure analysis investigations, provides consulting support, and assists with litigation cases across multiple industries. Her engagement in both academia and industry allows her to maintain current engineering practice in the classroom while contributing practical expertise to the organizations she serves. <!--\n.btn-primary {\n    background-color: #041E42;\n    padding: 10px 14px;\n    font-weight: 700;\n    font-size: 15px;\n    text-align:center;\n    color: white;\n    text-transform: uppercase;\n    \n  \n\n}\n\n.btn-primary:hover {\n    background-color: #FF8200;\n    color: #041E42;\n}\n\n.utep-profiles.utep-blue, .utep-profiles.utep-blue h2 {\n\t color: white;\n}\n .utep-profiles.utep-orange, .utep-profiles.utep-orange h2 {\n\t color: rgb(0, 33, 71);\n}\n .utep-orange {\n\t background-color: rgb(255, 121, 0);\n}\n .utep-blue {\n\t background-color: rgb(0, 33, 71);\n}\n .utep-profiles {\n\t height: auto;\n}\n .utep-profiles > div {\n\t padding: 0;\n}\n .profilePics{\n\t background-image: url(Images/profiles/johndoe.jpg);\n\t background-size: cover;\n\t background-position: center;\n\t height: 400px;\n}\n .utep-profiles .arrow-right {\n\t top: 25%;\n\t position: absolute;\n\t left: 0;\n}\n .utep-profiles .arrow-left {\n\t top: 25%;\n\t position: absolute;\n\t right: 0;\n}\n .arrow-down {\n\t border-left: solid transparent;\n\t border-right: solid transparent;\n\t border-top: solid rgb(0, 33, 71);\n}\n .arrow-left {\n\t border-top: solid transparent;\n\t border-bottom: solid transparent;\n\t border-right: solid rgb(0, 33, 71);\n}\n .arrow-right {\n\t border-top: solid transparent;\n\t border-bottom: solid transparent;\n\t border-left: solid rgb(255, 121, 0);\n}\n .arrow-sm {\n\t border-width: 5px;\n}\n .arrow-md {\n\t border-width: 15px;\n}\n .arrow-lg {\n\t border-width: 30px;\n}\n .utep-profile {\n\t padding: 5% 10% 1% 10%;\n}\n .utep-profiles .btn {\n\t background-color: white;\n\t color: rgb(0, 33, 71);\n\t width: 40%;\n\t padding-top: 7px;\n\t padding-bottom: 7px;\n\t font-weight: bold;\n\t max-width: 250px;\n\t min-width: 130px;\n\t margin-top: 10px;\n}\n.whitep{\n    color:#fff !important;\n}\nh2{\n    padding: 0px;\n    margin: 0px 0