{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/aerospace/frontiers/energy.html", "title": "Energy and Sustainability Frontier", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About About Aerospace Center Student Success Research Stations Mission Crew Aerospace Leadership Frontiers STAR Frontier Space Frontier Aeronautics and Defense Frontier Energy and Sustainability Frontier Astro Fab Astro Fab Explore Prosperity Explore Prosperity Digital Engineering Digital Engineering Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Aerospace Center Main Content Energy and Sustainability Frontier <!--\n.carousel-caption {\n    display: block !important;\n}\n--> <!--\n@media (max-width: 991px) {\n    .fw-section{\n            background-attachment: unset !important;\n        }\n    }\n--> Energy & Sustainability Frontier The Energy & Sustainability Frontier at the Aerospace Center is at the forefront of innovative energy solutions , advancing research from sub-pilot to commercial-scale in fossil, nuclear, and renewable energy technologies . Our mission is to drive sustainable, resilient, and efficient energy systems that support both terrestrial and space applications , contributing to national security, economic growth, and environmental responsibility. Key Research Areas: Advanced Fossil Energy & Carbon Management Developing\u00a0next-generation clean energy technologies\u00a0that reduce carbon emissions (CO 2 , NO X , SO X , particular matter, etc.) while maximizing thermal efficiency. Innovating\u00a0carbon capture, utilization, and storage (CCUS)\u00a0solutions to minimize the environmental impact of fossil fuel use. Designing novel & advanced nanocatalytic systems for converting carbon dioxide into valuable products for space applications while simultaneously reducing the carbon footprint on Earth. Nuclear Energy & Space Power Systems Advancing\u00a0microreactor and modular nuclear technologies\u00a0for space and terrestrial applications. Developing innovative materials with high resistance to harsh environments for nuclear reactors. Researching\u00a0radioisotope power systems (RPS) and fission surface power\u00a0to enable long-duration space missions and off-grid energy solutions. Renewable Energy & Sustainable Power Solutions Driving\u00a0solar, wind, and bioenergy innovations\u00a0to support commercial and defense energy resilience. Exploring\u00a0green, blue, and turquoise hydrogen as well as Sustainable Aviation Fuel production, storage, and utilization\u00a0for\u00a0net zero-emission power generation. Prototype-to-Commercial Demonstration & Testing Providing\u00a0end-to-end technology development, from\u00a0concept validation to full-scale implementation. Offering\u00a0state-of-the-art testing and evaluation\u00a0for commercial energy solutions, ensuring reliability and performance in extreme environments. Energy Conversion, Storage & Grid Resiliency Developing\u00a0advanced battery technologies, fuel cells, electrolyzers, and energy conversion/storage systems\u00a0to enhance\u00a0grid stability, energy security, and space power applications. Exploring\u00a0AI-driven energy management and smart grid technologies\u00a0to optimize power distribution and efficiency. By bridging\u00a0cutting-edge research with real-world implementation, the\u00a0Energy & Sustainability Frontier\u00a0is driving the\u00a0future of clean energy, power resilience, and sustainable solutions for both Earth and space e