developed. CIDS has several pilot units available for desalination experiments. These are available for contract research or lease agreements. Mobile equipment ranges from 0.2-0.5 gallon per minute product water to 10-40 gallon per minute product water an include ultrafiltration, electrodialysis, and reverse osmosis technologies. Engineering Lab Physical Sciences Lab and ED laboratory equipment Pilot Equipment CIDS Water Treatment Process Testing Lab-1 (Room, E203) Electrodialysis Contaminant removal Salt and mineral recovery Point-of-use/Point-of-entry water treatment Total suspended solids and Total dissolve solids method equipment CIDS Water Quality Analysis Lab (Room, E207) General water quality (pH, conductivity, turbidity, alkalinity) Colorimetetric methods Perkin Elmer Optima 7300DV ICP-OES Dionex ICS 2100 \"Integral\" Ion Chromatograph Dionex ICS ICS1100 & ICS2100 Ion Chromatograph (anions and cations) with auto-sampler Agilent 8453 UV-Vis spectrophotometer Shimadzu Total Organic Carbon analyzer (TOC-VCSH) Agilent 7890A Series GC with autosampler Physical Sciences Lab (Room, PSCI402) Membrane distillation Coulter Counter MS4 particle counter CERRO TM DI water system Bipolar membrane testing Hardness sensor development CIDS Laboratory ED Systems ED systems with two or four compartment designs with 0.2-0.5 m2 exposed area (per cell pair/quad) 1-2 gpm mobile ZDD system (NF/RO + EDM) CIDS Pilot Equipment 15-gpm UF system (3) 20-gpm NF/RO systems 40-gpm ZDD system (NF/RO + EDM) <!--\n    .accWrapper > div {\n    padding-left:24px;\n    }\n    .collapseToggleControl.collapsed span.glyphicon:before {\n        content: \"\\002b\";\n    }\n    .collapseToggleControl span.glyphicon:before {\n        content: \"\\2212\";\n    }\n    .optionalblock {\n        margin-top: 30px;\n        margin-bottom: 30px;\n    }\n /*flex*/\n.highligtsWrapper {\n    display: flex;\n    display: -webkit-flex;\n    flex-wrap: wrap;\n    margin-left: -14px;\n}\n.highligtsWrapper .col-md-4: