{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/aerospace/frontiers/star-frontier.html", "title": "STAR Frontier", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About About Aerospace Center Student Success Research Stations Mission Crew Aerospace Leadership Frontiers STAR Frontier Space Frontier Aeronautics and Defense Frontier Energy and Sustainability Frontier Astro Fab Astro Fab Explore Prosperity Explore Prosperity Digital Engineering Digital Engineering Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Aerospace Center Main Content STAR Frontier <!--\n.carousel-caption {\n    display: block !important;\n}\n--> <!--\n@media (max-width: 991px) {\n    .fw-section{\n            background-attachment: unset !important;\n        }\n    }\n--> Space Technologies and AI-Driven Research (STAR) in Advanced Materials Science Frontier The STAR Frontier at the Aerospace Center is pioneering the fusion of\u00a0Artificial Intelligence (AI) and Advanced Materials Science, accelerating discoveries for space, defense, and industry. Our mission is to position\u00a0Texas as a leading hub\u00a0for aerospace materials research, driving rapid innovation for spacecraft, satellites, and hypersonic systems. AI-Powered Materials Innovation AI-Accelerated Materials Engineering AI-Guided Materials Discovery AI-Augmented Manufacturing AI-Driven Materials Discovery & Process Modeling Leveraging machine learning and computational modeling to accelerate the discovery of novel materials for space structures, propulsion systems, and lunar In-Situ Resource Utilization ( ISRU) applications. Our work integrates AI with physics-based simulations to optimize materials for manufacturability, durability, and performance in extraterrestrial conditions. By integrating\u00a0AI and machine learning, we streamline material development, enhance predictive modeling, and enable real-time analytics\u2014leading to\u00a0lighter, stronger, and more resilient materials\u00a0for extreme space conditions. <!--\n.responsive-img {\n        width: 90%; /* Default width */\n        height: auto;\n        max-height: 319px;\n        float: left;\n        margin-right: 15px;\n    }\n\n    @media (max-width: 768px) { \n        /* For tablets and smaller screens */\n        .responsive-img {\n            width: 60%; /* Increase width to make it more visible on smaller screens */\n            float: none; /* Remove float to center it */\n            display: block;\n            margin: 0 auto; /* Center image */\n        }\n    }\n\n    @media (max-width: 480px) { \n        /* For mobile screens */\n        .responsive-img {\n            width: 80%; /* Make it larger on small screens */\n        }\n    }\n--> Our interdisciplinary approach transforms\u00a0materials from prediction to production, reinforcing U.S. leadership in\u00a0space exploration, national defense, and commercial aerospace. With cutting-edge research and real-world applications, the STAR Frontier is shaping the next generation of space technologies and enhancing U.S. capabilities in defense, exploration, and commercial aerospace. <!--\n#myBtn {\n  display: none;\n  position: fixed;\n  bottom: 20px;\n  right: 30px;\n  z-index: 99;\n  font-size: 18px;\n  border: none;\n  outline: none;\n  background-color: #041e42;\n  color: white;\n  cursor: pointer;\n  padding: 15px;\n  border-radius: 4px;\n}\n\n#myBtn:hover {\n  background-color: #ff8200;\n}\n--> <!--\nh1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6   {text-a