{"url": "https://expertise.utep.edu/profiles/datillman", "title": "Daniel Tillman | Expertise Connector", "text": "Enhancements HELP PEOPLE CENTERS COMMUNITIES RESEARCH STORIES .wrap-main-search{\n    position: relative;\n    left: 10px;\n    bottom: 17px;\n  }\n  .search-main-box {\n   display: flex;\n  }\n  .searchTerm-main-box {\n    width: 100%;\n    border: 1px solid #b1b3b3;\n    border-right: none;\n    padding: 5px;\n    background: #ffffff;\n    outline: none;\n    color: #041E42;\n  }\n  .searchTerm-main-box:focus{\n    color: #041E42;\n  }\n  .searchButton-main-box {\n    width: 40px;\n    border: 1px solid #041E42;\n    background: #041E42;\n    text-align: center;\n    color: #fff;\n    cursor: pointer;\n    font-size: 20px;\n  } Daniel Tillman 809 Education Building El Paso Texas , 79968 datillman@utep.edu (915) 747-0153 Community Community of Engaged Scholars NETWORKS .networkprofile\n{\ntext-decoration: none;\n} Daniel A. Tillman Associate Professor, Teacher Education .titleEventStyle{\n  font-size: 12px;\n  font-weight: bolder;\n  position: relative;\n  font-family: \"Myriad Pro\", \"Trebuchet MS\", \"Arial\", sans-serif;\n} Daniel Tillman, Ph.D., is an Associate Professor in Educational Technology at The University of Texas at El Paso (UTEP) as well as the co-director of the College of Education Makerspace. His current research focuses on the diffusion of technology innovations into K-12 education, physical and digital multimedia in elementary school science and mathematics education, and the STEM career pipeline and mainline. He teaches both graduate and undergraduate courses about instructional technology and instructional design, and has developed a hybrid graduate course on advanced digital multimedia design. He received his doctoral degree in Instructional Technology at The University of Virginia in 2012 under the mentoring of Dr. Glen Bull. While at UVA, he served as a graduate fellow in the Curry School of Education's Center for Technology and Teacher Education and as the office manager for the Dynamic Media Research Laboratory. Prior to entering the Ph.D. program at The University of Virginia, he directed and edited documentary films for eight years. From 2005 to 2012 he served as an adjunct professor at George Mason University, where he taught undergraduate courses entitled: Introduction to Multimedia, Advanced Multimedia Design, and Documentary Filmmaking. .profile-titleStatment\n{\ncolor:#FF8200;\nfont-size:20px;\nfont-family: \"trebuchet ms\";\ntext-transform:uppercase;\n}\n.profile-infoStatement\n{\n\nfont-family: Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif;\nfont-size: 11px;\n}\n.profile-link\n{\ncolor:#FF8200 !important;\n}\n\n.awd_profile_link{\nposition: absolute;\nleft: 624px;\ntop: 0px;\ntext-decoration: underline;\n}\n\n.patent_profile_link{\nposition: absolute;\nleft: 624px;\ntop: 16px;\ntext-decoration: underline;\n}\n\n.student_profile_link{\nposition: absolute;\nleft: 624px;\ntop: 31px;\ntext-decoration: underline;\n} KEYWORDS Diffusion of Innovations within K-12 Education Science and Mathematics Education STEM Career Pipeline and Mainline Educational Technology and Instructional Design Digital Multimedia Production and Assessment Machine Learning and Deep Learning .expertise_keywords_custom_container{\n/*position: relative;\ntop: 14px;\nleft: 12px;*/\n}\n\n.in_the_new_title{\ncolor: #e47d00;\nfont-weight: bold;\nfont-size: 18px;\nfont-family: \"Trebuchet MS\";\n}\n\n.list_keywords{\nline-height: 14px;\n/*position: relative;\ntop: 13px;*/\n}\n\n\n#toggle_keywords{\nposition: relative;\nleft: 170px;\nbottom: 12px;\ncursor: pointer;\nfont-family: \"Verdana, Geneva, Sans-Serif\";\nfont-size: 12px;\ncolor: #13275d;\ntext-decoration: underline;\n} $(document).ready(function () {\n\n    var max = 5\n    if ($(this).find('li').length > max) {\n       \n        $(\"#list_keywords li:gt(\" + max + \")\").hide()   \n        $(\".toggle_keywords\").click(function() {\n           $(\"#list_keywords li:gt(\" + max +