{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/aerospace/about/research-stations.html", "title": "Research Stations", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About About Aerospace Center Student Success Research Stations Mission Crew Aerospace Leadership Frontiers STAR Frontier Space Frontier Aeronautics and Defense Frontier Energy and Sustainability Frontier Astro Fab Astro Fab Explore Prosperity Explore Prosperity Digital Engineering Digital Engineering Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Aerospace Center Main Content Research STATIONS <!--\n.carousel-caption {\n    display: block !important;\n}\n--> <!--\n@media (max-width: 991px) {\n    .fw-section{\n            background-attachment: unset !important;\n        }\n    }\n--> Research Stations The Aerospace Center is rapidly expanding its state-of-the-art facilities to propel groundbreaking aerospace research into new frontiers. Our new $80 million, 93,000-square-foot Advanced Manufacturing and Aerospace Center (AMAC) at UTEP is home to two research powerhouses: the Aerospace Center and the W.M. Keck Center for 3D Innovation. This advanced facility significantly enhances our research capabilities and increases opportunities for training the next generation of aerospace innovators. AMAC is more than a physical space ; it's a catalyst for building partnerships and collaborations that ignite frontier-breaking research! Fueled by cutting-edge infrastructure, research, and technology development, and strategic partnerships, our capabilities span designing, building, and testing technologies essential for space exploration, defense, and sustainable energy solutions. These combined assets position the Aerospace Center as a leader in aerospace, defense, and energy innovation, while offering students unparalleled hands-on research experiences. Our facilities meet strict ITAR compliance standards and support research within Controlled Unclassified Information environments. Aerospace Center Facility Highlights : Astro Fab (machine shop) | 985 sq. ft. Analytical Chemistry | 505 sq. ft. Manufacturing Analytics and Digital Engineering Lab | 1,548 sq. ft. Mission Operations (featuring a 27' display) | 681 sq. ft. plus support space Uncrewed Aerial Systems Assembly | 956 sq. ft. & Flight Space | 1,251 sq. ft. Analytical Testing | 1,931 sq. ft. Material Synthesis | 1,265 sq. ft. Space Environmental Testing | 2,097 sq. ft. Spacecraft Development | 1,749 sq. ft. Hypersonic Lab | 1,449 sq. ft. Clean Rooms: ISO8 | 423 sq. ft. & ISO7 | 124 sq. ft. Off-Campus Research Facilities: Alpha Site (Research Airport, Fabens, TX) Propulsion and Energy Systems Integration Facility | 10,200 sq. ft. Large-scale propulsion testing on 18-acre site with 5 test cells, vertical and horizontal test stands Bravo Site (UAS Flight Test Range, Tornillo, TX) 600-acre facility with 400-foot runways, Test Support Facility, LSTAR Radar, DeTect Harrier Radar, and 100 KW power trailer Spacecraft Design and Engineering Facility (Francis St, El Paso, TX) 8,840 sq. ft. with Satellite Ground Station (2.4 m S-band antenna, 436 MHz UHF antenna), training rooms, offices, and collaborative student spaces <!--\n.smaller-image {\n        max-width: 60%; /* Adjust as needed */\n        height: auto; /* Maintain aspect ratio */\n        display: block;\n        margin: 0 auto; /* Center image */\n    }\n\n    @media (max-width: 768px) {\n        .smaller-image {\n            max