{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/aerospace/about/student-success.html", "title": "Student Success", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About About Aerospace Center Student Success Research Stations Mission Crew Aerospace Leadership Frontiers STAR Frontier Space Frontier Aeronautics and Defense Frontier Energy and Sustainability Frontier Astro Fab Astro Fab Explore Prosperity Explore Prosperity Digital Engineering Digital Engineering Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Aerospace Center Main Content Student Success <!--\n@media (max-width: 991px) {\n    .fw-section{\n            background-attachment: unset !important;\n            background-size: contain !important;\n        }\n    }\n--> At The University of Texas at El Paso's Aerospace Center, we are redefining education and workforce development through transformational learning experiences and hands-on research in our cutting-edge labs. Our mission is to empower students with the skills, knowledge, and real-world expertise needed to meet the growing demands of the aerospace, defense, and STEM industries. The nation is facing a critical workforce challenge: the need for a new wave of globally-minded, highly skilled talent to fuel innovation and maintain global competitiveness. The Department of Defense (DoD) and industry partners are urgently seeking professionals who not only have technical expertise but also the adaptability and problem-solving capabilities required for today\u2019s rapidly evolving challenges. At the Aerospace Center, we take pride in bridging this gap by providing students with unparalleled opportunities to engage in advanced research, develop industry-aligned skills, and gain valuable experience that positions them as leaders in aerospace. Our student-centered approach ensures that every individual thrives academically and professionally while contributing to the talent pipeline that drives our nation's security and economic vitality. The Aerospace Center\u2019s research programs empower students with unparalleled opportunities for social and economic mobility. By joining our team as research assistants, junior engineers, engineers, or technicians, students gain invaluable hands-on experience that sets them apart in the competitive job market. This practical training provides a significant edge, enabling our graduates to excel in their careers. Many of our alumni have secured positions with prestigious organizations such as NASA, Blue Origin, Lockheed Martin, Raytheon, and others, launching them into successful and impactful professional journeys. <!--\n.responsive-left-img {\n        width: 50%; /* Adjust the width as needed */\n        height: auto;\n        max-height: 366px;\n        float: left;\n        margin-right: 15px; /* Adds spacing between image and text */\n        padding-top: 50px; /* Extra space above */\n        padding-bottom: 50px; /* Extra space below */\n    }\n\n    @media (max-width: 768px) { \n        /* Adjust for tablets and smaller screens */\n        .responsive-left-img {\n            width: 60%;\n            float: none;\n            display: block;\n            margin: 20px auto; /* Adds padding and centers the image */\n        }\n    }\n\n    @media (max-width: 480px) { \n        /* Adjust for mobile screens */\n        .responsive-left-img {\n            width: 80%;\n        }\n    }\n--> Our student-centered model is what sets our graduates apart and makes them highly sought after by aerospace industry leaders. Recognizing that many of our students work while pursuing their education, we hire them as research assistants, engineers, junior engineers and technicians, ensuring their work directly contributes to their future careers. Unlike many universities, where research opportunities are often reserved for master\u2019s and Ph.D. students, 50% of our students working in The Aerospace Center are undergraduates. In our labs, students integrate classroom theory and practice with industry-aligned skills development through an iterative Design-Build-Test cycle in multidisciplinary teams. Our research portfolio addresses emerging challenges and opportunities in aerospace, leveraging cutting-edge digital tools, state-of-the-art facilities, and industry-grade equipment to reflect current trends. Students also engage directly with industry and agency partners through collaborative research, mentoring, and professional presentations. Whether leading lab tours or showcasing their work at conferences and symposiums, these experiences prepare them to excel in real-world environments. <!--\n.responsive-left-img {\n        width: 40%; /* Adjust the width as needed */\n        height: auto;\n        max-height: 366px;\n        float: left;\n        margin-right: 15px; /* Adds spacing between image and text */\n        padding-top: 50px; /* Extra space above */\n        padding-bottom: 50px; /* Extra space below */\n    }\n\n    @media (max-width: 768px) { \n        /* Adjust for tablets and smaller screens */\n        .responsive-left-img {\n            width: 60%;\n            float: none;\n            display: block;\n            margin: 20px auto; /* Adds padding and centers the image */\n        }\n    }\n\n    @media (max-width: 480px) { \n        /* Adjust for mobile screens */\n        .responsive-left-img {\n            width: 80%;\n        }\n    }\n--> <!--\n#myBtn {\n  display: none;\n  position: fixed;\n  