 supports research investigators, department administrators and our partner research support offices by providing comprehensive support services for the successful administration of externally funded sponsored projects. Services include assistance with proposal submission, award negotiations, non-financial and financial award mangement and data systems support. Our goal is to deliver our support services in an efficient and professional manner while maintaining full compliance with Sponsor, Federal, State and Institution guidelines. Office of Sponsored Projects Cory Brown Director - Office of Sponsored Projects cjbrown5@utep.edu (915) 747-5732 Kelly Hall, Rm. 606 The Office of Sponsored Projects (OSP) is the centralized unit charged with providing comprehensive support to members of The University of Texas at El Paso (UTEP) research community engaged in the preparation and submission of proposals and the management of funded projects. OSP strives to maintain a supportive environment for research and scholarly endeavors and encourages faculty and staff to seek external funding to support the mission of the University and to explore alternatives to advance their professional interest. View OSP Contact OSP Grant Management Accounting Yesenia Castaneda Director - Grant Management Accounting yncastaneda@utep.edu (915) 747-5698 Kelly Hall, Rm. 615 Grant Management Accounting provides sound financial oversight and to process and manage the University\u2019s federal, state, local, and private programs in accordance with the post-award agreements. CGA\u2019s commitment is to provide responsible fiscal management of contracts and grants in a responsive and efficient manner for the overall achievement to our research community as well as to our funding agencies. View GMA Contact GMA <!--\n#myBtn {\n  display: none;\n  position: fixed;\n  bottom: 20px;\n  right: 30px;\n  z-index: 99;\n  font-size: 18px;\n  border: none;\n  outline: none;\n  background-color: #041e42;\n  color: 