{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/ada-advisorycommittee/frequently-asked-questions.html", "title": "FAQ's", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About About ADA Advisory Committee Committee Members Members Meetings Meetings UTEP ADA Coordinator UTEP ADA Coordinator Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support ADA Advisory Committee Main Content UTEP ADA Advisory Committee UTEP ADA Advisory Committee FAQ's There is a physical barrier on the sidewalk/doorway/hallway, who do I contact to report it? Use the Facilities Report button to report an issues with doors, sidewalks, or any other physical barrier. The door to my building is stuck or the automatic door opener does not work, who do I call or report it to? Use the Facilities Report button to report any issues with doors, sidewalks, or any other physical barrier. I just broke my arm/leg/bone and I am having difficulty getting to class on time, what can I do? Students should apply for accommodations with the Center for Accommodations and Support Services (CASS). Utilize the button on our main page to quickly get you to the cassportal. Who should I contact for an ADA accommodation for the workplace? An employee can initiate a request for an ADA accommodation by notifying the ADA Coordinator in the Equal Opportunity (EO) Office of the nature of the disability and the accommodation being requested. Where do students go to request ADA accommodations for the classroom? If a student needs an ADA accommodation for the academic setting, they need to contact the Center for Accommodations\u00a0and Support Services (CASS) at (915) 747-5148 or visit www.utep.edu/student-affairs/cass/ .\u00a0Reasonable accommodations are provided only to students with known disabilities who are\u00a0registered with the CASS Office. Who is protected by the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA)? The ADA, prohibits employment discrimination against qualified individuals with disabilities.\u00a0 A \u201cqualified individual\u201d means an individual who, with or without reasonable accommodation, can perform the essential functions of the employment position that such individual holds or desires. What is a reasonable accommodation? A reasonable accommodation is any modification or adjustment to a job or the work environment that will enable an employee with a disability to perform the essential job functions. People Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso Office of the Vice President for Business Affairs ADA Advisory Committee 500 W University El Paso, Texas 79902 E: ADAAdvisoryCommittee@utep.edu THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Texas Veterans Portal Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 | SITE FEEDBACK Modal X"}
