{"url": "https://expertise.utep.edu/profiles/jricketts", "title": "Jason Ricketts | Expertise Connector", "text": "Enhancements HELP PEOPLE CENTERS COMMUNITIES RESEARCH STORIES .wrap-main-search{\n    position: relative;\n    left: 10px;\n    bottom: 17px;\n  }\n  .search-main-box {\n   display: flex;\n  }\n  .searchTerm-main-box {\n    width: 100%;\n    border: 1px solid #b1b3b3;\n    border-right: none;\n    padding: 5px;\n    background: #ffffff;\n    outline: none;\n    color: #041E42;\n  }\n  .searchTerm-main-box:focus{\n    color: #041E42;\n  }\n  .searchButton-main-box {\n    width: 40px;\n    border: 1px solid #041E42;\n    background: #041E42;\n    text-align: center;\n    color: #fff;\n    cursor: pointer;\n    font-size: 20px;\n  } Jason Ricketts 405 Geological Sciences Building El Paso Texas , 79968 jricketts@utep.edu (915) 747-5599 Web Site Community Community of Engaged Scholars NETWORKS .networkprofile\n{\ntext-decoration: none;\n} Jason William Ricketts Associate Professor, Earth, Environmental and Resource Sciences .titleEventStyle{\n  font-size: 12px;\n  font-weight: bolder;\n  position: relative;\n  font-family: \"Myriad Pro\", \"Trebuchet MS\", \"Arial\", sans-serif;\n} Dr. Ricketts is a geologist with a major focus on structural geology, tectonics, low-temperature thermochronology, and fluid-fault interactions. Much of his research centers on brittle tectonics in Earth\u2019s upper crust. His research combines field methods and observations with various analytical techniques and modeling efforts to investigate processes which control deformation. His expertise centers on the development of the Rio Grande rift of Colorado, New Mexico, and western Texas, where he routinely conducts field work with students and colleagues. .profile-titleStatment\n{\ncolor:#FF8200;\nfont-size:20px;\nfont-family: \"trebuchet ms\";\ntext-transform:uppercase;\n}\n.profile-infoStatement\n{\n\nfont-family: Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif;\nfont-size: 11px;\n}\n.profile-link\n{