{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/liberalarts/theatre-dance/", "title": "Theatre and Dance", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About Mission Our Chair's Welcome Department Accomplishments and Achievements Past Productions Season and Tickets Academic Programs Theatre Program Dance Program People Faculty and Administration UTEP Alumni News & Events Recent News Current Events In memoriam: Ingeborg Heuser In memoriam: Myron Nadel Resources Business Center Forms COVID Resources Student Organizations Student Space Rentals Degree Plans Scholarships Careers Theatre Education The Dinner Theatre The Dinner Theatre Give Now Give Now Scholarship Donations The Wise Theatre Renovations Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Theatre & Dance College of Liberal Arts Main Content UTEP College of Liberal Arts Theatre & Dance 2025-2026 Season LEARN MORE Welcome LEARN MORE Theatre Program LEARN MORE Dance Program LEARN MORE Student Organizations LEARN MORE Past Productions LEARN MORE The Dinner Theatre LEARN MORE Mission/Vision/Values LEARN MORE Previous Next UTEP College of Liberal Arts Theatre & Dance Theatre and Dance What is your story? The Department of Theatre and Dance at the University of Texas-El Paso is made up of diverse artists and scholars whose devotion to exceptional teaching, service, creative practice, and research aligns with the University mission by contributing to the quality of life in El Paso, the surrounding region, and beyond. Our dedicated student-centered program offers many performance and design opportunities within our season of shows at the Wise Family Theater, the June Sadowski Kruszewski Studio Theatre, and the Dinner Theater, along with traveling productions, student projects, and the Chican@/Latin@ Theatre series. Collectively, the department hosts 20 productions a year. The UTEP Department of Theatre and Dance is committed to allowing student artists to refine their skills for a professional career.. Our Core Values We are the voice for the voiceless and advocate for social change. We are leaders for social justice in our region, using theatre and dance as a platform. Through our courses, research, productions, and mentorships, we guide and support students as role models and allies and pave the way for their success and social mobility. We are thrilled to announce our 2025\u20132026 season, filled with powerful stories and unforgettable performances! We open on October 24 with I Am Not Your Perfect Mexican Daughter by Isaac G\u00f3mez, based on the bestselling novel by Erika L. S\u00e1nchez\u2014a moving and heartfelt story that will set the tone for an inspiring season. Then, on November 14 , prepare to be dazzled by Andrew Lloyd Webber\u2019s legendary musical CATS , based on T.S. Eliot\u2019s Old Possum\u2019s Book of Practical Cats . To close out the fall semester, we bring you the enchanting play The River Bride by Marisela Trevi\u00f1o Orta, opening December 3 in the June Sadowski Kruszewski Studio Theatre. The spring semester begins on February 19, 2026 , with Slow Emergences , a transformative dance concert exploring how communities can grow and adapt in the face of global crises. On March 27 , we head to New York City\u2019s East Village for Jonathan Larson\u2019s groundbreaking musical RENT , a story of love, resilience, and chosen family. Finally, on April 17 , we present Sarah Ruhl\u2019s Orlando , a witty and imaginative adaptation of Virginia Woolf\u2019s classic novel. We are overjoyed to continue sharing important and diverse stories with the El Paso community, and we can\u2019t wait to welcome you into our audience for this extraordinary season of theatre and dance! RECENT NEWS // \nvar calendarID = \"0a799bh9avsb007qthpgnvoe9o\";   // Google Calendar ID\nvar type = \"news\";                               // \"news\" or \"events\"\nvar maxReslts = \"\";                              // max # of results, \"\" for all\nvar divID = \"news-list\";                         // name of &lt;div&gt;\nvar time = \"current\";                            // \"past\" or \"current\"\nvar yearmonth = \"\";                              // specific \"year-Month\", \"\" for all\nvar listStyle = \"minimal\";                       // \"minimal\", \"small\", \"large\" or \"verbose\"\nvar order = \"descending\";                        // \"ascending\" or \"descending\"\nvar newWindow = \"yes\";                           // \"yes\" or \"no\"\nvar imgAlignment = \"left\";                       // \"left\" or \"right\"\ndepartmentalListings(calendarID, type, maxReslts, divID, time, yearmonth, listStyle, order, newWindow, imgAlignment);\n// Your browser does not support JavaScript. For a listing of news, please visit: https://calendar.google.com/calendar/embed?src=0a799bh9avsb007qthpgnvoe9o@group.calendar.google.com&ctz=America/Denver&mode=AGENDA For a complete list, please visit the News page. CURRENT & UPCOMING EVENTS View All Current and Upcoming Events <!--\nul#lwe {\n\tlist-style-type: none;\n\tpadding-left: 0;\n}\n\n.lwe {\n\tclear:both;\n\tmargin-bottom:30px;\n}\n\nspan.lwn0 {\n   display:block;\n} \n\n.lwn {\n    font-weight:600;\n    color: #041E42;\n}\n\n.lwn a {\n    font-size: 24px;\n    font-family: \"Tungsten A\", \"Tungsten B\", \"Open Sans\", sans-serif;\n    font-weight: 500;\n    text-transform: uppercase;\n    word-spacing: 3px;\n    letter-spacing: 2px;\n    line-height: 1.2;\n}\n\n\n.lwd sp