{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/liberalarts/theatre-dance/resources/student%20organizations.html", "title": "Student Organizations", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About Mission Our Chair's Welcome Department Accomplishments and Achievements Past Productions Season and Tickets Academic Programs Theatre Program Dance Program People Faculty and Administration UTEP Alumni News & Events Recent News Current Events In memoriam: Ingeborg Heuser In memoriam: Myron Nadel Resources Business Center Forms COVID Resources Student Organizations Student Space Rentals Degree Plans Scholarships Careers Theatre Education The Dinner Theatre The Dinner Theatre Give Now Give Now Scholarship Donations The Wise Theatre Renovations Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Theatre & Dance College of Liberal Arts Main Content UTEP College of Liberal Arts Theatre & Dance Resources UTEP College of Liberal Arts Theatre & Dance Resources Student Organizations Playmakers The main goal of\u00a0Playmakers is to raise scholarship funds for incoming\u00a0Theatre and Dance students at UTEP. The student group\u00a0was founded on a\u00a0\u201cPay it Forward\u201d ideal\u00a0in order for students to support one another in\u00a0education and preparation for the professional world.\u00a0 It is a great organization for\u00a0students to join and meet the heart of student body of\u00a0the department. Playmakers\u00a0help produce student-based productions in the department, such as \"Reasons to be Pretty\" (Summer 2016), \"Bent\" (Summer 2017), and \"Sons of the Prophet\" (Summer 2018) and coordinate social events for\u00a0students to enjoy and share their experiences in the field. Currently, Playmakers is preparing workshops to tour the schools in El Paso, to share their\u00a0love and knowledge for theatre. Please contact\u00a0Playmakers\u00a0through\u00a0Facebook at UTEP Playmakers for any information or inquiries. \" Desert Dance Desert Dance, a Registered Student Organization, is open to any UTEP student who is interested in supporting dance in the Department of Theatre and Dance, in other locations on campus, and throughout the greater community.\u00a0 Some of the projects Desert Dance is involved in include fundraisers for student travel to the American College Dance Association festivals, presentation of master classes taught by guest artists, and creating scholarships for UTEP Dance Majors. Membership requires participation in occasional meetings, helping in fundraising efforts, and the payment of membership dues. Resources Business Center Forms COVID Resources Student Organizations Student Space Rentals Degree Plans Scholarships Careers Theatre Education Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Theatre and Dance Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso Department of Theatre and Dance Fox Fine Arts Building, Room 371D 500 W University El Paso, Texas 79902 For season information: E: hwmaccarthy@utep.edu P: 915-747-5118 For program information: E: rfmayer@utep.edu P: 915-747-5502 THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Texas Veterans Portal Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 | SITE FEEDBACK