{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/liberalarts/theatre-dance/academic-programs/bachelor-program.html", "title": "Theatre Program", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About Mission Our Chair's Welcome Department Accomplishments and Achievements Past Productions Season and Tickets Academic Programs Theatre Program Dance Program People Faculty and Administration UTEP Alumni News & Events Recent News Current Events In memoriam: Ingeborg Heuser In memoriam: Myron Nadel Resources Business Center Forms COVID Resources Student Organizations Student Space Rentals Degree Plans Scholarships Careers Theatre Education The Dinner Theatre The Dinner Theatre Give Now Give Now Scholarship Donations The Wise Theatre Renovations Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Theatre & Dance College of Liberal Arts Main Content UTEP College of Liberal Arts Theatre & Dance Academic Programs UTEP College of Liberal Arts Theatre & Dance Academic Programs Theatre Program UTEP THEATRE Come tell your story here. BACHELORS OF FINE ARTS IN THEATRE If you want to eat, drink, and sleep theatre, you might be ready for UTEP\u2019s Bachelors of Fine Arts program! Designed to prepare you for a professional career or further conservatory study, the BFA Theatre program will help you realize the full potential of your talent. Whether your ambition is to become a professional actor, scenic designer, or costume artisan, the BFA program at UTEP will equip you with the tools you need to take your next step. Because of the intensive nature of the BFA tracks, you will not be able to carry a minor or second major, but the additional training is worth the sacrifice. The UTEP Department of Theatre and Dance offers a Bachelors of Fine Arts degree with concentrations \u00a0in: PERFORMANCE TECHNOLOGY & DESIGN MUSICAL THEATRE STAGE MANAGEMENT BACHELOR OF ARTS in Theatre Arts with a Concentration in All-Levels Theatre Education There are two Bachelor of Arts degree plans students can choose from: Theatre Arts and Theatre Arts with a Concentration in All-Levels Theatre Education. All Theatre majors must take a minimum of 120 credits to graduate, 45 of which must be at the 3300-4300 level. Outside of the Theatre credits , all theatre students must take 42 credits to satisfy the University Core requirements. All BA students must complete 18 credits to satisfy the Liberal Arts General Education requirements, and 18 credits to satisfy the requirement for a minor (see the catalog for minor options and requirements). Students seeking teacher certification must satisfy the Education component by taking 18 prescribed credits in place of a minor. The UTEP Department of Theatre and Dance offers two Bachelor of Arts degree plans in: BA in Theatre Arts BA in Theatre Arts with a Concentration in All-Levels Theatre Education MINOR IN THEATRE Perhaps your educational priorities are in another field of study, but you still have a hunger for theatre. Or maybe you have always been curious about theatre, and now you want to try it. If theatre is important to you, but not the focus of your educational plan, a UTEP Minor in Theatre could be the right answer for you! A minor allows you to learn about every aspect of theatre, while still reserving most of your curricular hours for a major in another field of study. The UTEP Department of Theatre and Dance offers a Theatre Minor in: THEATRE ARTS What's your story? For more information on admission and how to become a miner, visit: https://www.utep.edu/student-affairs/admissions/ . For scholarship information, click the following link: Theatre Scholarships Back to our Degree Programs. Academic Programs Theatre Program Dance Program Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso Department of Theatre and Dance Fox Fine Arts Building, Room 371D 500 W University El Paso, Texas 79902 For season information: E: hwmaccarthy@utep.edu P: 915-747-5118 For program information: E: rfmayer@utep.edu P: 915-747-5502 THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Texas Veterans Portal Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 | SITE FEEDBACK Modal X"}
{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/liberalarts/theatre-dance/about/prices.html", "title": "Season and Tickets", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About Mission Our Chair's Welcome Department Accomplishments and Achievements Past Productions Season and Tickets Academic Programs Theatre Program Dance Program People Faculty and Administration UTEP Alumni News & Events Recent News Current Events In memoriam: Ingeborg Heuser In memoriam: Myron Nadel Resources Business Center Forms COVID Resources Student Organizations Student Space Rentals Degree Plans Scholarships Careers Theatre Education The Dinner Theatre The Dinner Theatre Give Now Give Now Scholarship Donations The Wise Theatre Renovations Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Theatre & Dance College of Liberal Arts Main Content UTEP College of Liberal Arts Theatre & Dance About UTEP College of Liberal Arts Theatre & Dance About UTEP DEPARTMENT OF THEATRE AND DANCE 2025-2026 SEASON I Am not your perfect Mexican Daughter Written By Isaac G\u00f3mez Based on the book by Erika L. S\u00e1nchez Directed by Adriana Dom \u00ed nguez Synopsis : Julia Reyes isn\u2019t your perfect Mexican daughter she\u2019s a brave, sharp Chicago teen torn between her immigrant parents\u2019 expectations and her dream to write. After her sister\u2019s tragic death, Julia\u2019s world unravels as she faces grief, mental health struggles, and the pressure of tradition. Navigating high school and poverty, she turns to her journal to share her truth and survive, it reminds us our dreams are real\u2014and they matter. Raw and powerful, I Am Not Your Perfect Mexican Daughter challenges us to speak up, seek help, and keep going\u2014even when it feels impossible. MATURE CONTENT Wise Family Theater 7:30 PM Performances October 24*, 25, 30 & November 1, 2025 2:00 PM Performances October 26 & November 2, 2025 *Discount Performance - All Tickets $10 Purchase Tickets for I Am Not Your Perfect Mexican Daughter Here \u201cI Am Not Your Perfect Mexican Daughter\u201d is presented by arrangement with Concord Theatricals on behalf of Samuel French, Inc. www.concordtheatricals.com CAts Music by Andrew Lloyd Webber Based on \u2018Old Possum\u2019s Book of Practical Cats\u2019 by T.S. Eliot Directed by Jaime Barba Synopsis: CATS is set amongst a larger-than-life junkyard playground and is alive with purr-fect felines including Rum Tum Tugger, Mr. Mistoffelees, Macavity, Jennyanydots, Old Deuteronomy, Skimbleshanks and Grizabella. The Jellicle Cats come out to play on one special night of the year \u2013 the night of the Jellicle Ball. One by one, they tell their stories for the amusement of Old Deuteronomy, their wise and benevolent leader, who must choose one of the Cats to ascend to The Heaviside Layer and be reborn into a whole new Jellicle life. The Dinner Theatre: Dinner Performances (6:30 P.M.) November 14, 15, 20*, 21, 22, 28, 29 2025 Matinee Dinner Performance (1:00 P.M.) November 16*, 2025 (Meal Served) Non-Dinner Evening Performances (7:30 P.M.) November 19**, 26**, 2025 Non-Dinner Matinee Performances (2:00 P.M.) November 23**, 30**, 2025 **(No Meal Served / General Admission Seating) *Discount Dinner Performance Tickets on Sale Dates UTEP Students/Faculty/Staff/Alumni and Groups 20+ - October 6, 2025 General Public - October 7, 2025 The River bride Written by Marisela Trevi \u00f1 o Orta Directed by Samantha Michelle Nava Synopsis: Set in a Brazilian fishing village along the Amazon, The River Bride unfolds like a haunting fairytale\u2014two sisters, Helena and Belmira, who struggle to be true to each other and themselves, are thrown when a mysterious man is drawn from the water\u2019s depths, pulling them into a dance of risk, hope, and long-held secrets. Exploring themes of regret, missed opportunities, and love, The River Bride offers no promises - it demands a silent surrender, a leap into the unseen, where trust may falter. But what if the ever-changing current hides more than it reveals? What is left behind? June Sadowski Kruszewski Studio Theatre 7:30 PM Performances December 3*, 4, 5 & 6, 2025 2:00 PM Performances December 6* & 7, 2025 *Discount Performance - All Tickets $10 Purchase Tickets for The River Bride Here \u201cThe River Bride\u201d is presented by arrangement with Concord Theatricals on behalf of Samuel French, Inc. www.concordtheatricals.com Slow emergences: moving through crises, dance as opportunity Artistic Director Melissa Melpignano Synopsis: What does it mean to take time in an era of relentless acceleration? Slow Emergences centers dance, performance, and embodied practices to rediscover what speed and global crises so often destroy. In place of the reactive emergency mindset that demands rapid but often detrimental solutions, we explore emerging methods grounded in care and sustained attention. Through performances, actions, panels, and community gatherings, we offer spaces of collective reflection and radical imagination. Together, we ask how healthcare, climate, social welfare, and pedagogy might be reimagined to support long-term livability and communal transformation\u2014for the well-being of many, not just the few. Wise Family Theatre 7:30 PM Performances February 19*, 20, 21, 2025 2:00 PM Performance February 22, 2025 *Discount Performance - All Tickets $10 Tickets on Sale Date: January 27, 2026 rent Books, Music and Lyrics by Jonathan Larson Synopsis: Set in the East Village of New York City, Rent is about falling in love, finding your voice, and living for today. Based loosely on Puccini\u2019s La Boheme, Jonathan Larson\u2019s Rent follows a year in the life of a group of impoverished young artists and musicians struggling to survive and create in New York\u2019s Lower East Side, under the shadow of HIV/AIDS. How these young bohemians negotiate their dreams, loves, and conflicts provides the narrative thread to this groundbreaking musical. This is theatre at its best \u2013 exuberant, passionate and joyous. The Dinner Theatre Dinner Performances (6:30 P.M.) March 27, 28 & April 2*, 3, 4, 9*, 10, 11, 2026 Matinee Dinner Performance (1:00 P.M.) March 29*, 2026 (Meal Served) Non-Dinner Evening Performances (7:30 P.M.) April 1**, 8**, 2026 Non-Dinner Matinee Performances (2:00 P.M.) April 5**, 12**, 2026 **(No Meal Served / General Admission Seating) *Discount Dinner Performance Tickets on Sale Dates UTEP Students/Faculty/Staff/Alumni and Groups 20+ - October\u00a06, 2025 General Public - October\u00a07, 2025 orlando Written by\u00a0Sarah Ruhl Adapted from the novel by Virginia Woolf Directed by Jay Stratton Synopsis: Orlando is no ordinary noble. Dashing, bold, and full of restless charm, they sweeps through centuries\u2014seducing queens, chasing adventure, and defying every rule society dares to impose . But under a moonlit sky, a mysterious encounter changes everything. Orlando falls into an enchanted sleep... and awakens transformed. Sarah Ruhl\u2019s dreamlike adaptation of Virginia Woolf\u2019s classic novel is a journey through time and identity. Dancing across five centuries, Orlando is the fantastical tale of someone who refuses to be bound by societal norms. Who are we, really\u2014when time, gender, and expectation no longer define us? Wise Family Theatre 7:30 Performances April 17*, 18, 24 & 25, 2026 2:00 PM Performances April 19 & 26, 2026 *Discount Performance - All Tickets $10 Tickets on Sale Date :\u00a0January 27, 2026 \u201cOrlando (Ruhl)\u201d is presented by arrangement with Concord Theatricals on behalf of Samuel French, Inc. www.concordtheatricals.com The summer production to be performed at The Dinner Theatre will be announced at a later date. UTEP DEPARTMENT THEATRE AND DANCE BOX OFFICE SECOND FLOOR, FOX FINE ARTS Please call our number for any questions! (915) 747-5118 Representatives from the UTEP Ticket Center will open the box office one hour prior to curtain. NO REFUNDS OR EXCHANGES 15 minutes after curtain, tickets will no longer be sold . Tickets are only valid on the printed date. Tickets may also be purchased at the UTEP Ticket Center (915-747-5234) OR ticketmaster.com (convenience charges do apply) TICKET PRICES for Wise Family Theatre and June Sadowski Kruszewski Studio theatres: Adults: $18; UTEP Faculty/Staff, Seniors: $15 Military, Groups (10+), Alumni (with card), Non-UTEP Students: $15; UTEP Students (with a valid ID), Children (ages 4-12): $12 SEATING: PATRONS ARRIVING LATE WILL BE SEATED AT THE HOUSE MANAGER\u2019S DISCRETION IN THE WISE FAMILY THEATRE PLEASE REFER TO YOUR TICKET FOR LATE SEATING POLICY IN THE JUNE SADOWSKI KRUSZEWSKI STUDIO THEATRE (formerly known as the UTEP STUDIO THEATRE). IF THERE IS LATE SEATING, YOU WILL BE SEATED AT THE HOUSE MANAGER'S DISCRETION THE CENTER SECTION (SECTION C) IN THE WISE FAMILY THEATER IS RESERVED SEATING THERE IS NO ADDITIONAL COST TO SIT IN THE CENTER ALL SEATS IN THE JUNE SADOWSKI KRUSZEWSKI STUDIO THEATRE ARE GENERAL ADMISSION ADDITIONAL POLICIES: PROGRAMS WILL ONLY BE GIVEN UPON ENTRANCE TO THE THEATER FOOD & BEVERAGES ARE NOT ALLOWED INSIDE THE THEATER VIDEO & PHOTOGRAPHY ARE NOT ALLOWED INSIDE THE THEATER Above: Map of Wise Family Theatre GETTING TO OUR SPACES The Google Map above guides you to the Wise Family Theatre (second floor), the Box Office (second floor) and the June Sadowski Kruszewski Studio Theatre (first floor) as all are located within the Fox Fine Arts Center on campus. Free parking is available in the Sun Bowl Garage for all of our theatrical events, beginning one hour before show time. Link for Google Map above: Google Map Link The videos above will guide you to the Wise Family Theatre, the June Sadowski Kruszewski Studio Theatre, and to our box office. About Mission Our Chair's Welcome Past Productions Season and Tickets Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Theatre and Dance Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso Department of Theatre and Dance Fox Fine Arts Building, Room 371D 500 W University El Paso, Texas 79902 For season information: E: hwmaccarthy@utep.edu P: 915-747-5118 For program information: E: rfmayer@utep.edu P: 915-747-5502 THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Texas Veterans Portal Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 | SITE FEEDBACK Modal X"}
