{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/liberalarts/theatre-dance/about/chairswelcome.html", "title": "Our Chair's Welcome", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About Mission Our Chair's Welcome Department Accomplishments and Achievements Past Productions Season and Tickets Academic Programs Theatre Program Dance Program People Faculty and Administration UTEP Alumni News & Events Recent News Current Events In memoriam: Ingeborg Heuser In memoriam: Myron Nadel Resources Business Center Forms COVID Resources Student Organizations Student Space Rentals Degree Plans Scholarships Careers Theatre Education The Dinner Theatre The Dinner Theatre Give Now Give Now Scholarship Donations The Wise Theatre Renovations Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Theatre & Dance College of Liberal Arts Main Content UTEP College of Liberal Arts Theatre & Dance About UTEP College of Liberal Arts Theatre & Dance About Our Chair's Welcome Greetings from the Department Chair \u00a1 Bienvenidos! Hello and Welcome to the UTEP Department of Theatre and Dance. We are a dynamic and inclusive community of artists and scholars committed to shaping the future of performance. Located in El Paso, Texas, one of the safest cities in the U.S. and uniquely positioned along the U.S.-Mexico border, our department draws rich inspiration from the vibrant cultural landscape that surrounds us. This distinctive setting fuels our creativity, informs our storytelling, and strengthens our commitment to serving the diverse communities of our region and beyond. Our faculty are nationally and internationally recognized scholars and working artists who bring their professional expertise into the classroom and rehearsal studios. Their deep engagement in both academic and creative work is matched by their dedication to mentoring the next generation of performers, designers, choreographers, educators, and arts leaders. Our students are curious, passionate, and engaged. They come from a wide array of backgrounds, and together we explore repertoire that reflects the diversity of our world, stories in which our audiences can see themselves and each other. We produce an exciting season of plays and dance performances every semester that showcases the talent, creativity, and collaborative spirit of our students. Whether your interest lies in acting, dance, design and technology, musical theatre, stage management, or theatre and dance education, our degree programs are designed to challenge, inspire, and prepare you for a future in the performing arts. Our alumni have gone on to prestigious graduate programs and successful careers in performance, production, education, and beyond. We invite you to learn more about our programs, our productions, and the many opportunities we offer. With a range of scholarships and a commitment to fostering a welcoming, supportive environment, we are here to help you thrive. We look forward to welcoming you to our creative community! Sincerely, Henry\u00a0MacCarthy, Ph.D Chair, Department of Theatre & Dance Associate Professor \u200b\u200b About Mission Our Chair's Welcome Past Productions Season and Tickets Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Theatre and Dance Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso Department of Theatre and Dance Fox Fine Arts Building, Room 371D 500 W University El Paso, Texas 79902 For season information: E: hwmaccarthy@utep.edu P: 915-747-5118 For pr