{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/gov-relations/", "title": "Government Relations", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Government Relations Main Content Welcome to the Office of Government Relations What We Do The Office of Government Relations (OGR) strives to promote dialogue and engagement on a wide range of policy and budget issues. OGR works with elected officials, the UT System Administration and Board of Regents, and government agency officials to address concerns that affect higher education. Our goal is to advance UTEP\u2019s mission by working with decision-makers in the community. Policies enacted in Austin and Washington can have profound effects on our student population, the University, and our local community. We work to facilitate the passage and enaction of sound policies to keep UTEP progressing as an engine of opportunity and economic output for El Paso and the Borderplex region. To meet these goals, we engage in the following activities: work with elected officials on high-impact policies and conduct analysis on policy implications; coordinate meetings and campus visits with elected officials and ranking agency officials; develop strategies to demonstrate the impact of higher education on the region and the effects of policies on local communities; and communicate priorities and aid decision-makers in understanding UTEP\u2019s role as an institution of higher education in the region, state, and country. Please feel free to contact us at gr@utep.edu for any questions on policy, legislative updates, or inquiries on our work. Government Relations Staff Andrea Cortinas Executive Vice President and Chief of Staff acortinas@utep.edu Dustin Meador Deputy Chief of Staff dlmeador@utep.edu Joanne Richardson Assistant Vice President for Business Affairs, Budget and Personnel Services jrichardson@utep.edu Legislative Links Texas Legislature Online Texas Legislative Sessions and Years Additional Resources About UTEP Handbook of Operating Procedures Chapter 2: Speech, Expression, and Assembly Regents' Meetings UTEP SB 18 Report UTEP Government Relations At a Glance Media Inquiries Please contact UTEP News Email: news@utep.edu Phone: 915-747-5526 Associations AAHHE - American Association of Hispanic in Higher Education Association of Public and Land-Grant Universities Excelencia in Education HACU - Hispanic Association of Colleges and Universities Contact Us Email: gr@utep.edu #theBanner .theContent {\n    padding-top:6%;\n    padding-bottom:6%;\n    max-width:40%;\n    max-height: 400px;\n}\n#theBanner p {\n    font-size:16px;\n}\na.p-links {color: #337ab7 !important; }\n\n.fw-section .line {\n    border-top: 3px solid #041E42;\n    margin: 0 auto;\n}\n\n@media (max-width: 767px) {\n     #theBanner .theContent {\n         max-width:100%;\n     }\n}\n@media only screen and (max-width: 767px){\n      .fw-section.fw-section-bgImage.background-blue {\n         background-image: none !important;\n    }\n    \n    \n}\n.panel-heading h3 {\n    color: #fff;\n    text-transform: uppercase;\n    margin-top: 7px;\n    padding-left: 20px !important;\n    letter-spacing: 2px;\n    \n}\n\n.highligtsWrapper {\n\t    display: flex;\n\t    display: -webkit-flex;\n\t    flex-wrap: wrap;\n\t}\n\n.highligtsWrapper .col-md-4,\n.highligtsWrapper .col-md-6 {\n           margin-bottom: 30px;\n    }\n    \n.highligtsWrapper .col-xs-12