{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/financial-aid/resources/goldmine-guide.html", "title": "Guide to Goldmine", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search How to Apply Applying for Financial Aid Scholarships Types of Aid The Paydirt Promise The Miner Success Grant Scholarships Financial Aid Grants Student Employment Tuition Waivers and Exemptions Student Loans Summer Financial Aid Financial Aid by College Financial Aid for Transfer Students Financial Aid for Military Students Financial Aid for Graduate Students Eligibility Who is Eligible for Financial Aid How Are My Awards Calculated How Do I Stay Eligible More Information Your Cost of Attendance For Parents Other Ways to Pay for College Our Policies Code of Conduct Consumer Information Resources Guide to Goldmine Forms Upload Your Documents Sign Up for Direct Deposit Net Price Calculator Frequently Asked Questions Contact Us Contact Us Leadership Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Financial Aid and Scholarships Main Content UTEP Financial Aid and Scholarships Resources UTEP Financial Aid and Scholarships Resources Guide to Goldmine Goldmine is your student portal, where you can register for classes and find information about your degree plan, your grades, and your financial aid and scholarships . You can access Goldmine from the MyUTEP dashboard , the UTEP Go app , or directly at goldmine.utep.edu . However you do it, you will need to log in using your UTEP username and password; if you've been admitted but haven't set up your account yet, visit newaccount.utep.edu or call the HelpDesk at 915-747-HELP. If you haven't been admitted yet, you can find out your financial aid status at MyStatus . Logging In Visit goldmine.utep.edu and log in with your UTEP credentials. Accessing the Financial Aid and Scholarships Module Select Financial Aid and Scholarships from the main menu to access the Financial Aid and Scholarships Home page.\u00a0The most current year is displayed; you can select a different year from the Award Year dropdown on the top right corner. Important Information Required Click on View Questions to provide important information needed to confirm your eligibility. You must answer all questions before you can accept your awards . Student Requirements Documents and other pending requirements are also listed in the home page; review the list carefully and click on each item to read instructions on what to submit and how. Check back often as new documents may be needed to complete your application and determine your eligibility. Requirements that have been completed will show at the bottom of the list in green. Click on the arrow to the right of each requirement to expand its description, including links to submit your documents, download forms, etc. Viewing Your Award Offer The Award Offer tab shows the breakdown of your estimated costs, your expected enrollment status (we assume you will attend full-time unless you tell us otherwise), your housing status, and your Student Aid Index as determined on your FAFSA. After your cost of attendance, you will see any grants, scholarships, work-study, and loans you are eligible for.\u00a0After reviewing your awards and making your loan selections, click Submit . Depending on your financial aid package, you may need to accept terms and conditions for your grants or scholarships. Accepting a Student Loan The Award Offer tab also shows student loans you've been offered. If you are eligible and wish to accept student loans, you can do so in the Take Action dropdown next to the offered amount.\u00a0You can accept the entire amount, a portion, or none of it \u2013 but you should always borrow responsibly. After reviewing your awards and making your loan selections, click Submit . Depending on your financial aid package, you may need to accept terms and conditions for your grants or scholarships. Student loans are an important part of your financial aid offer, and can be a great investment in your future. If you have questions or concerns about borrowing, email studentloans@utep.edu to consult with a Student Loan Debt Specialist who will be happy to answer your questions. Accepting Terms and Conditions After reviewing your awards and making your loan selections, click Submit . Depending on your financial aid package, you may need to accept terms and conditions for your grants or scholarships. Satisfactory Academic Progress (SAP) Review your satisfactory academic progress (SAP) status for each term in the Satisfactory Academic Progress tab. Your SAP status will appear after final grades are posted for the preceding term. <!--\n    .accWrapper > div {\n    padding-left:24px;\n    }\n    .collapseToggleControl.collapsed span.glyphicon:before {\n        content: \"\\002b\";\n    }\n    .collapseToggleControl span.glyphicon:before {\n        content: \"\\2212\";\n    }\n    .optionalblock {\n        margin-top: 30px;\n        margin-bottom: 30px;\n    }\n /*flex*/\n.highligtsWrapper {\n    display: flex;\n    display: -webkit-flex;\n    flex-wrap: wrap;\n    margin-left: -14px;\n}\n.highligtsWrapper .col-md-4:nth-last-child(1) {\n    margin-bottom: 30px;\n}\n.highligtsWrapper .well {\n\tbox-shadow:0px 2px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);-webkit-box-shadow:0px 2px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);;\n\theight: 100%;\n\tpadding: 0;\n}\n.highligtsBody {\n\tpadding: 0 24px 0 24px;\n}\n.highligtsBody .btn-primary {\n    \tdisplay:block;\n    \tmargin-top: 30p