 financial aid and is considered a dependent student, they will need your help consenting to the use of your income information and signing the FAFSA or TASFA . Without it, your child will not be eligible for any grants and most types of need-based financial aid. If your child's application is selected for verification or has any conflicting information, you may need to submit certain signed documents to confirm the correct information. We want to engage with you and help you understand the process and your child's eligibility and status. However, the Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act of 1974 (FERPA), prohibits us providing information from a student to anyone else, unless your child gives us permission to do so. If your child agrees, they can submit an Authorization to Release Education Records to the Office of Registration and Records . Without a release, we can only answer general questions about financial aid and scholarships. Either way, we will be happy to talk to you - you can schedule an in-person or virtual appointment by visiting financialaid.utep.edu/talk or you can email studentfinancialaid@utep.edu . <!--\n    .accWrapper > div {\n    padding-left:24px;\n    }\n    .collapseToggleControl.collapsed span.glyphicon:before {\n        content: \"\\002b\";\n    }\n    .collapseToggleControl span.glyphicon:before {\n        content: \"\\2212\";\n    }\n    .optionalblock {\n        margin-top: 30px;\n        margin-bottom: 30px;\n    }\n /*flex*/\n.highligtsWrapper {\n    display: flex;\n    display: -webkit-flex;\n    flex-wrap: wrap;\n    margin-left: -14px;\n}\n.highligtsWrapper .col-md-4:nth-last-child(1) {\n    margin-bottom: 30px;\n}\n.highligtsWrapper .well {\n\tbox-shadow:0px 2px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);-webkit-box-shadow:0px 2px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);;\n\theight: 100%;\n\tpadding: 0;\n}\n.highligtsBody {\n\tpadding: 0 24px 0 24px;\n}\n.highligtsBody .btn-primary {\n    \tdisplay:block;\n    \tmargin-top: 30px;\n}\n\n.highligtsWrapper .col-md