{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/financial-aid/more-information/cost-of-attendance.html", "title": "Your Cost of Attendance", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search How to Apply Applying for Financial Aid Scholarships Types of Aid The Paydirt Promise The Miner Success Grant Scholarships Financial Aid Grants Student Employment Tuition Waivers and Exemptions Student Loans Summer Financial Aid Financial Aid by College Financial Aid for Transfer Students Financial Aid for Military Students Financial Aid for Graduate Students Eligibility Who is Eligible for Financial Aid How Are My Awards Calculated How Do I Stay Eligible More Information Your Cost of Attendance For Parents Other Ways to Pay for College Our Policies Code of Conduct Consumer Information Resources Guide to Goldmine Forms Upload Your Documents Sign Up for Direct Deposit Net Price Calculator Frequently Asked Questions Contact Us Contact Us Leadership Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Financial Aid and Scholarships Main Content UTEP Financial Aid and Scholarships More Information UTEP Financial Aid and Scholarships More Information Your Cost of Attendance Your cost of attendance , COA, or budget, is an estimate of how much it costs for you to live and study while you're enrolled at UTEP. The COA is used to calculate your financial need and how much financial aid you can receive , but it's not the amount you pay - your net price could be much lower if you are eligible for grants , scholarships , and other types of aid, like exemptions . If you are registered, you can see the exact charges and expected financial aid in your statement . If you are in the process of being admitted, or just curious, you can estimate what your net price could be using our Net Price Calculator . UTEP only bills you for direct costs like tuition, but your COA includes\u00a0allowances for things you pay outside of the University, like school supplies and living expenses. Your cost of attendance is also the maximum amount of financial aid you can receive from UTEP. Here are the components of your COA: Tuition and fees The average cost of tuition and fees for students based on your program, whether you are a Texas resident, and how many credits you enroll in. This is an approximation of what you pay to UTEP, but it's not a bill. After you register for classes, you can see exactly how much your tuition costs in the student portal. We assume you will attend full-time until you tell us otherwise or until census day, when your enrollment is \"locked\" for financial aid purposes. Living expenses (food and housing) The average cost of food and housing for a student in El Paso, Texas. This is not something you pay to UTEP, unless you live in UTEP housing, and it's an expense you probably would pay even if you were not a college student. However, if you receive financial aid while attending UTEP, it can help you pay for these costs. We calculate a different amount of food and housing depending on if you live with your parents or other family members, by yourself, or at UTEP dormitories. We only include housing and food in your cost of attendance if you are attending at least half-time. Books and school supplies The average cost of books and school supplies for a typical student. Transportation The cost of getting to UTEP from home and back, or from UTEP to work, etc. The estimate we use includes the cost of gas and typical maintenance of a vehicle, but not car payments. Personal expenses An allowance for things like clothing, laundry, personal hygiene items, etc. Your actual costs may vary, depending on lifestyle choices you make. We only include these costs if you are attending at least half-time. Loan origination fees If you borrow a student loan , we add the average cost of origination fees to your COA. Health insurance (if required by your program) Certain programs, like the Doctor of Physical Therapy program, require you to buy health insurance. If you are in that program, we include the average cost of health insurance in your COA. Other costs that can be included There are other costs that can be added to your COA, but we don't include them automatically. Examples are: Dependent care or day care, based on the number and ages of your children and other dependents. The cost of a required professional license or certification. The cost of a study abroad program. Expenses because of having a disability. If you pay for any of these, submit a cost of attendance review request. Here are the current cost of attendance amounts for each level or program and residency status. Tuition and fees are based on full-time enrollment and will be reduced if you enroll less than full-time. If you attend less than half-time, your cost of attendance will only include tuition and fees, books and supplies, transportation, and dependent care expenses: TX resident, living with family TX resident, living on your own TX resident, living on campus Non-resident, living with family Non-resident, living on your own Non-resident, living on campus Graduate students Breakdown of the estimated cost of attendance of a UTEP student Things you pay to UTEP: Tuition and fees (full-time) $8,508 Things you pay outside of UTEP: Housing and food $5,416 Transportation $2,600 Books and supplies $1,646 Personal miscellaneous $2,036 Total cost of attendance (including living expenses): $20,206 Breakdown of the estimated cost of attendance of a UTEP student Things you pay to UTEP: Tuition and fees (full-time) $8,508 Things you pay outside of UTEP: Housing and food $12,764 Transportation $2,600 Books and supplies $1,646 Personal miscellaneous $2,036 Total cost of attendance (including living expenses): $27,554 Breakdown of the estimated cost of attendance of a UTEP student Things you pay to UTEP: Tuition and fees (full-time) $8,508 University housing and meal plan $10,996 Things you pay outside of UTEP: Transportation $1,720 Books and supplies $1,646 Personal miscellaneous $2,036 Total cost of attendance (including living expenses): $24,906 Breakdown of the estimated cost of attendance of a UTEP student Things you pay to UTEP: Tuition and fees (full-time, without any waivers) $21,164 Things you pay outside of UTEP: Housing and food $5,416 Transportation $2,600 Books and supplies $1,646 Personal miscellaneous $2,036 Total cost of attendance (including living expenses): $32,862 Breakdown of the estimated cost of attendance of a UTEP student Things you pay to UTEP: Tuition and fees (full-time, without any waivers) $21,164 Things you pay outside of UTEP: Housing and food $12,764 Transportation $2,600 Books and supplies $1,646 Personal miscellaneous $2,036 Total cost of attendance (including living expenses): $40,210 Breakdown of the estimated cost of attendance of a UTEP student Things you pay to UTEP: Tuition and fees (full-time, without any waivers) $21,164 University housing and meal plan $10,996 Things you pay outside of UTEP: Transportation $1,720 Books and supplies $1,646 Personal miscellaneous $2,036 Total cost of attendance (including living expenses): $37,562 Breakdown of the estimated cost of attendance of a UTEP student Program Tuition and Fees Housing and Food (Off Campus) Books and Supplies Transportation Personal Expenses Health Insurance Total COA Master of Social Work, TX Resident $ 9,446.00 $ 12,764.00 $ 1,266.00 $ 2,600.00 $ 2,036.00 $ 28,112.00 Master of Social Work, Non-Resident $ 