{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/student-affairs/housing/current-residents/how-to-videos.html", "title": "How-To Videos/Instructions", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search Information Common Questions Dining on Campus Information for Parents and Family Maps Mission and Vision Off Campus Housing Future Residents Apply Now International Students Why Live On-Campus? Floor Plans and Rates Take A Tour Living Learning Communities Current Residents How-To Videos/Instructions Resident Handbook Check-Out Information Resident Portal Submit a Work Order Residential Events Events for Residents Room Reservation Request Camps And Conferences Camps and Conferences People Staff Contact Us and Office Hours Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Housing and Residence Life Division of Student Affairs Main Content UTEP Division of Student Affairs Housing and Residence Life Current Residents UTEP Division of Student Affairs Housing and Residence Life Current Residents How-To Videos/Instructions Excellent! You are living on campus and you can start enjoying the benefits and responsibilities. Below we have a range of videos showing you how to access our online amenities as well as procedural videos for special situations that may arise. Instructions Available: Click on the different title tabs to view the different instructions and videos. Responding to Fire Alarm Safety in Halls Garbage Disposal Activate Streaming Device Don't Burn the Property!: Responding to a Fire Alarm Miner Village SCA/RA On Call: 915-525-1452 Miner Canyon SCA/RA On Call: 915-637-8236 Miner Heights SCA/RA On Call: 915-996-0922 Keeping Our Properties Safe Remember! Our properties are as safe as you make them. Watch the video below and find out how you can contribute to our safety. Do Not Ruin Your Restroom! Toilets are not a garbage disposal tool. Please be mindful of what you flush. Flushing certain elements can result in your restroom having plumbing issues or even the whole property. The video below is a dramatic interpretation of what we mean. Sending a Request to the UTEP Help Desk If you are trying to connect your smart device (web-enabled TVs [smart TVs], Roku, Chromecast, etc.) you may realize that your device isn\u2019t already connected. Here at UTEP, we all share one large wireless network where we need to send a request to the UTEP Help Desk to have our device(s) to be activated on the network. You\u2019ll need some information before you ask to activate your device(s) DISCLAIMER: GAMING CONSOLES ( PlayStations, Xboxes, Nintendo consoles, etc) and WIRELESS PRINTERS will not be accepted on the wireless network! With the device(s) that you have, write down the device(s): MAC Address and Model # (usually on the back, on the bottom of the device, on your device(s)\u2019 box [original packaging], or the device(s)\u2019 User Manual, or your device(s)\u2019 network settings), and Brand, your full name. Call the UTEP Help Desk (915)-747-4357 Choose option #1 on the automated system Say \u201cI am a UTEP Student currently living on campus, and I would like my [device(s)] activated on the network.\u201d Supply the representative on the phone the information you wrote down. The Help Desk will generate a request and send it to an associated Networking Team (the networking team grants access to the requested device(s). NOTE: This Networking Team is not a part of UTEP but they do work directly with UTEP. This is important because if the UTEP Help Desk updates their policy, the Networking Team may not receive the notification of the change in policy right away. Ex) If the UTEP Help Desk decides to update their policy to where Roku\u2019s are not allowed anymore, the Networking Team may not cut off access to Rokus till later in the future. You should receive a confirmation email that your request has been received. Depending on your device, it may be connected to the network that same day. Guest Housing Student Housing Contract Floor Plans and Rates Contact Us and Office Hours Resident Portal Apply Now Submit a Work Order Resident Handbook Summer Applications Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso Housing and Residence Life Boquillas Hall 3490 Sun Bowl Drive El Paso, Texas 79902 E: housing@utep.edu P: (915) 747-5352 F: (915) 747-5651 THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Texas Veterans Portal Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 | SITE FEEDBACK Modal X"}
{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/student-affairs/housing/future-residents/living-learning-communities.html", "title": "Living Learning Communities", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search Information Common Questions Dining on Campus Information for Parents and Family Maps Mission and Vision Off Campus Housing Future Residents Apply Now International Students Why Live On-Campus? Floor Plans and Rates Take A Tour Living Learning Communities Current Residents How-To Videos/Instructions Resident Handbook Check-Out Information Resident Portal Submit a Work Order Residential Events Events for Residents Room Reservation Request Camps And Conferences Camps and Conferences People Staff Contact Us and Office Hours Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Housing and Residence Life Division of Student Affairs Main Content UTEP Division of Student Affairs Housing and Residence Life Future Residents UTEP Division of Student Affairs Housing and Residence Life Future Residents What is a Living Learning Community? A Living Learning Community (LLC) is a community built to connect residents with common interests and provide them with the opportunity to engage and attend specialized programming to fit those interests. Why should I join a Living Learning Community? Joining a Living Learning Community provides its members with opportunities to connect with others who have similar interests and goals to themselves. LLCs provide members the opportunity to attend specialized programming to meet with specific interest or focus. How do I join a Living Learning Community? As a first year student you can pick your LLC as part of your room selection process. If you chose not to select an LLC at that time, you can always go back to the Resident Portal and join an LLC via the Requests page. Living/Learning Community options Emerging Leaders Community - A community focused on developing leadership skills through participation in leadership opportunities within the residential and UTEP communities. Intramural Sports Learning Community - A community focused on developing relationships with those who have an interest or focus on their physical wellbeing, whether they have just started their journey into physical wellness or have a well-established routine. Where will Living Learning Community participants live on campus? Living Learning Community members will live across any of the FYRE residence halls: Guadalupe, Sacramento, Copper, Whispering Springs. You get to pick your room assignment and your LLC of choice will not impact what you can see on the resident portal. Does my roommate need to be in the same LLC for us to live together? Each resident can choose their own LLC. Participants in a specific LLC will come together during specific programs for that LLC providing an additional community for everyone. People living together can choose to be part of the same LLC but are not required to. How is a Living Learning Community different than standard housing on campus Your LLC selection will not impact your housing. Students that chose not to participate in an LLC will live in the same buildings and will have access to all residential events. There will be special events/programs catered to the specific LLCs. Does it cost anything to join a Living Learning Community It does not cost anything to join a Living Learning Community! People Floor Plans and Rates Contact Us and Office Hours Resident 