{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/student-affairs/housing/off-campus-housing.html", "title": "Off Campus Housing", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search Information Common Questions Dining on Campus Information for Parents and Family Maps Mission and Vision Off Campus Housing Future Residents Apply Now International Students Why Live On-Campus? Floor Plans and Rates Take A Tour Living Learning Communities Current Residents How-To Videos/Instructions Resident Handbook Check-Out Information Resident Portal Submit a Work Order Residential Events Events for Residents Room Reservation Request Camps And Conferences Camps and Conferences People Staff Contact Us and Office Hours Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Housing and Residence Life Division of Student Affairs Main Content UTEP Division of Student Affairs Housing and Residence Life UTEP Division of Student Affairs Housing and Residence Life Off Campus Housing Below is a list of resources and suggestions that may help you in your search for off-campus housing while attending UTEP. While this list is not exhaustive, it is a good place to start. Property Location El Paso is a fairly large city with various locations from the downtown city center to the many suburbs surrounding the city. If you do not have a vehicle, you may depend on the Sun Metro bus routes that can be found in the Transportation Around El Paso section below. Finding a property on a bus route will make it easier for you to get to campus. If you have a vehicle, you may have additional options available to you. Please remember to verify parking availability around the property you may rent. Additionall y, you will have to purchase a parking permit to park on campus at UTEP. As you are locating a place to live, you are encouraged to visit the property and neighborhood at various times of the day and night. This will give you the opportunity to gauge yo ur level of comfort and safety as things may seem different during the day as opposed to the evening. Word of mouth is helpful when determining where to live in the El Paso area. Reaching out to other UTEP students and asking for recommendations will help as you weigh your options about off - campus living. Navigating the lease/Contract The Lease you sign with an Owner or Management Company is a legally binding contract that will outline what is expected of you as the tenant in a property. Some things to look out fo r are listed below \u2022 What is the monthly rent? \u2022 Will you require a parent or guardian to sign the lease as well? \u2022 Is a security deposit required? How much must be paid? Is it refundable? \u2022 Can you have pets in the apartment? How do you get approved for an Emo tional Support Animal? \u2022 Is the lease 10 months (August \u2013 May) or 12 months (calendar year)? \u2022 What is the penalty if the lease is terminated early? \u2022 Are all repairs covered by the owner or Management Company? \u2022 Is there enough parking for all tenants of the apar tment? Is a parking permit required? \u2022 Is the property furnished? Utilities Some properties include utilities in the monthly rent. Make sure you clearly understand what is included and what you may be responsible for in addition to your monthly rent. Bel ow are some common utilities you should discuss with the owner or manager. \u2022 Electric \u2022 Water \u2022 Gas \u2022 Trash \u2022 Cable \u2022 Internet \u2022 Air Conditioning o Is air conditioning provided? o What type of air conditioning is in the unit ? \u25aa Refrigerated \u2013 Cooler temperatures, removes humidity, more expensive to run \u25aa Evaporative \u2013 W arm air is pulled ove r a wet pad allowing the water to evaporate, lowering the temperature of the air. Less expensive to run. o If air conditioning is not provided, can you bring your own personal air conditioning unit? Will it fit in the window, or will you need to purchase a unit that sits on the floor? Insurance Many property owners may require you to acquire renters insurance. Renters insurance will help you replace your per sonal property if anything were to happen while you are renting a property. Even if it is not required, you are highly encouraged to obtain renter\u2019s insurance in case of an emergency. Safety and Security There are many things property owners and managers put into place to ensure the safety and security of their tenants. Ensuring proper lighting, locking windows and doors, and additional security measures that may be available at the property. You should also verify that the property has ample smoke and/o r fire detection systems, and ensure they are functioning properly upon moving in. Transportation around El Paso The Miner Metro is free for students and runs regularly throughout the academic semester when classes are in session. Please visit the link below for additional information. Miner Metro Sun Metro is the local bus company serving the greater El Paso area. Please visit their website for all routes, fairs, and information about planning your r oute to campus. Sun Metro Campus Engagement While you are living off - campus, please make sure you stay in touch with the UTEP Engagement Activities via Minetracker On-Campus support While living off campus, your success as a student remains a priority for the UTEP community. There are many campus resources available to you that can be found on the Division of Student Affairs website below. Division of Student Affairs <!--\n    .accWrapper > div {\n    padding-left:24px;\n    }\n    .collapseToggleControl.collapsed span.glyphicon:before {\n        content: \"\\002b\";\n    }\n    .collapseToggleControl span.glyphicon:before {\n        content: \"\\2212\";\n    }\n    .optionalblock {\n        margin-top: 30px;\n        margin-bottom: 30px;\n    }\n /*flex*/\n.highligtsWrapper {\n    display: flex;\n    display: -webkit-flex;\n    flex-wrap: wrap;\n    margin-left: -14px;\n}\n.highligtsWrapper .col-md-4:nth-last-child(1) {\n    margin-bottom: 30px;\n}\n.highligtsWrapper .well {\n\tbox-shadow:0px 2px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);-webkit-box-shadow:0px 2px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);;\n\theight: 100%;\n\tpadding: 0;\n}\n.highligtsBody {\n\tpadding: 0 24px 0 24px;\n}\n.highligtsBody .btn-primary {\n    \tdisplay:block;\n    \tmargin-top: 30px;\n}\n\n.highligtsWrapper .col-md-4 {\n   margin-bottom: 30px;\n}\n\n.lightWhiteBg {\n\tbackground: rgba(255,255,255,.85);\n    padding: 4px 24px 24px 24px;\n    margin-bottom: 20px;\n}\n--> <!--\ndiv.facebook .pp_top .pp_left{background:#fff;}div.facebook .pp_top .pp_middle{background:#fff;}div.facebook .pp_top .pp_right{background:#fff;}div.facebook .pp_content_container .pp_left{background:#fff;}div.facebook .pp_content_container .pp_right{background:#fff;}div.facebook .pp_expand{background:url(//www.utep.edu/university-communications/_UC-Global-Files/lightbox/theme/sprite.png) -31px -26px no-repeat;cursor:pointer}div.facebook .pp_expand:hover{background:url(//www.utep.edu/university-communications/_UC-Global-Files/lightbox/theme/sprite.png) -31px -47px no-repeat;cursor:pointer}div.facebook .pp_contract{background:url(//www.utep.edu/university-communications/_UC-Global-Files/lightbox/theme/sprite.png) 0 -26px no-repeat;cursor:pointer}div.facebook .pp_contract:hover{background:url(//www.utep.edu/university-communications/_UC-Global-Files/lightbox/theme/sprite.png) 0 -47px no-repeat;cursor:pointer}div.facebook .pp