{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/student-affairs/housing/information/common-questions.html", "title": "Common Questions", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search Information Common Questions Dining on Campus Information for Parents and Family Maps Mission and Vision Off Campus Housing Future Residents Apply Now International Students Why Live On-Campus? Floor Plans and Rates Take A Tour Living Learning Communities Current Residents How-To Videos/Instructions Resident Handbook Check-Out Information Resident Portal Submit a Work Order Residential Events Events for Residents Room Reservation Request Camps And Conferences Camps and Conferences People Staff Contact Us and Office Hours Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Housing and Residence Life Division of Student Affairs Main Content UTEP Division of Student Affairs Housing and Residence Life Information UTEP Division of Student Affairs Housing and Residence Life Information Common Questions Questions and Answers: When is the deadline to submit a housing application? There is no deadline to submit a housing application. We accept applications year round. The sooner you submit your application, the greater chance you have at getting the room style you want. Can I make changes to my application once it has been submitted? Yes. You can edit your application up until you get a room assignment. Am I signing a contract when I submit my housing application? Yes. As part of the application you will be asked to sign the housing contract. For students under 18 years of age will be asked to assign a proxy to sign their contract. This will be their parents or legal guardians.\u00a0 So please read the obligations, penalties and cancellation policies stated in the Housing and Residence Life contract before signing your contract. Can I choose my own roommate? Yes. You have the option of choosing your own roommate. You must select them on your application, and they must select you on their application. How are roommates chosen? At the time you submit your application you have the option of selecting\u00a0 roommate. You can also select your roommate during the room selection process. If you do not participate in the room selection process we will use the answers that you listed on the roommate selection questions section of the housing application. This will help us find a roommate similar in age and interests. How are room assignments done? For room selection timelines click HERE : Can I cancel my application/room assignment after it has been submitted? All students must complete the Housing Contract Cancellation form available in the Resident Portal. I don't like my room assignment; can I request to change it? Students will have the option of doing a room change via the resident portal. For the timeline of when room changes are available click HERE . Do you have a maid service? Rooms are only cleaned in the event of a maintenance-related emergency, and trash is collected at specific locations . Residents are responsible for the cleanliness of their rooms and can be charged for excessive cleaning if staff determine it is necessary. Can my friend and I live together in the same apartment? We suggest that if you are serious about living with a friend, that you turn in your applications together and that you both indicate that you wish to live together on both applications. NOTE: We discourage friends from living together because while it is nice to live with someone you know, friendships tend to be tested and sometimes strained. Can I have guests/visitors in my apartment? Student housing has no restrictions on visitation by members of the opposite sex. There are guidelines regarding the length of time an out of town visitor can stay with you, and all visitors must be approved by your roommate(s). How safe is Campus Living? All properties are require residents to scan their Miner Gold Card to access the building. There are Resident Assistants that serve in an on-call rotation for the residents that live here. They try to stress safety to their residents and encourage them to lock their front doors and to keep us notified of strangers in the complex. There are emergency call boxes in and around the complex in the event a resident needed to contact the police immediately. What kind of activities are available for residents? Programming in the halls varies from month to month, and social and educational activities are planned by each staff member. Residents are invited to discuss issues going on in their hall, participate in community service projects, and plan activities for all residents.\u00a0 Student housing residents are also often asked to participate in focus groups for future housing projects and on-campus issues. Can my child live with me? UTEP does not offer family housing. Can my dog live with me? According to our Resident Handbook , only fish in aquariums are allowed in student housing.\u00a0Pets that are found can be taken and the resident will be held judicially and financially responsible for any damage caused by the pet. For Emotional Service Animals policies click HERE . Are the buildings co-ed? Individual housing units will be assigned by gender, and it is entirely possible for a building population to have male and female residents living in close proximity. Can we remove the furniture? Furniture is not to be removed from student rooms under any circumstance unless the circumstance presented to staff is of a medical nature and/or emergency situation.\u00a0 Requests to move furniture should be submitted in writing to the Director. <!--\n    .accWrapper > div {\n    padding-left:24px;\n    }\n    .collapseToggleControl.collapsed span.glyphicon:before {\n        content: \"\\002b\";\n    }\n    .collapseToggleControl span.glyphicon:before {\n        content: \"\\2212\";\n    }\n    .optionalblock {\n        margin-top: 30px;\n        margin-bottom: 30px;\n    }\n /*flex*/\n.highligtsWrapper {\n    display: flex;\n    display: -webkit-flex;\n    flex-wrap: wrap;\n    margin-left: -14px;\n}\n.highligtsWrapper .col-md-4:nth-last-child(1) {\n    margin-bottom: 30px;\n}\n.highligtsWrapper .well {\n\tbox-shadow:0px 2px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);-webkit-box-shadow:0px 2px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);;\n\theight: 100%;\n\tpadding: 0;\n}\n.highligtsBody {\n\tpadding: 0 24px 0 24px;\n}\n.highligtsBody .btn-primary {\n    \tdisplay:block;\n    \tmargin-top: 30px;\n}\n\n.highligtsWrapper .col-md-4 {\n   margin-bottom: 30px;\n}\n\n.lightWhiteBg {\n\tbackground: rgba(255,255,255,.85);\n    padding: 4px 24px 24px 24px;\n    margin-bottom: 20px;\n}\n--> <!--\ndiv.facebook .pp_top .pp_left{background:#fff;}div.facebook .pp_top .pp_middle{background:#fff;}div.facebook .pp_top .pp_right{background:#fff;}div.facebook .pp_content_container .pp_left{background:#fff;}div.facebook .pp_content_container .pp_right{background:#fff;}div.facebook .pp_expand{background:url(//www.utep.edu/university-communications/_UC-Global-Files/lightbox/theme/sprite.png) -31px -26px no-repeat;cursor:pointer}div.facebook .pp_expand:hover{background:url(//www.utep.edu/university-communications/_UC-Global-Files/lightbox/theme/sprite.png) -31px -47px no-repeat;cursor:pointer}div.facebook .pp_contract{background:url(//www.utep.edu/university-communications/_UC-Global-Files/lightbox/theme/sprite.png) 0 -26px no-repeat;cursor:pointer}div.facebook .pp_contract:hover{background:url(//www.utep.e