{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/registrar/transcripts/apostille.html", "title": "Apostille", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About FERPA FERPA 101 FERPA Annual Notice.pdf Students Registration MyUTEP Class Search Student Forms Faculty and Staff Faculty Resources Transcripts Order Transcripts Apostille Graduation Graduation Information Diploma Information People Contact Us Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Registration & Records Main Content Apostille Apostille Process with the Texas Secretary of State (TXSOS) What is an Apostille? Apostilles are authenticated documents for use in foreign nations. Said documents are issued for use in other countries, specifically, countries that are members of the Hague Convention of 1961. In simple terms, apostilles validate the seal and signature of a Notary Public on the document(s) so that it/they can be accepted in a foreign country. UTEP is authorized to process OFFICIAL TRANSCRIPTS and ORIGINAL DIPLOMAS issued from our institution for the purpose of apostille validation. The actual apostille is issued by the Texas Secretary of State after receiving notarized documents from UTEP. To complete an Apostille through UTEP, you are required to bring: an official transcript an original diploma (s)\u00a0 --> you can order a diploma replacement HERE or both ...to the Registration and Records office. If you prefer to use a photocopy of your diploma, UTEP staff will make a copy from the original, which you must supply. You are also required to purchase and provide us with the following items: Each Apostille incurs a $15.00 fee. We accept BLANK money orders (MO) in the amount of $15.00 each (ex: you want an Apostille for 3 documents then you must submit 3 blank MO for $15.00 each) \u2013 the transcript department will fill out the money order(s) as required by the Texas Secretary of State Two priority mail envelopes (approximately 12 X 9 inches) Two priority mail stamps - $10.10 each (one to send to TXSOS and the other for TXSOS to return to UTEP). Alternatively, a third priority mail stamp and envelope can be provided if you wish for the transcript department to mail your final documents to you (USA only, we do not mail overseas) You must specify the name of the country for which the Apostille Certification is for; (ex: MEXICO, RUSSIA, SPAIN, etc.) If you are not able to visit our office in person, then you must provide an original diploma via mail-- no photocopies accepted. You can also designate a person such as a relative or friend, to deliver these items on your behalf. There is an Approximate 5-Week Turn-Around Time Transcripts Order Transcripts Apostille Schedule-Guide.pdf Academic Calendars Enrollment-Services-Rooms.pdf FERPA Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso Registration and Records Mike Loya Academic Services Building Room 107 500 West University Avenue El Paso, Texas 79968 E: records@utep.edu P: (915) 747-5544 F: (915) 747-8764 THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Texas Veterans Portal Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 | SITE FEEDBACK Modal X"}
{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/registrar/transcripts/order-transcript.html", "title": "Order Transcripts", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About FERPA FERPA 101 FERPA Annual Notice.pdf Students Registration MyUTEP Class Search Student Forms Faculty and Staff Faculty Resources Transcripts Order Transcripts Apostille Graduation Graduation Information Diploma Information People Contact Us Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Registration & Records Main Content Order Transcripts UTEP transcripts are cumulative. This means your transcripts will reflect a complete record of your academic history (Undergraduate, Graduate, and Doctoral courses) completed at UTEP. Partial transcripts are NOT available (ex: only Graduate, but not Undergraduate). Please read the information below before ordering your transcripts. Order Transcripts Track Transcript Order Ordering Official Transcripts Transcripts being collected from our campus office require identity authentication. Please bring a valid photo ID for the release of your documents when you are picking up any in-person \"Hold for Pickup\" orders. If you are authorizing the release of your transcript to someone else, please email: transcripts@utep.edu and provide the full name of the person collecting your transcripts with a picture of your valid photo ID attached to the email. They too will need to show their valid photo ID when they come to pick up your transcript. RUSH Processing Cost Official Transcript (Same day CAMPUS PICK-UP ONLY) $8 + $5 Per Transcript STANDARD Processing Cost Official Transcript - Electronic (2 hours) $5 Per Transcript Official Transcript - Mail-US (3 - 10 business days) $5 Per Transcript Official Transcript - Certified Mail-US (3-10 business days with tracking) $12 + $5 Per Transcript Official Transcript - Mail-International (11-30 business days) $10 Per Transcript Official Transcript - Express Mail-US (2-3 business days) $39 + $5 Per Transcript Official Transcript - Express Mail-International (5-10 business days) $75 + $10 Per Transcript Official Transcript - HOLD for pick up (24-hours) $5 Per Transcript *** Please note due to national shipping delays, mailing times may be longer than noted above. If you need your transcript by a specific date, we recommend using certified or express mail so you are provided with a tracking number for your order*** Important Information If you stopped attending UTEP prior to 1983 your order will require an additional 3-5 business days for processing (please follow the instructions listed below). If you attended UTEP before 1983 but continued attending after 1983, please continue to use the transcript ordering link above and when asked if you attended prior to 1983, please select no since you continued your studies. All transcript fees (and any express shipping fees) must be paid for at the time of request. We will not mail transcripts and then bill you, nor can transcript fees be charged to your studetnt account. Printed transcripts cannot be scanned by UTEP staff due to FERPA federal laws. You cannot hand-deliver UTEP transcripts to EPCC, EPCC will only accept transcripts sent to them by UTEP. Your SSN will be printed on transcripts going to other colleges and universities, which will be used in matching documents and for financial aid and federal/state data reporting requirements. Business is not conducted on days when UTEP is closed (weekends and holidays). Please plan accordingly. If you place your order using incorrect information, we may not be able to reimburse your order due to user error (this includes incorrect attendance dates, typos of any kind- including email address mistakes, and incorrect selections of any kind). Tips for Ordering w/o Delays If you did NOT attend UTEP before 1983, please answer that question by selecting \"No\". Be careful to make the correct processing selection: RUSH vs. STANDARD (See price grids above for details). Don't see \"United States\" as the country to choose from in your order? Please be sure you selected MAIL-US, instead of MAIL-INTERNATIONAL. You should be able to select \"previous\" within the order form, at the bottom. If you cannot find a college or university in the list provided, choose \"Not in List\" to free-type their info. Is your degree conferred (awarded)? If yes, then choose to \"Process current transcript as is\". See PDF with screen captures for clarification. Are you awaiting degree conferral in the current semester when you are generating a transcript order? If yes, choose \"After Degree Is Awarded\". See PDF with screen captures for clarification. Unofficial Transcript To access your unofficial transcript, please login to my.utep.edu with your UTEP credentials and go to GoldMine. In GoldMine, select: Student Records / Academic Transcripts / All Levels / Submit . Once you see your unofficial transcript on your browser screen, you can simply print or save it as a PDF via your browser print menu (or select CTRL P for the printer menu). If you no longer have access to the student portal, please email transcripts@utep.edu to request your unofficial transcript. Unofficial transrcipts are processed within 1-2 business days. Please provide the following with your request: Complete name used while attending UTEP UTEP student ID number (if you have it) scan of driver's license or other valid photo ID (or email directly from Miners account) To request submission of your unofficial transcript to another UTEP department, please email your request using your UTEP email address to transcripts@utep.edu and specify the department name and department e-mail address where it should be delivered. Transcripts to EPCC Transcript Submission to EPCC for academic purposes is free of charge. Please send an email to transcripts@utep.edu from your Miners account. You can also send it from a different account, but be sure to include a scan of your valid photo ID (driver's license, passport, military ID). Message Subject Line: Transcript Request to EPCC First Name: Last Name UTEP Student ID#: DOB: UTEP will submit official electronic transcripts to EPCC only for admission purposes. If you are seeking employment at EPCC please request your transcript here . Additionally, your official transcript can only be submitted to the admissions office at Valle Verde campus- EPCC . For submission to other EPCC campuses or offices, you must contact the Valle Verde campus to forward your transcript accordingly after receiving from UTEP. Please allow one business day to complete your request and two business days for EPCC to receive your transcript. We will notify you once we send your transcript. Do note that failure to submit a request with complete information may result in delays. UT Coordinated Admission Program (CAP) Students Transcript submission to UT Austin for academic purposes is free of charge for UT CAP students only. Official transcripts will be routinely scheduled for submission to UT Austin every semester after grades are posted and sent via the SPEEDE delivery. Visit UTEP's Academic Calendar each semester for details about dates when grades post to student records. UT CAP students, please do not submit orders online via UTEP's transcript ordering link, as this method is not acceptable. Please send an email to transcripts@utep.edu from your Miners account and provide your UTEP student ID number for follow up and/or further questions. Background Investigations UTEP will generate an unofficial transcript upon receipt of a signed student release form. Background investigators have the option to send signed release forms as follows: Landline Fax # - 915-747-8764 Walk-in - Mike Loya Building, room 107 E-mail via DOD Safe Site (where applicable) Mail - 500 W. University Ave. I Registration and Records I Mike Loya ASB, Room 107 I El Paso, TX I 79968 There is a 24-hour turnaround time to process background investigation requests. I stopped attending UTEP before 1983 Since you stopped attending UTEP before 1983 your student record is not in our current student/alumni institutional database. In order to request a transcript please email transcripts@utep.edu with the following information: Message Subject Line: Transcript Request for Attendance Prior to 1983 First Name: Last Name (previous names, where applicable) : DOB: Attendance dates: Last 4 digits of SSN: Current phone number: Once we retrieve your record, a representative from our office will contact you to advise on next steps to complete your order. Please consider that this may take between 5 to 10 business days. Mail Request Transcript requests by mail need to include: Your name (previous name(s) while attending UTEP) UTEP student ID number or Date of birth Dates of attendance Day time telephone number The complete address where your requested transcript(s) will be sent (home, college, university, or employment). Your signature A copy of your valid photo ID Your check or money order payable to UTEP Mail to: UTEP Registration and Records Office ATTN: Transcripts Mike Loya Academic Services Bldg. Rm 107 500 W University Ave El Paso TX 79968 Contact Us P. (915) 747-7326 F. (915) 747-8764 E. transcripts@utep.edu Business Hours: Monday through Friday (except major holidays) 8:00 AM to 5:00 PM <!--\n.btn-primary {background-color: #f44336;}\n--> document.getElementById(\"title-aria\").style.display = \"none\"; Transcripts Order Transcripts Apostille Schedule-Guide.pdf Academic Calendars Enrollment-Services-Rooms.pdf FERPA Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso Registration and Records Mike Loya Academic Services Building Room 107 500 West University Avenue El Paso, Texas 79968 E: records@utep.edu P: (915) 747-5544 F: (915) 747-8764 THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Texas Veterans Portal Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 | SITE FEEDBACK Modal X"}
{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/vpba/student-business-services/payment%20options/format.html", "title": "Payment Options", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search Paying for Tuition Payment Options Tuition and Mandatory Fees Tuition and Mandatory Fees: Summer 2026 Tuition and Mandatory Fees: Spring 2026 Tuition and Mandatory Fees: Fall 2025 Tuition and Mandatory Fees: Summer 2025 Tuition and Mandatory Fees: Spring 2025 Tuition and Mandatory Fees: Fall 2024 Historical Tuition and Mandatory Fees Course Fee Summary Major Fee Summary Resources Resources Important Dates Third-Party - Military Tuition Assistance On Demand Statement Complete Withdrawals Tuition Set Aside Guaranteed Tuition Plan Miner Shoppe Health Insurance About About SBS Office Hours Refunding Refunds Returned Unearned Tuition Assistance Policy FAQs Frequently Asked Questions Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Student Business Services Business Affairs Main Content UTEP Business Affairs Student Business Services Paying For Tuition UTEP Business Affairs Student Business Services Paying For Tuition Payment Options Student Business Services offers the following payment options: Important News about Credit Card Payments Effective May 1, 2023, the convenience fee for using a credit card will increase to 2.95% on payments for tuition, fees and other charges including housing, parking, traffic fees and fines, library fines, student health insurance and repatriation insurance.\u00a0 The conveniene fee covers charges assessed by credit card companies to provide the service.\u00a0 The University does not profit from this fee. To avoid the convenience fee, students may pay online with an electronic check.\u00a0 Payments by cash or personal paper check are accepted at the Student Business Services cashier windows. Online at Pete's Payment Options Pete's Payment options allows you to: Check your balance Make payments credit card (2.95% fee will apply) E-Check (no fee) ACH will be validated before payment is accepted View your payment history Generate and print On Demand Statement Enroll in Payment plan Add authorized users (parents, employers, etc) to view your bill and make payments on your behalf How can I pay for my balance? In person, our cashiers only accept cash and personal paper checks. Online, payments can be made with credit cards (a 2.95% convenience fee will be applied) or electronic checks. If you are mailing your payment, the payment must be received by the close of business (5 p.m. MST) on the payment deadline due date. Go to Pete's Payment Option now! Cash Payments Student Business Services office hours are Monday to Friday from 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. for in person payments or departmental deposits (no appointment required). Appointments are required, via QLess , for office visits, not related to in person payments or departmental deposits. Virtual Services Student Business Services may assist students virtually with inquiries via email at sbs@utep.edu, via QLess (phone or MS Teams) or via phone at (915) 747-5116. For In Person Visits Please schedule an appointment via QLess for all services not related to in person payments or departmental deposits Face masks are strongly encouraged. Stay at least 6 feet apart from those around you. Payment Plan For FALL/SPRING balance is divided into 5 equal payments. For SUMMER balance is divided into 3 payments. All payments are due by 5:00 p.m. (MST) according to the due dates for the respective term. SPRING 2024 example\u200b example UTEP Tuition&fees $500 20% down payment Due upon enrollment $500 UTEP Meal Plan $600 Payment 2 Due on 2/15/24 $500 Parking Permit $300 Payment 3 Due on 3/15/24 $500 UTEP Housing $600 Payment 4 Due on 4/15/24 $500 Health Insurance $500 Payment 5 Due on 5/15/24 $500 $2,500 $2,500 Set up fee Due upon enrollment $25 FALL 2023 example\u200b UTEP Tuition&fees $500 20% down payment Due upon enrollment $500 UTEP Meal Plan $600 Payment 2 Due on 9/15/23 $500 Parking Permit $300 Payment 3 Due on 10/16/23 $500 UTEP Housing $600 Payment 4 Due on 11/15/23 $500 Health Insurance $500 Payment 5 Due on 12/15/23 $500 $2,500 $2,500 Set up fee Due upon enrollment $25 Please note the following items cannot be added to the payment plan and are due immediately if the Payment plan is selected: Student General Property Deposit Installment Tuition Handling Fee Service Fees (Late Registration and Add/Drop) Fines (Traffic and Library) Discretionary Fees (liability insurance) Amounts due for financial holds from prior periods. Study Abroad related charges (housing, meal plans etc..) Payment plans cannot be canceled once selected. Please make sure the payment plan is your best option before enrollment. Students that are under 18 years of age and want to enroll in the payment plan: Parent or Guardian needs to email sbs@utep.edu a copy of their driver's license on behalf of the student; SBS will then reply with step by step instructions so they can process the Authorized User Payment Plan Payment Plan Tutorial Enroll in a Payment Plan now Tuition Loan For FALL/SPRING balance is divided into 5 equal payments. Payment 1 is deferred to be due at a later date. For SUMMER balance is divided into 3 payments.\u00a0Payment 1 is deferred to be due at a later date. All payments are due by 5:00 p.m. (MST) according to the due dates for the respective term. SPRING 2023 example example UTEP Tuition&Fees $500 20% - Deferred Due on 4/14/23 $500 UTEP Meal Plan $600 Payment 2 Due on 2/15/23 $500 Parking Permit $300 Payment 3 Due on 3/15/23 $500 UTEP Housing $600 Payment 4 Due on 4/17/23 $500 Health Insurance $500 Payment 5 Due on 5/15/23 $500 $2,500 $2,500 Set up fee Due upon enrollment $25 Interest rate Due on Apr 14th SUMMER 2022 example\u200b example UTEP Tuition&Fees $500 34% - Deferred Due on 7/29/22 $850 UTEP Meal Plan $600 Payment 2 Due on 7/1/22 $825 Parking Permit $300 Payment 3 Due on 8/1/22 $825 UTEP Housing $600 $2,500 Health Insurance $500 Set up fee Due upon enrollment $25 $2,500 Interest rate Due on July 29th Please note the following items cannot be added to the payment plan and are due immediately if the Payment plan is selected: Student General Property Deposit Installment Tuition Handling Fee Service Fees (Late Registration and Add/Drop) Fines (Traffic and Library) Discretionary Fees (liability insurance) Amounts due for financial holds from prior periods. Study Abroad related charges (housing, meal plans etc...) Tuition Loans cannot be canceled once selected. Additionally, no other charges can be added. Make sure all the charges are in your account before processing a Tuition Loan. Students that are under 18 years of age and want to enroll in the tuition loan: Student needs to email sbs@utep.edu ; SBS will then email student & parent guardian Tuition Loan documents via DocuSign with additional instructions. Enroll in a Tuition Loan now Book Loan A book loan is a short-term loan that is available at the beginning of each semester. This is not a cash option. Funds are directed to your Miner Gold Card and can be used only at the UTEP Bookstore. Get a Book Loan now! 3rd Party Sponsor A third-party is an entity which guarantees payment of tuition and/or fees on behalf of a student with whom it has a relationship. Examples of a third party are: Employers City, County, State or Federal Government Military Units Foreign Governments Private Organizations For non - military students: All students being sponsored by a third-party entity need to submit a Statement of Understanding (SOU) by the payment deadline . Once the SOU is received, Student Business Services will review and process the form. Once the form is processed, Student Business Services will code the student's account to secure the students's classes from being dropped due to nonpayment. If payment is not received, the student is responsible for the balance and registration will be restricted until payment is submitted. For more information about non-military third-party sponsorship click here. For military students and their dependents: Student Business Services no longer requires a SOU form. Contact Military Student Success Center at (915) 747-5342 or via email to mssc@utep.edu for pre-certification requirements. International Payments UTEP accepts international payments via Flywire Flywire is a secure and convenient way to make international education payments to UTEP. Flywire allows you to pay online, typically in your home currency, and its trusted by colleges and universities worldwide including UTEP. Why use Flywire? Pay from banks worldwide. For most countries and territories, you can pay in your home currency and Flywire sends funds in US dollars directly to UTEP. Take advantage of their competitive foreign exchange rates that you can see in real time, up front. Choose from a variety of payment methods that may range from bank wire transfers, credit cards, e-wallet and more. Track the progress of your payment anytime online. Receive email and text alerts each step of the way including when your payment reaches UTEP. Flywire offers multilingual customer support. Contact for help via email, phone or live chat while making your payment! Go to flywire.com/contact for more phone numbers and other contact options. How to make payment online Go to Flywire . Login using you utep.edu email and the password Complete all required information Select a payment option from the list shown; options can include local domestic bank transfer, credit cards, e-wallet or other local payment options depending on your country. Send your payment to Flywire as instructed. Flywire Customer Support Information Phone: +1 800 346 9252 Email: suport@flywire.com Web: flywire.com/contact Academic Calendar Important Dates Petes Payment Options Book Loan Third Party Sponsor Payment flywire Student Business Services Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso Student Business Services Mike Loya Academic Services Building, Room 118 500 W University El Paso, Texas 79968 E: sbs@utep.edu / sbsrefunds@utep.edu P: (915) 747-5116 F: (915) 747-5933 THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Texas Veterans Portal Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 | SITE FEEDBACK Modal X"}
