{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/titleix/training.html", "title": "Training", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search TItle IX Information Title IX Coordinators SB 212 Filing a Report Training On and Off Campus Resources Important Definitions FAQs Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Title IX Main Content UTEP Title IX UTEP Title IX Available Trainings Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 is a federal law that prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex in education programs or activities operated by recipients of federal financial assistance to include sexual harassment and sexual violence. Although all faculty, staff, and student employees are required to complete a compliance module about Title IX, it is widely recognized that some staff, faculty and student employees are more likely than others to learn of incidents of sexual violence and sexual harassment including sexual assault, domestic violence, dating violence and stalking due to their role on campus. This workshop will provide information, resources and guidance on what to do if you are made aware of and incident of sexual harassment or sexual violence and the steps you must take to report the incident immediately to the Title IX Coordinator, Deputy Title IX Coordinators or appropriate department. Register for a Training If you would like to attend a Title IX training,\u00a0please register on Mine Tracker. Schedule a\u00a0Training If you would like to schedule a Title IX departmental or group training, please contact the Title IX Program at (915) 747-8117 or titleix@utep.edu . Title IX Training Title IX training of Title IX coordinators, investigators, decision makers and other facilitators: In accordance with federal law, please find below Title IX training materials for the 2022-2023 academic year: UT System Training 2022-2023 Avoiding Bias+Conflicts of Interest Training Investigation Report Writing Training Sexual Misconduct Investigations--Procedural Elements Sexual Misconduct Interview and Questioning Approaches Sexual Misconduct Appellate Officer Training Sexual Misconduct Hearing Officer Training Sexual Misconduct Advisor Training Sexual Misconduct Universtity Representative Training Other Training Zoom Training for SM Hearing Officers, September 30, 2020 2nd Zoom Training, December 14, 2020 NASPA Informal Resolution Certificate Program, November 12 - November 14, 2020 Links Title IX Coordinators SB 212 Filing a Report On and Off Campus Resources Confidential Resources Training Important Definitions Pregnancy FAQs Submit a Title IX Report EOAA Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso Office of Institutional Compliance -- Title IX Office Kelly Hall, Room 312 500 W University El Paso, Texas 79968 E: TitleIX@utep.edu P: (915) 747-8358 F: (915) 747-6486 THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Texas Veterans Portal Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 | SITE FEEDBACK Modal X"}
{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/titleix/sb-212.html", "title": "SB 212", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search TItle IX Information Title IX Coordinators SB 212 Filing a Report Training On and Off Campus Resources Important Definitions FAQs Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Title IX Main Content UTEP Title IX UTEP Title IX SB 212 Important sexual misconduct reporting requirement under texas law During the 2019 Texas legislative session,\u00a0Senate Bill 212\u00a0was passed into state law, codified under Texas Education Code \u00a7 51.252 . This law requires all employees of Texas universities to report incidents of sexual harassment, sexual assault, dating violence, or stalking allegedly committed by or against a student or employee, to a Title IX Coordinator or Deputy Title IX Coordinator. Under this new law, an employee who fails to report or falsely reports such an incident will also be subject to criminal liability (misdemeanor) and termination of employment. SB 212 Highlights The bill requires an employee who in the course and scope of employment, witnesses or receives information regarding an incident that the employee reasonably believes constitutes sexual harassment, sexual assault, dating violence, or stalking, and which is alleged to have been committed by or against a person who is a student or employee of the institution at the time of the incident, must promptly report the incident to the institution\u2019s Title IX Coordinator or Deputy Title IX Coordinator. If an employee is required to report and fails to make a report, or with the intent to harm or deceive, knowingly makes a report that is false, then the offense is a Class B misdemeanor; If it is shown at trial that the employee acted with an intent to conceal the incident, then the offense is a Class A misdemeanor. The institution will be required to terminate an employee whom the institution determines, in accordance with the institution\u2019s disciplinary procedure, to have committed the offense of failing to report or making a false report to the institution. The Title IX Coordinator must submit a written report of the reports received by the institution, to be submitted quarterly to the President. At least once during each fall or spring semester, the President will be required to submit to the Board of Regents, and post on the institution\u2019s website, a report that must include: The number of reports received by the institution; The number of investigations conducted as a result of those reports; The disposition, if any, of any disciplinary processes arising from those reports; The number of those reports for which the institution determined not to initiate a disciplinary process, if any; and Any disciplinary actions taken regarding failure to report or false reports to the institution. The institutional implementation requirements of this bill will take effect January 1, 2020. Employees who have been designated as confidential employees are required to report the type of incident only. Students who are also employees are strongly encouraged, but not required, to report. In order to fully understand the requirements of the law, the manner in which reports can be made to UTEP\u2019s Title IX Coordinator or Deputy Title IX Coordinators, and resources and support available at UTEP for those who have been impacted by sexual misconduct, all UTEP employees are strongly encouraged to participate in a Title IX training session .\u00a0 Please click here to register for a Title IX training. CEO Report under Texas Education Code \u00a7 51.253(c) Effective January 1, 2020, Texas Education Code (TEC), Section 51.253(c) requires an institution or system's Chief's Executive Officer (CEO) submit a report (\"CEO Report\") at least once during each fall or spring semester to the institution's governing body and post the report on the organization's website. The Texas Higher Education Board (THECB) requires annual certification of compliance for the TEC requirements in October of each year. The CEO Report must contain (1) all reports by employees under the TEC, Section 51.252 that constitutes \"sexual harassment,\" \"sexual assault,\" \"dating violence,\" or \"stalking\" (as defined in the TEC, Section 51.251), and (2) any disciplinary actions taken under TEC, Section 51.255. For the purposes of complying with the CEO's TEC reporting requirements, the following CEO Report includes all of the required reporting by UTEP to U.T. System Board of Regents and THECB for the respective academic year: 2020 CEO Report 2021 CEO Report 2022 CEO Report 2023 CEO Report 2024 CEO Report 2025 CEO Report Reference to Applicable Texas Statutes: CEO's Administrative Reporting Requirements: Tex. Educ. Code Section 51.253(c) THECB Compliance Requirements: 19 Tex. Admin. Code Section 3.19(a) Links Title IX Coordinators SB 212 Filing a Report On and Off Campus Resources Confidential Resources Training Important Definitions Pregnancy FAQs Submit a Title IX Report EOAA Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso Office of Institutional Compliance -- Title IX Office Kelly Hall, Room 312 500 W University El Paso, Texas 79968 E: TitleIX@utep.edu P: (915) 747-8358 F: (915) 747-6308 THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Texas Veterans Portal Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 | SITE FEEDBACK Modal X"}
{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/compliance/conflicts-of-interest/request-approval-of-outside-activities.html", "title": "Request for Approvals of Outside Activities", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About About Us Contact Us Ethics Training Training Requirements Online Training Frequently Asked Questions New Employee Packet Departmental Training Review Modules Standards of Conduct Guide Standards of Conduct Guide Committees Executive Endowment Conflicts of Interest Conflicts of Interest Conflict of Interest, Commitment, and Outside Activities Information Request for Approvals of Outside Activities Submit a Disclosure Policy Definitions Training Resources Outside Activity Portal Compliance Helpline Compliance Helpline Warning Signs Helpline FAQs Other Reporting Options Protection from Retaliation Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Office of Institutional Compliance Main Content UTEP Office of Institutional Compliance Conflicts of Interest UTEP Office of Institutional Compliance Conflicts of Interest Request for Approvals of Outside Activities A Request for Approval form is submitted for an outside activity that will occur in the future. Outside activities that require prior approval are: All outside employment or other compensated activity Any outside activity, regardless of compensation, that reasonably appears to create a conflict of interest or a conflict of commitment; Outside board service as described in Section 29.6.4 of the policy; and Foreign Affiliations - Any substantial relationship between an employee and any program sponsored, funded, directed, or controlled by a foreign government, foreign agency, or foreign institution. In particular, any participation in\u00a0foreign talent programs\u00a0or honorary / position titles that may be perceived as employment of a foreign institution. Note: Some activities may be considered pre-approved. (Please see section 29.6.3 of the policy for more information). Substantial relationships with foreign entities are not considered pre-approved and a request for approval must be submitted. All employees must electronically request and receive prior approval before engaging in an outside activity with annual approval required thereafter. The permissible level of time commitment to outside activities cannot exceed an average of 8 hours per week, during the term of an appointment, without approval of the President or designee and a written management plan. Employees must log onto the Outside Activity Portal to request approval at the following URL: https://apps.utsystem.edu/ActivityPortal/. Below is a training tool available to assist with completing the required request for approval: Tutorial Video (must log onto portal to view.) All requests for approval should be routed according to the following process: Academic Departments - The request should first be routed by the requester to the respective Department Chair. The request will then be routed through by each approver as follows: 1. Department Chair 2. Dean 3. Provost Office 4. Mary Solis, Institutional Compliance (mavitia@utep.edu) All Other Departments - The request should first be routed by the requester to the Director/Department Head. The request will then be routed through by each approver as follows: 1. Director/Department Head 2. Appropriate Vice President 3. Mary Solis, Institutional Compliance (mavitia@utep.edu) The Office of Institutional Compliance is the designated final approver for all requests for approval. If you have any questions, please contact us at 747-6478 or by email conflictsofinterest@utep.edu To read the full policy, please go to the Handbook of Operating Procedures, Section V, Chapter 29 . Outside Activity Portal: https://apps.utsystem.edu/ActivityPortal/ .theCol {padding: 12px 0;}\n\t.theBox {background: #f8f8f8;padding: 12px;margin: 12px 0;box-shadow: 0px 0px 5px 0px rgba(0, 0, 0, .2);font-weight: 600;border-top: 1px solid #fff;}\n\t.theBox p {margin:0;text-align: center;}\n\t.theSVG {max-width: 36px;margin: 0 auto;display: block;} Conflicts of Interest Conflicts of Interest Submit a Disclosure Request for Approvals of Outside Activities Conflict of Interest, Commitment, and Outside Activities Information Policy Definitions Training Resources Online Training Compliance Helpline Risk Management Conflicts of Interest Handbook of Operating Procedures Title IX Outside Activity Portal // \n$(\".dropdown-menu a[href^='https://']\").attr(\"target\",\"_blank\");\n$(\".leftSidebar .nav a[href^='https://']\").attr(\"target\",\"_blank\");\n$('.dropdown-menu a[href*=\".pdf\"]').attr(\"target\",\"_blank\");\n$('.leftSidebar .nav a[href*=\".pdf\"]').attr(\"target\",\"_blank\");\n$('.carousel a[href*=\".pdf\"]').attr(\"target\",\"_blank\");\n// Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso Office of Institutional Compliance Kelly Hall, Room 308 500 West University Avenue El Paso, Texas 79968 E: complianceoffice@utep.edu P: (915) 747-6478 THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Texas Veterans Portal Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 | SITE FEEDBACK Modal X"}
