vost and Vice President for Academic Affairs Main Content Welcome to the Faculty & Administrator Resource Hub Access resources, policies, and data to support your teaching, research, service, and leadership efforts. <!--\n::placeholder {\n    color: black !important;\n    opacity: .5 !important;\n}\n\ntable {\n    width: 100%;\n    border: none;\n}\n\n.table-bordered,\n.table-bordered td,\n.table-bordered th {\n    border: none !important;\n}\n\n.table-bordered tbody tr {\n    border-bottom: 1px solid #dcdcdc; /* Subtle divider between rows */\n}\n\nth, td {\n    padding: 8px;\n    text-align: left;\n}\n\ntr:hover {\n    background-color: #ffffff;\n}\n\n.keyword {\n    display: none;\n}\n\n.alert {\n    padding: 20px;\n    background-color: #ffeb99;\n    color: black;\n}\n\n.toolbar {\n    background-color: #041e42 !important;\n    border-radius: 15px;\n    padding: 30px;\n    margin-top: 5px;\n    color: #ffffff;\n}\n\n.closebtn {\n    margin-left: 15px;\n    color: white;\n    font-weight: bold;\n    float: right;\n    font-size: 22px;\n    line-height: 20px;\n    cursor: pointer;\n    transition: 0.3s;\n}\n\n.closebtn:hover {\n    color: black;\n}\n\n\n.searchbutton {\n    color: #000000 !important;       /* Black text */\n    background-color: #ff8200;   /* orange background */\n    border: none;                    /* No border */\n    cursor: pointer;                 /* Pointer on hover */\n    font-size: 16px;                 /* Optional: adjust text size */\n    padding: 8px 12px;               /* Optional: spacing */\n   margin-top: 10px; /* Adds space between input and button */\n\n}\n--> Access the Support you Need Use keywords to search for the resource you need or browse the categorized lists below to get started. Search community, engagement, cce, scholarship, service, learning, based Center for Community Engagement: The Center for Community Engagement (CCE) serves as UTEP\u2019s resource center for faculty, staff, and students who are interested in engaging in the community through a variety of programs and activities. Visit the website at: https://www.utep.edu/cce/about/about-the-cce.html community, engagement, cce, scholarship, service, learning, based, courses, serving learning Community Engaged Courses: Discover how to design meaningful course and learning objectives for community-engaged learning. Gain valuable guidance on identifying and partnering with local non-profit organizations to enhance the impact of your course. Visit: https://www.utep.edu/cce/faculty/comunity-engagement-courses-faculty.html AI, Artificial Intelligence, teaching, Artificial, Intelligence, chatgbt, gbt, course, standards, use of ai, learning, AI in Teaching and Learning AI in Teaching and Learning: The following document includes ready-to-use syllabus language, guiding questions, and adaptable frameworks to help you align AI use with your course learning outcomes.: https://www.utep.edu/provost/_files/docs/instruction/utep-guidance-for-teaching-with-ai-technologies.pdf community, engagement, cce, scholarship, service, learning, based, fellow Community Engaged Fellows: Community Engaged Fellows work closely with faculty and staff to advance UTEP\u2019s mission and strategic goals. CCE Faculty Fellows are recognized for their strong record of community-engaged research and scholarship and have a deep understanding of the Provost\u2019s Task Force Report on Community Engagement. Connect with a fellow at: https://www.utep.edu/cce/about/faculty_fellows.html community, engagement, cce, scholarship, service, learning, based, ces Community Engaged Scholarship: Community engaged scholarship (CES) integrates the development, exchange, and application of knowledge between the university and the community to address real-world challenges. It involves collaboration, shared authority, and mutual benefit. Learn more: https://www.utep.edu/cce/faculty/community-engaged-scholarship-page.html community, engagement, cce, scholarship, service, learning, based, ces, grants Community Engagement Grants: Faculty, staff, students, and community members are encouraged to visit the link below to learn more about securing grants related to community engagement: Here registration, records, graduation, transcript, official, course, change, register, goldmine Registration and Records: Students can learn more about registering in Goldmine, retrieving a transcript, course withdrawals, and graduation candidacy by visiting: https://www.utep.edu/registrar/ policy, policies, guidelines, rules Policies: Visit the link below to reach a roster of Institutional, College and Departmental Academic Policies: https://www.utep.edu/provost/policies/policies-procedures.html career, fair, expo, internship, internships, job, interview, preparation, closet, career center, linkedin, linked in, resume, cv, careers Career Center: The Career Center aims to expose UTEP students to options that best fit their individual career needs and aspirations. The Career Center provides part-time and full-time job listings, internship, and experiential learning opportunities, career/job fairs, career development workshops and presentations, r\u00e9sum\u00e9 reviews, job search assistance, interview coaching, on-campus and virtual interviews, and employer contacts. Visit the website at: https://www.utep.edu/student-affairs/careers/ care, safe, safety, help, advocacy, violence, physical, sexual, financial, crime, support, counseling, crisis, 911, psychological, miners talk, line, health, wellness, police, emergency, suicide, danger, risk, caps Campus Advocacy, Resources, and Education (CARE): The CARE team is committed to respond, emotionally support, and empower UTEP students who become victims of crime by working side by side to assist in their recovery process. Learn more at: https://www.utep.edu/student-affairs/care/about/ wellness, doctor, medical, health, immunize, immunization, immunizations, nurse, insurance, center, healthy, body, mind, swhc, preventive, preventative, nutrition, shot, tetanus, physician, mental, physical, help UTEP Student Health and Wellness Center: The UTEP Student Health and Wellness Center (SHWC) provides high-quality healthcare and preventive services, including nutrition education and mental health care for all enrolled students to optimize their health and help them achieve academic success. Visit: https://www.utep.edu/chs/shc/ care, safe, safety, help, advocacy, violence, physical, sexual, financial, crime, support, counseling, crisis, 911, psychological, miners talk, line, health, wellness, police, emergency, suicide, danger, risk, caps UTEP Counseling and Psychological Services: CAPs provides career counseling, psycho-educational workshops, individual and group counseling, crisis intervention, and professional training experiences that are responsive to the individual, cultural, and demographic diversity of our students. Visit: https://www.utep.edu/student-affairs/counsel/about/mission-vision.html pregnant, pregnancy, accommodations, accommodation, title, title ix, ix, student, students, child, childbirth, miscarriage, doctor, baby Title IX for Pregnant and Parenting Students: Visit the website below to learn more about accommodations to students who are pregnant or have pregnancy-related conditions: https://www.utep.edu/titleix/pregnancy-and-parenting.html blackboard, technology, support, help, help desk, it Technology Support (HelpDesk): Contact the HelpDesk for all questions about UTEP technology services or to troubleshoot technology. Visit: https://www.utep.edu/technologysupport/supportservices.html adopt, adopted, homeless, home, live, living, fhar, insecurity, housing, house, food, pantry, hygiene, supplies, help, support, basic, needs, basic needs, advocacy, holistic, fsss, literacy, shelter Financial and Social Support Services (FSSS): FSSS educates and empowers students through increasing financial literacy and cultivating the skills necessary to make sound financial decisions. L