 with disabilities, accommodations and support services to help them pursue their academic, graduation, and career goals. Learn more at: https://www.utep.edu/student-affairs/cass/ community, engagement, cce, scholarship, service, learning, based, ces, grants, disseminating, publishing, disseminate, publish, scholarship Disseminating Community Engaged Scholarship: The Center for Community Engagement can provide guidance on taking community-engaged work from concept to documented scholarship. Visit: https://www.utep.edu/cce/faculty/faculty-engagement.html advising, advisor, fhar, financial Academic Advising Center: The Academic Advising Center (AAC) is responsible for providing advising services to incoming students for their first 45 hours of enrollment. The advising model focuses on three areas: advocacy, engagement and empowerment. To positively impact retention rates, degree completion, and time to degree, the AAC provides students with a Financial and Social Services Program, and a Student Success Help Desk. Visit: https://www.utep.edu/advising/ aid, financial, funds, tuition, money, stipend, scholarship, scholarships, loan, loans, affordable, affordability, barrier, resource, resources, funding, fund Financial Aid and Scholarships: The Office of Financial Aid and Scholarships supports UTEP's mission of increasing access to an excellent education by addressing affordability barriers and providing students with financial resources to help them persist. Visit: https://www.utep.edu/financial-aid// program, academic, definition, director, program director, academic program director Academic Program Definition: Visit the link below to understand how the term \u201cacademic program\u201d is defined at UTEP: https://www.utep.edu/provost/_files/docs/policies/academic-program-definition.pdf extension, clock, tenure, covid Extensions to the Tenure Clock in Response to the COVID-19 Pandemic: The memo issued in response to tenure clock extensions due to circumstances related to the COVID pandemic is available at: https://www.utep.edu/provost/_files/docs/faculty-evaluation/tenureextensioncovidsecondamended.pdf remote Faculty Remote Work Policy for Full-Time Faculty: The following document informs decisions related to remote work for full-time UTEP faculty members: https://www.utep.edu/provost/_files/docs/instruction/facultyremoteworkpolicy.pdf start up, startup, new, hire, lab New Hire Startup Award Guidelines: UTEP Guidelines for startup awards for new faculty hires are available at: https://www.utep.edu/provost/_files/docs/new-faculty/facstartuppolprocs.pdf regents, rules, regulations, system Regents' Rules and Regulations: The Rules and Regulations of the Board of Regents of The University of Texas System are available at: https://www.utsystem.edu/offices/board-of-regents/regents-rules-and-regulations grievance, complaint, student, harassment, grade, discrimination, conduct, concern Response and Resolution of Student Complaints: Visit the flowchart at the link below to guide you through the appropriate point of contact when addressing student grievances. https://www.utep.edu/provost/_Files/docs/policies/student-complaint_20230321.pdf small, class, size Small Class Policy: The Small Class Policy provides small class definitions and processes for classes that fall outside of the minimum enrollment. https://www.utep.edu/provost/_files/docs/instruction/small-class-policy.pdf standard, term, scheduling, pattern, term Standard Terms Pattern Policy: The document below outlines the standard term patterns recognized at UTEP. https://www.utep.edu/provost/_files/docs/curriculum/standard-term-patterns-policy.pdf distance learning, hybrid, online, University Distance Learning and Teaching Policies: Learn more about the responsibilities, processes, and resources for developing and offering hybrid and online courses and programs at UTEP by visiting the following link: https://www.utep.edu/extendeduniversity/cid/faculty-resources/policies.html textbook, authorization Use of Textbook Authorization: Use the form linked below to request authorization for use of textbooks (printed and digital), notebooks, manuals, and other classroom materials authored by UTEP faculty to be purchased by students. https://www.utep.edu/provost/_Files/docs/instruction/facultyauthoredtextbookadoptionform.doc internal, external, awards, honorifics Awards and Honorifics: Research Advancement supports faculty in pursuing recognition through awards, honorifics, and internal funding. More details available at: https://www.utep.edu/research/proposal-development/honorifics-awards/ controlled, unclassified, information, cui, government, dissemination, control Controlled Unclassified Information: Please visit the following website for more information about handling Controlled Unclassified Information (CUI): https://www.utep.edu/research/research-protections/cui/pages/cui-training.html export, control, international, travel, laptop, license Export Control: The Office of Research Compliance & Regulatory Assurances assists the UTEP community with compliance with federal and UT requirements related to export controls. Visit the following page to contact Export Control: Here fellowship, incentive, research Faculty Incentive Program for Fellowship Recipients: Learn more about fellowships accompanied by stipends at: https://www.utep.edu/provost/_files/docs/research-engagement-travel-agreement/utepfellowshippolicy.pdf incentive, ftip, internal, funding, pilot,pfp, pivot, sponsor, limited, submission, ls, infoready, opportunities, lo Find Funding: Pivot is an online database where you can find funding opportunities. Learn more at: https://www.utep.edu/research/proposal-development/find-funding/ post-award, post award, contract, management, grant, accounting Grant Management Accounting: Grant Management Accounting provides sound financial oversight and to process and manage the University\u2019s federal, state, local, and private programs in accordance with the post-award agreements. Learn more: Here hpc, high, performance, computer, network, data, model, research, computing, analysis High Performance Computing: High Performance Computing (HPC) services allow all researchers and colleges to access computing resources for very complex data analysis, solving numerical problems and execute any scientific software code as needed. Learn more: https://www.utep.edu/information-resources/research/about/hpc.html research, human, subjects, review board, review, board, irb Human Subject Research: Learn more about UTEP\u2019s Institutional Review Board which is responsible for protecting human subjects participating in research. Visit: https://www.utep.edu/research/human-subjects-research/ interdisciplinary, idr, research, team, symposium Interdisciplinary Research: UTEP supports the cultivation of ideas, research teams, and proposal development at UTEP. Learn more about interdisciplinary research at UTEP at: Here library, research, literacy, database, guide, reserves, inter, scholarly, publication, article, book, collection, borrow, ama, style, apa, chicago, mla, minerquest Library Research Services for Faculty: Visit the UTEP Library at the link below to learn more about services that support research on campus: Here intellectual, property, patent, otc, commercialization, commercialize, license, start up, start-up, commercial, marketing Office of Technology Commercialization: UTEP\u2019s Office of Technology Commercialization (OTC) manages UTEP\u2019s intellectual property and facilitates the transfer of technologies into commercial products. Learn more at: https://www.utep.edu/research/otc/ proposal, consultation, letters, development, training, planning, proposal development Proposal Development: Research & Innovation supports the UTEP faculty, researchers, and staff in crafting competitive, high-impact proposals. Learn more about services provided at: https://www.utep.edu/research/proposal-development/ data, support, an