demic Affairs Main Content UTEP Office of the Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs About UTEP Office of the Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs About Business Center The Provost Office Business Center aims to empower and support the academic community, our business center is committed to fostering an environment of innovation, efficiency, and excellence. Through comprehensive service integration and collaborative partnerships, we aim to streamline operations, enhance resource accessibility, and promote academic success for students, faculty, and staff. All Forms: Vendor Payment/Employee Reimbursement Travel Authorization Form Appointment Form About Us Isela Orozco Provost Administrative Officer riorozco@utep.edu (915) 747-6024 Ian Alvarado Business Center Specialist iaalvarado5@utep.edu (915) 747-6190 Diana Lares Business Center Specialist dmlaresgarcia2@utep.edu (915) 747-7078 Vivian R. Rivas, M.A. Senior Coordinator vrrivas2@utep.edu (915) 747-7855 Lucero Tarin Business Manager lsflores2@utep.edu (915) 747-7303 Contact Office of the Provost Administration Bldg Room 303 915-747-5725 provostbusinesscenter@utep.edu Helpful Links Academic Unit Directory Business Center Faculty Affairs Calendar Faculty Governance Faculty & Administrator Resource Hub body .navbar-default.utep-nav .navbar-nav > li > a {\n    padding-left: 9px;\n} Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso Office of the Provost Administration Building Room 310 500 W. University El Paso, Texas 79968 E: provostoffice@utep.edu P: (915) 747-5725 F: (915) 747-7522 THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Texas Veterans Portal Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 | SITE FEEDBACK Modal X"}
{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/provost/about/academic-support-units.html", "title": "Academic Support Units", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About Academic Support Units Business Center Colleges and Schools Faculty & Administrator Resource Hub Leadership Team Organizational Chart Faculty Affairs Faculty Administrators Student Success Student Success at UTEP Student Success Indicators UTEP Edge Academic Advising Center Career Center Core Curriculum Redesign Entering Student Experience Transfer Articulation Curriculum AI in Teaching and Learning Core Curriculum at UTEP Core Curriculum Redesign Curriculum Changes Curriculum Tracking and Status Online Course Development Policies Substantive Program Changes Sample Syllabi Texas Common Course Numbering (TCCNS) Assessment 2026 SACSCOC Reaffirmation Accreditation Program Assessment Graduate Program Review Inclusive Excellence Making Excellence Inclusive Exceptional Education for All History of Excellence Groups, Programs, and Curriculum Indigenous Land Acknowledgment Statement Hispanic-Serving Research Council Policies and Procedures Institutional Policies College and Departmental Academic Policies Academic Agreements Response and Resolution of Student Complaints Standard Term Patterns Occupational License Eligibility Request for Approval of Outside Activity Export Control Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Office of the Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs Main Content UTEP Office of the Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs About UTEP Office of the Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs About Academic Support Units The Academic Advising Center (AAC) is responsible for providing advising services to incoming students for their first 45 hours of enrollment. The advising model focuses on three areas: advocacy, engagement and empowerment. To positively impact retention rates, degree completion, and time to degree, the AAC provides students with a Financial and Social Services Program, and a Student Success Help Desk. COURI provides undergraduate students with impactful learning experiences through research, scholarly and creative activities, under the mentorship of faculty, and in collaboration with UTEP academic leaders, advisors and other supporting units. The Career Center aims to expose UTEP students to options that best fit their individual career needs and aspirations. The Career Center provides part-time and full-time job listings, internship, and experiential learning opportunities, career/job fairs, career development workshops and presentations, r\u00e9sum\u00e9 reviews, job search assistance, interview coaching, on-campus and virtual interviews, and employer contacts. The Center for Community Engagement connects students and faculty with community partners to share knowledge and resources for the improvement of both academics and societal challenges. The CCE supports the institutionalization of community engaged scholarship through student programming, faculty development, and curriculum development. The Entering Student Experience fosters an inclusive environment to ensure students from diverse backgrounds have a meaningful transition to UTEP.\u202f\u202fBuilding opportunities for engagement, belonging, agency, academic success, and professional preparation, we facilitate the continued development of our students\u2019 academic skills and unique strengths and empower them to succeed in their educational and professional pursuits. Extended University is UTEP\u2019s hub for online and other nontraditional academic programs, professional training and education, and community enrichment. We strive to live up to our name \u2013 Extended University \u2013 by increasing access to UTEP\u2019s outstanding educational opportunities for all who seek them out. Our three component units provide educational opportunities and services to support both nontraditional students and educators interested in new modes of teaching. The Graduate School, located on the Administration Building, Room 200, oversees more than 100 master's degree programs and certificates as well as 22 doctoral programs. The Graduate School team helps students explore options for graduate education, complete the admissions and enrollment process, and graduate in a timely manner through professional development, advising, and mentoring. The Graduate School also offers resources for undergraduates preparing to enter graduate school, postdoctoral fellows in residence, and those who supervise these emerging scholars. The Institute for Scholarship, Pedagogy, Innovation, and Research Excellence (InSPIRE) empowers educators to embrace innovative practices that create engaging learning environments. InSPIRE facilitates interdisciplinary collaboration and provides resources to educator scholars seeking to address challenges in higher education. The team at InSPIRE works strategically with faculty to offer technology solutions for teaching, learning, and research that enhances instruction and promotes student engagement and success. The library provides innovative and high quality services, programs, and resources that support UTEP's stated mission of education, research, scholarship, and community service. The library provides access to a range of print and electronic information resources that meet the individual needs of its users in its multicultural university community and the U.S. \u2013 Mexican Border Region. The Miner Learning Center (MLC) provides assistance in traditionally difficult core curriculum class sections by providing study sessions in order to improve academic performance. Academic support services include regularly scheduled, out-of-class, Peer Tutoring and peer-led study sessions, known as Peers Assisting Student Success (PASS) sessions. PASS and Peer Tutoring sessions are open to all students in the course and are attended on a voluntary basis, free of charge. The University Honors Program (UHP) is designed to attract, retain, and graduate academically talented students and maximize their professional, educational, and service opportunities. The goal of the Honors Program is to involve students in an ideal set of experiences that will best prepare them for their next steps and lifelong success. The dynamic interdisciplinary program promotes student engagement and integrates closely with the UTEP Student Success Framework (UTEP EDGE). Networking activities, scholarships, and special events that are a part of the program promote interaction and cultivate academic excellence across campus. The University of Texas at El Paso\u2019s University Writing Center (UWC) focuses on helping First Year to Ph.D students from all disciplines to better understand the rhetorical choices writers make in order to be effective communicators and writers. Moreover, the UWC works with faculty across campus to create and integrate effective multi-modal writing assignments into their classes and to use the UWC\u2019s resources and tutors in enhancing students\u2019 writing experiences. The UWC adapts pedagogies and methods to reflect professors\u2019 course content and to highlight our collaborative approach to writing. Helpful Links Academic Unit Directory Business Center Faculty Affairs Calendar Faculty Governance Faculty & Administrator Resource Hub body .navbar-default.utep-nav .navbar-nav > li > a {\n    padding-left: 9px;\n} Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso Office of the Provost Administration Building Room 310 500 W. University El Paso, Texas 79968 E: provostoffice@utep.edu P: (915) 747-5725 F: (915) 747-7522 THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Texas Veterans Portal Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 | SITE FEEDBACK Modal X"}
{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/human-resources/services/benefits/mental-health-support-and-resources.html", "title": "Mental Health Support and Resources", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About Our Mission Services Employment Opportunities Workforce Management Employee Support Services People Human Resources Staff Benefits Representatives Resources Handbook of Operating Procedures Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Office of Human Resources Main Content UTEP Office of Human Resources services Benefits UTEP Office of Human Resources services Benefits Mental Health Support and Resources UTEP is committed to providing faculty and staff an avenue for requisite programs and resources that facilitate and assist in managing mental health challenges that can impact both physical and mental health. Please contact benefits@utep.edu or HRLeaveAdmin@utep.edu for additional assistance. Resources: All one health Employee Assistance Program (EAP) Health and Wellness EAP Brochure 2024-2025 Living Well Resources Guide All One Health Website Parenting and Family Support Sign Up Page Drug-Free University Community and Workplace Sign Up Instructions Click Here EAP Newsletter Website Community Resources UTEP Resources National Alliance on Mental Illness (NAMI) Title IX Resources 1-800-950-6264 Counseling and Psychological Service Resource List National Suicide Prevention Lifeline Mental Health Service Providers & Community Agencies 1-800-273-8255 Traditional Behavioral Health Services 1-866-882-2034 Texas Department of Family and Protective Service 1-800-252-5400 Alcohol and Drug Abuse Hotline 1-800-662-4357 Center Against Sexual & Family Violence 1-915-593-7300 If you believe a student, staff or faculty member is in immediate danger, please contact UTEP Police at: 915-747-5611 Suicide Prevention: The National Suicide Prevention Lifeline\u2019s mission is to provide immediate assistance to individuals in suicidal crisis by connecting them to the nearest available suicide prevention and mental health service provider through a toll-free telephone number: 1-800-273-TALK (8255) . It is the only national suicide prevention and intervention telephone resource funded by the Federal Government. Online Resources: MDLIVE Behavioral Health Counseling: MDLIVE offers virtual visits for behavioral health counseling. Speak with a licensed counselor, therapist, or psychiatrist for support. You can choose who you want to work with for issues such as anxiety, depression, relationship problems, trauma, loss, and more. Click Here Digital Mental Health-Learn to Live Learn to Live (L2L) is a behavioral health digital platform available to UT SELECT and UT CONNECT members which offers condition-specific programs, each delivered in a user-paced multimedia experience. Find Learn to Live by logging in to Blue Access for\u00a0Members SM You may also visit Learn to\u00a0Live and follow these steps to enroll: Enter Access Code: BETTERME Once you enter the access code, you will be prompted to enter your BCBSTX identification number If you have questions, UT SELECT members can call a health advocate at 1-866-882-2034. Traditional Behavioral Health Services As a UT Select member you have choices of where to go for behavior health care. Click here to Know your Network . You may also contact the Health Advocate team 1-866-882-2034 for resources, a list of providers and additional information. Emotional Wellness | Mindfulness Apps and Resources | Guided Meditations | Additional Resources: Taking care of yourself including getting enough rest, healthy eating, and staying emotionally healthy is important all the time but especially during times of great change and stress. Click Here Quick Tips: Reduce Stress Through Deep Breathing Reduce Stress Through Guided Imagery Reduce Stress Through Progressive Muscle Relaxation \u200b For more information: You may email your questions to benefits@utep.edu or HRLeaveAdmin@utep.edu . UTEP does not endorse any specific service or vendor. This list is shared as a convenience for our members searching for resources. Benefits Benefits Online Appointment My UT Benefits Notary Service Retirement Programs Retiree Benefits / Services Leave Administration Lactation Room and Resources Mental Health Support and Resources Student Health Insurance Plan (SHIP) Additional Resources My UT Benefits Holiday Schedule Hiring Manager Resource Guide Handbook of Operating Procedures Forms Mine Training and Development // \n$(\".dropdown-menu a[href^='http://']\").attr(\"target\",\"_blank\");\n$(\".dropdown-menu a[href^='https://']\").attr(\"target\",\"_blank\");\n$(\".leftSidebar .nav a[href^='http://']\").attr(\"target\",\"_blank\");\n$(\".leftSidebar .nav a[href^='https://']\").attr(\"target\",\"_blank\");\n$('.dropdown-menu a[href*=\".pdf\"]').attr(\"target\",\"_blank\");\n$('.leftSidebar .nav a[href*=\".pdf\"]').attr(\"target\",\"_blank\");\n$(\".carousel-caption a[href^='http://']\").attr(\"target\",\"_blank\");\n$(\".carousel-caption a[href^='https://']\").attr(\"target\",\"_blank\");\n$('.carousel-caption a[href*=\".pdf\"]').attr(\"target\",\"_blank\");\n// Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso Office of Human Resources Administration Building, Rm 216 500 W University El Paso, Texas 79968 E: hrs@utep.edu P: (915) 747-5202 F: (915) 747-5815 THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency