{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/human-resources/services/benefits/lactation1.html", "title": "Lactation Room and Resources", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About Our Mission Services Employment Opportunities Workforce Management Employee Support Services People Human Resources Staff Benefits Representatives Resources Handbook of Operating Procedures Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Office of Human Resources Main Content UTEP Office of Human Resources services Benefits UTEP Office of Human Resources services Benefits Lactation Room Program The University of Texas at El Paso recognizes the importance and benefits of breastfeeding. We believe in providing a place on campus for nursing mothers to express milk or nurse their child in a private, comfortable and quiet space.\u00a0In support, the University has created convenient locations on campus to provide University employees and students the opportunity to maintain this benefit relationship for mom and baby. To begin the registration process and gain Miner Gold Card access to your preferred room,\u00a0please complete the electronic\u00a0Lactation Room Registration Form\u00a0by clicking here .\u00a0 If received after standard business hours, your request may take up to 24-48 hours to process. Lactation Room Locations Lactation Station 1 Union Building East Bhutan Lounge Hours of Operation 8 a.m. \u2013 5 p.m. Monday \u2013 Friday A Mamava pod, a freestanding structure that serves as a private nursing station, is located on the second floor next to the Office of International Programs and Study Abroad. A restroom is conveniently located nearby. To use this room, please register by clicking here . Lactation Station 2 Health Sciences and Nursing Building Room 400 Hours of Operation 8 a.m. \u2013 5 p.m. Monday \u2013 Friday \u200b The room is conveniently located on the fourth floor of the College of Health Sciences Building. The room contains one nursing station and a nearby restroom. To use this room, please register by clicking here . Lactation Station 3 University Towers Room 208 Hours of Operation 8 a.m. \u2013 5 p.m. Monday \u2013 Friday \u200b The room is conveniently located on the second floor of University Towers Building. The room contains two private spaces for nursing moms and a washing station. To use this room, please register by clicking here . Benefits of Breast Feeding What are the benefits to breastfeeding? Breastfeeding during the first six months of an infant\u2019s life may protect the infant against risks of obesity, asthma and type 2 diabetes. Breastfeeding lowers the risk of sudden infant death syndrome (SIDS) and gastrointestinal infections. Breastfeeding can help lower a mother\u2019s risk of high blood pressure, type 2 diabetes and breast and ovarian cancer. \u201cBreastfeeding provides unmatched health benefits for babies and mothers. It is the clinical gold standard for infant feeding and nutrition, with breast milk uniquely tailored to meet the health needs of a growing baby. We must do more to create supportive and safe environments for mothers who choose to breastfeed.\u201d Dr. Ruth Petersen, Director of CDC\u2019s Division of Nutrition, Physical Activity, and Obesity Source: Breastfeeding. (2018, August 20). Retrieved from https://www/cdc.gov/breastfeeding/about-breastfeeding/why-it-matters.html Resources The Office of Human Resources The Office of Human Resources provides support and resources for expectant mothers and their families.\u00a0 You can find more information by clicking here . UTEP Wellness Program UTEP Wellness Program provides opportunities to build a healthier future by giving tools, resources and peer support necessary to help make healthy lifestyle choices. Click here for more information. YWCA\u2019s Early Learning Academy YWCA\u2019s Early Learning Academy is conveniently located\u00a0on campus at the\u00a0University Heights 315 W. Schuster. You can find more information by clicking here . City of El Paso Public Health The City of El Paso Public Health information to include Women, Infant and Children (WIC) program and immunizations.\u00a0 You can find more information by clicking here . FOR FACULTY AND STAFF Blue Cross Blue Shield of Texas Special Beginnings Maternity Program The Blue Cross Blue Shield of Texas Special Beginnings\u00a0Maternity Program provides educational material and support for expectant mothers from early pregnancy through six weeks after delivery.\u00a0 You can find more information by clicking here . Parents & Kids Health To children, the world is full of excitement, thrills, opportunities, and questions. As parents, we want our children to be healthy from their heads to their toes.\u00a0To help support you and your family, Living Well recommends the resources at Kidshealth.org , a website for parents and kids with information and tips for staying healthy, growing up, and dealing with feelings, along with articles featuring interactive activities. The Healthy Family App is available from Blue Cross Blue Shield of Texas (BCBSTX). Scroll down the page on the BCBSTX website at the link above to find this handy app that can help you keep track of recommended screenings and vaccines for the whole family. It allows you to prepare and become more informed about recommended preventive care and to set reminders for when tests are needed. You can learn more and find out how to get the app at www.bcbstx.com/mobile . Employee Assistance Program Employee Assistance Program (EAP)\u00a0provides resources for Child Care, Community and Health referrals, Online Tips, Tools and Articles, Legal and Financial Consultations, Health and Wellness Education, and Crisis Intervention. Access EAP 24 hours per day, 7 days a week, 365 days per year at 1(866) 327-2400 or email at eap@deeroaks.com . Online at www.deeroakseap.com . Username: UTEP Password: UTEP FOR STUDENTS Academic Health Plans/SHIP Academic Health Plans/SHIP Special Beginnings maternity program offers ongoing support from prenatal to postpartum care. Beneficial educational resources are easily accessed online or on a mobile device. Convenient 24/7 Nurse Line with toll-free access to registered nurses for health information. Click here for more information. FOR FACULTY AND STAFF Ovia Health If you are pregnant or planning to get pregnant, download the Ovia Health\u00a0apps for virtual support throughout your pregnancy and parenthood. Ovia can also help identify risks early and if needed will connect you to Blue Cross and Blue Shield of Texas maternity specialists for additional support. You can find more information by clicking here . UTSaver Loan and Hardship Emergency Distributions Employees of the University of Texas System Administration who participate in the UTSaver 403(b) Tax Sheltered Annuity (TSA) or the UTSaver 457(b) Deferred Compensation Program (DCP) have several options available for accessing their retirement savings accounts while employed. In Hardship and Unforeseeable Emergency Distributions participants may find themselves with expenses they cannot resolve by any other means. For more information click here . ADDITIONAL RESOURCES Online Resources Breastfeeding Lactation Support \u2014 Binational Breastfeeding Coalition Breast Milk Counts - Working Moms Breast Milk Counts - Resources Breastfeeding Made Simple La Leche League International La Leche League Resources Medela Resources for your Family Medela Resources for Professionals Contact Us The University of Texas at El Paso Human Resources Services Administration Building, Rm 216 500 W University El Paso, Texas 79968 E: lactationstations@utep.edu P: (915) 747-5202 F: (915) 747-5815 General Services Employment Verification Employee Education Assistance Program Employee Service Awards Prior State Service Employee Form General Services Frequently Asked Questions My UT Benefits Holiday Schedule Hiring Manager Resource Guide Handbook of Operating Procedures Forms Mine Training and Development Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso Human Resources Services Administration Building, Rm 216 500 W University El Paso, Texas 79968 E: lactationstations@utep.edu P: (915) 747-5202 F: (915) 747-5815 THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Texas Veterans Portal Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 | SITE FEEDBACK Modal X"}
