{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/provost/student-success/", "title": "Student Success at UTEP", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About Academic Support Units Business Center Colleges and Schools Faculty & Administrator Resource Hub Leadership Team Organizational Chart Faculty Affairs Faculty Administrators Student Success Student Success at UTEP Student Success Indicators UTEP Edge Academic Advising Center Career Center Core Curriculum Redesign Entering Student Experience Transfer Articulation Curriculum AI in Teaching and Learning Core Curriculum at UTEP Core Curriculum Redesign Curriculum Changes Curriculum Tracking and Status Online Course Development Policies Substantive Program Changes Sample Syllabi Texas Common Course Numbering (TCCNS) Assessment 2026 SACSCOC Reaffirmation Accreditation Program Assessment Graduate Program Review Inclusive Excellence Making Excellence Inclusive Exceptional Education for All History of Excellence Groups, Programs, and Curriculum Indigenous Land Acknowledgment Statement Hispanic-Serving Research Council Policies and Procedures Institutional Policies College and Departmental Academic Policies Academic Agreements Response and Resolution of Student Complaints Standard Term Patterns Occupational License Eligibility Request for Approval of Outside Activity Export Control Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Office of the Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs Main Content UTEP Office of the Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs Student Success UTEP Office of the Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs Student Success Student Success at UTEP The Office of the Provost advances student engagement, learning, and progress to graduation through a cross-institutional collaboration of teams that lead UTEP\u2019s framework of high-impact practices (UTEP Edge), student transfer pathways, holistic advising, curriculum and program assessment, student employment, and developmental education. Together, we identify opportunities and provide solutions to ensure students\u2019 academic and professional success. Drawing from our institutional commitment to a culture of care and using data-driven insights, administrators, faculty, and staff within the Office of the Provost work in tandem with colleges, faculty, and programs to accelerate student success for all Miners. Student Success Indicators Providing Active and Engaged Learning UTEP provides an active and engaged learning experience for students through the UTEP Edge \u2013 the institution\u2019s official framework of learning outcomes. The Edge is an asset-based framework that builds on the successful foundation of UTEP\u2019s access, excellence, and impact mission and focuses on three foundational principles: talented students, engaging experiences, and lifelong success. The Edge was formed in 2016 as part of UTEP\u2019s Quality Enhancement Plan, which recognizes that students enter with many talents, great strengths, and big dreams. UTEP\u2019s asset-based plan commits to further developing students\u2019 strengths through high-impact, enriching experiences to ensure that every UTEP student receives the best holistic education necessary for success on our campus, in the professional world, and as community and global leaders. More about the UTEP Edge Streamlining Academic Transfer Pathways UTEP has established partnerships with two and four-year institutions and campus departments to create clear transfer pathways and co-enrollment plans to ensure a seamless transition between institutions. UTEP prioritizes a student-centered transfer experience by focusing on credit mobility and transfer student success and persistence. UTEP is committed to supporting transfer students\u2019 success through policy, practice, and action that enhances transfer opportunities, addresses credit acceptance complexities, minimizes course duplication, and ultimately facilitates a cost-effective path to graduation for our students. More about Transfer Articulation Elevating Holistic Advising UTEP\u2019s holistic advising model is designed to help our students identify and capitalize on their assets in order to cultivate strong foundations during their first three semesters. By elevating advising to deliberate and meaningful interaction with every student, UTEP empowers students to cultivate individual agency and assists them in developing individualized academic, financial, and engagement plans that carve a clear pathway to successful degree completion. More about Academic Advising Redesigning Core Curriculum Reimagining Core @ UTEP is an institution-wide effort to enhance student engagement, learning, and success across all core curriculum component areas. Through the dedicated efforts of faculty, staff, students, and administrators, our mission is to leverage such engagement to aid students in developing the academic and professional competencies to be successful at and persist in their endeavors during their tenure at UTEP and beyond. The Reimaging Core @ UTEP effort fulfills Goal 1, Initiative 2 of the UTEP Strategic Plan: Teaching, Learning, and Student Experience \u2014 incorporating immersion opportunities specific to our region and providing early opportunities for engaged and active learning throughout the foundational academic experience of the core curriculum.FB-98450 More about Reimagining Core @ UTEP Promoting Student Professional Growth UTEP fosters students' professional development and career readiness by taking a cross-institutional approach and collaborating with administrators and faculty from different departments. Additionally, the university develops strategic partnerships with campus departments, and local, regional, and national employers via the Career Center. This partnership facilitates student employment, internships, and professional development offerings, paving pathways for career success. Through these opportunities, students gain exposure to diverse work environments, access mentorship, expand their professional network, and cultivate transferable skills crucial for career readiness. More about the UTEP Career Center Fostering Entering Student Support The Entering Student Experience fosters an inclusive environment to ensure students from diverse backgrounds have a meaningful transition to UTEP.\u202f\u202fBuilding opportunities for engagement, belonging, agency, academic success, and professional preparation, we facilitate the continued development of our students\u2019 academic skills and unique strengths and empower them to succeed in their educational and professional pursuits. More about the Entering Student Experience <!--\n    .accWrapper > div {\n    padding-left:24px;\n    }\n    .collapseToggleControl.collapsed span.glyphicon:before {\n        content: \"\\002b\";\n    }\n    .collapseToggleControl span.glyphicon:before {\n        content: \"\\2212\";\n    }\n    .optionalblock {\n        margin-top: 30px;\n        margin-bottom: 30px;\n    }\n /*flex*/\n.highligtsWrapper {\n    display: flex;\n    display: -webkit-flex;\n    flex-wrap: wrap;\n    margin-left: -14px;\n}\n.highligtsWrapper .col-md-4:nth-last-child(1) {\n    margin-bottom: 30px;\n}\n.highligtsWrapper .well {\n\tbox-shadow:0px 2px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);-webkit-box-shadow:0px 2px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);;\n\theight: 100%;\n\tpadding: 0;\n}\n.highligtsBody {\n\tpadding: 0 24px 0 24px;\n}\n.hi