{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/strategic-plan/", "title": "UTEP Strategic Plan", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About Message from the President Leadership Implementation Council Planning Process History is a Woven Figure Strategic Advantages About Strategic Advantages Leverage Our Place Build Upon the Unique Diversity of Our People Reinforce Our Culture of Care Strengthen Our Engagement and Build Strong Partnerships Strategic Goals About Strategic Goals Teaching, Learning and the Student Experience Advance Discovery Community Impact and Public Service Shape the Future of Higher Education Resources Strategic Plan Resources Data and Reports Strategic Plan Metrics 2022 Annual Report Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support America\u2019s Leading Hispanic-Serving University \u2013 2030 Strategic Plan Main Content THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO AMERICA\u2019S LEADING HISPANIC-SERVING UNIVERSITY 2030 STRATEGIC PLAN STRATEGIC ADVANTAGES STRATEGIC GOALS 2022 ANNUAL REPORT UTEP is a comprehensive public research university that is increasing access to excellent higher education. We advance discovery of public value and positively impact the health, culture, education, and economy of the community we serve. One year into UTEP\u2019s 2030 Strategic Plan implementation, we want to take some time\u00a0to reflect on our progress. I am pleased to say that despite the challenges of the COVID-19 pandemic, we have had a successful first year. The plan focuses on the University\u2019s strategic advantages \u2013 our place, our people, our culture of care and our partnerships \u2013 and lays out a roadmap to leverage those advantages to achieve four goals tied to our mission during the next decade. Read more STRATEGIC ADVANTAGES LEVERAGE OUR PLACE The University of Texas at El Paso is at the heart of a vibrant city located at the westernmost tip of Texas, where three states and two countries converge along a 54-mile section of the Rio Grande in the mountainous Chihuahuan Desert. Learn More BUILD UPON THE UNIQUE DIVERSITY OF OUR PEOPLE Deeply woven into the University\u2019s character are the distinctive strengths of the people whom we serve. Learn More REINFORCE OUR CULTURE OF CARE With a focus on developing the talent of those who have grown up in our region, UTEP has emerged as America\u2019s most successful Hispanic-serving university. Learn More STRENGTHEN OUR ENGAGEMENT AND BUILD STRONG PARTNERSHIPS Partnerships are remarkably strong in the region. The alignment in West Texas among public school districts, El Paso Community College and the University is exceptional. Learn More Ten years from now, when we reflect on this decade of UTEP\u2019s history, it is my hope that this strategic plan will have been an important tool that helped us to focus our work and guide the way.\" - Heather Wilson President STRATEGIC GOALS TEACHING, LEARNING AND THE STUDENT EXPERIENCE Provide students an excellent and engaged education in an inclusive university that builds on student strengths and demonstrates a culture of care. Learn More ADVANCE DISCOVERY Advance research, scholarship and artistic expression with emphasis on areas of current and emerging strength. Learn More COMMUNITY IMPACT AND PUBLIC SERVICE Foster well-being in our community so that we all live healthier, more prosperous, and culturally enriched lives. Learn More SHAPE THE FUTURE OF HIGHER EDUCATION Positively 