{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/student-affairs/oipsa/office-of-international-programs/student-portal.html", "title": "Sunapsis", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search International Programs OIP Home F-1/J-1 visa PASE Program Resources and Forms Sunapsis Study Abroad Office of Study Abroad Application Process Disabilities Abroad Study Away Passport U.S. Passport Information People Staff Contact Us Student Resources Student Resources Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Office of International Programs and Study Abroad Division of Student Affairs Main Content UTEP Division of Student Affairs Office of International Programs and Study Abroad Office of International Programs UTEP Division of Student Affairs Office of International Programs and Study Abroad Office of International Programs Sunapsis Sunapsis: https://sunapsis.utep.edu Sunapsis is the online portal for international students and scholars to submit and check the status of requests, as well as the software system used by OIP staff to manage international student and scholar profiles and review requests. F-1 International Students: All requests must be submitted through Sunapsis. J-1 International Students & Exchange Visitors: All requests must be are requested via email to global@utep.edu or dbrandford@utep.edu . Submit request, at least, 2 weeks in advance to allow for processing. Once a request has been approved, you will receive an email to your UTEP email account with additional information. For assistance with Sunapsis, please contact global@utep.edu .\u00a0Wait 5 business days before requesting information on a pending request. LOGGING IN Most** F-1 International Students will log in using their UTEP username (not full email address) and password by clicking \"Login\" on the main Sunapsis screen. New/Transfer students must first visit https://newaccount.utep.edu to set up their UTEP email account. If you experience difficulties setting up your account, please call the phone number at the bottom of the New Account page. **F-1 International Students who have graduated and are participating in OPT may not be able to log in after\u00a0their UTEP account is deactivated by IT. Those students should follow these steps: Visit https://sunapsis.utep.edu and click on\u00a0the \"New Student/Scholar Login\" button on the bottom of the screen On the bottom of the \"Login to - Limited Services\" page, click on \"Email me my Limited Access PIN\" Enter your UTEP ID # and click \"Submit\" Check your UTEP and personal email for an email with your PIN. If you do not receive it within 10 minutes, please contact global@utep.edu Once you receive your PIN, visit https://sunapsis.utep.edu and click on\u00a0the \"New Student/Scholar Login\" button on the bottom of the screen Fill in your UTEP ID #, date of birth, and PIN, and click \"Login\" USING SUNAPSIS For any questions on which form to submit or questions about using Sunapsis, please contact global@utep.edu . NOTE: Newly admitted students will complete all I-20 applications from the \"Admissions Checklist\" group which can be found in their \"Requests\" section. Given below is a view of the page after the student logs into Sunapsis, followed by the functionalities explained: 1 -> E-form menu (will vary based on whether student is in Initial, Active, or OPT status) 2 -> Navigation bar with Alerts, Notifications, and Calendar updates related to the student 3 -> Notifications: List of recent updates and communications that were sent by email to the student 4 -> Requests: List of e-forms that have been started or submitted by the student, or adjudicated (approved/denied) by an OIP advisor 5 -> Events: This tab will appear if there are any upcoming OIP events with active registration. Register by clicking on \"Details\" and then clicking on \"I'm Going\" Office of International Programs Information F-1/J-1 visa PASE Program Resources and Forms Sunapsis MAIN PAGE OIP Home STUDY ABROAD PASSPORT FACILITY Frequently Asked Questions Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso Office of International Programs and Study Abroad Hours of operation: Monday - Friday 8:30 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. Union East, Room 203, 500 West University Ave. El Paso, Texas 79968 E: global@utep.edu P: (915) 747-5664 F: (915) 747-5794 THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Texas Veterans Portal Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 | SITE FEEDBACK Modal X"}
