 with the nomination by your study abroad advisor or coordinator.\u00a0 UTEP will accept applications only from students coming from universities that have active exchange agreement with UTEP and/or CONAHEC. For Faculty - Study abroad/away programs, in particular Faculty Led Programs, provide rewarding opportunities where faculty engage with students outside of a traditional classroom. The experiences are transformation for students and faculty.\u00a0 Faculty Led Programs are offered during the winter and spring break and summer terms. For Families - The Study Abroad Office encourages parents and families to support their student\u2019s international experience in ways that are unique to your relationship.\u00a0 The Office of Study Abroad follows Texas\u2019 policy regarding communicating with parents under the Family Education Rights and Privacy Act (FERPA) .\u00a0While the Study Abroad Office is happy to answer questions from parents, in many cases we are not able to share information due to FERPA regulations. Types of Programs EXCHANGE Learn More THIRD-PARTY Learn More FACULTY LED Learn More Learning Content FAQs Learn More Family and Friends Learn More Request a Presentation Learn More Marketing Your Experience Learn More Cycles of an Application Learn More Find Funding Learn More Health & Safety Learn More Study Abroad Alumni Learn More Is Study Abroad For Me? Learn More Application Process To learn about commonly selected programs BY UTEP students, the study abroad/away application process, paying for an education abroad and preparing a budget, visit Financial Resources . FEATURED NEWS STAY CONNECTED Study Abroad Types of Study Abroad Programs Frequently Asked Questions Student Safety First Miners Abroad MAIN PAGE UTEP Homepage Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso Office of International Programs Study Abroad Union East, Room 203 500 W. University Ave. El Paso, Texas El Paso, TX 79968 E: studyabroad@utep.edu P: (915) 747-5664 F: (915) 747-5794 TH