{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/audit/about/internship-program.html", "title": "Internship Program", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About About Us Mission & Vision Statement Internship Program General Information Services Provided Internal Audit Committee Professional Standards Professional Organizations and Certifications Resources Frequently Asked Questions People Meet Our Staff Organization Chart Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Office of Auditing and Consulting Services Main Content UTEP Office of Auditing and Consulting Services About UTEP Office of Auditing and Consulting Services About Internship Program The internship program is on a semester basis and provides students the opportunity to work for the Office of Auditing and Consulting Services. Students are involved in all phases of an internal audit, from drafting an audit program to conducting audit tests to writing the audit report. Students are also involved in internal control reviews, inventory counts, follow-up audits, compliance reviews, and other routine assignments. Students assist staff members with audits and/or are assigned their own audits. The students hired for the internship program must meet the following criteria: Completed Intermediate Accounting I Have a 3.00 overall grade point average (GPA) Have a 3.25 accounting GPA Be currently enrolled in or completed Auditing Principles Have strong computer skills, preferably in Microsoft Windows, Word, and Excel Possess good communication skills, both verbal and written Students looking to participate in the internship program may apply by sending your resume to audit@utep.edu . Questions concerning the internship program may also be addressed to e-mail address listed, calling us at 915-747-5191, or visiting us at our office located in room 402 of the administration building. About About Us Mission & Vision Statement Organization Chart Internship Program Resources Frequently Asked Questions Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso Office of Auditing and Consulting Services Administration Building,  Suite 402 500 West University Avenue El Paso, Texas 79968 E: audit@utep.edu P: (915) 747-5191 F: (915) 747-8913 THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Texas Veterans Portal Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 | SITE FEEDBACK Modal X"}
