{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/financial-aid/types-of-aid/scholarships.html", "title": "Scholarships", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search How to Apply Applying for Financial Aid Scholarships Types of Aid The Paydirt Promise The Miner Success Grant Scholarships Financial Aid Grants Student Employment Tuition Waivers and Exemptions Student Loans Summer Financial Aid Financial Aid by College Financial Aid for Transfer Students Financial Aid for Military Students Financial Aid for Graduate Students Eligibility Who is Eligible for Financial Aid How Are My Awards Calculated How Do I Stay Eligible More Information Your Cost of Attendance For Parents Other Ways to Pay for College Our Policies Code of Conduct Consumer Information Resources Guide to Goldmine Forms Upload Your Documents Sign Up for Direct Deposit Net Price Calculator Frequently Asked Questions Contact Us Contact Us Leadership Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Financial Aid and Scholarships Main Content UTEP Financial Aid and Scholarships Types of Aid UTEP Financial Aid and Scholarships Types of Aid Scholarships Scholarships are awards based on merit, awarded to students who demonstrate academic excellence, athletic or artistic talent, leadership, volunteering, or other traits. They can be considered a type of financial aid, and sometimes \u2013 but not always \u2013 require students to have financial need. Scholarships can be funded by UTEP, our generous donors, or foundations such as the Terry Foundation, McDonald\u2019s El Paso Scholarships, and the Hector and Gloria Lopez Foundation. Students can also apply for external scholarships. Scholarships for high school seniors If you are a high school student considering attending UTEP and you are in the top 25% of your junior class, you should apply for the UTEP Excellence Scholarship . Recipients of this award have different backgrounds and experiences, but they all demonstrate academic excellence, leadership, and service to others. The application asks you to list your past experiences and answer short essay questions, which are reviewed by a committee made up of UTEP faculty, staff, and alumni. Each applicant is scored based on how they embody the values of the scholarship. The high school GPA and ranking are also part of the scoring, so it's important for your transcript to be received by the Office of Admissions . SAT and ACT scores are not required nor considered. The application opens each year on October 1 st for students graduating high school the following year. The deadline to apply is January 31 st before your high school graduation, and state residents, international, and out-of-state students are welcome to apply. Submit your application at utep.edu/excellence . The scholarship amount ranges from $2,000 to $8,000 per year and is renewable for up to four years. To remain eligible, students must enroll full-time, maintain a 3.0 GPA, earn 30 credits each year, and participate in service activities at UTEP. Up to five top applicants are selected for the Presidential Scholarship, which covers the student\u2019s full cost of attendance, up to $20,000 per academic year. Continue reading to find more about scholarships you may apply for once you are admitted as a UTEP student, as well as state and external scholarships. Scholarships for UTEP students After you are admitted to UTEP, dig into the ScholarMine! With one single application, ScholarMine can match you with any of more than three hundred donor scholarships. These awards have different eligibility criteria, like college, field of study, GPA, etc., so the application is a mix of matching questions and short essay questions to showcase your leadership, professional development, service to others, and involvement in academic and research activities. Apply starting October 1 each year, at utep.edu/scholarmine . If selected for a UTEP scholarship funded by a donor, you will be asked to write a letter thanking them. Writing a thank you letter for a stranger may be awkward at first, but it is a valuable skill. Read our guide for tips on how to write a thank you letter to your donor . You may also qualify for external scholarships, listed below. Scholarships for graduate and doctoral students If you are a graduate student at UTEP, you may qualify for fellowships through the Graduate School . If you're a doctoral student, you may also qualify for the Texas Leadership Research Scholars program if you meet the following: You graduated from a Texas public high school or an institution of higher education in Texas (public, private, or independent). When you were an undergraduate student, you received either a Pell Grant, a TEXAS or TEG Grant , or a Leadership Scholarship. You are enrolled full-time in a research doctoral degree program at UTEP. You apply for financial aid . You are nominated by the Graduate School based on merit and leadership potential. More information is available at the program website . State scholarships The state of Texas also offers scholarships: The Texas Leadership Scholars Program , for top performing students with demonstrated financial need, leadership in their high school community, and academic success. You may be eligible if you: are a high school student graduating from an accredited Texas high school, you are graduating in the top 10% of your class or are nominated by a high school staff member, submit a FAFSA or TASFA demonstrating financial need, you are eligible for the TEXAS Grant , have evidence of leadership and service within your high school and community, are accepted to UTEP , and complete an application process . If you are planning to become a member of the armed forces, you may qualify for the Texas Armed Services Scholarship program . Athletic and other scholarships Student athletes may be eligible to receive a scholarship from UTEP Athletics to cover tuition and fees or other educational expenses. If you are awarded an athletic scholarship, it will be incorporated into your financial aid award offer. For more information, visit the financial aid and scholarships for student athletes compliance page . External scholarships In addition to UTEP scholarships, there are many external opportunities you can explore using a search engine, such as: fastweb.com finaid.org hsf.net Scholly Scholarships by Sallie studentscholarshipsearch.com If you are an admitted student, explore our external scholarships bulletin board and events site, where you can find up-to-date information about external scholarship opportunities, application deadlines, workshops, and more. <!--\n    .accWrapper > div {\n    padding-left:24px;\n    }\n    .collapseToggleControl.collapsed span.glyphicon:before {\n        content: \"\\002b\";\n    }\n    .collapseToggleControl span.glyphicon:before {\n        content: \"\\2212\";\n    }\n    .optionalblock {\n        margin-top: 30px;\n        margin-bottom: 30px;\n    }\n /*flex*/\n.highligtsWrapper {\n    display: flex;\n    display: -webkit-flex;\n    flex-wrap: wrap;\n    margin-left: -14px;\n}\n.highligtsWrapper .col-md-4:nth-last-child(1) {\n    margin-bottom: 30px;\n}\n.highligtsWrapper .well {\n\tbox-shadow:0px 2px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);-webkit-box-shadow:0px 2px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);;\n\theight: 100%;\n\tpadding: 0;\n}\n.highligtsBody {\n\tpadding: 0 24px 0 24px;\n}\n.highligtsBody .btn-primary {\n    \tdisplay:block;\n    \tmargin-top: 30px;\n