{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/financial-aid/resources/thank-you-donor-letter.html", "title": "Thank You Donor Letter", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search How to Apply Applying for Financial Aid Scholarships Types of Aid The Paydirt Promise The Miner Success Grant Scholarships Financial Aid Grants Student Employment Tuition Waivers and Exemptions Student Loans Summer Financial Aid Financial Aid by College Financial Aid for Transfer Students Financial Aid for Military Students Financial Aid for Graduate Students Eligibility Who is Eligible for Financial Aid How Are My Awards Calculated How Do I Stay Eligible More Information Your Cost of Attendance For Parents Other Ways to Pay for College Our Policies Code of Conduct Consumer Information Resources Guide to Goldmine Forms Upload Your Documents Sign Up for Direct Deposit Net Price Calculator Frequently Asked Questions Contact Us Contact Us Leadership Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Financial Aid and Scholarships Main Content UTEP Financial Aid and Scholarships Resources UTEP Financial Aid and Scholarships Resources Writing a Thank You Letter Many of the scholarships awarded by UTEP are funded thanks to generous donations from donors who believe in the value of education and want to give back to our institution and our community. Showing your own generosity by writing them a heartfelt letter of appreciation will remind them of why they gave in the first place and, perhaps, inspire them to help students following in your footsteps. Here are a few things to keep in mind while you are composing your letter. Plan what you want to say Begin by thinking about what receiving the scholarship means to you and how you plan to succeed with the donor's help. Opening Your first paragraph should state the purpose of your letter and the scholarship you received. Try using these sentence starters to help compose your letter: I am writing to thank you for\u2026 I am writing to express my sincere gratitude for\u2026 I am honored to be one of the recipients of\u2026 I am overjoyed\u2026 I am so grateful for... I wish to thank you for\u2026 I want to express my thanks to you for\u2026 When I received this gift, I felt\u2026 Body Share a little about yourself and why the scholarship is important to you and your commitment to succeed with the donor\u2019s help. I have just begun my college career and can already report\u2026 My plans at this time are to\u2026 I am thankful for this gift because it will allow me to\u2026 The reason I appreciate this gift is\u2026 I am delighted to inform you\u2026 My lifelong dream is to\u2026 Thanks to you, I can\u2026 Since receiving this scholarship, I\u2026 Your scholarship helped me\u2026 Other things to consider sharing with your donor in this paragraph: Your hometown Family background Why you chose UTEP Educational goals What you enjoy about UTEP Organizations you belong to Internships Future plans Post-graduation plans Career plans Closing Thank the donor again and commit to doing the best you can while at UTEP. What I like best about this gift is\u2026 I am thankful for this gift because\u2026 I am forever grateful that you\u2026 Again, thank you for\u2026 Thank you again for\u2026 I really appreciate\u2026 Again, thank you for your generosity. I promise I will \u2026 Final thoughts and examples Remember to write clearly and concisely and double-check for typos and grammatical errors. But above all, show your enthusiasm and be sincere . Your letter should not be longer than 2,000 characters. UTEP\u2019s University Writing Center can assist you in making sure that your letter is clear and concise in content and professional in appearance; they are located at the UTEP Library, room 227. Here are same examples of what your letter may look like: <!--\n    .accWrapper > div {\n    padding-left:24px;\n    }\n    .collapseToggleControl.collapsed span.glyphicon:before {\n        content: \"\\002b\";\n    }\n    .collapseToggleControl span.glyphicon:before {\n        content: \"\\2212\";\n    }\n    .optionalblock {\n        margin-top: 30px;\n        margin-bottom: 30px;\n    }\n /*flex*/\n.highligtsWrapper {\n    display: flex;\n    display: -webkit-flex;\n    flex-wrap: wrap;\n    margin-left: -14px;\n}\n.highligtsWrapper .col-md-4:nth-last-child(1) {\n    margin-bottom: 30px;\n}\n.highligtsWrapper .well {\n\tbox-shadow:0px 2px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);-webkit-box-shadow:0px 2px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);;\n\theight: 100%;\n\tpadding: 0;\n}\n.highligtsBody {\n\tpadding: 0 24px 0 24px;\n}\n.highligtsBody .btn-primary {\n    \tdisplay:block;\n    \tmargin-top: 30px;\n}\n\n.highligtsWrapper .col-md-4 {\n   margin-bottom: 30px;\n}\n\n.lightWhiteBg {\n\tbackground: rgba(255,255,255,.85);\n    padding: 4px 24px 24px 24px;\n    margin-bottom: 20px;\n}\n--> <!--\ndiv.facebook .pp_top .pp_left{background:#fff;}div.facebook .pp_top .pp_middle{background:#fff;}div.facebook .pp_top .pp_right{background:#fff;}div.facebook .pp_content_container .pp_left{background:#fff;}div.facebook .pp_content_container .pp_right{background:#fff;}div.facebook .pp_expand{background:url(//www.utep.edu/university-communications/_UC-Global-Files/lightbox/theme/sprite.png) -31px -26px no-repeat;cursor:pointer}div.facebook .pp_expand:hover{background:url(//www.utep.edu/university-communications/_UC-Global-Files/lightbox/theme/sprite.png) -31px -47px no-repeat;cursor:pointer}div.faceb