{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/uwc/", "title": "University Writing Center", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About About People Our Team Hours/Location Hours/Location Appointments Appointments Writing Help Online who The Writing Mine The Writing Mine Workshops Workshops FAQS FAQs Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support University Writing Center Main Content UTEP University Writing Center Any writer, Any writing LEARN MORE Where To Find Us LEARN MORE Schedule an Appointment LEARN MORE Support Writing Excellence LEARN MORE Workshops coming Fall 2025! LEARN MORE Previous Next UTEP University Writing Center University Writing Center Welcome to the UTEP Writing Center Welcome to University Writing Center\u2019s redesigned website. The new site has been created with two goals in mind. First, to offer UTEP students the opportunity to find resources and assistance on their own, from anywhere, at any time. Our Writing Help Online section provides answers to your most common questions and is continually updated with new information. Second, to offer live synchronous online writing consultations. Online writing consultations assist students from how to begin writing a paper to formatting and citation assistance. Consultants are available online to assist students with any writing needs at any stage of the process. Just as in our physical space, we offer all UTEP students, in any discipline, for any type of writing, an opportunity to collaborate with our talented team of consultants in refining their writing skills and offer resources for students. How we help Hey, Miners! At the Writing Center, we want to help you become independent writers \u2014here\u2019s how we do it: We help students at any point in their writing process and in any discipline. If you have pre-writing concerns like difficulties with brainstorming and outlining , we work with you to narrow down your ideas. And sometimes you just need a second opinion, so we are happy to make suggestions. Or if you already have your paper, and you are struggling with the grammatical aspect of it, we collaborate with you so you can learn new writing techniques. We understand that sometimes following a format or citation can be difficult, that is why we offer resources during sessions so you can feel confident when you do it on your own. Our mission is to help students learn how to apply these techniques with any writing and setting. We want to help you write on your own, so feel free to visit us! Click here to schedule an appointment\u00a0with a writing consultant Synchronous Sessions are live one-on-one with a UWC Consultant. We use a combination of Blackboard Collaborate ULTRA and SharePoint/One Drive to conduct the live sessions.\u00a0 For instructions on how use this system please click here. Online Writing Consultation 1 hour UWC Orientation (Scheduled by Faculty for class) 30 minutes In-Person Writing Consultation 30 minutes The Writing Mine About The University Writing Center first introduced \u201cThe Writing Mine\u201d in 2022 to give a space to our writing center community to write about their experiences and own knowledge about writing. All posts are written by members of our writing center staff, who range from undergraduates in a variety of fields and our graduate students who are working in fields of English Literature, Creative writing and finally Rhetoric and Writing Studies. Our posts have a variety of topics that discuss writing tips or writing \u201ctakes\u201d on a specific topic or opinion. Some of our pieces focus on being informative while others are opinion pieces from our writing staff. Hours of Operation End of Fall Semester The University Writing Center (UWC) will close early on Friday, December 12, 2025, at 2:00 PM . Wintermester Hours The UWC will be open for Wintermester during the following times: Monday \u2013 Friday: 10:00 a.m. \u2013 2:00 p.m. Saturday \u2013 Sunday: Closed Spring 2026 Regular semester hours will resume on Tuesday, January 20, 2026 . Information Hours/Location Appointments The Writing Mine Workshops Meet Our Team Our Team Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso University Writing Center Library 227 500 W University El Paso, Texas 79902 E: uwctutors@utep.edu P: (915) 747-5112 THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Texas Veterans Portal Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 | SITE FEEDBACK Modal X"}
