{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/programs/graduate/bioinformatics-ms.html", "title": "Bioinformatics, M.S.", "text": "College of Science Bioinformatics, M.S. The Master of Science in Bioinformatics is a Professional Science Master’s (PSM) degree designed to train science professionals who can decipher and interpret information embedded in complex biological systems. Graduates are prepared for technical fields in agriculture, biodiversity and environmental science, cancer research, drug design, genetic and infectious diseases, and health data management. .program-overview-section .w-col-5 {\n\tdisplay: none;\n}\n.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    width: 960px;\n}\n@media screen and (max-width: 991px) {\n\t.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n\t    width: 100%;\n\t}\n}\n.pp-wrapper {\n    background-position: 50% 0;\n} Request info Combines advanced studies in computational molecular biology, chemistry, computer science, mathematics and statistics Extensive training in genomics data analysis, molecular modeling and online database development Conduct research on biomolecular sequence analysis, ecoinformatics and phylogenetic analysis, and more GRAD GROWS INTO LEADERSHIP ROLE Lucia Alvarado is a clinical data manager for Ultragenyx Pharmaceutical Inc. in Boston. Her background in life sciences and biomedical research, including genomics and bioinformatics, was honed in part at UTEP. The bioinformatics program provided her with the foundation for an analytical problem-solving mindset and practice in effective collaboration with diverse, cross-functional teams. Lucia Alvarado M.S. 2004 Career Opportunities Our program prepares computational biologists for collaborative and multidisciplinary work with biomedical and clinical researchers. Our graduates work for organizations such as Dow AgroScience, MD Anderson Cancer Center, Pfizer and others. Research Scientist Bioinformatician Microbiologist .program-hero-section {\n    background-i