{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/programs/graduate/statistics-and-data-science-ms.html", "title": "Statistics and Data Science M.S.", "text": "College of Science Statistics and Data Science, M.S. The Master of Science in Statistics and Data Science is individually designed to meet students’ interests and goals. Students receive training in foundational courses in probability and statistics and can then choose from a variety of electives including data mining and data visualization. Students can opt for a thesis or a non-thesis option. Graduates of the program are equipped with the techniques and knowledge needed for careers in government and industry, as well as for the pursuit of further graduate studies. .program-overview-section .w-col-5 {\n\tdisplay: none;\n}\n.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    width: 960px;\n}\n@media screen and (max-width: 991px) {\n\t.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n\t    width: 100%;\n\t}\n}\n.pp-wrapper {\n    background-position: 50% 0;\n} Request info Faculty research covers theoretical and applied statistics, including data mining, bioinformatics, time series and more Gain real world experience by providing  consulting services through the Data Analytics Lab Teaching assistantships are available for full-time graduate students GRAD APPLIES HER STUDIES AS AN INVESTMENT DATA ANALYST Zaira Luján arrived in El Paso with a desire to conduct exceptional data visualization research after completing her undergraduate studies at the University of Rochester. She found the opportunity in UTEP’s statistics graduate program. Throughout her time at UTEP, Zaira conducted research using predictive modeling, served as a teaching assistant, and completed internships in data analysis and data visualization. Post-graduation, Zaira now works as an Investment Data Analyst for Thornburg Investment Management. Zaira Luján M.S. 2022 Career Opportunities In an increasingly data-driven world, being able to translate information into meaningful insights that can be used by organizations is a valuable skill. Our graduates are prepared for the pursuit of doctoral degrees as well as careers in business, health and the military, to name a few. Data Analyst Market Researcher Actuarial Analyst .program-hero-section {\n    background-image: url(_images/statistics-and-data-science-ms/banner.jpg);\n  }\n  @media screen and (max-width: 767px) {\n    .program-hero-section {\n      background-image: url(_images/statistics-and-data-science-ms/banner-m.jpg);\n    }\n  }\n  .column {\n    background-image: url(../..);\n  }\n  .pp-wrapper {\n    background-image: url(_images/statistics-and-data-science-ms/profile-1.jpg);\n  } @media screen and (max-width: 1210px) {\n            \t .w-form iframe {\n            \t\t height:1300px !important;\n            \t}\n            }\n             @media screen and (max-width: 991px) {\n            \t .w-form iframe {\n            \t\t height:900px !important;\n            \t}\n            }\n            \n             @media screen and (max-width: 840px) {\n            \t .w-form iframe {\n            \t\t height:1300px !important;\n            \t}\n            } Request information Financial Aid Program Page Apply Now Check out the classes you'll take Quick Links MY UTEP Library Events Calendar Parking and Transportation University Bookstore UTEP Directory UTEP News Campus Map Admissions Undergraduate Graduate Online Public Course Information Resources Cares Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Texas Veterans Portal Info Center Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 Search pages and people Apply Visit Request Info Current Students Faculty/Staff ABOUT UTEP Financial Aid Research Athletics Giving Admissions // element argument can be a selecto