{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/programs/graduate/physics-phd.html", "title": "Physics, Ph.D.", "text": "College of Science Physics, Ph.D. Students within UTEP’s doctoral program in physics are prepared for a career that provides novel solutions to society’s most pressing needs. Students will benefit from the program’s emphasis on quantum information sciences and faculty who are internationally renowned for their expertise in the density-functional theory-based design of quantum systems, quantum computing, quantum magnetism and quantum sensing. .program-overview-section .w-col-5 {\n\tdisplay: none;\n}\n.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    width: 960px;\n}\n@media screen and (max-width: 991px) {\n\t.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n\t    width: 100%;\n\t}\n}\n.pp-wrapper {\n    background-position: 50% 0;\n} Request info Contribute to cutting edge research carried out within state-of-the-art facilities Become an expert in quantum science and computing and enter the rapidly expanding field of quantum technology Physics graduates have among the highest earnings to debt ratio Meet Program Advisor Tunnah Baruah, Ph.D. Welcome to UTEP’s Ph.D. program in physics. Our students become experts in quantum science and computing, working across a variety of industries and scientific disciplines. Quantum computing’s impact will span health care and national security issues, among others, and graduates of UTEP’s physics doctoral program will be at the forefront of these issues, providing innovative solutions. Tunna Baruah, Ph.D. Assistant Chair and Graduate Advisor Career Opportunities Graduates of the doctoral program in physics will be highly qualified for work in the various industries that are and will be impacted by quantum information sciences. These industries include but are not limited to healthcare and national security. Quantum physicist Research staff scientist Research and Development Associate .program-hero-section {\n    backg