with proof of address. RCCF Form Students applying from a Texas private high school must submit the RCCF form with the High School transcript. High School Certification Incoming freshmen applicants graduating from an out-of-state high school must include the High School Certification form along with official transcripts. Military Resources Military Waiver A waiver to receive resident tuition for service members and dependents stationed in Texas who do not already meet Texas residency requirements. Intent to Establish Residency Form Intent to Establish Residence By registering a letter of intent to establish residence in Texas, eligible veterans and dependents may pay resident tuition without regard to length of time residing in Texas for one year. Choice Act Form Choice Act A qualifying veteran or dependent using certain VA Beneﬁts may qualify for tuition and fees at the resident rate within 3 years of discharge, regardless of formal state of residence. * Unsure about which military residency form best fits your needs?  Please check out this comprehensive guide to provided by the Military Student Success Center . Military Residency Options document.getElementById(\"title-aria\").style.display = \"none\"; Resources Forms Credit By Exam Meningitis Schedule a Tour Apply Now MyStatus Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso Office of Admissions and Recruitment Mike Loya Academic Services Building, Suite 102 601 W Schuster Ave El Paso, Texas 79968 E: futureminer@utep.edu P: (915) 747-5890 F: (915) 747-8893 THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Texas Veterans Portal Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 | SITE FEEDBACK Modal X"}
