{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/student-affairs/admissions/epcctoutep/", "title": "Transfer2UTEP", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search Majors and Academics Undergraduate Programs Top Tier R1 Status Research Visit Schedule a Tour Campus Map Events Student Type Freshman Student Transfer2UTEP International Student Admitted Students Check your Admissions Status Transfer2UTEP Transfer2UTEP Costs and Affordability Paying For College Office of Scholarships Contact Schedule a Virtual Appointment Connect with Us Request Information Departmental Staff Resources Forms Credit By Exam Resources Residency Meningitis Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Office of Admissions & Recruitment Division of Student Affairs Main Content Transfer2UTEP Greetings Future Miners! The Office of Admissions and Recruitment is dedicated to assisting our Transfer students in their transition to the University of Texas at El Paso easy and simple. We have provided this additional resource to assist you in looking up information on Course Equivalencies, Core Course Comparisons, Academic College Information for Transfers, and our schedule of upcoming Transfer Events. We look forward to welcoming you to campus soon and Go Miners! Application Process Academic Information Transfer Events EPCC Transfers Additional Resources 1. Submit your application. You will submit your application for admissions through the goApplyTexas.org website. If this is your first time using the website, you will need to create an account. Once you have created an account, follow the prompts to complete your application for The University of Texas at El Paso. You will choose a major , and list all the schools you have previously attended. Note that we will also use your application to determine admission into award. Apply now at goApplyTexas.org . Apply now Summer or Fall 2024 2. Send us your transcripts. We need official transcripts from all colleges or universities you have attended. When you apply, ask that these institutions send your official transcripts directly to our office. El Paso Community College and the University of Texas at El Paso have the capability to send transcripts electronically and share information. Please ask that your transcripts are sent electronically to expedite the completion of your application. Official Transcripts can be delivered electronically or by mail to: The University of Texas at El Paso Office of Admissions & Recruitment 102 Academic Services Building 500 W University El Paso, Texas 79968 4. Check your status. Once you have submitted your application, check your status at mystatus.utep.edu. Make sure your personal information is correct and you report any errors to us. If you need to make a change, submit the Student Information Update Form (SIUF) to submit@utep.edu . MyStatus 5. See if you have further application requirements. You may have just a few more things to do. Students 21 years of age or younger will need to submit proof that they have received the meningitis vaccine. A copy of your vaccination record can be emailed to our office at meningitis@utep.edu More information can be found by clicking below. Meningitis Information 6. Sign Up for Orientation Once you are admitted, you will be able to sign up for a Transfer Student Orientation where you will be able to meet with your Academic Advisor and register for courses. For more information visit the Office of New Student Orientation. Office of New Student Orientation 7. BECOME A MINER! Transfer Night Transfer nights are events that provide prospective transfer students have the opportunity to meet with a representative of the University of Texas at El Paso's Office of Admission and Recruitment and learn more about the transfer process. The event will take place from 5:00 pm - 7:00 pm on the dates listed below. Thursday, November 30, 2023 Thursday, December 14, 2023 Transfer Day Transfer day is an on-campus event for prospective transfer students. Transfer Day provides the opportunity to meet with representatives from academic colleges, student services, student life, and enrollment services. The event will take place on selected Saturdays listed below between the hours of 7:30 am- 1:00 pm. Saturday, October 23 rd Saturday, November 20 th Saturday, February 5 th Saturday, March 12 th UTEP-EPCC Consortium Agreement Students enrolled at both the University of Texas at El Paso and El Paso Community College can submit a consortium agreement form for the two institutions and receive Financial Aid. For more information please contact the Office of Financial Aid at 915-747-5204. Consortium Agreement Form EPCC Office Hours Students have the opportunity to speak with an Admissions representative at El Paso Community College - Valle Verde Campus Wednesday, November 29, 2023        |  8:00 am - 12:00pm |   1:00pm - 5:00pm Wednesday, December 6, 2023        |  8:00 am - 12:00pm |   1:00pm - 5:00pm Wednesday, January 31, 2024      |  8:00 am - 12:00pm |   1:00pm - 5:00pm Wednesday, February 7, 2024        |  8:00 am - 12:00pm |   1:00pm - 5:00pm Wednesday, February 14, 2024        |  8:00 am - 12:00pm |   1:00pm - 5:00pm Wednesday, February 21, 2024        |  8:00 am - 12:00pm |   1:00pm - 5:00pm Wednesday, March 6, 2024        |  8:00 am - 12:00pm |   1:00pm - 5:00pm Wednesday, March 20, 2024        |  8:00 am - 12:00pm |   1:00pm - 5:00pm Wednesday, March 27, 2024        |  8:00 am - 12:00pm