{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/student-affairs/admissions/admitted/index1.html", "title": "Admitted Miner Checklist", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search Majors and Academics Undergraduate Programs Top Tier R1 Status Research Visit Schedule a Tour Campus Map Events Student Type Freshman Student Transfer2UTEP International Student Admitted Students Check your Admissions Status Transfer2UTEP Transfer2UTEP Cost and Aid Costs and Financial Aid Office of Scholarships Contact Find Your Recruiter Schedule a Virtual Appointment Connect with Us Request Information Departmental Staff Resources Forms Credit By Exam Resources Residency Meningitis Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Office of Admissions & Recruitment Division of Student Affairs Main Content document.getElementById(\"title-aria\").style.display = \"none\"; COUNTDOWN TO UTEP ADMITTED MINER CHECKLIST We're here to help make each step toward becoming a UTEP Miner a smooth experience. Below are the immediate steps you need to complete before you begin attending UTEP. If you are an international student, click here . <!--\nh2 {\n    font-weight: 600;\n    text-transform: uppercase;\n    \n}\n#sec3 h3{\n    color: white;\n}\n\n#sec4 .background-gray{\n    background-color: #DADADA;\n}\n\n$(\"#theScriptsSection\").parent().css(\"padding\",0)\n--> 1. ACCEPT YOUR ADMISSIONS OFFER Let us know you accept our offer of admission and plan to attend UTEP. You will need your UTEP ID number to accept our offer. You can find your Student ID on your acceptance letter. I ACCEPT MY ADMISSIONS OFFER! 2. REGISTER FOR NEW STUDENT ORIENTATION New Student Orientation is required and free to all new students. At orientation you will learn about your major, connect with your academic advisor, and register for classes. You will also have the opportunity to discover student services and resources, and meet current UTEP students. To register for orientation, log into your MyStatus portal at mystatus.utep.edu, and select the session that works best for you. If you have trouble registering for an orientation session call the Office of New Student Orientation at 915-747-6752. Orientation sessions fill quickly and close in advance. REGISTER FOR ORIENTATION 3. FILL OUT THE FAFSA AND APPLY FOR FINANCIAL AID The Free Application for Federal Student Aid (FAFSA) is used to award federal grants, loans, work-study, and certain scholarships, and can be filed now for the 2019-2020 school year. We encourage you to file right away. UTEP’s Federal School Code is 003661 . If you have already applied, you can check your Financial Aid status by logging into mystatus.utep.edu. If you have any questions about Financial Aid or documents that you are being asked to submit, please contact the Office of Student Financial Aid as soon as possible or by calling 915-747-5204. APPLY FOR FINANCIAL AID | FAFSA.GOV CHECK MY FINANCIAL AID STATUS 4. ACTIVATE YOUR MINERS ACCOUNT All UTEP students are required to set up a UTEP account to access e-mail and student portals. After you attend orientation, all official university communication will be sent to your new UTEP e-mail. If you have any questions, please don’t hesitate to contact the UTEP HelpDesk at 915-747-5257. ACTIVATE MY MINERS ACCOUNT 5. EXPLORE YOUR HOUSING OPTIONS What’s so great about living on campus? In a word: everything! Students who live on campus enjoy benefits including from getting involved in their community, being close to classes and activities, living and learning with friends. We offer a variety of living options and floor plans including efficiencies and multi-bedroom units. All of our housing comes fully furnished with access to recreational areas, study areas, and the Miner Metro Shuttle. LEARN MORE 6. SUBMIT FINAL DOCUMENTS As you make the transition to becoming a member of the Miner nation and completing your high school diploma, please remember to submit copies of your final high school transcripts showing your high school graduation and ﬁnal grades. Transcripts must be sent from your high school to the Oﬃce of Admissions and Recruitment to allow you to register for future courses. Transcripts can be submitted electronically through the Texas Records Exchange (TREx), sent form another secure electronic platform to submit@utep.edu, or mailed directly to: Office of Admissions and Recruitment Mike Loya Academic Services Building The University of Texas at El Paso 500 W. University Ave. El Paso TX, 79968-0510 USA <!--\n.shadow {\n  box-shadow: 5px 5px 5px 5px #cfcfcf;\n  padding: 30px;\n}\n--> <!--\nbody {\n    position: relative;\n}\n\n/*header bg fix*/\n@media (min-width:1250px ) and (max-width: 1364px){\n\t.headerContainer {\n\t    width: 100%;\n\t}\n}\n/*Carousel FW*/\n#container + .container {\n\tmax-width: none !important;\n\twidth: auto!important;\n}\n.slide-transfer {\n    display:none!important;\n}\n.video-wrapper {\n\tmax-height: none !important;\n}\n.carousel-caption {\n\tdisplay: none;\n}\n.slide-transfer {\n\tdisplay: none;\n}\n/*FullWidthSection*/\n.fw-section {\n\tpadding-top: 40px;\n\tpadding-bottom: 60px;\n}\n.sectionAnchor {\n    padding-top:135px;\n    margin-top:-135px;\n}\n.fw-section h2 {\n\ttext-align: center;\n}\n.fw-section:after {\n\tclear: both;\n}\n.container-narrow {\n\tmax-width: 800px;\n}\n.row {\n\tmargin-left: 0;\n\tmargin-right: 0;\n}\n@media (max-width: 991px){\n    .col-md-4 {\n        width:100%;\n    }\n}\n/*