{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/student-affairs/admissions/admission-info/transfer-international.html", "title": "Transfer Student - International", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search Majors and Academics Undergraduate Programs Top Tier R1 Status Research Visit Schedule a Tour Campus Map Events Student Type Freshman Student Transfer2UTEP International Student Admitted Students Check your Admissions Status Transfer2UTEP Transfer2UTEP Costs and Affordability Paying For College Office of Scholarships Contact Schedule a Virtual Appointment Connect with Us Request Information Departmental Staff Resources Forms Credit By Exam Resources Residency Meningitis Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Office of Admissions & Recruitment Division of Student Affairs Main Content How to Apply Transfer Transfer International If you are an incoming international student who has earned a minimum of 12 credit hours of college-level and maintained a minimum GPA of 2.0 are eligible for Admission to UTEP as a Transfer student. If you have taken courses at college or universities outside of the United States, additional documentation may be required. Have you taken classes at a University or College in the United States? Use the following step-by-step instructions to successfully submit your application to UTEP. What Courses Transfer? Apply Online Like other Texas public universities, we use the ApplyTexas application. Use it to report your complete academic record, including college credit. The ApplyTexas summer/fall application opens on August 1. We accept applications throughout the year. There is no application fee for domestic applicants or essay requirement for admissions. Apply Below: Spring 2024 Summer 2022 or Fall 2024 Pay the Application Fee $65.00 application fee You can make a payment in person at Cashiers located at: Mike Loya Academic Services Bldg. 500 W. University Ave. El Paso, TX 79968-0510 If you cannot make the payment by check you can pay online. Pay Application Fee Make sure that you have been given a student ID number as it is required to make payments online. Make checks payable to The University of Texas at El Paso. Write your student ID number and/or full name and date of birth on your check or money order. Do not mail cash. Submit Official Transcripts Official High School or College transcripts must be sent directly from the schools attended in the U.S. or abroad. Foreign transcripts must also be accompanied by a Credential Evaluation by a certified credentialing service. Copies or faxes are considered unofficial and will not satisfy this admission requirement. College transcripts from outside of the United States must be accompanied by a credential evaluation. For a list of acceptable credential evaluation services click the link below. Credential Evaluation Services Send transcripts to: Office of Admissions & Recruitment 102 Academic Services Building The University of Texas at El Paso 500 W. University Ave. El Paso TX, 79968-0510 USA Note: All transcripts in languages other than English or Spanish must be accompanied by a certified English translation. Submit Test Scores All international students must submit entrance exam scores. Take one of the following exams and request your scores to be sent directly to UTEP from the testing center: SAT : minimum score of 1070 (reading + math sections) with a score of 480 on the reading section ACT : minimum composite score of 23 with a score of 19 on the English section TOEFL : minimum score of 500 on UTEP’s institutional paper-based exam or a minimum score of 61 on the Internet-Based TOEFL (IBT) TOEFL Exemptions . PAA: minimum score of 1000 Pearson Test of English (PTE): minimum score of 44 UTEP does not accept IELTS scores for admission. Test results may take up to 5 weeks to receive. Use the following testing codes to submit official scores: SAT : 6829 ACT : 4223 TOEFL : 6829 For more information, visit Student Assessment & Testing . Confirmation of Financial Resources International applicants must complete the Confirmation of Financial Resources form to determine if you meet the required economic resource requirement. For more information, visit the Office of International Programs . <!--\n    .accWrapper > div {\n    padding-left:24px;\n    }\n    .collapseToggleControl.collapsed span.glyphicon:before {\n        content: \"\\002b\";\n    }\n    .collapseToggleControl span.glyphicon:before {\n        content: \"\\2212\";\n    }\n    .optionalblock {\n        margin-top: 30px;\n        margin-bottom: 30px;\n    }\n /*flex*/\n.highligtsWrapper {\n    display: flex;\n    display: -webkit-flex;\n    flex-wrap: wrap;\n    margin-left: -14px;\n}\n.highligtsWrapper .col-md-4:nth-last-child(1) {\n    margin-bottom: 30px;\n}\n.highligtsWrapper .well {\n\tbox-shadow:0px 2px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);-webkit-box-shadow:0px 2px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);;\n\theight: 100%;\n\tpadding: 0;\n}\n.highligtsBody {\n\tpadding: 0 24px 0 24px;\n}\n.highligtsBody .btn-primary {\n    \tdisplay:block;\n    \tmargin-top: 30px;\n}\n\n.highligtsWrapper .col-md-4 {\n   margin-bottom: 30px;\n}\n\n.lightWhiteBg {\n\tbackground: rgba(255,255,255,.85);\n    padding: 4px 24px 24px 24px;\n    margin-bottom: 20px;\n}\n--> <!--\ndiv.facebook .pp_top .pp_left{background:#fff;}div.facebook .pp_top .pp_middle{background:#fff;}div.facebook .pp_top .pp_right{background:#fff;}div.facebook .pp_content_container .