{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/programs/graduate/construction-management-ms.html", "title": "Construction Management M.S.", "text": "College of Engineering Construction Management, M.S. Learn to oversee the complexities of projects of all sizes and manage multiple aspects of construction projects from concept to grand opening. UTEP faculty expertly translate their expertise to an online format and help students become well-versed leaders in project management, risk analysis and sustainability. .program-overview-section .w-col-5 {\n\tdisplay: none;\n}\n.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    width: 960px;\n}\n@media screen and (max-width: 991px) {\n\t.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n\t    width: 100%;\n\t}\n}\n.pp-wrapper {\n    background-position: 50% 0;\n} Request info Program accessible to working professionals through its 100% online option Prepare to earn certification through the American Institute of Constructors Help available through the college’s Pathways to Success in Graduate Engineering student support program DEGREE HELPED ALUM START HIS OWN BUSINESS After a 20-year career in the public sector, David Worley wanted to start his own engineering design and contracting business. He turned to UTEP to get more in-depth knowledge of construction management. Worley said UTEP faculty members were responsive and helped him develop skill sets that have carried over to the decisions he has made as a business owner near Houston. David C. Worley M.S. 2018 Career Opportunities UTEP provides students with hands-on experience and expertise to become a leader in the global construction industry. Construction management is a growing field with rewarding pay. This program provides students with the knowledge to take advantage of these industry trends. Safety Director Civil Engineer Construction Engineer .program-hero-section {\n    background-image: url(_images/construction-management-ms/banner.jpg);\n  }\n  @media screen and (max-wi