{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/programs/graduate/clinical-rehabilitation-counseling-mcrc.html", "title": "Clinical Rehabilitation Counseling, MCRC", "text": "College of Education Clinical Rehabilitation Counseling, MCRC UTEP’s Master of Clinical Rehabilitation Counseling program is for individuals who want to help people of all ages with mental, physical, emotional, cognitive or developmental disabilities to achieve more fulfilling lives. Coursework, field experiences and extracurricular opportunities provide graduates with a strong foundation in the philosophy, process and profession of rehabilitation counseling. .program-overview-section .w-col-5 {\n\tdisplay: none;\n}\n.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    width: 960px;\n}\n@media screen and (max-width: 991px) {\n\t.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n\t    width: 100%;\n\t}\n}\n.pp-wrapper {\n    background-position: 50% 0;\n} Request info There is a great need for rehab counselors among state agencies and community programs Students may apply for the $13K Rehabilitation Services Administration scholarship Possibly dual credentials as Certified Rehabilitation/Licensed Professional counselors PROFILE Omar Gonzalez is an El Paso native and a 100% VA disabled Navy retiree. The former NCO pursued this degree to help people with disabilities to live independently. He praised the program’s instructors, whose knowledge and real-world experiences augmented the curricula. Omar plans to work with the veteran community after he earns his degree and rehab counselor certification. Omar Gonzalez UTEP Class of 2022 Career Opportunities MCRC graduates are in demand among rehabilitation agencies in the region, the state and across the country. The agencies include CIGNA Corp., the Texas Division of Assistive and Rehabilitative Services and the U.S. Department of Veteran Affairs. Private practice College/disability service counselor Community mental health service provider .program-hero-sectio