{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/programs/graduate/chemistry-phd.html", "title": "Chemistry Ph.D.", "text": "College of Science Chemistry, Ph.D. This program prepares professional chemists for careers in teaching and research. Students conduct research in human disease and diagnostics, energy, environment and water. Graduates are positioned competitively for jobs in academic, industrial and public settings through an education that is complemented by modern research facilities and collaboration with local industry. .program-overview-section .w-col-5 {\n\tdisplay: none;\n}\n.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    width: 960px;\n}\n@media screen and (max-width: 991px) {\n\t.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n\t    width: 100%;\n\t}\n}\n.pp-wrapper {\n    background-position: 50% 0;\n} Request info Graduates enter fields such as agriculture, petroleum, pharmaceuticals, plastics, health, forensics, materials science, and more Modern facilities have capabilities in X-ray, NMR, Electron Paramagnetic Resonance, and Cryo-Electron Microscopy Collaborate with local industry to explore opportunities to commercialize research results GRAD SHINES AFTER SHIFT IN ACADEMIC JOURNEY Nathaniel Schocker, Ph.D., is a senior scientist at GlycosBio, an international biochemical company headquartered in Houston. He developed the broad technical skill set he uses in his current job while at UTEP, where he entered the chemistry program after completing a bachelor's degree in music from UT Arlington. Nathaniel Schocker, Ph.D. Ph.D. 2016 Career Opportunities A doctoral degree in chemistry opens a wide range of career options in industry, academia, government, nonprofit and entrepreneurship. Find opportunities with government agencies or law enforcement crime laboratories. Researcher Product developer Hazardous waste manager Professor Toxicologist Forensic chemist Epidemiologist .program-hero-section {\n    background-image: url(_images/chemistry-phd/banner.jpg