{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/programs/graduate/chemistry-ms.html", "title": "Chemistry M.S.", "text": "College of Science Chemistry, M.S. The M.S. in Chemistry prepares professional chemists for careers in teaching and research in academic, industrial and public sector settings. Students engage in experimental and/or theoretical research in a range of specializations from analytical chemistry and biochemistry to chemical physics. Graduates are equipped to enter both traditional fields of chemistry and adjacent fields such as forensics, health, and materials science studies. .program-overview-section .w-col-5 {\n\tdisplay: none;\n}\n.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    width: 960px;\n}\n@media screen and (max-width: 991px) {\n\t.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n\t    width: 100%;\n\t}\n}\n.pp-wrapper {\n    background-position: 50% 0;\n} Request info Lab facilities include X-Ray, NMR, Electron Paramagnetic Resonance, and Cryo-Electron Microscopy Fast-track your bachelor's and master's degrees through the five-year B.S.-M.S. option Join faculty research on nano-technology, materials science, organometallic chemistry, physical chemistry, and more UTEP grad focused on cancer therapeutics Roger Ashmus came to UTEP with the vision of a career in chemistry. At UTEP, he took advantage of the opportunities to conduct research, present at academic conferences, and write a thesis. After graduating with both his bachelor's and master's in chemistry from UTEP, Roger pursued doctoral studies at the University of Alberta and later completed a postdoctoral fellowship at Simon Fraser University. Today, he is a scientist at Seagen, a biotechnology research company focused on discovering, developing, manufacturing and commercializing targeted cancer therapeutics. Roger Ashmus M.S. 2010, B.S. 2007 Career Opportunities A master’s degree in chemistry opens a wide range of career options in industry, academia, government, nonprofit and entrepreneurship. Find opportunities with government agencies or law enforcement crime laboratories. Researcher Product developer Hazardous waste manager Professor Toxicologist Forensic chemist Epidemiologist .program-hero-section {\n    background-image: url(_images/chemistry-ms/banner.jpg);\n  }\n  @media screen and (max-width: 767px) {\n    .program-hero-section {\n      background-image: url(_images/chemistry-ms/banner-m.jpg);\n    }\n  }\n  .column {\n    background-image: url(../..);\n  }\n  .pp-wrapper {\n    background-image: url(_images/chemistry-ms/profile-1.jpg);\n  } @media screen and (max-width: 1210px) {\n            \t .w-form iframe {\n            \t\t height:1300px !important;\n            \t}\n            }\n             @media screen and (max-width: 991px) {\n            \t .w-form iframe {\n            \t\t height:900px !important;\n            \t}\n            }\n            \n             @media screen and (max-width: 840px) {\n            \t .w-form iframe {\n            \t\t height:1300px !important;\n            \t}\n            } Request information Financial Aid Program Page Apply Now Check out the classes you'll take Quick Links MY UTEP Library Events Calendar Parking and Transportation University Bookstore UTEP Directory UTEP News Campus Map Admissions Undergraduate Graduate Online Public Course Information Resources Cares Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Texas Veterans Portal Info Center Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 Search pages and people Apply Visit Request Info Current Students Faculty/Staff ABOUT UTEP Financial Aid Research Athletics Giving Admissions // element argument can be a selector string\n//   for an individual element\nvar flkty = new Flickity( '.co-carousel-wr', {\n  // options\n  freeScroll: true,\n