{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/programs/graduate/business-administration-phd.html", "title": "Business Administration Ph.D.", "text": "Woody L. Hunt College of Business Business Administration, Ph.D. UTEP’s Ph.D. in Business Administration program prepares new generations of college faculty from diverse backgrounds to meet critical teaching and research challenges projected in business and business education. The program offers research opportunities for specializations in accounting, finance, management, and marketing. .program-overview-section .w-col-5 {\n\tdisplay: none;\n}\n.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    width: 960px;\n}\n@media screen and (max-width: 991px) {\n\t.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n\t    width: 100%;\n\t}\n}\n.pp-wrapper {\n    background-position: 50% 0;\n} Request info UTEP is accredited by AACSB, a designation held by less than 5% of business schools 95% job placement within three months of graduating since 2018 Full-tuition support available through competitive fellowships STUDENT TAKES LONGTIME ACCOUNTING CAREER TO NEXT LEVEL After a successful 20-plus-year accounting career, Angelica Castro decided to challenge herself in UTEP’s Ph.D. in Business Administration program and pursue a career in academia or financial consulting. By combining her professional experience with research methodologies, Angelica engages in meaningful research with faculty advisors on U.S. and international financial reporting standards. Angelica Castro Ph.D. Class of 2024 Career Opportunities A Ph.D. in Business Administration opens doors for individuals interested in research careers or higher education teaching positions. UTEP graduates have gone on to teaching positions at New Mexico State University and Texas Woman's University. Professor Economist C-level Executive .program-hero-section {\n    background-image: url(_images/business-administration-phd/banner.jpg);\n  }\n  @media screen and (max-width: 767px) {\n    .p