{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/programs/graduate/biomedical-engineering-phd.html", "title": "Biomedical Engineering Ph.D.", "text": "College of Engineering Biomedical Engineering, Ph.D. Students in the biomedical engineering Ph.D. program will advance scientific discoveries alongside leading aerospace researchers who are assessing the health of human beings while they are in space. You can work directly with NASA’s Space Technology Research, Development, Demonstration and Infusion program to develop and apply new technologies that impact the development of commercial spaceflight. .program-overview-section .w-col-5 {\n\tdisplay: none;\n}\n.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    width: 960px;\n}\n@media screen and (max-width: 991px) {\n\t.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n\t    width: 100%;\n\t}\n}\n.pp-wrapper {\n    background-position: 50% 0;\n} Request info Acquire a depth of knowledge in your research area while also learning how to function on multidisciplinary teams. Work in a number of focus areas including microfluidics, biomechanics, tissue engineering and 3D printed biomaterials. Opportunities for intensive aerospace research in new Additive Manufacturing and Aerospace Center. PIONEERING AEROSPACE RESEARCH Andie Padilla feels primed for a successful career in the field of engineering thanks to the rigor of work she has experienced at UTEP. As a doctoral student in NASA’s Space Technology Research, Development, Demonstration and Infusion program, she has contributed to testing on 3D-printed bio-tissue produced at UTEP that will be integrated into a neural-sensing device and tested in suborbital space flight. Andie Padilla Ph.D. 2022, B.S. 2021 Career Opportunities The biomedical engineering program trains a new breed of creative investigators who are able to translate basic science discoveries into technology developments for the needs of society, government and industry. Bioinformatics Scientist Postdoctoral Researcher Biomedical Engineer .program-hero-section {\n    background-image: url(_images/biomedical-engineering-phd/banner.jpg);\n  }\n  @media screen and (max-width: 767px) {\n    .program-hero-section {\n      background-image: url(_images/biomedical-engineering-phd/banner-m.jpg);\n    }\n  }\n  .column {\n    background-image: url(../..);\n  }\n  .pp-wrapper {\n    background-image: url(_images/biomedical-engineering-phd/profile-1.jpg);\n  } @media screen and (max-width: 1210px) {\n            \t .w-form iframe {\n            \t\t height:1300px !important;\n            \t}\n            }\n             @media screen and (max-width: 991px) {\n            \t .w-form iframe {\n            \t\t height:900px !important;\n            \t}\n            }\n            \n             @media screen and (max-width: 840px) {\n            \t .w-form iframe {\n            \t\t height:1300px !important;\n            \t}\n            } Request information Financial Aid Program Page Apply Now Check out the classes you'll take Quick Links MY UTEP Library Events Calendar Parking and Transportation University Bookstore UTEP Directory UTEP News Campus Map Admissions Undergraduate Graduate Online Public Course Information Resources Cares Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Texas Veterans Portal Info Center Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 Search pages and people Apply Visit Request Info Current Students Faculty/Staff ABOUT UTEP Financial Aid Research Athletics Giving Admissions // element argument can be a selector string\n//   for an individual element\nvar flkty = new Flickity( '.co-carousel-wr', {\n  // options\n  freeScroll: true,\n  setGallerySize: false\n});\nif ($(window).width() < 768) {\n\tvar flkty = new Flickity( '.pchl-grid', {\n\t  // options\n\t  freeScroll: