{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/programs/graduate/spanish-ma.html", "title": "Spanish M.A.", "text": "College of Liberal Arts Spanish, M.A. The Spanish M.A. provides students with skills for the analysis of literary and cultural artifacts from Hispanic America, Spain, Brazil and the U.S.-Mexico border. The U.S.-Mexico border location makes this graduate program an ideal one for in-depth study and comparative study of Spanish-speaking and bilingual cultural production. .program-overview-section .w-col-5 {\n\tdisplay: none;\n}\n.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    width: 960px;\n}\n@media screen and (max-width: 991px) {\n\t.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n\t    width: 100%;\n\t}\n}\n.pp-wrapper {\n    background-position: 50% 0;\n} Request info Faculty are recognized for their research on Latin American, Spanish and Brazilian cultures Research emphasis positions students competitively for doctoral programs across the globe Complement your studies with a study abroad program that serves as an on-site language experience GRAD ON PATH TO PROFESSORIATE Romy Y. Cerón Canché’s dream is to teach literature and languages in higher education, so the Yucatan, Mexico, native chose this program for its varied curriculum. The degree plan honed her research and teaching skills, and primed her for Ph.D. studies in Spanish literature and culture at the University of Arizona, where she is assistant editor of the Arizona Journal of Hispanic Cultural Studies. Romy Y. Cerón Canché M.A. 2018 Career Opportunities Our graduates have an excellent command of Spanish, an understanding of Hispanic cultures on a global scale, and strong skills in research, textual analysis and instruction, which prepares them to work in a wide variety of fields and industries. High School/Community College teacher Public administrator Homeland security analyst Academic and literary publishing International business Non-profit organizational work Translation and/or interpretation Tourism industry Print or television journalism .program-hero-section {\n    background-image: url(_images/spanish-ma/banner.jpg);\n  }\n  @media screen and (max-width: 767px) {\n    .program-hero-section {\n      background-image: url(_images/spanish-ma/banner-m.jpg);\n    }\n  }\n  .column {\n    background-image: url(../..);\n  }\n  .pp-wrapper {\n    background-image: url(_images/spanish-ma/profile-1.jpg);\n  } @media screen and (max-width: 1210px) {\n            \t .w-form iframe {\n            \t\t height:1300px !important;\n            \t}\n            }\n             @media screen and (max-width: 991px) {\n            \t .w-form iframe {\n            \t\t height:900px !important;\n            \t}\n            }\n            \n             @media screen and (max-width: 840px) {\n            \t .w-form iframe {\n            \t\t height:1300px !important;\n            \t}\n            } Request information Financial Aid Program Page Apply Now Check out the classes you'll take Quick Links MY UTEP Library Events Calendar Parking and Transportation University Bookstore UTEP Directory UTEP News Campus Map Admissions Undergraduate Graduate Online Public Course Information Resources Cares Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Texas Veterans Portal Info Center Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 Search pages and people Apply Visit Request Info Current Students Faculty/Staff ABOUT UTEP Financial Aid Research Athletics Giving Admissions // element argument can be a selector string\n//   for an individual element\nvar flkty = new Flickity( '.co-carousel-wr', {\n  // options\n  freeScroll: true,\n  setGallerySize: false\n});\nif ($(window).width() < 768) {\n\tvar flkty = new Flickity( '.pchl-grid', {\n\t  // options\n\t  freeScroll: true,\n\t 