 now open! APPLY TODAY! Submission deadline is January 15, 2026. To be considered for admission to the program, applicants must have a bachelor's degree from an accredited university. A background in Business, Finance, Accounting, Economics or Statistics is helpful, but not required for admission into the program. A master's degree in business or a related field is preferred. Students entering the program without a master’s degree and/or a business background may be required to take up to eight “leveling\" graduate courses in addition to the Ph.D. coursework. Students without a working knowledge of elementary calculus and statistics may also be required to take extra coursework. Before submitting their application, applicants must select the area of concentration in which they would like to pursue their Ph.D . The Ph.D.  in Business Administration program offers four concentrations: Accounting, Finance, Management, and Marketing. If you have questions about the concentration you would like to pursue, you may contact the following professors: Concentration in Finance: Dr. Faith Xie - fxie@utep.edu Concentration in Management: Dr. Miguel Ramos-Gonzalez - maramosgonzalez@utep.edu Concentration in Marketing: Dr. John Zhu - jzhu2@utep.edu Concentration in Accounting: Dr. Jesse Glaze - jlglaze@utep.edu All applicants must submit the following materials through our online application system : The Graduate Degree Program Application Non-refundable application processing fee $45 for U.S. Citizens/Permanent Residents/Mexican Nationals $80 for International Applicants Official transcripts of all undergraduate and graduate coursework completed. Unofficial transcripts may be accepted with the initial application . A valid GMAT score report. Although GMAT scores are preferred, GRE scores are also accepted. Test scores may not be more than five years old. At least two letters of recommendation from academic or professional sources familiar with the applicant's background. The application system allows recommenders to be “registered” so they can submit their letters online. Letters can also be mailed directly to our Graduate School: UTEP Graduate School The University of Texas at El Paso Administration Building, Room 200 500 West University Ave. El Paso, TX 79968-0566 A current resume or curriculum vitae A personal statement of academic interests and goals related to the concentration you would like to pursue. International applicants must also submit acceptable scores on the TOEFL, IELTS, or Duolingo English Test. Test scores may not be more than two years old. If admitted, international students must complete all additional steps listed on the Office of International Programs (OIP) website . In addition, a personal or online interview may be required. Financial Support Subject to availability of funds and academic performance, admitted students are provided research and teaching assistantships for up to four years. Health insurance is included. Additionally, the program awards fellowships for incoming doctoral students that cover the cost of in-state tuition. No additional application is required. Other benefits are also available to graduate students. For more information, please visit the Human Resources website or call (915) 747-5202. Contact Us Dr. Richard Posthuma Director, Ph.D. Program Phone: (915) 747-8646 rposthuma@utep.edu Carolina Gonzalez, MBA Senior Coordinator - Ph.D. in Business Administration Business Room 102 Phone: (915) 747-5496 cegonzalez4@utep.edu PhD in Business Administration Ph.D. in Business Administration Program Description Admission Curriculum Academic Placements FAQ Why a Ph.D. in Business? Hunt Research Excellence Awards Concentrations Ph.D. Accounting Concentration Ph.D. Finance Concentration Ph.D. Management Concentration Ph.D. Marketing Concentration Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Graduate School Resources Graduate Graduate Admissions Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso Woody L. 