 of this program is to support graduate students in the College of Engineering, College of Science and the Woody L. Hunt College of Business who have an interest in the development and exploitation of inventions, for both commercial and non-commercial purposes. Requirements for Admission A bachelor's degree from UTEP's College of Engineering, Woody L. Hunt College of Business , or College of Science, or an equivalent degree from a similarly accredited college or university. Graduate students in good standing in UTEP's College of Engineering, Woody L. Hunt College of Business , or College of Science are eligible. A 3.0 cumulative undergraduate grade point average. Degree Plan The total number of hours required for the certificate is 15. Students will be required to complete the five courses listed below. BUSN 5330 Project Management MGMT 5314 Corporate Entrepreneurship ENGR 5381 Innovation and Entrepreneurship BUSN 5350 Innovation and Entrepreneurship Elective (see note 1) Note 1. Available electives include courses offered (a) by the College of Engineering, such as CS 5380 Intellectual Property Law and CE 5382 Cost Analysis, (b) by the Woody L. Hunt College of Business , such as MGMT 5314 Corporate Entrepreneurship, and (c) other appropriate graduate courses in Engineering and Business Administration, subject to program approval. Undergraduate Undergraduate Programs Corporate Academies at Hunt College Graduate Master of Accountancy Master of Business Administration (MBA) Ph.D. in Business Administration Certificates Certificate of Accountancy Certificate in Innovation and Entrepreneurship Corporate Academies Banking Academy Risk Management Human Capital Management Academy Enterprise Resource Planning Academy Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Graduate School Resources Graduate Graduate Admissions Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso Woody L. Hunt College of Business Business Administration Building 500 W University El Paso, Texas 79968 E: . P