ted a bachelor’s degree in accounting from an AACSB accredited business school. The degree consists of a four graduate core accounting courses required and approved by the Texas State Board of Public Accountancy so that students will qualify for candidacy to take the CPA examination, and a graduate elective accounting course in the student’s area of interest. Specific Requirements for the Certificate of Accountancy Degree Students who have not completed a bachelor’s degree in accounting from an AACSB accredited business school will need to consult with the graduate accounting advisor as to the leveling requirements to become eligible for admission to the Certificate of Accountancy program. Degree Plan Core Accounting Requirements (12 semester hours) ACCT 5302 Advanced Accounting ACCT 5314 Professional Writing for Accountants ACCT 5328 Federal Income Tax – Partnerships and Corporations ACCT 5329 Ethics in Accounting Graduate Level Accounting Electives (3 semester hours) Subject to the approval of the graduate accounting advisory, students are to take one graduate elective accounting course. “Due to federal Gainful Employment regulations, please be advised that this certificate program requires your review of its Gainful Employment Disclosure. ” Undergraduate Undergraduate Programs Corporate Academies at Hunt College Graduate Master of Accountancy Master of Business Administration (MBA) Ph.D. in Business Administration Certificates Certificate of Accountancy Certificate in Innovation and Entrepreneurship Corporate Academies Banking Academy Risk Management Human Capital Management Academy Enterprise Resource Planning Academy Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Graduate School Resources Graduate Graduate Admissions Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso Department of Accounting and Information Systems Business Room 260 500 W University El Paso, Texas 79902 E: coba_aisdept@utep.edu P: (915) 747-5192 F: (915) 747-8618 THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PAS