is a comprehensive description and self-analysis of the program, its governance, and available resources, faculty, students, academic curriculum, research, and community service. A site visit for reaccreditation by the Council on Education for Public Health was conducted on February 15 - 16, 2018. On September 7, 2018 CEPH re-accredited the UTEP MPH program for another 7 years, to expire on December 31, 2025. We welcome you to view a copy of our final accreditation report and self-study documents. These documents are available on our website by linking to the following: 2018 Final Accreditation Report 2012 Final Self-Study 2018 Final Self-Study Maria Duarte-Gardea, PhD, RD, LD Department Chair and Professor Department of Public Health Sciences College of Health Sciences/School of Nursing Bldg. Office # 403 The University of Texas at El Paso 500 West University Avenue El Paso, Texas, 79968 Tel: 915 – 747 – 7252 E-mail: moduarte@utep.edu Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso Department of Public Health Sciences Health Sciences and Nursing Building 500 W. University Ave. El Paso, Texas 79968 E: moduarte@utep.edu P: (915) 747-8214 THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Texas Veterans Portal Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 | SITE FEEDBACK Modal X"}
