EP Woody L. Hunt College of Business graduate msecon UTEP Woody L. Hunt College of Business graduate msecon Fast Track Program In order to apply for admission to the BBA Economics/MS Economics Fast Track Program, students are required to have a 3.3 cumulative grade point average and 90 credit hours of undergraduate coursework towards the BBA in Economics (at least 24 of which must be at UTEP).  Students admitted to the program may take 12 credit hours of graduate coursework in economics, selected from the following course offerings. Apply Here! MS Economics Course: Dually Counted Toward BBA Economics course: ECON 5305 Applied Mathematical Economics ECON 3372 Mathematical Economics ECON 5311 Managerial Economics ECON 3310 Managerial Economics ECON 5321 Public Choice ECON 3325 Public Choice ECON 5330 Public Sector Economics ECON 4330 Public Sector Economics ECON 5334 Urban Economics ECON 3335 Urban Economics ECON 5361 Applied International Economics ECON 4325 International Economics ECON 5365 Economic Development ECON 3367 Economic Development ECON 5366 Latin American Economics ECON 3366 Economics of Latin America ECON 5370 Applied Econometrics ECON 3373 Introduction to Econometrics Master of Science in Economics Admission Curriculum Fast Track Program Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Graduate School Resources Graduate Graduate Admissions Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso Economics and Finance Business Room 236 500 W University El Paso, Texas 79902 E: coba_advising@utep.edu P: (915) 747-5245 THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Texas Veterans Portal Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 | SITE FEEDBACK Modal X"}
