t: 1;\n      align-items: stretch;\n}\n#terNav a:hover {\n    background: #FF8200;\n    color: #041E42;\n    text-decoration: none;\n}\n#terNav.sectionAnchor {\n    margin-top:0;padding-top:0;\n}\n.terNavPar {\n    padding:0 !important;\n    background-color: #f2f2f2 !important;\n    box-shadow: 0px 1px 13px rgba(0,0,0,.25);\n    border-bottom: 1px solid #fff;\n    border-top: 1px solid #fff;\n}\n/*Secondary Navigation*/\n#secNav .optionalblock {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-flow: row nowrap;\n  justify-content: space-evenly;\n    align-items: stretch;\n\n}\n#secNav a {\n    display: block;\n    color:#041e42;\n    font-family: \"BebasNeue\", \"Open Sans\", sans-serif;\n    padding: 18px 15px;\n    text-align: center;\n    font-size: 28px;\n    font-weight: 500;\n    letter-spacing: 1px;\n    text-transform: uppercase;\n    line-height: 1.25;\n}\n#secNav a:hover {\n    background: #FF8200;\n    color: #041E42;\n    text-decoration: none;\n}\n#secNav.sectionAnchor {\n    margin-top:0;padding-top:0;\n}\n.secNavPar {\n    padding:0 !important;\n    background-color: #f2f2f2 !important;\n    box-shadow: 0px 1px 13px rgba(0,0,0,.25);\n    border-bottom: 1px solid #fff;\n    border-top: 1px solid #fff;\n}\n@media (max-width: 767px) {\n    #secNav .optionalblock {\n        display: flex;\n        flex-flow: wrap;\n        justify-content: center;\n    }\n    #secNav a {\n        padding: 18px 45px;\n    }\n}\n@media (max-width: 570px) {\n        #secNav .optionalblock {\n        display: flex;\n        flex-flow: wrap;\n        justify-content: center;\n    }\n    #secNav a {\n        padding: 18px 30px;\n    }\n}\n--> UTEP Graduate School Faculty Graduate Faculty and Council Proposals and Procedures Current Graduate Council Members Graduate Council Meeting Schedule Resolutions Graduate Studies Faculty Structures HOOP §3 Ch. 3 UTEP tenure track or tenured faculty, who are appointed in a unit that has a graduate program, are regular members of the Graduate Faculty. The rights and responsibilities of Graduate Faculty are specified in the Graduate School By-Laws section of the Handbook of Operating Procedures (Chapter 3). Individuals who have the relevant academic background and experience, but are not members of the Graduate Faculty (e.g., non-tenure track faculty, visiting scholars, professional staff), may apply for temporary membership to the Graduate Faculty. There are three levels of temporary members that have different rights and responsibilities as outlined in the Graduate School By-Laws. This form can be used to apply for temporary membership. Click here All units that offer a graduate program must have a Program Committee on Graduate Studies that oversees their respective graduate program. Graduate Program Committees must also identify a Graduate Program Director to represent the program (see Graduate School By-Laws for responsibilities of Graduate Program Committees and Directors). The Graduate Council serves as the administrative arm for the regular members of the Graduate Faculty and guides university policies for graduate education.  The Graduate Council is comprised of 20 members: Chair of the Graduate Council Two members each from the College of Education, College of Engineering, College of Health Sciences, College of Liberal Arts, College of Science, and the Woody L. Hunt Colleges of Business; Four at-large members President of the Faculty Senate The Dean of the Graduate school (ex-officio) A student representative (non-voting) To access Graduate School By-laws . Click here To access the Advisor Handbook that provides an overview of degree requirements as well as relevant processes and policies. Click here To access the Graduate Catalog . Click here Proposals and Procedures UTEP encourages progressive and continuous improvement of its academic programs. Each Department assumes responsibility for all graduate programs within its area or interdisciplinary program unit. All official communication and information concerning a