{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/programs/graduate/political-science-ma.html", "title": "Political Science M.A.", "text": "College of Liberal Arts Political Science, M.A. UTEP’s location on the U.S.-Mexico border makes it an excellent place to study law, conflict, globalization, political behavior, and institutions. Students pursuing an M.A. in Political Science strive to explain, analyze and interpret political phenomena with the help of award-winning faculty in research and teaching. Students receive personalized mentorship, yielding outcomes that include doctoral candidates and positions in the public and private sector. .program-overview-section .w-col-5 {\n\tdisplay: none;\n}\n.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    width: 960px;\n}\n@media screen and (max-width: 991px) {\n\t.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n\t    width: 100%;\n\t}\n}\n.pp-wrapper {\n    background-position: 50% 0;\n} Request info Full or partial tuition assistance is available for teaching and research assistants Faculty expertise in public policy, democracy, political economy, political behavior, conflict, international cooperation, and law Ample opportunities for students to engage in original research, attend academic conferences, and co-author papers ENVIRONMENTAL INTEREST HELPS GRAD Jonathan Picado found his professional passion as an undergraduate: environmental law. He enrolled in the master’s program with a goal to enhance his writing and research skills. Invested faculty and rigorous courses prepared him for law school, where he is now a research assistant and a student writer on the Iowa Law Review. He spent summer 2022 as a law clerk with the U.S. Department of Justice. Jonathan Picado B.A. 2018, M.A. 2020 Career Opportunities Our high-impact courses prepare graduates for a wide variety of career paths. Most of our graduates earn jobs in business, education, government service, and the military or nonprofit organizations. Others choose to pursue a doctoral degree. Nonprofit managers/researchers Political campaign aides Dual-credit teachers .program-hero-section {\n    background-image: url(_images/political-science-ma/banner.jpg);\n  }\n  @media screen and (max-width: 767px) {\n    .program-hero-section {\n      background-image: url(_images/political-science-ma/banner-m.jpg);\n    }\n  }\n  .column {\n    background-image: url(../..);\n  }\n  .pp-wrapper {\n    background-image: url(_images/political-science-ma/profile-1.jpg);\n  } @media screen and (max-width: 1210px) {\n            \t .w-form iframe {\n            \t\t height:1300px !important;\n            \t}\n            }\n             @media screen and (max-width: 991px) {\n            \t .w-form iframe {\n            \t\t height:900px !important;\n            \t}\n            }\n            \n             @media screen and (max-width: 840px) {\n            \t .w-form iframe {\n            \t\t height:1300px !important;\n            \t}\n            } Request information Financial Aid Program Page Apply Now Check out the classes you'll take Quick Links MY UTEP Library Events Calendar Parking and Transportation University Bookstore UTEP Directory UTEP News Campus Map Admissions Undergraduate Graduate Online Public Course Information Resources Cares Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Texas Veterans Portal Info Center Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 Search pages and people Apply Visit Request Info Current Students Faculty/Staff ABOUT UTEP Financial Aid Research Athletics Giving Admissions // element argument can be a selector string\n//   for an individual element\nvar flkty = new Flickity( '.co-carousel-wr', {\n  // options\n  freeScroll: true,\n  setGallerySize: false\n});\nif ($(window).width() < 768) {\n\tvar flkty = new 