{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/programs/graduate/physical-therapy-dpt.html", "title": "Physical Therapy DPT", "text": "College of Health Sciences Physical Therapy, DPT UTEP’s Doctor of Physical Therapy program prepares highly qualified doctors of physical therapy to provide culturally proficient and linguistically competent care in the U.S.-Mexico border region and beyond. Graduates are committed to patient-centered care, evidence-based practice, the community’s health, life-long learning and the advancement of the physical therapy profession. .program-overview-section .w-col-5 {\n\tdisplay: none;\n}\n.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    width: 960px;\n}\n@media screen and (max-width: 991px) {\n\t.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n\t    width: 100%;\n\t}\n}\n.pp-wrapper {\n    background-position: 50% 0;\n} Request info First in the nation to integrate Spanish language training across the curriculum Remarkable 100% placement rate for graduates Accredited by Commission on Accreditation in Physical Therapy Education (CAPTE) Alumna Dedicated to Helping Underserved Communities Briana Dawkins is very passionate about working with underserved communities. The Houston native picked UTEP’s DPT program because of its emphasis on cultural competency and its commitment to community service. Briana created UTEP's DPT Diversity, Equity and Inclusion Committee (now Committee on Inclusive Excellence) to promote dialogue, reflection and research. As a physical therapist, she aims to help patients regain function and mobility. Briana Dawkins DPT 2022 Career Opportunities Physical therapists provide care for people with or at risk for injuries, illnesses, disabilities and other health-related conditions, and promote optimal physical function. Licensure is required in each state to practice. Physical Therapist Clinical Research Professional Sports .program-hero-section {\n    background-image: url(_images/physical-therapy-dpt/banner.jpg);\n  }\n