{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/programs/graduate/philosophy-ma.html", "title": "Philosophy M.A.", "text": "College of Liberal Arts Philosophy, M.A. Students pursuing this degree combine logic and ethics to solve quandaries that arise in law, science, engineering and society. Graduates will be equipped with historical context of philosophy’s greatest questions, an understanding of new philosophical questions and a unique point of view that prepares them for advanced degrees in philosophy, law, medicine and science. .program-overview-section .w-col-5 {\n\tdisplay: none;\n}\n.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    width: 960px;\n}\n@media screen and (max-width: 991px) {\n\t.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n\t    width: 100%;\n\t}\n}\n.pp-wrapper {\n    background-position: 50% 0;\n} Request info Learn from faculty with expertise in epistemology, phenomenology and Latin American philosophy Crystallize the ability to understand and break down complex existential and ethical problems across industries and societies Earn a strong foundation for doctoral programs in philosophy PHILOSOPHY HELPS HUMANITY Edgar M. Llamas believes philosophy helps people to question and clarify their lives, and to think for themselves. The El Paso native said this program, with its conceptually open faculty, taught him to conduct independent research, which helped get him admitted to the philosophy Ph.D. program at the University of Oregon. His professional goal is to become a tenured philosophy professor. EDGAR MAURICIO LLAMAS B.A. 2018, M.A. 2021 Career Opportunities Our graduates often work in government or nonprofit organizations. Others enter Ph.D. programs or pre-professional degree programs in areas such as law and medicine. Many graduates enter positions in secondary or higher education. Professor/high school teacher Technology analyst/programmer Government administrator .program-hero-section {\n    background-image: url(_images/philosophy-ma/banner