{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/programs/graduate/pharmacy-pharmd.html", "title": "Pharmacy Pharm.D.", "text": "School of Pharmacy Pharmacy, Pharm.D. UTEP pharmacy students learn technical Spanish, participate in study-away and engage with trained preceptors to better serve diverse patients. With the opportunity to study under experienced professors, students can take advantage of research opportunities including studies on bioengineered therapeutics and ovarian, lung and pancreatic cancer treatments. .program-overview-section .w-col-5 {\n\tdisplay: none;\n}\n.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    width: 960px;\n}\n@media screen and (max-width: 991px) {\n\t.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n\t    width: 100%;\n\t}\n}\n.pp-wrapper {\n    background-position: 50% 0;\n} Request info Take advantage of research funding opportunities Study at the only pharmacy school on the U.S.-Mexico border Develop a wide range of ethical, social, behavioral and communication skills to help you succeed in your career Student is Ready to Serve Her Community As someone passionate about health care, student Heather Howell admires UTEP’s commitment to ensuring graduates of the pharmacy program are uniquely prepared to serve people in a binational region. In addition to a quality education and opportunities to work with local and national pharmacy organizations, she is also learning pharmaceutical Spanish to better support the people she will serve. Heather Howell Pharm.D. '24 Career Opportunities Pharmacy graduates have career opportunities in academia, industry, consulting, community practice, regulatory agencies and many other areas. Ambulatory Care Pharmacist Cardiology Pharmacist Community Pharmacist Geriatric Pharmacist Hospital Pharmacist Infectious Disease Pharmacist Nucelar Pharmacist Oncology Pharmacist Pediatric Pharmacist Industry Pharmacist Poison Control Pharmacist Veterinary Pharmacist Psychiatric Pharmacist Emergency Medicine Pharmacist .p