{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/programs/graduate/occupational-therapy.html", "title": "Occupational Therapy, OTD", "text": "College of Health Sciences Occupational Therapy, OTD UTEP’s new Doctor of Occupational Therapy program will prepare entry-level occupational therapists who will improve quality of life and reduce health disparities in the U.S.-Mexico borderland and beyond. Courses include foundational and clinical sciences, general occupational therapy evaluation, treatment and evidence-based practices, as well as research and occupation-based practices that incorporate cultural and contextual relevance. .program-overview-section .w-col-5 {\n\tdisplay: none;\n}\n.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    width: 960px;\n}\n@media screen and (max-width: 991px) {\n\t.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n\t    width: 100%;\n\t}\n}\n.pp-wrapper {\n    background-position: 50% 0;\n} Request info Volunteer in the community and gain educational and professional experience in the Student Occupational Therapy Association. Curriculum includes two courses in conversational Spanish to enhance student's Spanish communication during clinical encounters. Dedicated faculty have diverse interest areas and strong practitioner backgrounds. A CHANCE TO PURSUE A PASSION The ability to help people in various settings from hospitals to schools was one of the reasons Elena chose a career in occupational therapy. But the opportunity to learn from distinguished faculty is what attracted her to UTEP’s occupational therapy program. Elena hopes to combine her passion for science, education and health care working as an occupational therapist with children. Elena Pinaroc Master of Occupational Therapy, 2022 Career Opportunities The OTD is the highest level of academic preparation that an entry-level occupational therapist can obtain. It is expected to be the required degree program to enter the occupational therapy profession in the coming years. Hospital occupational therapist School occupational therapist Home health occupational therapist .program-hero-section {\n    background-image: url(_images/occupational-therapy/banner.jpg);\n  }\n  @media screen and (max-width: 767px) {\n    .program-hero-section {\n      background-image: url(_images/occupational-therapy/banner-m.jpg);\n    }\n  }\n  .column {\n    background-image: url(../..);\n  }\n  .pp-wrapper {\n    background-image: url(_images/occupational-therapy/profile-1.jpg);\n  } @media screen and (max-width: 1210px) {\n                .w-form iframe {\n                    height: 1200px !important;\n                }\n            }\n                    @media screen and (max-width: 991px) {\n                .w-form iframe {\n                    height: 800px !important;\n                }\n            }\n                    @media screen and (max-width: 831px) {\n                .w-form iframe {\n                    height: 1200px !important;\n                }\n            } Request information Financial Aid Program Page Apply Now Check out the classes you'll take Quick Links MY UTEP Library Events Calendar Parking and Transportation University Bookstore UTEP Directory UTEP News Campus Map Admissions Undergraduate Graduate Online Public Course Information Resources Cares Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Texas Veterans Portal Info Center Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 Search pages and people Apply Visit Request Info Current Students Faculty/Staff ABOUT UTEP Financial Aid Research Athletics Giving Admissions // element argument can be a selector string\n//   for an individual element\nvar flkty = new Flickity( '.co-carousel-wr', {\n  // options\n  freeScroll: true,\n  setGallerySize: false\n});\nif ($(window).width() < 768) {\n\tvar flk