{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/programs/graduate/music-mm.html", "title": "Music M.M.", "text": "College of Liberal Arts Music, M.M. The Master of Music degree provides a flexible and affordable program with intensive training in theory, conducting, composition, music education, and instrumental and vocal performance. Conducting majors have a distance-learning option. This degree prepares graduates for doctoral study and for a variety of careers in K-12 schools, academia and as professional musicians. .program-overview-section .w-col-5 {\n\tdisplay: none;\n}\n.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    width: 960px;\n}\n@media screen and (max-width: 991px) {\n\t.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n\t    width: 100%;\n\t}\n}\n.pp-wrapper {\n    background-position: 50% 0;\n} Request info Faculty provide one-on-one instruction in the student’s area of specialty The Center for Arts Entrepreneurship offers presentations by industry leaders, and insights into career options. The online conducting concentration appeals to working professionals. High School Choir Director Uses Master’s Skills Daily El Pasoan Nadiah Eleskandrany always has been fervent about music and teaching. She uses her graduate degree daily as a high school choir director in East Texas. Nadiah said the flexibility of the online program allowed her to manage school and her full-time teaching schedule. She called her UTEP professors supportive, and said that the curricula furthered her knowledge, abilities and confidence. NADIAH ELESKANDRANY M.M. 2021 Career Opportunities Master of Music graduates pursue careers as performers, educators and composers, but they can use the wide range of skills learned to explore careers such as music marketers, promoters, entrepreneurs, recording engineers and arts administrators. Public School or Community College Teacher Professional musician Professional Ensemble Director .program-hero-section {\n    background-image: url(_images/music-m-