{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/programs/graduate/kinesiology-ms.html", "title": "Kinesiology M.S.", "text": "College of Health Sciences Kinesiology, M.S. UTEP’s M.S. in Kinesiology is for students who wish to improve their knowledge and skills related to the science of human movement. The program offers research and learning opportunities in motor behavior, strength and conditioning, and metabolic and exercise research, with faculty mentors that specialize in each area. Degree can be earned in person or online. .program-overview-section .w-col-5 {\n\tdisplay: none;\n}\n.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    width: 960px;\n}\n@media screen and (max-width: 991px) {\n\t.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n\t    width: 100%;\n\t}\n}\n.pp-wrapper {\n    background-position: 50% 0;\n} Request info Online M.S. in Kinesiology degree available through Finish@UT. Access to five state-of-the-art research labs, including the Stanley E. Fulton Gait Research and Movement Analysis Lab Fast-track option allow undergraduates to earn graduate credit while completing the B.S. in kinesiology degree Degree Prepares Alumnus for Research Career In UTEP's MiNER lab, Ali Mossayebi jumpstarted his research career by investigating new and effective ways to manage metabolic and cardiovascular diseases. He has presented his work at conferences such as the American Diabetes Association. He also has manuscripts under review in peer-reviewed scientific journals. Ali plans to continue his success in UT Austin's Kinesiology and Health Education Ph.D. program. Ali Mossayebi M.S. Kinesiology 2022 Career Opportunities Graduates are prepared for competitive entry into research and entry-level teaching positions in industry, government, or academia, or they may continue their education in a doctoral program such as UTEP's Interdisciplinary Health Sciences Ph.D. program. Strength and Conditioning Coach Exercise physiologist Kinesiologist .program-hero-section {\n    bac