{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/programs/graduate/integrated-engineering-ms.html", "title": "Integrated Engineering, M.S.", "text": "College of Engineering Integrated Engineering, M.S. This degree is a personalized 33-hour multidisciplinary program that enables students to tailor their engineering coursework to align with their interests. Students combine a primary concentration in an engineering field with a secondary concentration in another field, either in or outside engineering. Possible secondary concentrations are numerous, including education, business administration, computer science, information technology, and fields in the sciences, the liberal arts, and the health sciences. .program-overview-section .w-col-5 {\n\tdisplay: none;\n}\n.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    width: 960px;\n}\n@media screen and (max-width: 991px) {\n\t.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n\t    width: 100%;\n\t}\n}\n.pp-wrapper {\n    background-position: 50% 0;\n} Request info Take your pick of courses in any of UTEP’s renowned engineering programs such as aerospace or computer science. Students can obtain practical experience with internships at top companies such as Lockheed Martin and Raytheon. Benefit from departmental integration that draws on expertise of all engineering departments. ARMY VET RELISHES OPPORTUNITY AT UTEP Matthew Hilding developed varied interests while in the U.S. Army. As such, the master’s program in engineering offered avenues to explore multiple fields. Hilding relished the chance, earning a fellowship with the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration. Today, he is an electrical engineer with Leidos in Albuquerque. Matthew Hilding M.S. 2018, B.S. 2017 Career Opportunities Program graduates enjoy successful careers in engineering and technology companies in the U.S. and abroad; in service science and engineering companies such as Apple, AT&T, Halliburton, Google and IBM; and in aerospace, defense, energy and manufacturing industries, including NASA and Department of Defense laboratories; and in academic positions. Project Engineer Engineering Manager Design Engineer Process Engineer Sales Engineer Systems Engineer Operations Supervisor Supply Quality Engineer Professor .program-hero-section {\n    background-image: url(_images/engineering-ms/banner.jpg);\n  }\n  @media screen and (max-width: 767px) {\n    .program-hero-section {\n      background-image: url(_images/engineering-ms/banner-m.jpg);\n    }\n  }\n  .column {\n    background-image: url(../..);\n  }\n  .pp-wrapper {\n    background-image: url(_images/engineering-ms/profile-1.jpg);\n  } @media screen and (max-width: 1210px) {\n            \t .w-form iframe {\n            \t\t height:1300px !important;\n            \t}\n            }\n             @media screen and (max-width: 991px) {\n            \t .w-form iframe {\n            \t\t height:900px !important;\n            \t}\n            }\n            \n             @media screen and (max-width: 840px) {\n            \t .w-form iframe {\n            \t\t height:1300px !important;\n            \t}\n            } Request information Financial Aid Program Page Apply Now Check out the classes you'll take Quick Links MY UTEP Library Events Calendar Parking and Transportation University Bookstore UTEP Directory UTEP News Campus Map Admissions Undergraduate Graduate Online Public Course Information Resources Cares Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Texas Veterans Portal Info Center Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 Search pages and people Apply Visit Request Info Current Students Faculty/Staff ABOUT UTEP Financial Aid Research Athletics Giving Admissions // element argument can be a selector string\n//   for an individual element\nvar flkty 