{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/programs/graduate/emba.html", "title": "Executive Master of Business Administration, EMBA", "text": "Woody L. Hunt College of Business Executive Master of Business Administration, EMBA You have made a mark in your business or organization. Now, take the next step and scale your impact as a leader with UTEP’s 16-month hybrid Executive MBA program. Designed for seasoned professionals, the UTEP EMBA’s blend of online modules and bi-monthly, in-person Saturday sessions are held in the heart of Downtown El Paso. The UTEP EMBA provides deep business insights and classmates with diverse industry experience. .program-overview-section .w-col-5 {\n\tdisplay: none;\n}\n.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    width: 960px;\n}\n@media screen and (max-width: 991px) {\n\t.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n\t    width: 100%;\n\t}\n}\n.pp-wrapper {\n    background-position: 50% 0;\n} Request info Designed for leaders with at least five years of managerial experience Network with peers who have leadership experience across a variety of industries Learn from accomplished faculty in accounting, logistics, international commerce and finance EMBA grad applies business principles as mayor of Las Cruces Ken Miyagishima was already the m ayor of Las Cruces, New Mexico and an established business leader when he decided to pursue a UTEP Executive MBA. He found that the principles of business he learned in classes, such as strategic and financial management , were immediately applicable to his economic development platform as m ayor and his leadership of the Farmers Insurance southern New Mexico district. He appreciated th at the faculty tie d business theory and principles to students’ areas of interest. Ken Miyagishima EMBA 2021 Leadership Pathways EMBA graduates expand their leadership skills and hone their ability to pivot into a variety of industries thanks to their financial, strategic and organizational acumen. The EMBA reinforces and positions graduates for managerial and C-suite roles in any business-related function across all industries. Chief Executive Officer Chief Financial Officer Chief Information Officer Chief Marketing Officer Vice President of Sales Director of Human Resources Business Development Manager Management Consultant Operations Manager Strategy Director Project Manager Global Product Manager Investment Banker .program-hero-section {\n    background-image: url(_images/emba/banner.jpg);\n  }\n  @media screen and (max-width: 767px) {\n    .program-hero-section {\n      background-image: url(_images/emba/banner-m.jpg);\n    }\n  }\n  .column {\n    background-image: url(../..);\n  }\n  .pp-wrapper {\n    background-image: url(_images/emba/profile-1.jpg);\n  } @media screen and (max-width: 1210px) {\n            \t .w-form iframe {\n            \t\t height:1300px !important;\n            \t}\n            }\n             @media screen and (max-width: 991px) {\n            \t .w-form iframe {\n            \t\t height:900px !important;\n            \t}\n            }\n            \n             @media screen and (max-width: 840px) {\n            \t .w-form iframe {\n            \t\t height:1300px !important;\n            \t}\n            } Request information Financial Aid Program Page Apply Now Check out the classes you'll take Quick Links MY UTEP Library Events Calendar Parking and Transportation University Bookstore UTEP Directory UTEP News Campus Map Admissions Undergraduate Graduate Online Public Course Information Resources Cares Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Texas Veterans Portal Info Center Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 Search pages and people Apply Visit Request Info Current Students Faculty/Staff ABOUT UTEP Financial Aid R