{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/programs/graduate/electrical-engineering-ms.html", "title": "Electrical Engineering M.S.", "text": "College of Engineering Electrical Engineering, M.S. Students in the Master of Science in Electrical Engineering gain advanced knowledge in electric power and energy, microelectronics and semiconductor devices, electronics packaging, RF and microwave devices and systems, communication systems, and control and signal processing. Students work with faculty involved in local, national and international collaborations that enhance opportunities for research, technical training and developing professional networks. .program-overview-section .w-col-5 {\n\tdisplay: none;\n}\n.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    width: 960px;\n}\n@media screen and (max-width: 991px) {\n\t.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n\t    width: 100%;\n\t}\n}\n.pp-wrapper {\n    background-position: 50% 0;\n} Request info Funding is available for fellowships, scholarships and graduate assistantships Opportunities exist to gain hands-on experience doing research or working on real-world projects under faculty supervision Select from a thesis or non-thesis option to build an academic pathway that works with your life PRIME PROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCES AT UTEP LEAD GRAD TO GM Juan Carlos Muñoz credits UTEP with changing his life. On campus, he was involved in the Baja Challenge and the Student Government Association. Off campus, he served internships at NASA and Freeport-McMoRan. Today, he is helping to develop the next generation of electric vehicles as a design release engineer with General Motors. Juan Carlos Muñoz M.S. Electrical Engineering 2015, B.S. Electrical Engineering 2012 Career Opportunities Graduates have been hired by Texas Instruments, El Paso Electric, Raytheon Technologies, Intel, Microsoft, Amazon, Boeing, Lockheed Martin, IBM, NASA, Blue Origin, national laboratories and more. They are also recruited by companies and government agencies in engineering, health and non-technology sectors. Electrical engineer Energy engineer Aerospace engineer .program-hero-section {\n    background-image: url(_images/electrical-engineering-ms/banner.jpg);\n  }\n  @media screen and (max-width: 767px) {\n    .program-hero-section {\n      background-image: url(_images/electrical-engineering-ms/banner-m.jpg);\n    }\n  }\n  .column {\n    background-image: url(../..);\n  }\n  .pp-wrapper {\n    background-image: url(_images/electrical-engineering-ms/profile-1.jpg);\n  } @media screen and (max-width: 1210px) {\n            \t .w-form iframe {\n            \t\t height:1300px !important;\n            \t}\n            }\n             @media screen and (max-width: 991px) {\n            \t .w-form iframe {\n            \t\t height:900px !important;\n            \t}\n            }\n            \n             @media screen and (max-width: 840px) {\n            \t .w-form iframe {\n            \t\t height:1300px !important;\n            \t}\n            } Request information Financial Aid Apply Now Check out the classes you'll take Quick Links MY UTEP Library Events Calendar Parking and Transportation University Bookstore UTEP Directory UTEP News Campus Map Admissions Undergraduate Graduate Online Public Course Information Resources Cares Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Texas Veterans Portal Info Center Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 Search pages and people Apply Visit Request Info Current Students Faculty/Staff ABOUT UTEP Financial Aid Research Athletics Giving Admissions // element argument can be a selector string\n//   for an individual element\nvar flkty = new Flickity( '.co-carousel-wr', {\n  // options\n  freeScroll: true,\n  setGallerySize: false\n});\nif ($(window).width()