{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/programs/graduate/educational-administration-med.html", "title": "Educational Administration M.Ed.", "text": "College of Education Educational Administration, M.Ed. UTEP's Master of Education in Educational Administration is designed to train future school and university leaders and administrators. Students have the option to choose one of two concentrations based on their goals: K-12 administration (in person) and higher education leadership (fully online). Students will walk away with real-world and theoretical knowledge to help them lead the next generation of K-12 and university students. .program-overview-section .w-col-5 {\n\tdisplay: none;\n}\n.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    width: 960px;\n}\n@media screen and (max-width: 991px) {\n\t.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n\t    width: 100%;\n\t}\n}\n.pp-wrapper {\n    background-position: 50% 0;\n} Request info Earn real-world experience through a semester-long, field-based administration internship Flexible schedules include options for online, hybrid, hi-flex and face-to-face courses K-12 leaders may take courses toward principal certification, further advancing their careers DEGREE MADE COLLEGE ADVISOR A BETTER LEADER Deyna Aragon’s passion has been to help students navigate college to achieve successful outcomes. She chose the M.Ed. in Educational Administration for its balance of theory and practical application. She immediately was able to use what she learned in the classroom. Today she is a senior academic advisor at the University of Oklahoma. Deyna Aragon B.A. 2016, M.Ed. 2020 Career Opportunities Graduates secure leadership roles in higher education as well as K-12 public and private schools at the campus and central office levels. They make essential contributions to the learning and holistic development of students. Community College/University Leader Superintendent/Central Office Administrator Assistant Principal/Principal .