{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/programs/graduate/criminology-and-criminal-justice-ms.html", "title": "Criminology and Criminal Justice M.S.", "text": "College of Liberal Arts Criminology and Criminal Justice, M.S. This degree, which is offered in a thesis-track or a non-thesis track (professional track), to appeal to different educational goals, prepares individuals to identify problems and develop solutions through the application of criminological theories and policies to varied social issues that contribute to crime. They learn how to implement these solutions within a variety of justice-related agencies. .program-overview-section .w-col-5 {\n\tdisplay: none;\n}\n.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    width: 960px;\n}\n@media screen and (max-width: 991px) {\n\t.program-overview-section .w-col.w-col-7 {\n\t    width: 100%;\n\t}\n}\n.pp-wrapper {\n    background-position: 50% 0;\n} Request info Our faculty conducts research collaborations with students that will help advance scholarship and policy Students provided with theoretical, methodological and analytical tools required to teach and conduct research Faculty is engaged in cutting-edge research that prepares students for the challenges of criminal justice practice ALUMNA STRIVES FOR SAFER SOCIETIES Roxana Muniz is an El Paso County probation officer who works to create safer communities through offender interventions. Her master’s degree enhanced her skills and knowledge to deal with criminal behavior. Roxana’s degree led to a promotion and opportunities with federal agencies. She plans to pursue a master’s degree in Latin American Border Studies, and a job as a federal probation officer. Roxana Muniz B.A. 2014, M.S. 2021 Career Opportunities This degree helps law enforcement officers to pursue promotions or serve as an entry point for a competitive job at a federal agency. Our thesis track prepares students who later aspire to enter a Ph.D. program in criminal justice or criminology. Law Enforcement Officer Special agent at a federal agency (FBI, DEA, ATF, Secret Service, etc.) Criminologist .program-hero-section {\n    background-image: url(_images/criminology-and-criminal-justice-ms/banner.jpg);\n  }\n  @media screen and (max-width: 767px) {\n    .program-hero-section {\n      background-image: url(_images/criminology-and-criminal-justice-ms/banner-m.jpg);\n    }\n  }\n  .column {\n    background-image: url(../..);\n  }\n  .pp-wrapper {\n    background-image: url(_images/criminology-and-criminal-justice-ms/profile-1.jpg);\n  } @media screen and (max-width: 1210px) {\n            \t .w-form iframe {\n            \t\t height:1300px !important;\n            \t}\n            }\n             @media screen and (max-width: 991px) {\n            \t .w-form iframe {\n            \t\t height:900px !important;\n            \t}\n            }\n            \n             @media screen and (max-width: 840px) {\n            \t .w-form iframe {\n            \t\t height:1300px !important;\n            \t}\n            } Request information Financial Aid Program Page Apply Now Check out the classes you'll take Quick Links MY UTEP Library Events Calendar Parking and Transportation University Bookstore UTEP Directory UTEP News Campus Map Admissions Undergraduate Graduate Online Public Course Information Resources Cares Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Texas Veterans Portal Info Center Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 Search pages and people Apply Visit Request Info Current Students Faculty/Staff ABOUT UTEP Financial Aid Research Athletics Giving Admissions // element argument can be a selector string\n//   for an individual element\nvar flkty = new Flickity( '.co-carousel-wr', {\n  // options\n  freeScroll: true,\n  setGallerySize