{"url": "https://www.utep.edu/business/graduate/macc/macc.html?mc-program-grad", "title": "Master of Accountancy - UTEP Business", "text": "(function(d, s, id) {\n  var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n  if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n  js = d.createElement(s); js.id = id;\n  js.src = \"//connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.7\";\n  fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n}(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk')); Skip to main content MinerAlert Search pages and people Toggle navigation Search About About Hunt College Accreditation Contact Us Our Mission and Vision Hunt Insights Hunt Connect Academic Programs Undergraduate Programs Master of Accountancy Master of Business Administration (MBA) Master of Science in Economics with Data Analytics Ph.D. in Business Administration Certificate of Accountancy Certificate in Innovation and Entrepreneurship Corporate Academies at Hunt College Departments Accounting and Information Systems Department Economics and Finance Marketing, Management and Supply Chain People Current Doctoral Students Dean's Office Faculty UTEP Campus Directory Research Center for Free Enterprise Border Region Modeling Project Center for Multicultural Management and Ethics Hunt Institute The Mike Loya Center for Innovation and Commerce Seminars Alumni and Partners Alumni Hunt Business Leadership Council Giving to UTEP Distinguished Alumni Gold Nuggets Resources Student Resources Faculty and Staff Resources BUSN Space Reservation Data Request Search pages and people My UTEP Resources for INFORMATION FOR: Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Parents Quick Links X Quick Links Library Parking & Maps UTEP News Events Student Affairs Business Affairs Employment Opportunities University Bookstore Technology Support Woody L. Hunt College of Business Main Content UTEP Woody L. Hunt College of Business graduate macc UTEP Woody L. Hunt College of Business graduate macc Master of Accountancy <!--\n.macc-alert {\n    background: #f2f4f7; /* light neutral */\n    border-left: 6px solid #041e42; /* UTEP navy accent */\n    padding: 25px 28px;\n    margin-bottom: 30px;\n    border-radius: 4px;\n  }\n\n  .macc-alert h2 {\n    margin: 0 0 18px 0;\n    font-family: \"Tungsten A\", \"Tungsten B\", \"Open Sans\", sans-serif;\n    font-size: 40px;\n    color: #041e42;\n    text-transform: uppercase;\n    letter-spacing: 0.5px;\n  }\n\n  .macc-alert p {\n    margin: 0 0 16px 0;\n    font-family: \"Open Sans\", sans-serif;\n    font-size: 18px;\n    color: #2e3240;\n    font-weight: 700;\n    text-transform: uppercase;\n    line-height: 1.45;\n  }\n--> Program Update Beginning Fall 2026, the MAcc program will move to a fall-only admission cycle. All future applications will be considered for fall entry. Program updates reflecting recent CPA exam changes are also underway. Our MAcc program is designed for individuals preparing for careers in professional accounting fields or for practicing accountants wishing to increase their knowledge. The MAcc program provides a learning environment that develops a diverse set of skills in students to prepare them for professional careers in a dynamic world. There are two components to the Master of Accountancy program. The Pre-Master of Accountancy requirements consists of 36 semester hours of courses in accounting, business law, economics, quantitative methods, marketing, and finance. Students who have completed a bachelor’s degree in accounting from an AACSB accredited business schools are not required to complete leveling courses. The MAcc course of study is 30 semester hours of graduate level coursework including 27 hours of accounting core courses, and 3 hours of accounting capstone. Completion of the MAcc degree meets the educational requirements to sit for the CPA exam in Texas. <!--\n.table-container {\n      width: 100%;\n      display: table;\n    }\n    .table-row {\n      display: table-row;\n    }\n    .table-cell {\n      display: table-cell;\n      padding: 10px;\n      text-align: center;\n      vertical-align: middle;\n    }\n    .btn {\n      display: inline-block;\n      padding: 10px 20px;\n      font-size: 16px;\n      color: #fff;\n      background-color: #007bff;\n      border: none;\n      border-radius: 4px;\n      text-decoration: none;\n      cursor: pointer;\n    }\n    @media (max-width: 600px) {\n      .table-row {\n        display: block;\n      }\n      .table-cell {\n        display: block;\n        width: 100%;\n      }\n      .btn {\n        width: 100%;\n        box-sizing: border-box;\n        margin-bottom: 10px;\n      }\n    }\n--> Admissions Curriculum Certificate Tuition & Scholarships AACSB Accreditation The Woody L. Hunt College of Business has earned AACSB Accreditation for both it's Business Administration and Accounting programs. Less than 5 percent of business schools worldwide have earned this prestigious designation from AACSB International-The Association to Advance Collegiate Schools of Business—which provides global leadership in advancing management education. Contact Us Sarah Robertson Assistant Professor of Practice Chair, Graduate Accounting Programs Committee Business Administration Building, Room 243 Phone: (915) 747-5014 sarobertson@utep.edu Admission and Advising UTEP Graduate Business Center 201 E. Main, Suite 110. Phone: (915) 747-7768 Fax: (915) 532-8213 macc@utep.edu Resources Download the Certificate of Accountancy Brochure (PDF) Master of Accountancy Master of Accountancy Admission Requirements Application Deadlines MAcc Curriculum Certificate of Accountancy MAcc Fast Track MAcc FAQ Contact Us Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions MAcc Store Graduate School Resources Graduate Graduate Admissions Connect With Us The University of Texas at El Paso Department of Accounting and Information Systems Business Room 260 500 W University El Paso, Texas 79902 E: coba_aisdept@utep.edu P: (915) 747-5192 F: (915) 747-8618 THE UNIVERSITY OF TEXAS AT EL PASO CARES Act Compliance Clery Crime Statistics Emergency Information Employment Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Report Fraud Required Links State Reports Texas Veterans Portal Title IX Reporting Title IX Sexual Misconduct Policy UT System Web Accessibility Web Privacy Policy 500 West University Avenue | El Paso, TX 79968 | 915-747-5000 | SITE FEEDBACK Modal X"}
